{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.1 (Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases): appended steps 1-9 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and created specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (10 obligations, 9 acceptance bindings, 8 behavior seams, 4 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 1 ADD_RED / 2 CLOSE_RED: tabulated imports become the core TabulatedNK case. The kernel moves out of MaterialImport.buildTabulatedClosure, which is deleted.\n- 3: AbscissaKind moves from DispersionModels.fs into Dispersion.fs.\n- 4 ADD_RED / 5 CLOSE_RED: Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian oscillator become law data cases.\n- 6 ADD_RED / 7 CLOSE_RED: Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann become law data cases; the Faddeeva series moves too.\n- 8: Silicon and Langasite carry a published-law case.\n- 9: EpsAxisEvaluated and the custom equality are deleted.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The brief misses Silicon and Langasite. MaterialLibrary.fs:455,476-477 build both from EpsAxisEvaluated closures that restate OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs, and their indices are not finite term sums. Step 8 adds the closed set PublishedIndexLaw (int tags 1-3, tryOfWire) with the case PublishedLawAxis. Its kernels move from Dispersive.fs, which then calls them, and the MaterialLibrary restatements are deleted, so each closed form exists once and the engine numbers are bit-identical. The planner should reflect this in .spec-md sec 3.1; S1.4's 'every built-in round-trips' and S1.5's export then carry these cases.\n2. The brief says DispersionModelsTests \"stays green unchanged\". That cannot hold: three of its facts match EpsAxisEvaluated (lines 330, 381, 545). Their match arms follow the new cases, and their assertions, including the exact closure equalities, are unchanged. The two lowering-equality reds (steps 4 and 6) are added to this class.\n3. Facet keys: the four oscillator laws and the published laws keep the existing key 'Evaluated (transcendental)'. LibraryFacetsTests therefore stays unchanged, and so does Silicon's key. The tabulated case gets the new key 'Tabulated n/k'. Fact names that say 'evaluated case/segment' are kept, because they now denote these closed-form cases.\n4. MaterialComplexity.isEditable keeps every non-term-data case view-only: tabulated, the oscillator laws and the published laws. Editing behaviour is unchanged. Tabulated imports now gain a defined band (their sample range), so the out-of-band diagnostic flags requests outside it. This is intended.\n5. TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate validates and does not sort (typed TabulatedTableError: Empty, SampleCountMismatch, Unsorted). The importer sorts with the old Array.sortBy. AbscissaKind.abscissaAt is bit-identical to Units.fromMeters for every unit, so the moved kernels are pinned with exact Assert.Equal against G17 literals captured from the pre-move closures.\n6. Gates: seam-plan rows adopted as the lower bound. kit-acceptance is left out: it is not runnable before S12.1. constructor-unit-tests runs whole (light, 13 s) except on ADD_RED steps. ui-smoke and the ui-tests classes MaterialsWindowTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, MaterialEditorWindowTests and OutOfBandBadgeTests are added where the changed code is exercised.\n7. effects.contracts stay empty: these are data shapes, not proxy contracts, as in STL 0239. Step 9 clears every textual EpsAxisEvaluated mention, so S1.2's s02-no-eps-axis-evaluated invariant holds.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.2 (A material's physics is its complexity): appended steps 10-14 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (11 obligations, 5 acceptance bindings, 4 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 10-14). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 10 Langasite's dispersive gyration becomes core data: PublishedGyrationLaw / LangasiteGyrationLaw, with RhoWithDispValue's new case PublishedLawRho. The kernels move from OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs. A published law is view-only: isEditable is false and the new PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr is raised.\n- 11 Every fixture that builds a MaterialEntry from engine properties states its physics as data while properties is still a field: FsxAcceptanceTests material, the DispersionModelsTests minted-id fact and Report.fs dtoToEntry.\n- 12 The view-only Edit gating of MaterialsControls is deleted.\n- 13 complexity becomes mandatory and properties a member, with every consumer changed.\n- 14 Comment and test-name sweep, so the grep behind s03-complexity-mandatory finds nothing.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The brief misses the closure physics FsxAcceptanceTests stores as library materials (FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:85-88, :246-251, :344-353, :386-387).\n   - Once properties is derived, a fixture can only state a material as a complexity. Most of the script materials have a data form: constants, the Sellmeier glass via DispersionModel.toEpsAxis, Silicon via S1.1's published law, and the EUV indices.\n   - The engine Langasite preset has none. Its rho (Dispersive.fs:40-63) is transcendental, and RhoWithDispValue carries only DispersionFormula components.\n   - Step 10 therefore adds the gyration law, mirroring S1.1 step 8, so 001 sec B's \"physics is pure data\" holds and the LangasiteOnSilicon script comparisons keep their numbers. The built-in Langasite keeps its constant gyration, so no library number moves.\n   - The planner should reflect this in .spec-md sec 3.1/3.2. S1.4's schemas and S1.5's export then carry the case.\n2. MaterialsControls: the brief's \"with nothing replacing it\" is read as applying to the production gating.\n   - The control has no product host; only MaterialsControlsTests mounts it.\n   - Its view-only fact is migrated to a successor proving that every selected row offers Edit. That keeps a branch-reaching behaviour test and the ui-smoke count.\n   - The Materials window's own isEditable gate (MaterialsWindowView.editableSelection) is unchanged.\n3. Report.fs: a metadata-only re-import now carries an explicit vacuum complexity, whose composition is bit-identical to the former vacuumProperties. Such an entry is therefore constant term data and editable, where the None used to make it view-only.\n4. MaterialEditorView: deleting the None arms of the view-only preview requires the view-only case to carry the shown complexity: ViewOnlyMaterial of reason * shown.\n   - presetProperties and viewOnlyComplexity are deleted.\n   - NkDispersionChart.previewAnisotropy becomes a one-line alias, so it is deleted and its two callers read complexity.anisotropy.\n   - The captions \"view-only engine preset\" and \"coded engine closure\" are made accurate. After S1.1 the view-only entries are tabulated or law data, not engine closures.\n5. Test effects:\n   - Two facts lose their subject and are deleted: MaterialComplexityTests \"every built-in carries Some complexity…\" and MaterialEditorWindowTests \"spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree…\".\n   - Four facts whose names state the option or a coded preset are renamed.\n   - \"a coded-preset material (spectrum-spanning band) never flags\" keeps its name: Silicon's band is still spectrum-spanning.\n6. Gates:\n   - seam-plan's rows are adopted as the lower bound.\n   - kit-acceptance is left out, because it is not runnable before S12.1.\n   - constructor-unit-tests and ui-smoke run whole (whole_suite: light). Step 10 also runs unit-tests (RhoWithDispValueTests, EpsWithDispValueTests) and the FsxAcceptanceTests class.\n   - Step 14 selects all 46 ui-tests classes, because seam-plan treats its edit to the OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj comment (the comment says \"complexity = Some\", which S1.3's invariant forbids) as reaching every class.\n7. Contract effects are declared where the inventory has a complete consumer census: RhoWithDispValue, MaterialComplexityEditError, MaterialEditability, MaterialsControlsRow.editability, MaterialEntry.complexity, EditorMode and previewAnisotropy. The 19-file census for MaterialEntry.complexity equals step 13's code edits.\n8. Validation: `executability check` over a scratch copy of the folder, with a dummy final WIRE step appended, reports no finding for steps 10-14. The real folder reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.3 (Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID): appended steps 15-20 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (12 obligations, 6 acceptance bindings, 2 behavior seams, 2 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 15 SampleIds and PresetIds land in ElementId.fs; the seeds read them; the Ui's SeedEntryIds is deleted, and its four test consumers re-point. The preset ids keep their old text in this step.\n- 16 The constructor suite's fixtures name presets through PresetIds.\n- 17 LibraryWindowTests does the same.\n- 18 The rest of the UI suite does the same.\n- 19 ADD_RED / 20 CLOSE_RED: every seeded entry id and every minted source id is the canonical string of a GUID. Step 20 mints the 33 preset GUIDs, drops the src- prefix from newSourceId, and adds the live-Library GUID lookup fact.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Where the modules live. Brief: \"beside MaterialIds\". SampleIds and PresetIds go in ElementId.fs module Library, right after SampleId (:36-47). SampleId is declared there, and ElementId.fs compiles after MaterialLibrary.fs. MaterialIds and CategoryIds stay where they are.\n2. Names (ELEV015):\n   - SampleIds members carry an Id suffix (glassPlate1mmId ... langasiteSiliconId), because the same-named SeedSamples values live until S1.7.\n   - PresetIds reuses SeedEntryIds' five names (source600, detectorIntensity, polarizerLp, polarizerCpLeft, polarizerCpRight), so SeedEntryIds is deleted in the same step.\n   - The 28 source names are pinned in step 15.\n3. Two phases instead of one big switch:\n   - A single step that mints GUIDs would have to re-point about 25 test files at once.\n   - So steps 15-18 move every reference onto the members while the values are unchanged, and every step stays green.\n   - Then a red-green pair flips the values.\n   - The GUID literals are minted while implementing step 20 and frozen from then on (S1.5 exports them). The spec does not pin them.\n4. Fixtures follow AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin', which holds for fixtures. Each helper that wrapped a string id now takes an ElementValueId: ExperimentControlsTests and WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests bind/filmOnR2, FsxAcceptanceTests TableRun.sourceEntry, SolverHandoffWindowTests baseExperiment, ElementRendererBindingTests drawableOf, PlacedSampleEmissionTests entry/bind, PolarizerBehaviorTests polarizer/extractedLabels, and SourceLibraryTests wavelengthOf. So no fixture re-wraps .value.\n5. Classes:\n   - The brief's grep reaches classes its list omits: PlacedSampleEmissionTests, SceneProxyTests, ElementRendererBindingTests, InverseConstructorTests, and TableAndElementRotationTests (a SeedEntryIds consumer). All are edited.\n   - Two listed classes hold no seeded preset id and are not edited: EnvironmentRoundTripTests (\"src-d65\" is a SourceSpecId, SourceSpec.fs:243) and ScrollExtentTests (\"src-x\" is a test-local NewSource id).\n   - Test-local user-source ids and ExperimentRunTests' \"src-t\" stay.\n6. Old-shape facts:\n   - LightSourceEditorTests 'Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id' asserted the src- prefix. It now asserts the GUID shape and is red at step 19.\n   - The LibraryWindowTests id-format facts and its two sorted lists build their expected text from the members.\n   - MainSceneMsgTests' InlineData theory carries the kind code only, through a private expectedSeedOf map. Its name, rows and count are unchanged.\n7. Scope kept minimal:\n   - Tests that read SeedSamples.x.id (or a sample entry's entryId) are not re-pointed. S1.6/S1.7 re-point every seed-value read to the catalogue fixture.\n   - Schematic.fs needs no change: it already names built-ins through MaterialIds (Schematic.fs:47-58).\n   - effects.contracts stay empty, as in S1.1: the change is to id values and constant modules, not to a proxy contract.\n8. Gates:\n   - seam-plan's rows are adopted as the lower bound.\n   - kit-acceptance is left out, because it is not runnable before S12.1.\n   - seam-plan's step-20 \"final step runs every planned gate\" rows (unit-tests, kit-acceptance) are an artifact of step 20 being the current tail, and are not adopted.\n   - constructor-unit-tests and ui-smoke run whole (light) on the steps that touch their code. The ADD_RED selects SourceLibraryTests. Step 15 adds constructor-unit-tests for its Domain change, which seam-plan omits.\n   - Step 20 selects all 46 ui-tests classes, because every class that binds a preset sees the new values.\n9. Budget: 6 steps against a soft 10-18. The work is one identity move, three mechanical fixture passes and one red-green pair. Splitting further would add gate runs without isolating any risk.\n10. Validation: `executability check` on the real folder reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding. On a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step, it reports findings only for that placeholder. After step 20, the grep behind S1.4's s04-no-seeded-string-preset-ids invariant finds nothing.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.4 (Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas): appended steps 21-31 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (18 obligations, 11 acceptance bindings, 7 behavior seams, 2 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 21: ProjectJson.options and its five converters MOVE into the new Storage CanonicalJson.fs. Every reader re-points: ProjectJson, GroupsLibrary, RecentFiles, Report, UserEnvironment, DispersionModelsTests. This is exactly the inventory's census.\n- 22 ADD_RED / 23 CLOSE_RED: Complex and Matrix<double> converters.\n- 24: Domain LibraryEntryFiles.fs holds the ids, provenance and name rule.\n- 25: the payload, content, envelope, builders and decoders.\n- 26: the catalogue manifest and its uniqueness check.\n- 27: the canonical form and contentHashOf.\n- 28: int-tag converters for the closed sets.\n- 29: SchemaValidation.validateWith.\n- 30: entry files and six per-kind schemas plus a common one.\n- 31: the catalogue manifest file and the every-built-in proof.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The envelope is two records: LibraryEntryContent (every field but the hash) and LibraryEntryEnvelope { content; contentHash }.\n   - Domain cannot hash, because canonical JSON is Storage's, and the hash covers exactly the content.\n   - The FILE stays flat (001 sec B): Storage adds contentHash beside the content's keys, as ProjectJson.serializeProject adds schemaVersion.\n2. The payload holds only what the envelope does not (the brief's \"the payload holds the rest\").\n   - It uses remainder records: SamplePayloadData, SourcePayloadData and PolarizerPayloadData; a material's complexity; a detector's kind; a category's visibility.\n   - A preset's protection and a category's origin derive from provenance. A builder whose value disagrees answers ProvenanceMismatchErr.\n   - Facets are derived, never stored. categoryOpt and descriptionOpt follow naming_conventions.md's Opt rule.\n3. The envelope id is LibraryEntryId (Guid), kind-neutral.\n   - MaterialId, SampleId and CategoryId gain toLibraryEntryId; ElementValueId gains tryToLibraryEntryId (a parse).\n   - The reverse direction would make each pair a bijection (ELEV006), and a call-site re-wrap is ELEV001. So the six decoders are the one place a GUID becomes a kind's id, and they are marked StorageBoundary.\n   - CategoryName.toEntryName files a category's name without a re-wrap.\n4. KitId is born in S1.4, because the kit-import provenance needs it. S4.1's Kit module MUST reuse it (ELEV014). The planner should amend the .spec-md sec 5 'Kit module' row.\n5. UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr carries SchemaVersionMismatchInfo { fileExtension; found; expected }, and ContentHashMismatchErr carries ContentHashMismatchInfo { entryId; recorded; computed }.\n   - Records are used because ELEV011 refuses two same-typed fields in one case.\n   - The extension names the kind (001 sec A) because the manifest, and S4's kit files, are not LibraryEntryKinds.\n6. Validation stays schema-first, as the brief orders, and the typed version error stays reachable.\n   - Each schema checks the schema header unconditionally and the rest only under if version = 1.\n   - The shared definitions live once in library-common.schema.json, which the others reference by $id. There are eight schema files, not seven, so no definition is copied.\n7. The numbers: a probe of the current options over the built-ins showed three gaps.\n   - System.Numerics.Complex reads back as zero, so the EUV Mo/Si complexities do not round-trip today.\n   - Matrix<double> cannot be read, so a constant-Mueller polarizer fails.\n   - That is the red pair of steps 22/23.\n   - Step 28 writes LibraryEntryKind and S1.1/S1.2's TabulatedInterpolation, PublishedIndexLaw and PublishedGyrationLaw as their int tags. Every other fieldless union keeps the serializer's case name, as the project, groups and environment formats store it; giving them int tags is out of scope.\n8. The canonical form:\n   - Keys are sorted ordinally, numbers are invariant shortest round-trip, escaping is UnsafeRelaxedJsonEscaping, and no BOM is written.\n   - The file is indented (two spaces, LF) and ends with one LF.\n   - The hash is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the COMPACT rendering, so whitespace never moves it.\n   - A frozen-literal fact pins the text and the hash of a test-local value, which guards S1.5's committed hashes.\n9. The manifest does not store its own hash; manifestHash computes it for S3.\n   - tryCreate sorts the rows by kind tag, then by file name.\n   - It refuses equal file names of one kind ignoring case (the Windows rule), and one id and version twice. Equal names across kinds are allowed.\n10. SchemaValidation:\n   - validateWith holds the one evaluation body.\n   - GroupsLibrary.validateGroupsLibrary and UserEnvironment.validateUserEnvironment were copies of it and now call it. Environment messages gain nested locations; no fact asserts them.\n   - Report.validateEntryElement is unchanged: it evaluates a $id-less wrapper of the project schema's materialEntry def with a fixed message, a format outside this section.\n11. Seed use: the every-built-in facts (step 31) and a few fixtures (the Langasite / multilayerQw / tunable-source / EUV Mo values) read the code seeds while they exist. S1.6/S1.7 re-point or delete them with the seeds.\n12. Gates:\n   - seam-plan's rows are adopted as the lower bound.\n   - Steps 21 and 29 edit Ui code, so they add ui-smoke and the ui-tests classes exercising UserEnvironment (AppShellSeamTests, DataFilePickerFolderTests, LocalizationTests).\n   - Step 29 adds constructor-unit-tests, because the round-trip facts of the changed validators live there.\n   - seam-plan's step-31 \"final step runs every planned gate\" row is an artifact of 31 being the current tail, and is not adopted.\n   - kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1. unit-tests is not selected, because no solver, Optimization or MuellerInverse code changes.\n13. effects.contracts stay empty, as in S1.1 and S1.3.\n   - The section adds data shapes and modules, not proxy contracts.\n   - StorageError gains cases without any consumer edit; no match on it is exhaustive.\n   - The options move edits exactly the census of ProjectJson.options.\n14. Budget: 11 steps against a soft 15-25. Each step is one reviewable unit with its own facts, and splitting further would add gate runs without isolating risk.\n15. Validation: `executability check` on the real folder reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding. On a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step, it reports findings only for that placeholder.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.5 (The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds): appended steps 32-36 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (12 obligations, 5 acceptance bindings, 3 behavior seams, 2 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 32 ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:CatalogueProxy>: Domain CatalogueFiles.fs (after LibraryEntryFiles.fs). It holds CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue, CatalogueError, CatalogueData { manifest; envelopes } with tryCreate and validate, the [<ReferenceEquality>] CatalogueProxy { readCatalogue; writeCatalogue }, and its in-memory double createInMemory. CatalogueProxyTests drives the double.\n- 33 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT: Storage CatalogueFolderStore.fs (after EntryFileJson.fs) holds CatalogueProxy.create (folder : FolderName) and LibraryFileText.writeAtomically. Errors.fs gains StorageError.describe. CatalogueFolderTests runs the real proxy over folders under the test output.\n- 34 ADD_RED / 35 CLOSE_RED: BuiltInCatalogueParityTests reads Catalogue/Builtin from the test output, so it is red while no catalogue is copied. Step 35 then writes export-builtin.fsx, runs it once, commits Catalogue/Builtin/ (the manifest and one file per seed) and adds the Storage.fsproj Content item.\n- 36: export-builtin.fsx is deleted.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Pinned shapes and names (all checked unused in the tree and in the spec):\n   - The proxy record is Domain's, as .spec-md sec 5 says; Storage's create is an extension static member on it, the shape sec 5 gives KitProxy.create.\n   - The folder is an STL FolderName, following ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder. No CatalogueFolder type is added; S3 can add one if registration needs it.\n   - The file and module names are CatalogueFiles (Domain) and CatalogueFolderStore (Storage, the ExperimentDataStore precedent). The latter avoids taking the bare name CatalogueFolder from a later section.\n2. The shipped catalogue's identity is a Domain well-known id, CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue = 499ae2ca-4f4c-4d4f-b53e-62ef2627130a, shaped like MaterialIds (.spec-md sec 3.3).\n   - It was minted at authoring time so that the export, the parity facts and later sections share one literal.\n   - The name \"Built-in\" is data in the manifest, written by the export and asserted by the test.\n3. The errors are Domain values, because Domain cannot see StorageError:\n   - Five reason-string cases, plus InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr of LibraryEntryError for step 26's refusal.\n   - StorageError.describe is the honest render (ELEV002) that a rejected file's reason carries.\n4. One consistency rule, CatalogueData.validate, is called by the in-memory double, the folder read and the folder write:\n   - the manifest MUST be exactly the one CatalogueManifest.tryCreate makes from the envelopes, with the envelopes in row order;\n   - so the sort and uniqueness rules stay step 26's alone.\n5. Read and write rules the brief left open:\n   - Read considers only top-level files with a library-entry extension. A README, a stale *.tmp and the manifest itself are not entry files.\n   - Read reports a missing row file before an unlisted entry file. Names compare OrdinalIgnoreCase, step 26's Windows rule.\n   - Write never deletes. It refuses a folder holding an unlisted entry file, so a written folder always reads back equal.\n   - Write is atomic per file (*.tmp, then File.Move with overwrite), with entries first and the manifest last.\n   - Write validates no schema (it writes typed values), so it runs inside the fsx, where no schema/ folder sits beside the assemblies.\n6. The export script:\n   - It references the OpticalConstructor.Tests Release x64 output. A class library's own bin holds no NuGet dependencies (verified: Storage's bin lacks FSharp.SystemTextJson and JsonSchema.Net), while the test output holds Domain, Storage and every dependency.\n   - It writes through CatalogueProxy.create(...).writeCatalogue, so no second writer exists.\n   - The parity facts compute their expectation by sealing the seeds independently. The test is an oracle and shares no code with the generator; both are deleted (step 36 and S1.7).\n7. Exact outputs:\n   - Step 35's effects list all 62 paths (.catalogue-json plus one file per seed). They were derived at authoring time from the seed names in MaterialLibrary.fs and ElementId.fs with step 24's FileStem rule.\n   - No two names collide ignoring case, and no name holds an MSBuild-special character (% $ @ ; ').\n   - git check-ignore --no-index was run on representative paths. The manifest, entry files with unicode names and the script are committable: [Bb]in/ (.gitignore:23) does not match Builtin/. Only *.tmp (.gitignore:78) matches, which is intended.\n   - .gitattributes gives the new kinds text eol=lf.\n8. The deletion step 36 has no compiled edit. It runs constructor-unit-tests on BuiltInCatalogueParityTests, with build as its prerequisite, so the committed folder is proven again without its generator. Its \"only Builtin/ remains\" clause, and step 35's \"none git-ignored\", are directly observable acceptance with no gate, as S1.4 step 21's \"nothing names ProjectJson.options\" is.\n9. Gates:\n   - seam-plan's rows for steps 32-35 (build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests) are adopted.\n   - constructor-unit-tests runs whole (whole_suite light, 13 s) except on the ADD_RED and the deletion step, which select BuiltInCatalogueParityTests.\n   - seam-plan's step-36 \"final step runs every planned gate\" row is an artifact of 36 being the current tail, and is not adopted.\n   - kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1. unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests are not selected: no solver, Ui or Optimization code changes, and the Content item adds files without changing a UI behaviour.\n10. Contract:\n   - ADD_CONTRACT declares a create effect for OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueFiles.CatalogueProxy (the STL 0239 precedent).\n   - ADD_TEST actions name the three new classes.\n11. Budget: 5 steps against a soft 6-12. The section is one proxy (contract, then implementation), one red-green parity pair and one deletion. Splitting further would add gate runs without isolating any risk.\n12. Mechanical repair outside S1.5's own rows: the S1.4 behavior seam s14-numbers-green (step 23) was removed from .execution-contract-json.\n   - Step 23 (CLOSE_RED) declares no test effect, so the checker's BEHAVIOR_TEST rule can never be met there. It surfaced once the deeper checks ran on a staged copy.\n   - S14-NUMBERS keeps its checks at steps 22 and 23 and its seam s14-numbers-red at step 22, so no acceptance is weakened.\n13. Validation:\n   - `executability check` on the real folder reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding and the unminted <STORE:CatalogueProxy> placeholder (sec 9.6).\n   - On a staged copy outside the repo, with the placeholder final WIRE step and the two contract anchors turned into IMPLEMENT (no identity shard may be written), it reports findings only for that placeholder.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.6 (CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue): appended steps 37-44 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (16 obligations, 8 acceptance bindings, 8 behavior seams, 2 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 37 RENAME_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0008 (SeedingProxy -> CatalogueImportProxy, former_name SeedingProxy): Seeding.fs moves to Domain/CatalogueImport.fs, after SampleStore.fs.\n  - SeedingError becomes CatalogueImportError, SeedRejectedErr becomes ImportRejectedErr, and InMemorySeedStores becomes InMemoryCatalogueStores.\n  - The Seeding project is deleted: its files, its folder, its slnx entry and its one ProjectReference.\n  - RENAME_TEST covers both test classes, and the Domain doc comments are re-pointed.\n  - seedAll keeps its seed-fed body for this one step.\n- 38: Storage's CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn () is the one place <base>/Catalogue/Builtin is written. The parity test's readBuiltIn reads through it.\n- 39: LibraryEntryError.describe and CatalogueError.describe, the ELEV002 renders a composition root logs.\n- 40 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0008: seedAll becomes importCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData).\n  - It decodes each entry by kind and pushes category, then material, then sample, then preset; the first error stops it.\n  - importFrom (catalogue : CatalogueProxy) reads, then imports. The new error cases are UndecodableEntryErr and CatalogueUnreadableErr.\n  - Stub facts and in-memory facts over the Built-in catalogue replace the five seed-fed facts.\n  - From this step, 'SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding' finds nothing under Berreman/, so S1.7's s07-no-seeding-seam holds when S1.7 starts.\n- 41: the BuiltinCatalogue fixture (OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs, linked into Ui.Tests), with BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests.\n- 42: DefaultStores composes from the catalogue. The in-memory bundle's preset proxy keeps the seeded By-kind tree.\n- 43: MainWorkbenchTests composes through the fixture.\n- 44 WIRE: AppContext.create composes from the catalogue. The comments the switch makes false are fixed, and AppContextTests proves the import.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Anchor shape. SeedingProxy is the inherited contract STORE_XDUO_0008 (.contract-ids/XDUO-json, declaringProject OpticalConstructor.Seeding).\n   - The move is RENAME_CONTRACT: a mechanical move and rename, carrying former_name for the rename grep.\n   - The re-sourcing is IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT on the same id. No id is minted.\n   - The identity shard's name and declaringProject (CatalogueImportProxy, OpticalConstructor.Domain) are the cycle's to update.\n2. Names.\n   - The orchestrator is importCatalogue, not seedAll, because S1.7's invariant forbids the text 'seedAll' under Berreman/.\n   - ImportRejectedErr is the renamed SeedRejectedErr, as the brief asks.\n   - Every other new name was checked unused in the tree, the section plan and the spec.\n3. The grouping tree, a gap in the brief.\n   - The Select bay's rows come only from libraryTrees (TableAndElementRotationView.fs libraryState), and the empty preset store answers Ok [] (ElementId.fs createInMemoryEmpty).\n   - Composing the app and the test scenes over the empty store would empty the Select bay. It would fail the ui-smoke fact 'the Select bay survives select, bind, and kind-change re-renders'.\n   - S1.7 derives the tree from the entries. Until then, the in-memory bundle's preset proxy answers the existing seeded By-kind tree, whose leaves are the frozen ids the catalogue carries.\n   - This is the one seed reader the app keeps after S1.6. S1.7's deletion of Library.createInMemory removes it.\n4. Reuse.\n   - One read-then-import (CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom) serves both composition roots and the fixture. S2.3 and S2.4 call it over the SQLite proxies.\n   - One Storage member (createBuiltIn) writes the shipped folder's path.\n   - Each composition root logs its own failure. That is two lines per root, not a copied body.\n5. Samples and order.\n   - Samples go through saveSample only, not also saveLibraryEntry as seedEntries' SampleItems did, because liveLibrary serves samples from the samples store.\n   - Preset order now follows the catalogue's rows. The Select bay (tree order) and the Library window (sortNodesByLabel) do not show it.\n6. Tests.\n   - The new import facts read the Built-in catalogue, never the seeds, so S1.7 has nothing to re-point in them.\n   - The fixture adds per-kind lists (materials, categories, samples, presets) beside the stores and the id lookups, because S1.7 re-points the readers of the seed lists to them.\n   - MainWorkbenchTests keeps its one seed reader (sampleBandsState) for S1.7.\n7. Caching. DefaultStores reads the catalogue folder at every initMain (), and no cache is added (.spec-md sec 8). The fixture loads once per process, as the brief says.\n8. Gates.\n   - seam-plan's rows for steps 37-40 are adopted: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.\n   - constructor-unit-tests and ui-smoke run whole wherever they run (whole_suite light).\n   - Step 41 adds ui-smoke, because the linked file enters the Ui.Tests assembly. seam-plan's ui-tests and kit-acceptance rows for it are not adopted: no Ui.Tests class changes, and KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1.\n   - Steps 42 and 44 select every ui-tests class that consumes DefaultStores (initMain, initTableAndElementRotation) or AppContext.create, from the inventory census.\n   - WireUiCompositionTests and WireUi0040CompositionTests hold only ui-smoke facts. A selected ui-tests arm for them would be empty (SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM), so whole-suite ui-smoke covers them.\n   - seam-plan's step-44 'final step runs every planned gate' row is the current-tail artifact and is not adopted.\n   - unit-tests is not selected: no solver, Optimization or BerremanTestSupport code changes.\n9. Validation.\n   - executability check and step_compiler check_spec on the real folder each report one finding: SELECTION_REQUIRED step 44 [unit-tests].\n   - It exists only because step 44 is the current tail. Declaring it would break the next mapper's validation once step 44 is no longer final, so it is left.\n   - On a staged copy outside the repo, with a placeholder final step that declares every gate, both pass with no findings.\n10. Outside this mapper's scope.\n   - .user-md/Berreman/arc-runner.user-md:44 still lists 'Seeding' among the Optical Constructor projects.\n   - AGENTS.md:574 ('The Main scene's Library is LIVE') still calls the presets seeded; S1.7, which deletes SeedSources, touches the same gotcha.\n11. Budget: 8 steps against a soft 10-18. The seam is one move, one contract re-sourcing, two small prerequisites, one fixture and three composition switches. Splitting further adds gate runs without isolating any risk.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S1.7 (The code seed values are deleted): appended steps 45-58 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (19 obligations, 14 acceptance bindings, 6 behavior seams, 2 closing scopes). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 45: the BuiltinCatalogue fixture gains store doubles that replace the self-seeding stores one for one: materialStore, sampleStore, categoryStore, library (), sources () and source id. Each is filled through the store's own write verb.\n- 46: tryFindCategory, tryFindCategoryByName and CategoryId.categoryName resolve through a category list handed in.\n  - LibraryFacets.materialFacets / libraryFacets take the categories.\n  - LibraryWindowContext gains categories.\n  - Report.fs import/export take them.\n  - MaterialsWindowView's liveMaterialFacets override is deleted (one resolution, not two).\n- 47: LibraryTree.byKind derives the By kind tree (kind, then facet, then leaf).\n  - liveLibrary and Library.createInMemoryEmpty derive it.\n  - S1.6 step 42's seeded-tree override in CatalogueImport.createInMemory is deleted.\n- 48: the Details bay's band names come from the live MaterialProxy. TableAndElementRotationView's materialLibrary (= MaterialLibrary.standard) is deleted.\n- 49: MaterialEditorWindow's categories parameter becomes mandatory, and its self-seeding default goes.\n- 50: Experiments.seedExperiments goes; createInMemoryExperiments answers nothing.\n- 51-53: re-point the constructor suite (material/category, sample/source/Library, facet/library-file classes).\n- 54-56: re-point the UI suite (material windows, Library window and scenes, sample readers).\n- 57: DELETE_TEST BuiltInCatalogueParityTests (no successor); ADD_TEST BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests (one fact).\n- 58: delete the seed values and the self-seeding stores. The empty stores take the plain name createInMemory; docs and AGENTS.md's LIVE-Library gotcha are corrected.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Product seed readers the brief misses. Each gets its own step so the deletion step only deletes:\n   - TableAndElementRotationView.fs `materialLibrary = MaterialLibrary.standard` (band display names) -> step 48;\n   - MaterialEditorWindow.fs's `defaultArg categories (CategoryProxy.createInMemory ...)` -> step 49;\n   - Report.fs dtoToEntry/exportMaterials (tryFindCategoryByName / categoryName) -> step 46;\n   - LibraryFacets.materialCategoryDef (categoryName) -> step 46, which threads categories into LibraryWindowContext. The census adds LightSourceEditorTests and WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests as context builders.\n   The planner may add LibraryWindowView.fs, MaterialEditorWindow.fs and Report.fs to .spec-md sec 0.1.\n2. seedExperiments holds no library value. It is deleted because the brief names it and .spec-md sec 3.3 deletes every other seed value; no product code reads listExperiments. ExperimentProxyTests' two seed facts are delete+create pairs, so the count is unchanged.\n3. The derived tree's facets, which the brief leaves open:\n   - samples by SubstrateKind (Thin films / Thick plates / Mirrors);\n   - sources by tuning (Fixed lines / Tunable);\n   - polarizers by PolarizerCategory.label;\n   - detectors as direct leaves;\n   - leaves keep their input order.\n   The Select bay now also lists samples created in the Library window and user sources. A fact proves this (LibraryControlsTests). No product test depended on the seeded labels except SourceLibraryTests' Sources group, which compares order-independently.\n4. Fixture doubles. They make every re-point a one-for-one swap with the same arguments (custom VersionsInUse and referencing lookups included). Step 46's tests and later steps use them, so they land first (step 45).\n5. Renames. The plain names become free, so MaterialProxy/SampleProxy/CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty and Library.createInMemoryEmpty take createInMemory in step 58, in the same step as the deletion, so no doc names a missing member in between.\n   - The semantic-drift guard: step 56's acceptance proves neither test suite calls a self-seeding store.\n   - Step 58 greps Berreman/OpticalConstructor before renaming, and stops on any stray call.\n6. Fact names that say \"seed\" are kept (no renames); their bodies read the fixture. Facts that took a seed by position take it by well-known id (e.g. MaterialPreviewTests' head = Silicon). SeedSources.tunables becomes the four tunable PresetIds, so ExperimentRunTests' assertion stays meaningful.\n7. Earlier sections' facts re-pointed here are S1.3 steps 19-20 (SourceLibraryTests), S1.4 steps 22/25/30/31 (CanonicalJsonTests, LibraryEntryFilesTests, EntryFileJsonTests) and S1.5 step 33 (CatalogueFolderTests).\n8. The integrity fact pins 12 materials, 5 categories, 11 samples, 28 sources, 3 polarizers and 2 detectors (step 35's 61 entries). S7.1, which adds built-in item models, MUST update it.\n9. Contract effects are declared only where the inventory census's consumers are all in-step edits:\n   - step 46: change_shape on the category lookups, facets, LibraryWindowContext and Report import/export;\n   - step 47: create LibraryTree.byKind;\n   - step 48: change_shape bandsState;\n   - step 50: retire seedExperiments.\n   Seed-value retirements carry none: their static census lists test files re-pointed in steps 51-56 and the Seeding files S1.6 deleted (the S1.1 step 9 precedent).\n10. 001 sec T 'From section 1', and the later sections' s08-no-seed-modules / s08-t1-no-code-seeds greps, hold from step 58 (its acceptance runs them).\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates':\n   - build and elevation on every step;\n   - constructor-unit-tests on steps touching Domain, Storage or OpticalConstructor.Tests (whole suite, light);\n   - ui-smoke on steps touching Ui, Ui.Tests or the linked fixture;\n   - ui-tests by touched class, plus the classes that exercise the changed product code;\n   - smoke-only classes (EmbeddedChartTests, WireUi0040CompositionTests, WireUiCompositionTests) stay out of ui-tests to avoid SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM.\n   unit-tests is not selected (no solver, Optimization or BerremanTestSupport change). kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1.\n12. Budget: 14 steps against a soft 12-25.\n13. Validation:\n   - On the real folder, executability check and check_spec each report only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding.\n   - On a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step whose gates are bound, both report no findings.\n   - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s17/build_s17.py.\n14. Outside this mapper's scope: .user-md/Berreman/arc-runner.user-md:44 still lists 'Seeding' (noted by S1.6).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S2.1 (The library model in EF Core, created without migrations): appended steps 59-64 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (17 obligations, 6 acceptance bindings, 5 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 59 RETIRE_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0007 (TestDbContext, component, csharp): the EF proof goes with its only consumer.\n  - Deleted: Test.cs, TestDbContext.cs, Migrations/ (initial migration, designer, snapshot), the false csproj comment, TestDbMigrationTests.fs, fixtures/database-appsettings.json.\n  - Tests.fsproj loses those items, its direct EF Core package and its App and Database references (TestDbMigrationTests was the only test file opening any of them).\n  - ConfigKey.databaseProvider and mssqlConnectionString are deleted; sqliteConnectionString stays with a one-line doc.\n  - DELETE_TEST TestDbMigrationTests: the suite falls by its seven cases on purpose.\n- 60 ADD_COMPONENT <STORE:LibraryDbContext> (component, csharp, OpticalConstructor.Database): LibraryEntities.cs (seven entities) and LibraryDbContext.cs.\n  - Tables: EntryVersion, LatestVersion, EntryFacet, SampleMaterial, CatalogueImport, PulledSource, SchemaStamp.\n  - Storage.fsproj references Database. ADD_TEST LibraryDatabaseTests with the table/column listing fact.\n- 61: EntryLifecycle, EntryProtection and new PinState (VersionPinned / VersionUnpinned) gain value/tryOfDb; SampleStructure.referencedMaterialVersions, with referencedMaterials as its projection.\n- 62: Errors.fs gains LibrarySchemaVersion (current = 1), LibrarySchemaMismatchInfo { foundOpt; expected }, LibrarySchemaMismatchErr and LibraryDatabaseExn.\n  - New Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs: LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString), run, IDisposable.\n  - One unpooled connection per handle (:memory: lives with it; one writer behind a lock), foreign keys on, WAL for files, EnsureCreated then stamp; a missing or different stamp is a mismatch and the file is untouched.\n- 63: EntryVersionState, StoredEntryVersion, versionRow / toStoredVersion through the entry file text, LibraryRowInvalidErr, EntryProvenance.kindValue / catalogueIdOpt.\n- 64: LibraryEntryEnvelope.facetRows and sampleMaterialRows.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Anchors.\n   - STORE_XDUO_0007 is TestDbContext in the identity shard (component, csharp), so its replacement is RETIRE_CONTRACT plus a new ADD_COMPONENT, mirroring how spec 0038 registered it.\n   - The F# seam steps are plain IMPLEMENT, so ADD_COMPONENT carries no IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT obligation.\n   - The cycle mints <STORE:LibraryDbContext>.\n2. PinState is born in S2.1 (step 61) because the version row stores it.\n   - S2.2 (\"Pinned replaces VersionsInUse\") MUST reuse this type and its int tags, not declare a second one (ELEV014/016).\n   - The planner may note it beside .spec-md sec 5's PinState row.\n3. Facet-key rows are pinned as \"the entry's own discrete facets\".\n   - They are evaluated through the existing catalogue over empty lists: materialFacets [] for materials, libraryFacets [] [] for samples and presets, none for categories, no numeric facet.\n   - The category row's value is therefore the category GUID text (CategoryId.categoryName [] after step 46), so a rename never stales a row.\n   - Material-derived sample facets are left to the sample-material rows.\n4. Sample-material rows keep versions (MaterialVersionId), hence SampleStructure.referencedMaterialVersions. The material side is an indexed key, not a foreign key, so a sample may be stored before its materials (an import or snapshot order).\n5. Row state versus file.\n   - Lifecycle and pin live only in the row (EntryVersionState).\n   - Protection, provenance kind and catalogue id are derived from the provenance and checked on read: a row that disagrees with its payload is LibraryRowInvalidErr.\n6. The schema stamp version lives in F# (LibrarySchemaVersion.current = 1, Errors.fs).\n   - The step-60 fact pins the model's exact tables and columns, so a model change fails it until the listing and the version are raised together.\n   - A database without a stamp (another app's file) is LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = None }.\n7. The tables nobody writes yet: LatestVersion (S2.2/S3.1), CatalogueImport (S3.1) and PulledSource (S13) are model only here; their F# mappings belong to the sections that use them. The CatalogueImport row is keyed by catalogue id: one recorded manifest hash per catalogue (001 sec B).\n8. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL: LibraryDbContext, the seven Library*Row entities, LibraryDatabaseStore, LibraryDatabase, LibrarySchemaVersion, LibrarySchemaMismatchInfo, the three StorageError cases, EntryVersionState, StoredEntryVersion, PinState and its cases.\n9. Contract effects.\n   - Declared: create on LibraryDbContext, PinState, referencedMaterialVersions, LibraryDatabase, EntryVersionState and StoredEntryVersion; retire on ConfigKey.databaseProvider and mssqlConnectionString.\n   - The C# retirements (TestDbContext, Test, the migration types) carry none, because the inventory's census for them is unresolved (source generators: SYMBOL_CENSUS_UNKNOWN). The step's grep proves them gone.\n10. Invariants. From step 59, the later s09/s47 no-test-db grep (TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalConstructorMssql) finds nothing; step 59's own grep is a case-insensitive superset.\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates': build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered; whole_suite light) on every step.\n   - executability seam-plan proposes exactly these gates for steps 59-64.\n   - No Ui code or UI test changes, so there is no ui-smoke or ui-tests; unit-tests is not selected; kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1.\n12. Budget: 6 steps against a soft 10-18. The section is one deletion, one C# model, one tag step and three seam steps; splitting further would add gate runs without isolating risk.\n13. Validation:\n   - On the real folder, executability check and check_spec each report only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding and the unminted <STORE:LibraryDbContext> placeholder (sec 9.6).\n   - On a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step whose gates are bound and the placeholder anchor neutralised, both report no findings.\n   - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s21/build_s21.py.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S2.2 (Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories): appended steps 65-71 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (19 obligations, 7 acceptance bindings, 4 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 65 IMPLEMENT: the pin replaces the seam, in one step because deleting the type changes every caller.\n  - Lifecycle: VersionsInUse, VersionUsage and usageOf go; decideVersioning takes the stored latest version's PinState (step 61's type, reused).\n  - Experiments.boundVersions and versionsInUseSeam go; VersionRef, ElementBinding.versionRefOpt and Experiment.versionRefs stay.\n  - MaterialProxy / SampleProxy gain pinMaterialVersion / pinSampleVersion; the in-memory stores keep a pin per version (new and minted versions unpinned) and lose the VersionsInUse argument.\n  - MaterialVersionInUseErr / SampleVersionInUseErr become MaterialVersionPinnedErr / SampleVersionPinnedErr, with the same payload.\n  - MaterialError.unknownMaterialVersion takes the text Propagation.resolveMaterialVersion already built.\n  - Every caller is re-pointed by one rule: the fixture, both suites, the stubs, CatalogueImport.createInMemory and the Ui captions. Comments and fsproj comments drop the seam, so S2.3's s10-no-versions-in-use invariant holds from step 65.\n- 66 IMPLEMENT: MaterialProxyContract / CategoryProxyContract (abstract) hold the store facts; their in-memory subclasses keep the class names MaterialProxyTests / CategoryProxyTests.\n- 67 IMPLEMENT: the version-row operations on LibraryDbContext, in LibraryDatabaseStore.fs.\n  - Reads: tryLatestStored, tryStoredVersion, storedVersionsOf, latestStoredOfKind.\n  - Writes: stageVersion, stageLatest, stageRemoval.\n  - The rule's outcomes: stageNewEntry, stageEdit. Nothing saves; each store saves once per run.\n  - Fixture BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase (). Four LibraryDatabaseTests facts.\n- 68 IMPLEMENT: MaterialEntry.versionPayload (MaterialMetadata becomes public) and the shared refusals MaterialError.unknownMaterial, stillReferenced and versionsPinned. resolveMaterialWithDisp also calls unknownMaterial.\n- 69 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0001: MaterialProxy.createInDatabase (Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs).\n  - Adds MaterialStoreUnavailableErr.\n  - ADD_TEST MaterialProxySqliteTests: 22 contract facts plus 2 of its own.\n- 70 IMPLEMENT: the shared refusals CategoryError.unknownCategory, duplicateCategory, builtInNotRemovable and stillReferenced.\n- 71 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0003: CategoryProxy.createInDatabase (Storage/CategoryDatabaseStore.fs).\n  - Adds CategoryStoreUnavailableErr.\n  - ADD_TEST CategoryProxySqliteTests: 8 contract facts plus 2 of its own.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The pin rule is the brief's: a pinned version with a physics change mints the next version, and everything else behaves as today. A metadata-only edit of a pinned version therefore still mutates it in place.\n   - 001 sec C says \"'edit latest' follows Lifecycle.decideVersioning\", whose load-bearing rule is that metadata never versions.\n   - So 001's \"a pinned version never mutates\" is read as its physics. 001 names the kit snapshot hash as the second safeguard.\n   - Step 61's PinState doc says \"never mutates\"; the planner may sharpen it to \"its physics never changes in place\".\n2. Anchors.\n   - The proxies keep their record shapes plus one pin field, so there is no MODIFY_CONTRACT: it would open a temporary contract.\n   - The SQLite creates are IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT on the inherited STORE_XDUO_0001 / 0003, as step 40 did for STORE_XDUO_0008. No id is minted.\n   - There are no reds: every step lands its code with the facts that prove it.\n3. Contract suites.\n   - The in-memory classes keep their names, so every existing fact id survives (xUnit v3 reports an inherited fact under its concrete class). Only the SQLite classes take ADD_TEST.\n   - Stub and pure facts stay in the in-memory classes alone, because running them twice proves nothing.\n   - One assertion changes: the composed removal fact checks the referencing samples through the test-local ReferencingSamples, where it checked listSamples answering Ok. The SQLite variant has no SampleProxy until S2.3, so it reads the sample rows instead.\n4. Provenance in the SQLite stores.\n   - A material first saved through saveMaterial is UserProvenance, and an edit keeps the stored provenance.\n   - A category follows its origin: BuiltInCategory is BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (the one built-in catalogue), and UserCategory is UserProvenance.\n   - CatalogueImport (S1.6) pushes decoded values, which carry no provenance. A built-in material imported through saveMaterial would therefore be filed as a user entry.\n   - S2.4 / S3.1 must write catalogue envelopes with their provenance through step 67's stageVersion / stageLatest. Noted for the planner and the S2.4 / S3.1 mappers.\n5. New error cases MaterialStoreUnavailableErr and CategoryStoreUnavailableErr: no existing case names a failure of the store below the proxy (.spec-md sec 4 'Errors and IO').\n6. Refusal texts become members when the second holder arrives (steps 65, 68, 70; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy').\n   - Propagation.resolveMaterialVersion and MaterialLibrary.resolveMaterialWithDisp already held identical texts, and now call the members.\n   - The in-memory sample pin refusal stays inline, because nothing else holds it yet; S2.3's SQLite sample store moves it.\n7. Category edits.\n   - The SQLite updateCategory applies decideVersioning (visibility is the physics, the name the metadata) with the stored pin. No verb pins a category in S2.2, so it acts in place, as the in-memory store does.\n   - An update that changes a category's origin is InvalidCategoryErr in SQLite, because origin derives from provenance. The in-memory store still accepts it; no consumer changes an origin (the category editor keeps it).\n   - An id held by an entry of another kind is DuplicateMaterialIdErr / DuplicateCategoryIdErr naming that kind's extension.\n8. Contract effects.\n   - Declared: change_shape on decideVersioning; retire on VersionUsage, usageOf, boundVersions and versionsInUseSeam; create on both createInDatabase members.\n   - Omitted: VersionsInUse, MaterialProxy, SampleProxy and the three error unions. Their baseline census names OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs and SeedingInMemoryTests.fs, which steps 37 and 40 replaced, and authorizing deleted paths would mislead the worker.\n   - Step 65's closing grep, the s10 invariant and the build (FS0025 as an error) prove those changes instead.\n9. AppContext.fs needs no change: step 44 replaced its store construction with CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory, so the brief's \"fix their callers (AppContext.fs, tests)\" reduces to the tests and CatalogueImport.fs.\n10. Gates follow executability seam-plan and .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'.\n   - build and elevation run on every step, and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light) on every step. That includes the text-moving steps 68 and 70, for which seam-plan proposed no test gate: the suite asserts those texts.\n   - ui-smoke (all_discovered) runs on 65, 69 and 71, where Ui code or Ui test files change.\n   - ui-tests runs on 65 over the 13 classes seam-plan names (EmbeddedChartTests holds only ui-smoke facts).\n   - kit-acceptance is dropped (not runnable before S12.1), and unit-tests does not apply.\n   - seam-plan's \"final step runs every planned gate\" row for step 71 is the mid-campaign artefact.\n11. Budget: 7 steps against a soft 14-24.\n   - The replacement is atomic, because deleting the seam's type breaks every caller at once.\n   - A proxy record lands whole, with no field left a stub, so each SQLite store is one step with its suite.\n   - The text moves and the row operations are their own steps. Splitting further would add gate runs without isolating risk.\n12. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL: pinMaterialVersion, pinSampleVersion, MaterialVersionPinnedErr, SampleVersionPinnedErr, MaterialStoreUnavailableErr, CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, createInDatabase, MaterialDatabaseStore, CategoryDatabaseStore, the LibraryDbContext members, freshLibraryDatabase, MaterialProxyContract, CategoryProxyContract, MaterialProxySqliteTests, CategoryProxySqliteTests, versionPayload and the refusal builders.\n13. Validation:\n   - On the real folder, executability check and check_spec each report only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding.\n   - On a staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step, both pass with no findings.\n   - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s22/build_s22.py (seam plan in seam.json; logs check-real.log and check-staged.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S2.3 (SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library): appended steps 72-80 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (22 obligations, 9 acceptance bindings, 5 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 72 IMPLEMENT: members both samples stores call, moved out of the in-memory store unchanged.\n  - Sample.versionPayload over a now-public SampleMetadata.\n  - SampleQuery.selectFrom, the search filter.\n  - SampleError.unknownSample, unknownSampleVersion and versionsPinned, the texts step 65 left inline.\n- 73 IMPLEMENT: SampleProxyContract (abstract) holds the 21 store facts; its in-memory subclass keeps the name SampleProxyTests.\n- 74 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0002: SampleProxy.createInDatabase (Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs).\n  - Adds SampleStoreUnavailableErr.\n  - stageVersion writes each version's sample-material rows from its own structure.\n  - ADD_TEST SampleProxySqliteTests: 21 contract facts plus 2 of its own.\n- 75 IMPLEMENT: SourceProxyContract holds the two user-sources store facts; the in-memory subclass keeps the name SourceLibraryTests.\n  - The userSource helper takes an ElementValueId.\n  - The insert/replace/remove fact saves under newSourceId ().\n- 76 IMPLEMENT: SourceProxy.createInDatabase (Storage/SourceDatabaseStore.fs).\n  - Adds SourceVersionPinnedErr and SourceStoreUnavailableErr; the in-memory text moves to SourceError.unknownSource.\n  - ADD_TEST SourceProxySqliteTests: 2 contract facts plus 3 of its own.\n- 77 IMPLEMENT: LibraryError gains PresetRefusedErr. LibraryError.entryAlreadyHeld holds the duplicate refusal, which the in-memory preset store now answers. A new LibraryProxyTests fact covers addEntry.\n- 78 IMPLEMENT: LibraryProxyContract (abstract liveStores and emptyPresetStore) holds 10 live-Library and preset-store facts; the in-memory subclass keeps the name LibraryProxyTests.\n- 79 IMPLEMENT (Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs):\n  - LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase, the preset store.\n  - LibraryProxy.createInDatabase, which is liveLibrary over the three database stores.\n  - ADD_TEST LibraryProxySqliteTests: 10 contract facts plus 4 of its own.\n- 80 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores, moved out of createInMemory. LibraryDatabaseTests proves that importFrom fills an empty database through the four database stores.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Anchors.\n   - SampleProxy is the inherited STORE_XDUO_0002 (.contract-ids/XDUO-json), so its SQLite create is IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT, as steps 69 and 71 did. No id is minted.\n   - SourceProxy, LibraryEntryStore and LibraryProxy have no registered id and keep their shapes, so their steps are plain IMPLEMENT. An ADD_CONTRACT would declare a proxy that already exists.\n   - There are no reds: every step lands its code with the facts that prove it.\n2. Who keeps a source. The brief says the preset store is \"for detectors, polarizers and built-in sources\". In the database every source is one kind (SourceEntryKind), so the two stores split them by the protection the provenance gives (step 24):\n   - the user-sources store lists and resolves only UserManaged sources;\n   - the preset store serves detectors, polarizers and ProtectedBuiltIn sources.\n   This keeps the live view's order: presets first, then user sources, as the in-memory composition gives. The database preset store refuses a SampleItem and a UserManaged SourceItem (PresetRefusedErr). The in-memory double still accepts them, because the fixture's library () adds samples, so those refusals are SQLite-only facts.\n3. The preset refusal.\n   - The in-memory store answered a duplicate id with LibraryUnavailableErr, \"the only fitting existing case\".\n   - Step 77 adds PresetRefusedErr and moves the duplicate to it in both stores. LibraryUnavailableErr now means only that the store beneath the proxy failed, which is the database preset store's failure case, so LibraryError needs no StoreUnavailable case.\n   - No test asserted LibraryUnavailableErr. CatalogueImport's library reason gains the case, so an import's rejection text is unchanged.\n4. Sources are versioned in the database while the surface stays unversioned (the brief).\n   - A save decides on the stored and incoming content's { physics = payload (wavelength and tuning); metadata = name } with the stored pin, reusing ofSourcePreset rather than a second payload mapping.\n   - S2.2's removal rule extends to sources: SourceVersionPinnedErr. No pin verb is added, because the surface has none; S3/S4's kit and export paths pin.\n   - The database refuses a non-GUID source id (InvalidSourceErr), an id held by a built-in source (ProtectedSourceRefusedErr) and another kind's id (InvalidSourceErr). The in-memory double keeps its old leniency, so the contract fact that stores a source now uses newSourceId ().\n5. Ordering. The database has no insertion order.\n   - Samples sort by id, as the in-memory map lists them (S2.2's rule for materials).\n   - User sources and presets sort by name, then id, because their in-memory stores keep insertion order, which the database cannot reproduce, and a GUID order would scramble the Select bay's groups.\n   - The SourceProxy doc says so. Facts that compared ordered lists across stores compare as sets (the step 20 precedent).\n6. Lifecycle of presets. The database preset store offers only ActiveEntry presets and resolves any latest preset (001 §B: \"Mark InactiveEntry (still resolvable)\"). That is the same rule liveLibrary applies to samples, and a SQLite fact proves it. The in-memory store has no lifecycle, so the contract facts agree.\n7. The live view.\n   - LibraryProxy.createInDatabase is liveLibrary over the three database stores. It reuses liveLibrary and the derived tree and has no logic or boundary mark of its own.\n   - The in-memory LibraryProxyTests now runs its live facts over liveLibrary composed as AppContext.create composes it (freshStores + SourceProxy.createInMemory), where it ran them over the fixture's preset double (BuiltinCatalogue.library ()). Their assertions are unchanged; the 7 facts carry change_expectation effects.\n8. Reuse.\n   - Every text, filter and payload a second store needs becomes a member when the second store arrives (steps 72, 76, 77), as S2.2 did.\n   - The source-pinned and wrong-store refusals have one holder each and stay inline.\n   - CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores is the one import adapter for both store families. The brief's \"CatalogueImport writes into either\" is proved over an empty :memory: database. AppContext.create still composes the in-memory stores; S2.4 switches it.\n9. Provenance. As S2.2 note 4 records, values pushed through the proxies carry no provenance:\n   - a sample or user source first saved is UserProvenance;\n   - a preset follows its protection (BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue or UserProvenance);\n   - an edit keeps the stored provenance.\n   S2.4 / S3.1 still write catalogue envelopes with their own provenance through stageVersion / stageLatest.\n10. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s23/seam.json):\n   - build and elevation run on every step, and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light) on every step. That includes step 72, the text move, for which seam-plan proposed no test gate, because the suite asserts those texts (S2.2 steps 68/70).\n   - ui-smoke runs on step 74 alone, the one step that edits Ui code (ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs).\n   - No step edits a UI test class, so the brief's \"ui-tests by touched class\" selects none.\n   - kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1, and unit-tests does not apply. seam-plan's \"final step runs every planned gate\" row for step 80 is the mid-campaign artefact.\n11. Budget: 9 steps against a soft 12-20. Each store lands whole with its suite, and the text moves and the test-class conversions are their own steps. Splitting further would add gate runs without isolating risk.\n12. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL: SampleMetadata (made public), selectFrom, unknownSample, unknownSampleVersion, versionsPinned (on SampleError), unknownSource, entryAlreadyHeld, PresetRefusedErr, SampleStoreUnavailableErr, SourceStoreUnavailableErr, SourceVersionPinnedErr, SampleDatabaseStore, SourceDatabaseStore, PresetDatabaseStore, createInDatabase on its four new receivers, ofStores, SampleProxyContract, SourceProxyContract, LibraryProxyContract, LiveLibraryStores, SampleProxySqliteTests, SourceProxySqliteTests and LibraryProxySqliteTests.\n13. Validation:\n   - On the real folder, executability check and check_spec each report only the mid-campaign §9.3 \"final step must WIRE\" finding.\n   - On a staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step, both pass with no findings.\n   - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s23/build_s23.py (census.json, seam.json; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-wired.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S2.4 (Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database): appended steps 81-90 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (23 obligations, 10 acceptance bindings, 7 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 81 IMPLEMENT: Domain WorkbenchSettings.fs gains DataLocations, every 001 sec G location.\n  - defaultsUnder (documents) holds the defaults as configured text, environment variables unexpanded. shippedCatalogueDefault is the relative \"Catalogue\".\n  - CatalogueProxy.createBuiltInUnder (shipped) is the one home of \"Builtin\"; createBuiltIn reads through it.\n- 82 IMPLEMENT: AppConfig.readDataLocations.\n  - ConfigKey gains six folder keys; the connection string stays OpticalConstructorSqlite through tryGetConnectionString.\n  - Missing or refused keys are written back; variables are expanded and relative folders rooted at the install folder (private resolveLocations).\n  - The UI test project gets its own appsettings.json (:memory: library, TestRun/* folders).\n  - ADD_TEST AppConfigTests.\n- 83 IMPLEMENT: loadWorkbenchSettings answers WorkbenchSettings * DataLocations.\n  - AppContext.create (locations) (settings); exports come from locations.exportsFolder (the Documents path at the root is deleted).\n  - New fixture TestAppScope (testLocations, freshAppContext); every UI test composition goes through it.\n- 84 IMPLEMENT: LibraryDatabase gains:\n  - origin (CreatedLibraryDatabase / OpenedLibraryDatabase);\n  - openOrCreate creates a missing database folder;\n  - vacuumInto;\n  - restoreFrom: checks the backup's stamp, VACUUMs INTO the pre-restore file, then copies through SQLite's online backup into the open handle.\n- 85 ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:LibraryBackupProxy> (Domain LibraryBackup.fs): LibraryBackupName, LibraryBackupError, the proxy and its in-memory double. LibraryBackupProxyContract + LibraryBackupProxyTests.\n- 86 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <STORE:LibraryBackupProxy>: Storage LibraryBackupStore.fs.\n  - LibraryBackupTime (yyyyMMdd-HHmmss).\n  - Naming: library-<stamp>.db, then -2, -3 on collision; only such files are listed, newest first.\n  - LibraryBackupProxy.createInDatabase.\n  - LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests runs over a file database under the test output.\n- 87 IMPLEMENT: LibraryDatabase.recreate. It copies the old file into Backups, deletes it with its -wal/-shm/-journal files, and creates a new stamped library.\n- 88 WIRE: AppContext.create answers Result<AppContext, StorageError> over the configured database.\n  - It composes the database stores and imports Catalogue/Builtin only into a newly created library.\n  - LauncherWindow(opened) shows an open failure with the four buttons disabled.\n  - TestAppScope unwraps and gains fileLocations.\n- 89 IMPLEMENT: AppContext.recreateLibrary (shared private compose). LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened) offers \"Recreate library from catalogues\" for LibrarySchemaMismatchErr alone.\n- 90 WIRE_UI: \"Back up library now...\" and \"Restore library...\" in the Library window.\n  - Semantic messages, a restore gate, ConstructorUiId ids, AppContext.libraryBackups.\n  - Threaded through LibraryWindow, EditorLaunchers (both opens), the constructor model and Program.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. DataLocations is its own record beside WorkbenchSettings, not a field of it.\n   - AppContext.create takes it as its own parameter, and loadWorkbenchSettings answers the pair from its one provider.\n   - Why: WorkbenchSettings.defaults stays pure and unchanged, and the tests use it everywhere. A default that held %LOCALAPPDATA% would let any test that composes defaults open the user's library (.spec-md sec 3.9). Each composition now has to say where its library lives.\n2. Configured text vs resolved value.\n   - Domain holds the defaults as text (defaultsUnder takes the Documents folder, so Domain reads no environment).\n   - AppConfig, the IO boundary, expands environment variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder.\n   - That makes 001's <install>\\Catalogue\\ a plain relative default (\"Catalogue\"). It is also why the test run's settings can stay inside the test output.\n3. The UI test project's own appsettings.json (step 82).\n   - The headless session starts the real App, whose Startup reads appsettings.json beside the test assembly. The output copy holds today's write-backs.\n   - From step 88 that startup opens the configured library. Without a test copy, every UI test run would create %LOCALAPPDATA%/.../library.db.\n   - The project's own Content item replaces the App's transitive one by TargetPath (MSBuild's _TransitiveItemsToCopyToOutputDirectory removal). G4 pins the content.\n4. Restore replaces the content of the one open handle through SQLite's online backup (SqliteConnection.BackupDatabase). It does not swap the file and reopen.\n   - Every store is a view over that handle, so \"replaces it and reopens\" is met with no recomposition.\n   - It also avoids Windows file locks and stray WAL files.\n   - The backup's stamp is checked before anything is written. The pre-restore backup (VACUUM INTO) is the undo (.spec-md sec 10.5).\n5. \"Picks a backup\" is a list of the backups in the Library window (identify), then Restore beside Cancel (confirm). There is no native file dialog, so the flow is semantic messages end to end and headless-testable.\n6. Time and naming.\n   - Backups take an injected unit -> LibraryBackupTime clock, as ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder takes `now`. ClockProvider is sec 5's S4.1 shape and is not introduced early.\n   - The stamp is seconds (yyyyMMdd-HHmmss) with -2, -3 on collision. A restore backs up in the same second it is asked, so a collision rule is required. The ordering is read back from the name, so it is deterministic under a fixed test clock.\n7. Import on start, and the open failure.\n   - Only a newly created library imports Catalogue/Builtin (LibraryDatabase.origin). An opened library is not re-imported; S3.1 adds the every-start import by manifest hash.\n   - openOrCreate now creates the database folder, which step 62 did not. On a fresh machine the default folder does not exist.\n   - LibraryDatabaseExn and other open failures show on the launcher with no remedy button, because only a schema mismatch is cured by recreating.\n   - Recreate asks no confirmation. The old file kept in Backups is the undo, and the library is unusable until something is done.\n8. The launcher stays an imperative Avalonia window, as it is today (Program.fs:134). Its new controls carry ConstructorUiIds, and the tests raise Click by id, as LauncherTests already does.\n9. The brief lists MainWorkbenchTests and the FsxAcceptanceTests bench among the compositions to point at :memory:.\n   - Both compose the in-memory doubles and never call AppContext.create, so they open no database and reach no file. They keep their composition.\n   - MainWorkbenchTests changes only its launcher stub (step 90).\n   - Every AppContext.create composition (AppContextTests, LauncherTests, TableAndElementRotationTests, the three WireUi*CompositionTests) goes through TestAppScope.\n10. Preferences, kits and catalogue-export locations are read, written back and carried in DataLocations (brief). Their readers are S3.3 and S5; AppContext gains no locations field until one needs it.\n11. Census-driven scope.\n    - The executability census lists today's AppContext.create and LauncherWindow consumers. So step 88 authorizes the composition test files, which keep their code because they compose through TestAppScope since step 83.\n    - The checker also found WireUiFinalCompositionTests constructing LauncherWindow, which the brief missed; steps 88 and 89 edit it.\n    - The record-field addition of step 90 declares no contract effect on AppContext, because no consumer constructs the record.\n    - openOrCreate's behaviour change carries no contract effect, because the census cannot resolve a symbol this spec creates (step 62). Its obligation and the I1/I2 facts cover it.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s24/seam.json, seam-wired.json):\n    - build and elevation on every step;\n    - constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light) on the Domain/Storage steps 81, 84-87;\n    - ui-smoke (all_discovered, light) on every step touching App, Ui or the UI tests;\n    - ui-tests by class: 82 AppConfigTests; 83 and 88 the composition classes; 89 LauncherTests and WireUiFinalCompositionTests; 90 seam-plan's six plus AppContextTests, because AppContext.fs changes. WireUiCompositionTests and WireUi0040CompositionTests hold ui-smoke facts only, so a ui-tests arm for them would be empty.\n    - kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1, and unit-tests does not apply.\n13. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL: DataLocations, defaultsUnder, shippedCatalogueDefault, createBuiltInUnder, readDataLocations, resolveLocations, the six ConfigKey literals, TestAppScope, testLocations, fileLocations, freshAppContext, LibraryDatabaseOrigin with its two cases, vacuumInto, restoreFrom, recreate, LibraryBackup, LibraryBackupName, LibraryBackupError with its three cases, LibraryBackupProxy, LibraryBackupStore, LibraryBackupTime, recreateLibrary, LibraryRestoreGate with its cases, LibraryBackupRefusedErr, the five Library-window messages, and the nine new ConstructorUiIds.\n14. Validation:\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only the two pre-mint placeholder notices for steps 85/86 (sec 9.6).\n    - On a copy with the placeholder neutralised, it reports only SELECTION_REQUIRED for step 90's constructor-unit-tests and unit-tests. This is the mid-campaign \"the final step runs every planned gate\" artefact, the counterpart of S2.3's sec 9.3 note; the next section's steps make 90 non-final.\n    - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step appended, the check passes with no findings.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s24/build_s24.py (stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-deep.log, check-wired.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S3.1 (Import on every start and the per-entry decision table): appended steps 91-101 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (24 obligations, 11 acceptance bindings, 9 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 91 IMPLEMENT: EntryProvenance gains ForkProvenance of EntryForkInfo (original id, version and provenance). A fork is UserManaged / UserCategory; kindValue 5, no catalogue id; library-common.schema.json gains the fifth shape, recursive.\n- 92 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueProxy.readManifest (manifest only, no entry file), shared with readCatalogue in the folder store. CatalogueProxy.builtInFolderUnder is the one home of \"Builtin\"; createBuiltInUnder reads through it.\n- 93 IMPLEMENT: the pure table in CatalogueImport.fs: HeldEntry(Version), ImportOrigin, LatestMove, ImportAction, ImportStatus (the six 001 sec B rows), ImportMode, ImportDecision (decide, unlisted, mode, byDefault, rowName, split), ImportChoice. LibraryEntryContent.referencedEntryIds. ADD_TEST ImportDecisionTests.\n- 94 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueImportProxy becomes envelope-level (tryHeldEntry, heldEntriesNamed, heldEntriesOf, putEntryVersion, retireEntry); ofStores is its in-memory implementation. decideCatalogue on the proxy. CatalogueImportContext { proxy; sealEntry; newEntryId } with apply, importCatalogue, importFrom. Storage CatalogueImportStore.fs: CatalogueImportContext.create. Fixture, DefaultStores and AppContext call through the context.\n- 95 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0008: CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase over the entry-version rows; ofStores folded into createInMemory and deleted; AppContext's created-database import composes it. CatalogueImportContract (abstract) with CatalogueImportInMemoryTests and the new CatalogueImportSqliteTests.\n- 96 IMPLEMENT: every decision row, the user-entry rule and the hold-back as contract facts over both stores.\n- 97 IMPLEMENT: the import log (CatalogueImportTime, CatalogueEntryCount, CatalogueImportLogEntry; loggedImports, logImport, forgetImport) in memory and over the CatalogueImport table.\n- 98 IMPLEMENT: importOnStart with the manifest-hash skip; context gains hashManifest, now, openCatalogue; FolderImportResult, PendingCatalogueImport, StartupImportReport.\n- 99 IMPLEMENT: registerFolder (CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr), settle, registeredFolders; unregistering is forgetImport.\n- 100 WIRE: AppContext.catalogueImports and pendingImports; importOnStart on every start (the created-only branch deleted); AGENTS.md gotcha names importOnStart.\n- 101 WIRE_UI: \"Register catalogue folder...\" (folder picker -> RegisterCatalogueFolder), the Catalogue folders list with Unregister, the import status; catalogueImports threaded along step 90's libraryBackups path.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The seam reads and writes whole envelopes.\n   - The table needs each held version's hash and provenance, which the per-kind stores do not expose, and S2.3 note 9 already routes catalogue envelopes past them. So CatalogueImportProxy's four save fields are replaced by an envelope-level seam (step 94), and the database implements it over the version rows (step 95).\n   - The in-memory double keeps its envelopes in a closure and pushes each NEW entry into its four bundled stores, so the fixtures and the test scene still hold the imported catalogue. A later version or retirement is the seam's own; its facts read the seam.\n   - Step 94 leaves AppContext's created-database import on ofStores over the database stores, which is step 88's behaviour unchanged; step 95 replaces it the next step. This keeps each step green and reviewable.\n2. Forks.\n   - \"Provenance keeps the original id\" is a fifth provenance case (step 91), so the flag travels in the file, the row and a kit snapshot. It keeps the original's version and provenance too, so a CC-BY source's attribution survives a fork.\n   - A fork is a new entry at version 1, sealed through an injected sealer, because Domain does not hash (step 26). Its id comes from an injected newEntryId.\n   - The entry schemas stay version 1, because no entry file has been released.\n3. CatalogueImportContext is the *Context convention: the seam plus the sealer, the id minter, the manifest hasher, the clock and the folder opener. Storage's create supplies the real ones; facts replace fields by record update. ClockProvider (sec 5, S4.1) is not introduced early, as S2.4 note 6 did.\n4. The table's precise rules.\n   - \"The latest moves only for a protected built-in from a catalogue\" is read as: BuiltInProvenance c, arriving from catalogue c itself, at a version above the held latest. Moving the latest backwards, or for a built-in arriving through another catalogue, would let a second catalogue override the first.\n   - An id held as another kind is a divergence and forks, because one id cannot name two kinds.\n   - Alternatives: every row that writes offers SkipIncomingEntry; a name collision also offers one RebindToHeldEntry per same-name entry (001's \"use my Si instead\"); reuse and retire offer none. This gives the dialog (S3.2) its overrides (001 sec O).\n   - Re-binding writes nothing and answers the binding; S4.2's kit snapshots consume it.\n   - \"Si - from A\" is rowName, a caption. Renaming the entry would change its hash and make every later import a divergence.\n5. References never dangle.\n   - apply refuses a written entry that names an entry the same apply skips or re-binds (DanglingReferenceErr), before it writes.\n   - split holds an unasked row back with any awaiting row it references (a material in a colliding category, its samples), transitively. The rows that do apply unasked therefore never point at an undecided entry.\n6. \"Then log the import\" applies when no row waits. A catalogue with awaiting rows applies its unasked rows and leaves the log as it was, so the next start decides those rows again; settle (step 99) logs it once the dialog's choices are applied. Without this, a cancelled dialog would lose the rows until the catalogue next changed. For a folder being registered, this means that it is not registered until its rows are settled; the Library window says so.\n7. \"An entry the catalogue no longer lists\" retires only entries whose latest provenance is BuiltInProvenance of that catalogue. Membership is not recorded otherwise, and 001's Summary rule (\"user entries are never touched\") forbids retiring a user entry. An already inactive entry produces no row, and a reuse never reactivates one (not in 001's table).\n8. The start-up order: the shipped folder, then every logged folder except the CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue row, which is the shipped catalogue's. registerFolder refuses that id and any id already logged. Unregistering is forgetImport: no confirmation, no undo needed (entries stay; registering again restores the row).\n9. LibraryDatabase.origin (step 84) loses its product reader in step 100 but stays: its facts in LibraryDatabaseTests and the backup suites read it.\n10. The Library window's folder picker is an IO edge in the shape of pickDataFile / attachDataFileButton; headless facts send RegisterCatalogueFolder directly, and the acceptance presses Unregister after registering through the app scope. verbButton gains verbButtonOn so the picker verb keeps the one look.\n11. Test moves: the UndecodableEntryErr fact migrates to CatalogueImportInMemoryTests (only the double decodes); \"importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused\" becomes \"...reuses every entry and writes nothing\" (re-import is now Reuse); LibraryDatabaseTests' step-80 fact migrates into CatalogueImportSqliteTests' inherited \"importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue\". These are fact moves, recorded as migrate/rename effects, so no class verb applies.\n12. Contract effects are declared only for symbols the checker can resolve (inventory or created by this spec); EntryProvenance and AppContext.create carry none, as S2.4 note 11 did.\n13. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s31/seam.json):\n    - build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light) on steps 91-99;\n    - ui-smoke (all_discovered, light) on 94, 95, 100, 101, which touch Ui code;\n    - ui-tests by class: 94 AppContextTests, MainWorkbenchTests (the fixture), TableAndElementRotationTests (DefaultStores); 95 and 100 the AppContext composition classes (step 88's set); 101 step 90's set plus TableAndElementRotationTests.\n    - seam-plan proposed only constructor classes for 94/95 (it reads test effects) and kit-acceptance for 100; kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 and unit-tests does not apply.\n14. Budget: 11 steps against a soft 12-22. Each step lands its code with its facts; the contract rows (96) are their own step.\n15. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL: EntryForkInfo, ForkProvenance, HeldEntry, HeldEntryVersion, ImportOrigin, CatalogueImportOrigin, LatestMove and its cases, ImportAction and its seven cases, ImportStatus and its six cases, ImportMode and its cases, ImportDecision, ImportChoice, ImportSplit, ImportOutcome, EntryRebinding, EntryFork, EntryVersionPut, CatalogueImportContext, CatalogueImportTime, CatalogueEntryCount, CatalogueImportLogEntry, PendingCatalogueImport, FolderImportResult and its cases, FolderImportReport, StartupImportReport, the six new error cases, CatalogueImportStore, importRow, toLogEntry, verbButtonOn, pickCatalogueFolder, ImportStoreSet, the two messages and the five ConstructorUiIds.\n16. Validation:\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only SELECTION_REQUIRED for step 101's constructor-unit-tests and unit-tests: the mid-campaign \"final step runs every planned gate\" artefact noted by S2.3 and S2.4; the next section makes 101 non-final.\n    - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step appended (specs/0050/.artifacts/s31/wired), the check passes with no findings.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s31/build_s31.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S3.2 (The import dialog and single-file drop): appended steps 102-112 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (24 obligations, 11 acceptance bindings, 10 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 102 IMPLEMENT: ImportOrigin gains DroppedFileOrigin (the file's leaf name) and describe; rowName reads it ('Silicon — from lab-silicon.material-json'); a dropped file never moves the latest. CatalogueImportProxy.decideEntry holds decideCatalogue's per-envelope body, so one body decides catalogue rows, dropped files and S4.2's snapshots.\n- 103 IMPLEMENT: LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName (extension, ignoring case) and LibraryFileText.readEntryFile (Storage CatalogueFolderStore.fs). readEntryFile is readCatalogue's per-row read, moved, so one body reads an entry file.\n- 104 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueImportContext gains readEntryFile, filled by Storage's create, and decideDroppedFiles. The new error cases are DroppedFileRefusedErr and UnresolvedReferenceErr. decideDroppedFiles:\n  - names every refused file at once;\n  - collapses equal duplicates and refuses contradicting ones;\n  - refuses a reference to an entry neither held nor dropped;\n  - writes nothing.\n  Four contract facts run over both stores.\n- 105 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueImportProxy.tryHeldEnvelope, in memory and over tryStoredVersion, for the diff preview.\n- 106 IMPLEMENT: Domain EntryTextDiff.fs (EntryTextLine, EntryDiffLine with SameEntryLine / RemovedEntryLine / AddedEntryLine, and diffLines: common ends, then LCS over the middle) and Storage LibraryEntryEnvelope.diffFrom. ADD_TEST EntryTextDiffTests.\n- 107 IMPLEMENT: Ui ImportDialogView.fs, the pure MVU:\n  - ImportDialogRequest (SettlePendingCatalogue / ApplyDroppedEntries), ImportDialogApplied with its summary, ImportDialogContext, ImportDiffState, the model;\n  - the messages DecideImportRow, OverrideImportRow, ToggleImportDiff, ApplyImportChoices and CancelImportDialog; only ApplyImportChoices reaches the seam (settle or apply);\n  - captions and keys in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain, and ten ConstructorUiIds (ImportDecisionList, ImportApplyButton, …).\n  ADD_TEST ImportDialogTests (9 facts).\n- 108 IMPLEMENT: ImportDialogWindow (WindowFit.keepOnScreen) and EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles, the one drop seam (DragDrop over DataTransfer.TryGetFiles). It joins ScrollExtentTests and adds an Apply smoke fact.\n- 109 IMPLEMENT: MaterialsWindow, MaterialsWindowContext, SampleEditorWindow and EditorLaunchers.openMaterialsWindow carry the CatalogueImportContext, threaded through the app, the strip and every test construction. No behaviour changes.\n- 110 WIRE_UI: Materials window drop. It adds DropMaterialEntryFiles / MaterialsImportApplied, the importStatus / importError fields with materialsImportStatusText, the DropEntryFiles member, and an acceptance fact over the app scope.\n- 111 WIRE_UI: Library window drop. DropLibraryEntryFiles / LibraryImportApplied, and a registration whose rows await (step 101) opens the dialog. 'Review imports…' (ReviewPendingImports) reopens it, and a settled registration leaves pendingImports. There is an acceptance fact over the app scope.\n- 112 WIRE_UI: the Launcher opens the dialog at start over AppContext.pendingImports. It shows launcherPendingImportsText and launcherReviewImportsButton while any import waits; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply removes it.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Origin of a dropped file. DroppedFileOrigin holds the file's leaf name, so the 001 sec B caption reads 'Si — from <file>'. A dropped file never moves the latest: the move rule names CatalogueImportOrigin only, keeping 001's 'only for a protected built-in from a catalogue'.\n2. A drop is refused as a whole when any file fails, naming every bad file. This mirrors apply's 'check before any write'. A partially opened dialog would hide the refused files.\n3. An entry naming an id neither held nor dropped is refused (UnresolvedReferenceErr) before the dialog opens. Without this, an applied drop could store a sample whose material does not exist. This extends S3.1 note 5 ('references never dangle') to drops.\n4. The diff preview is a line diff of the two canonical entry files (step 27: sorted keys, one value per line), so it compares payloads field by field without a diff package.\n   - Its held side is: for a divergence, the same version when held (else the latest); for a new version, the held latest; for a name collision, the re-bind target or else the first same-name entry.\n   - The held envelope is read through the new tryHeldEnvelope as the view renders, as the windows' views re-query their stores.\n5. The brief's 'decide / override / apply / cancel' messages are DecideImportRow (back to the default), OverrideImportRow (an offered alternative only), ApplyImportChoices and CancelImportDialog. ToggleImportDiff is the preview's.\n   - Rows are keyed by entry id, the key settle matches choices by (step 99).\n   - The opener learns the result through ImportDialogApplied, and its summary is the one status text.\n6. Reuse of the button look. MaterialsWindowView's brush, messageColor, positiveBackground, negativeBackground, verbButton and actionButton become public, and ImportDialogView calls them: the spec 0048 R2 'lower declaration serves both' rule LibraryWindowView already follows for LifecycleAction.\n   - This avoids a seventh private copy. The other views' existing private copies are not swept.\n   - ELEV015 compares public names only (Softellect Analyzers NoDuplicatePublicName.fs), and no other public namesake exists.\n   - ImportDialogView.fs and ImportDialogWindow.fs therefore compile between MaterialsWindowView.fs and MaterialsWindow.fs. So MaterialsWindowContext's opener is typed over Domain values (ImportDecision list -> unit) and its completion message carries the summary caption. LibraryWindowContext, compiled later, takes the ImportDialogRequest.\n7. Every Materials window carries the import seam, the Select-state one a Sample editor opens included. So SampleEditorWindow takes it too (step 109, threading only), rather than an optional parameter that would make drops work only on some opens.\n8. The drop handler is an IO edge in the shape of pickDataFile. Headless facts send the windows' drop message, through the DropEntryFiles members the handler also calls, and assert DragDrop.GetAllowDrop. Avalonia 12.1.4's DragDrop.SetAllowDrop / AddDragOverHandler / AddDropHandler, DragEventArgs.DataTransfer, DataFormat.File and TryGetFiles were checked in the package.\n9. The Launcher keeps the still-waiting imports in one local mutable list (the window is the IO edge). It opens the dialog over the first at its first Opened and offers 'Review imports…' while any wait. Cancel keeps the import waiting; settle runs only on Apply.\n10. S3.1 step 101 left LibraryWindowModel.pendingImports 'for the import dialog'. Step 111 consumes it: the registration opens the dialog, Review imports reopens it, and LibraryImportApplied removes the settled import.\n11. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: Domain EntryTextDiff.fs, Ui ImportDialogView.fs and ImportDialogWindow.fs (EntryFileDrop), OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s32/seam.json):\n    - build and elevation on every step;\n    - constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light, the S3.1 choice) on 102-106;\n    - ui-smoke (all_discovered) on 107-112;\n    - ui-tests by class on 107-112, each a superset of seam-plan's proposal.\n    seam-plan proposed kit-acceptance from 107, which is not runnable before S12.1. EmbeddedChartTests, WireUi0040CompositionTests and WireUiCompositionTests hold no ui-tests facts (SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM), so they run under ui-smoke only.\n13. Contract effects are declared only where the consumer census is satisfied. MaterialsWindow and LibraryWindow keep their constructor in 110/111, so those steps declare their contexts' shape only. Step 109's threading carries change_expectation effects on four facts whose constructions change and whose assertions stay. WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests (an EditorLaunchers record update) and WireUiFinalCompositionTests (a LauncherWindow consumer) are authorized edits that keep their code.\n14. Budget: 11 steps against a soft 10-18.\n15. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL (specs/0050/.artifacts/s31/namecheck.py): DroppedFileOrigin, decideEntry, tryOfFileName, readEntryFile, DroppedFileRefusedErr, UnresolvedReferenceErr, decideDroppedFiles, tryHeldEnvelope, EntryTextDiff, EntryTextLine, EntryDiffLine and its three cases, diffLines, diffFrom, every ImportDialog* type, case and function, EntryFileDrop, acceptEntryFiles, the ten import* UiIds, materialsImportStatusText, libraryReviewImportsButton, launcherPendingImportsText, launcherReviewImportsButton, DropMaterialEntryFiles, DropLibraryEntryFiles, MaterialsImportApplied, LibraryImportApplied, ReviewPendingImports, openImportDialog, importError and DropEntryFiles. STL's diff-line cases (DiffAdded, DiffRemoved, DiffContext) are avoided.\n16. Validation:\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only SELECTION_REQUIRED for step 112's constructor-unit-tests and unit-tests: the mid-campaign 'final step runs every planned gate' artifact noted by S2.3, S2.4 and S3.1.\n    - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step appended (specs/0050/.artifacts/s32/wired), the check passes with no findings.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s32/build_s32.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S3.3 (Export, Export my library and licence attribution): appended steps 113-121 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (22 obligations, 9 acceptance bindings, 9 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 113 IMPLEMENT: attribution in Domain LibraryEntryFiles.fs.\n  - EntryAttribution (LicenceAndCitation / LicenceNameOnly) with text. EntryLicence.attributionWith holds the one CC-BY rule (SPDX id starting CC-BY, ignoring case).\n  - EntryProvenance.attributionOpt: a pulled entry's licence, through any fork; None for built-in, user and kit-import.\n  - EntryAttributionLine; LibraryEntry.attributedEntryIds (the entry, then a sample's referenced materials).\n  - Fixture BuiltinCatalogue.fs: licensedMaterialContent, userMaterialContent, userCategoryContent, sampleContentOver, putSealedEntries (shared by both suites).\n- 114 IMPLEMENT: CatalogueImportProxy.attributionLinesOf (latest provenance, ids in order); a contract fact over both stores.\n- 115 IMPLEMENT: the seam gains heldUserEntries and pinEntryVersion.\n  - In memory, material and sample pins go through S2.2's pinMaterialVersion / pinSampleVersion; other kinds hold no pin in memory.\n  - The database pins any kind's row through the new LibraryDbContext.stagePin. The database pinMaterialVersion / pinSampleVersion now call it, so one body pins a row.\n- 116 IMPLEMENT: single-entry export.\n  - LibraryExportError (ExportedEntryNotHeldErr, ExportLibraryRefusedErr, ExportFileWriteErr) and CatalogueImportProxy.tryLatestEnvelope.\n  - Context fields writeEntryFile and exportFolderOpt; CatalogueImportContext.exportEntry pins, then writes the canonical file.\n- 117 IMPLEMENT: catalogue exports.\n  - CatalogueExportTarget, context field newCatalogueId; three new error cases (ExportCatalogueRefusedErr, ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr, EmptyLibraryExportErr).\n  - exportEntries: read, user-reference closure, per-kind name check, occupied-folder check, pin, write. exportUserLibrary over heldUserEntries.\n  - Storage CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder.\n- 118 IMPLEMENT: shared window pieces and the default folder.\n  - MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn and pickLibraryFolder become the one body; LibraryWindowView's private verbButton, verbButtonOn and pickCatalogueFolder are deleted.\n  - AppContext sets exportFolderOpt to DataLocations.cataloguesFolder.\n- 119 WIRE_UI: Materials window.\n  - Export… (save dialog) and Export shown to catalogue… (folder picker); ExportSelectedMaterial / ExportShownMaterials; the export status line; the attribution panel.\n  - pickEntryExportFile and attributionPanel; captions in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain; four ConstructorUiIds.\n- 120 WIRE_UI: Library window.\n  - Export…, Export shown to catalogue… and Export my library…; three messages; LibraryExportRefusedErr; the export status line; the attribution panel (a sample credits its materials); five ConstructorUiIds.\n  - Includes an end-to-end fact: Export my library over the app library is registered by a fresh library.\n- 121 WIRE_UI: Details bay. TableAndElementRotationModel.detailsAttributionLines, appended to the Details title.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Export lives on CatalogueImportContext, the library-exchange seam every library window and the constructor model already carry (steps 101, 109). A separate export context would need step 109's threading a second time.\n   - So the context gains writeEntryFile, newCatalogueId and exportFolderOpt.\n   - exportFolderOpt is None from Storage's create, so no test or default composition names Documents (.spec-md sec 3.9). AppContext sets the configured catalogues folder (001 sec G), which closes S2.4 interpretation 10.\n   - The planner may rename the context to say exchange; nothing else depends on the name.\n2. The pin. The brief names S2.2's pin verbs, which exist for materials and samples only (S2.3 interpretation 4: sources, presets and categories have none).\n   - Every exported kind must be pinned, so the pin goes on the envelope seam as pinEntryVersion.\n   - In memory it calls S2.2's verbs for materials and samples. In the database one shared stagePin serves the seam and both verbs (reuse at the third holder).\n   - Pins come after every refusal and before any write, so a written file always names a frozen version. A failed folder write leaves its pins, which only make the next physics edit mint a version.\n3. 'A selection or a category'. Both windows select a single entry, so a catalogue export takes the entries the window shows: its text filter and facet constraints applied (the existing filteredEntries, LibraryWindowView.fs:518, MaterialsWindowView.fs:476). A material-category facet makes it that category's export. No multi-select is added.\n4. Closure. A catalogue export adds the user entries its entries reference (referencedEntryIds, transitively). It does not add built-ins, because every library imports the shipped catalogue. So the folder imports cleanly elsewhere, and an export of user entries never meets a built-in's file name. A single-entry file stays one entry; a drop that lacks its references is refused by S3.2's UnresolvedReferenceErr.\n5. One version per entry. A catalogue folder names each entry's file by its name (001 sec A), so it carries each entry's latest version. A sample whose layer names an older version of a material resolves that version only where it is held. The kit snapshot (S4.2) carries exact versions.\n6. Export my library exports every user entry (protection UserManaged: user, kit-import, pulled, forked), inactive ones included. The file carries no lifecycle, so they return active, and the data is kept. This preserves what the user owned when the database is recreated (001 sec C).\n7. Target folders. An export never overwrites a catalogue: a folder whose manifest reads, or is rejected, is ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr. A missing folder is created by the writer. Each export is a new catalogue (fresh id, version 1, named by the folder through CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder). There is no merge, re-export version bump or option. A single-entry file's overwrite is guarded by the save dialog's own prompt.\n8. Attribution reads the latest version's provenance through the seam (HeldEntry.provenance). Licence data lives in the envelope, not on the per-kind values.\n   - A surface showing a sample credits the sample and the materials of its layers. 001's 'CC-BY entries show their attribution' is read as covering the data the surface shows.\n   - Kits carry attribution with no code here, because their snapshots are the entry files (S4.2), whose provenance holds licence and citation.\n9. UX (.spec-md sec 10): exports are one click with no confirmation. They write new files, delete nothing and finish in well under a second for a library, so no JobRunner progress applies. The status line states that the exported versions are now pinned. No opposing button pair is added.\n10. Reuse at the second holder. Both windows need a press-with-owner verb box and a folder picker. LibraryWindowView's private copies (steps 101, 107's unswept verbButton) move to the public MaterialsWindowView ones, per the lower-declaration rule of S3.2 interpretation 6. Their look, ids and messages are unchanged.\n11. Names were checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL (specs/0050/.artifacts/s31/namecheck.py). NothingToExportErr exists (ExperimentExport.fs), so the case is EmptyLibraryExportErr. A window field exportStatus exists in TableAndElementRotationView, so the windows use entryExportStatus / entryExportError.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s33/seam.json).\n    - build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, whole_suite light) on 113-117.\n    - ui-smoke (all_discovered, light) on 118-121, which touch Ui code.\n    - ui-tests by class on 118-121, each a superset of seam-plan's proposal: 118 AppContextTests, ImportDialogTests, LibraryWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests; 119 MaterialsWindowTests, SampleEditorWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests, WindowLauncherTests; 120 LibraryWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests; 121 LayerBandsControlsTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, TableAndElementRotationTests.\n    - seam-plan proposed kit-acceptance on 118-120, which is not runnable before S12.1. unit-tests does not apply.\n13. Budget: 9 steps against a soft 8-14. Each step lands its code with its facts. The shared window refactor (118) is its own step, so 119 and 120 add behaviour only.\n14. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: none. Every change lands in existing files (CatalogueImport.fs, LibraryEntryFiles.fs, CatalogueImportStore.fs, LibraryDatabaseStore.fs, the two window views, ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs, TableAndElementRotationView.fs, AppContext.fs).\n15. Validation:\n    - On the real folder, executability check and check_spec report only SELECTION_REQUIRED for step 121's constructor-unit-tests and unit-tests. This is the mid-campaign 'final step runs every planned gate' artefact noted by S2.3-S3.2; the next section makes 121 non-final.\n    - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step appended (specs/0050/.artifacts/s33/wired), executability check and check_spec pass with no findings.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s33/build_s33.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S4.1 (The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext): appended steps 122-131 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (23 obligations, 10 acceptance bindings, 10 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 122 IMPLEMENT: Domain Kit.fs (module Kit, after EntryTextDiff.fs).\n  - ClockTime (UTC) and [<ReferenceEquality>] ClockProvider { now }.\n  - KitError with describe: KitIoErr, NotAKitFolderErr, KitAlreadyExistsErr, KitFileRejectedErr, InvalidKitNameErr.\n  - KitName (tryCreate refuses blank; fileStem = step 24's FileStem.ofText), KitAuthor, KitNotes, SendExcludeGlob.\n  - KitFile (schemaVersion, step 24's KitId, name, author, created, modified, notes, sendExclude): currentSchemaVersion 1, extension and fileName .kit-json, create at one instant.\n  - KitFolder of FolderName; KitAccess (ReadWriteKitAccess / ReadOnlyKitAccess).\n  - ADD_TEST KitTests.\n- 123 IMPLEMENT: KitRelativePath.tryCreate (forward slashes; refuses empty, rooted, drive-bearing and escaping paths). KitFileKind with its five 001 sec A extensions, fileNameOf and all. KitFileText, KitDataFile. MissingKitFileErr, InvalidKitPathErr.\n  - ContentHash.ofBytes becomes the one SHA-256 hex body; step 27's contentHashOf calls it (a move, every hash unchanged).\n- 124 IMPLEMENT: the .kit-json text.\n  - schema/kit.schema.json, version-gated like the catalogue manifest; SchemaValidation.validateKitFile.\n  - Storage KitFolderStore.fs (after CatalogueImportStore.fs) with KitFile.fileText and KitFileText.parseKitFile; a version mismatch is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr carrying KitFile.extension.\n  - Reuse at the second holder: JsonNode.canonicalFileText (the indented rendering plus one LF, now shared by entry, manifest and kit file texts) and CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText (step 31's parse order, now shared by manifest and kit file; StorageBoundary-marked).\n  - ADD_TEST KitFileJsonTests.\n- 125 ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:KitProxy> (Domain KitFolders.fs, after Kit.fs).\n  - KitProxy { initialiseKit; readKitFile; writeKitFile }.\n  - InMemoryKitFolder (create, placeLabFile, paths), shared by every in-memory proxy over it.\n  - KitProxy.createInMemory.\n  - KitProxyContract (abstract) with KitProxyTests (in memory). ADD_TEST KitProxyTests.\n- 126 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <STORE:KitProxy>: Storage KitProxy.create (folder : KitFolder).\n  - Building it touches nothing. initialise creates a missing folder, data and library, and writes .kit-json last.\n  - A refused text is KitFileRejectedErr naming .kit-json; every IO exception is KitIoErr.\n  - FileName.writeBytesAtomically holds step 33's atomic body; LibraryFileText.writeAtomically calls it.\n  - KitProxyFolderTests runs every contract fact over folders under the test output. ADD_TEST KitProxyFolderTests.\n- 127 IMPLEMENT: listKindFiles, readKindFile, writeKindFile, deleteKindFile, generic over KitFileKind, in both implementations. Includes a failed-replace fact (the file held open).\n- 128 IMPLEMENT: readDataFile by KitRelativePath: the text with a BOM dropped, ContentHash.ofBytes of the stored bytes.\n- 129 IMPLEMENT: the lock.\n  - MachineName, UserName, KitLockOwner (STL ProcessId reused), KitLockHolder.describe, KitLockedErr.\n  - acquireLock (ClockTime) / releaseLock in both implementations.\n  - Folder: .oc/lock canonical JSON; stale = unbinding text, or this machine with an ended process; taken by a no-overwrite move.\n- 130 IMPLEMENT: recordStamps / changedKitFiles. Stamps cover the .kit-json and every per-kind file, live inside the proxy and follow its own writes.\n- 131 IMPLEMENT: KitReadOnlyErr; KitProxy.readOnlyView; KitContext { proxy; kitFile; access; clock } with openKit, close, saveKitFile.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Reuse, never a second copy.\n   - KitId is step 24's type, whose doc already says S4.1 reuses it.\n   - \"The filesystem-safe name rule as a member\" is KitName.fileStem over step 24's FileStem.ofText. Kit file stems are made by that same rule, so no second rule exists.\n   - ProcessId is Softellect.Sys.Primitives.ProcessId (STL Sys/Primitives.fs:802).\n2. KitFileKind declares now the five per-kind kit extensions of 001 sec A: items, setups, experiments, studies, fit runs. That is the closed set 001 sec P says KitProxy covers.\n   - The verbs are generic over the kind's extension and text-level (KitFileText).\n   - Later sections (S4.3 experiments and setups, S7.1 items, S11 studies and fit runs) bring each kind's format and codec over these kinds. They add NO case and NO proxy verb.\n   - The .kit-json is not a kind; it has typed verbs.\n3. One text type, KitFileText, serves kit files and lab files. Two types would need a conversion each way, which ELEV006 forbids.\n   - A read drops a leading UTF-8 BOM from the text, never from the hashed bytes.\n   - The in-memory double hashes a text as its UTF-8 bytes, so both stores agree.\n4. ContentHash is also the data-file hash (.spec-md sec 5 DataAttachment). The in-memory double needs a hash and Domain cannot reach Storage, so the SHA-256 body moves to Domain (ContentHash.ofBytes).\n5. The data-file read lands here, because the brief marks only copy-in and snapshots as S4.2's. KitRelativePath backs it.\n6. The change check:\n   - Stamps live inside each proxy and are never written (.spec-md sec 3.12: no stamp).\n   - Folder stamps are SHA-256 of the bytes; the double compares contents.\n   - recordStamps replaces the record (at open, after a reload). The proxy's own writes and deletes move it, so only other writers' changes are answered.\n   - Lab files, .oc and *.tmp files are never stamped. The reload offer is S5.3's.\n7. The lock:\n   - Foreign means not taken by this proxy, so two windows in one process are two holders.\n   - Live unless it names this machine and a process that has ended. An unbinding lock is stale, because .oc is cache, safe to delete (001 sec A).\n   - Taken through a .oc/lock-<GUID>.tmp moved without overwrite, so two racing openers never both hold it. Release deletes only its own.\n   - No break-lock verb: 001 sec E offers read-only instead.\n   - In memory, the n-th proxy over a folder is process n of machine and user \"in-memory\", so createInMemory takes only the folder.\n8. Read-only is structural.\n   - KitContext.openKit under ReadOnlyKitAccess holds proxy.readOnlyView, whose every write verb answers KitReadOnlyErr. Nothing reached through a read-only context can write, not even .oc.\n   - S4.2's new write verbs (copy-in, snapshots) MUST also be refused by readOnlyView.\n9. KitFile.modified is when the app last wrote the kit file (KitContext.saveKitFile). Other kit-file writes leave .kit-json alone, so a git-managed kit does not churn it.\n10. initialiseKit:\n    - It refuses a folder that holds a .kit-json (KitAlreadyExistsErr), so nothing is silently overwritten.\n    - It creates a missing folder and writes .kit-json last, so a folder is a kit only once whole.\n    - writeKitFile requires an initialised kit.\n    - The KitId is minted by the caller (S5.2 New kit...). The system clock is composed by the code that first opens a kit in the app (S4.3 / S5.2). Neither is added here.\n11. The schema-version mismatch is StorageError.UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr at the codec (step 30 built the case for kit files). KitProxy reports it as KitFileRejectedErr naming .kit-json and both versions, because ELEV016 keeps a case name to one union.\n12. Kit.fs compiles after EntryTextDiff.fs, early enough for Experiments (S4.3, S9.1) to name its types. A later section that needs a later file's type (S7.1 items over MuellerInverse's ParameterAxis) MAY move its one Compile line.\n13. Names:\n    - Every new name was checked unused in the tree, the spec and STL (specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py).\n    - ClockProvider has an STL namesake in Softellect.Trust. Berreman references only Softellect.Sys, and ELEV014 compares only the assemblies the compilation sees, so it is no collision.\n    - MachineName and UserName appear in STL only as properties.\n14. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/seam.json).\n    - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered; whole_suite light, 13 s measured) on every step, which matches seam-plan on 122-130.\n    - No step touches Ui, Ui.Tests, App, Optimization or the run law, so ui-smoke, ui-tests, unit-tests and kit-acceptance do not apply. Seam-plan's extra gates on 131 are the \"final step runs every planned gate\" artefact.\n15. Budget: 10 steps against a soft 14-24. Each step lands one capability across both implementations with its facts. No step is padded.\n16. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n    - Domain KitFolders.fs (KitProxy, InMemoryKitFolder, KitContext) beside Kit.fs.\n    - Storage KitFolderStore.fs and schema/kit.schema.json.\n    - Tests KitTests.fs, KitFileJsonTests.fs, KitProxyTests.fs.\n17. Validation:\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only the two pre-mint placeholder notices for steps 125/126 (sec 9.6) and the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note that step 131 is not a WIRE step; the next section makes 131 non-final.\n    - On a copy with the placeholder neutralised, only the sec 9.3 note remains.\n    - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step appended, the check passes with no findings.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/build_s41.py (stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-deep.log, check-wired.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S4.2 (Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution): appended steps 132-144 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (26 obligations, 13 acceptance bindings, 13 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 132 IMPLEMENT: pure shapes in Kit.fs.\n  - KitDataFolder (root data; tryCreate) and its copyTargetFor rule: the name, then ' (2)', ' (3)'… before the extension, ignoring case.\n  - KitFolder.tryKitPathOf; LabFileSource (STL FileByteContent reused).\n  - DataAttachment with KitDataFile.attachment; DataAttachmentStatus with statusAgainst.\n- 133 IMPLEMENT: KitProxy.tryKitPathOf and copyInFile in both implementations.\n  - InMemoryKitFolder.kitFolder (C:/in-memory-kit) and removeLabFile.\n  - FileName.writeNewBytesAtomically shares one body with writeBytesAtomically over STL ExistingFilePolicy.\n  - readOnlyView refuses copy-in.\n- 134 IMPLEMENT: KitProxy.attachLabFile (in place inside the kit, copied in from outside) and KitProxy.attachmentStatus.\n- 135 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Ui and both test suites): DataFilePath is deleted.\n  - Experiment.dataFileOpt holds a DataAttachment.\n  - ExperimentDataProxy gains attachDataFile and attachmentStatus and loads by attachment.\n  - createFileBacked (kit) reads the picked file and works through the kit; loadAndValidate takes the attachment.\n  - The picker passes a FileName. New: DataFileAttachFailed and KitError.caption.\n- 136 IMPLEMENT (Ui): loading a collection computes each attachment's status and flags changed and missing data.\n- 137 IMPLEMENT: LibraryVersionRef and EntryReference.\n  - LibraryEntryContent.references; referencedEntryIds now derives from it.\n  - VersionRef.entryReference, ElementBinding.entryReferenceOpt, Experiment.libraryReferences.\n- 138 IMPLEMENT: KitProxy.listSnapshots / writeSnapshot over library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json. Adds SnapshotExistsErr; the folder snapshot is byte-identical to the catalogue file.\n- 139 IMPLEMENT: Domain KitLibrary.fs (after CatalogueImport.fs).\n  - KitLibraryError; KitLibraryContext { kit; imports }.\n  - snapshotReferences: closure, pin first, write once, keep the kit's copy.\n  - ADD_TEST KitLibraryTests.\n- 140 IMPLEMENT: ImportOrigin.KitSnapshotOrigin and decide's kit defaults.\n  - Defaults keep the kit's copy; add, add version, fork and re-bind are offered.\n  - No category re-binding.\n- 141 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryContext.resolveSnapshots over CatalogueImportProxy.decideEntry.\n- 142 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryOverlay, EntryReplacement, KitLibraryStores.\n  - overlaidWith on LibraryProxy, MaterialProxy, SampleProxy and CategoryProxy.\n  - openOverlay.\n- 143 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryContext.confirm (apply, then pin what an add choice wrote).\n- 144 IMPLEMENT (Ui): ImportDialogRequest.ResolveKitSnapshot and the kit captions of ImportDecision.actionCaption.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The constructor holds no kit until S4.3. Its brief: TableAndElementRotationModel holds a KitContext in place of experimentData; the Program.fs windows take a KitContext; the KitFolderPicker.\n   - Changing Experiment.dataFileOpt forces the constructor's attach flow to change in this section.\n   - So the data seam (ExperimentDataProxy) carries attach and status and is built over one kit.\n   - The composition roots (AppContext, defaultExperimentProxies) compose it over the session's in-memory kit, as they compose the scene and collection seams in memory today.\n   - Attaching a real picked file still works: the Storage seam reads its bytes, so an in-memory kit can hold the copy.\n   - S4.3 replaces that kit with the opened folder kit.\n2. Copy-in takes bytes, not an outside path.\n   - So the in-memory kit needs no outside world.\n   - The folder copy writes exactly those bytes, with a no-overwrite move, so the hash is of the bytes the kit holds.\n   - The picked-file read is the data seam's one IO of its own.\n3. \"In place\" means the picked absolute name lies under the kit folder: KitFolder.tryKitPathOf, pure path arithmetic. The in-memory folder stands for C:/in-memory-kit.\n4. The status runs on open.\n   - Today the constructor opens experiments by loading a saved collection, so that arm computes the statuses (step 136).\n   - The check before each fit is S11.2's; its brief names S4.2's flag.\n5. The snapshot trigger.\n   - The brief's 'binding a sample, material or preset' is a reference recorded in kit content.\n   - Kit content that binds library versions exists from S4.3: the experiment and setup files.\n   - S4.2 delivers the closure snapshot (KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences) and an experiment's references (Experiment.libraryReferences).\n   - S7.1 (items) and S11.5 (promote) call it, as their briefs say.\n   - The constructor's binding is not wired here, because the constructor has no kit. The S4.3 mapper SHOULD call snapshotReferences when it writes experiment and setup files.\n6. The open path is complete and tested, in Domain and in the dialog's MVU: resolveSnapshots, then the import dialog's ResolveKitSnapshot, then confirm, then openOverlay. Its opener is the kit open of S4.3 (the KitFolderPicker) and S5.2 (the start screen).\n7. Kit-origin defaults.\n   - Applying a kit row's default writes nothing (001 sec E: 'nothing changes in the database unconfirmed').\n   - The user opts in to Add to my library, Add this version, or a fork.\n   - A category name collision offers no re-binding, because nothing in a kit binds a category.\n8. Re-binding is session-scoped: confirm answers it and openOverlay applies it.\n   - Persisting it would rewrite kit references that the S4.3+ formats hold.\n   - .kit-json gains no field.\n9. Pins.\n   - snapshotReferences pins only the versions it writes, and pins before writing (export's order).\n   - confirm pins what an add choice wrote.\n   - Resolution and the overlay never pin: opening changes nothing unconfirmed.\n10. Overlay reads go through step 25's decoders, so no entry id becomes a kind's id anywhere else (ELEV006 forbids LibraryEntryId to ElementValueId). openOverlay resolves re-bound entries to held envelopes.\n11. Reuse, never a second copy.\n    - LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText writes the snapshot files: one byte form for catalogue, database and kit.\n    - The no-overwrite writer shares writeBytesAtomically's body.\n    - referencedEntryIds derives from references: one walk.\n    - Resolution calls decideEntry: one decision body. confirm calls apply.\n12. DataFilePath's two remaining mentions are spec 0044 history notes, in MuellerReconstruction.fs and MuellerDataStore.fs, files that S9 rewrites. Editing them would pull in unit-tests, so step 135's closing grep excludes them.\n13. Names: every new name was checked unused in the tree, STL and the spec (specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py). versionRef is a local in Experiments.fs, so the envelope member is libraryVersionRef.\n14. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s42/seam.json).\n    - Domain, Storage and Tests steps run build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered; whole_suite light, 13 s).\n    - Steps 135, 136 and 144 add ui-smoke (all_discovered; light, 27 s) and ui-tests selected by the classes they touch. Those classes match seam-plan's.\n    - Seam-plan's kit-acceptance on 135 and 136 is the shared-test-project artefact. KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1 (brief), so it is not selected. The extra gates on 144 are the final-step artefact.\n    - unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these files.\n15. Budget: 13 steps against a soft 12-22.\n16. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: Domain KitLibrary.fs; Tests KitLibraryTests.fs.\n17. Validation.\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note (the final step is not WIRE), as before this section.\n    - A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes with no findings.\n    - A negative probe, one consumer removed from step 135's edits, is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS, so the consumer census is enforced.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s42/build_s42.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S4.3 (Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go): appended steps 145-156 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (25 obligations, 12 acceptance bindings, 12 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 145 IMPLEMENT (Domain): KitFolder.namedKitFile (the kit named for the folder's leaf); KitFolderPicker { pickKitFolder : unit -> Async<KitFolder option> }; KitContext.openOrInitialise (open read-write, initialise only a folder holding no kit, KitLockedErr passed through); KitContext.createInMemory (an initialised in-memory kit, no lock).\n- 146 IMPLEMENT: the experiment file. ExperimentId.fileStem (E<n>), ExperimentFile, schema/experiment.schema.json + validateExperimentFile, new Storage KitContentFiles.fs (after KitFolderStore.fs) with ExperimentFile.fileText / KitFileText.parseExperimentFile. ADD_TEST KitContentFileJsonTests.\n- 147 IMPLEMENT: the setup file of a scene. SceneName.fileStem, SceneFile (the name kept inside), SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences, schema/setup.schema.json + validateSceneFile, the codec.\n- 148 IMPLEMENT: typed members on KitProxy: writeExperiment, deleteExperiment, readExperiments (by id; one unreadable or misnamed file refuses the read), writeScene, readScene, readSceneNames. SceneRoundTripTests and ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests re-pointed at kit folders.\n- 149 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment / recordScene: snapshotReferences first, then the write (the S4.2 mapper's request: S4.3 calls snapshotReferences when it writes experiment and setup files).\n- 150 IMPLEMENT (Ui): new KitOpening.fs (before TableAndElementRotationView.fs): ClockProvider.system, OpenedKit (library, data seam, experiments, scenes, snapshot rows, overlay; pendingDecisions, withRebindings), openKitAt, KitFolderPicker.ofWindow (Avalonia), scratchKit. ADD_TEST KitOpeningTests.\n- 151 IMPLEMENT: Scene.SceneProxy and AppContext.scenes deleted. DELETE_TEST SceneProxyTests -> SceneRoundTripTests (the SceneName and SnapMode facts migrate; the two proxy facts go).\n- 152 IMPLEMENT: the model holds kit + kitStatus in place of the collection store, name, list and status; initWith works in the scratch kit; loadKit (step 136's open-time statuses moved there); commit / attach record and remove deletes the experiment file; the collection messages, ids and ExperimentCollectionProxy (+ store, ExperimentCollectionError, CollectionName.tryCreate) deleted; AppContext loses experimentData and experimentCollections. DELETE_TEST ExperimentCollectionProxyTests -> ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests. After it, git grep \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/ finds nothing (S4.4's invariant).\n- 153 IMPLEMENT: scene save and load in the constructor: SceneSetName / SceneSave / SceneLoad, sceneName, savedScenes, the Scene: row, ids sceneNameField, saveSceneButton, savedScenes, savedScene. ADD_TEST SceneSaveLoadTests.\n- 154 WIRE_UI: MainConstructorWindow / InverseConstructorWindow (context, opened : OpenedKit), library stores overlaid with the kit's snapshots, the kit released on Closed; LauncherWindow gains pickerFor : TopLevel -> KitFolderPicker; Main and Inverse pick, then openKitAt; launcherKitErrorText. TestAppScope.kitPickerOf; every window-building test passes a folder kit.\n- 155 WIRE_UI: a foreign lock shows the holder with Open read-only / Cancel on one row (positive / negative colours, a gap); Open read-only opens over the read-only context.\n- 156 WIRE_UI: resolution on open: pending snapshot rows open the import dialog (ResolveKitSnapshot) first; Apply opens the constructor over the re-bound overlay; Cancel closes the kit and opens nothing.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. KitFolderPicker answers Async<KitFolder option>, not the brief's unit -> KitFolder option: Avalonia's folder dialog (IStorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync) completes on the UI thread, and blocking the dispatcher on it deadlocks. Headless tests answer at once, so Async.StartImmediate completes synchronously.\n2. The windows take (context : AppContext, opened : OpenedKit). OpenedKit carries the KitContext (opened.library.kit) with what was read and resolved at open, because a window cannot fail: the reads (experiments, scenes), the snapshot resolution and the overlay come first, and a kit whose files do not read is refused on the launcher and closed again, so it is never opened with an experiment left out.\n3. \"In place of experimentData\": .spec-md sec 0.1 says the constructor hosts a KitContext in place of the scene and collection seams. The measured-data seam stays a model field, as the seam tests substitute (AGENTS.md), but it is built over the window's kit (OpenedKit.experimentData), never app-scoped, so AppContext loses experimentData too (the S4.2 mapper's interpretation 1 anticipated this).\n4. The model held no scene seam (only AppContext did) and had no scene save/load surface. The collection builder's name / Save / saved-list row is replaced by a Scene: row with the same shape, so saving and loading a scene are semantic messages backed by buttons. The kit is the collection: every committed experiment is its own E<n>.experiment-json, loaded when the kit opens; named collections have no kit file kind (001 sec A), and 001 sec L grows the Study from them in S11.\n5. CollectionName and ExperimentCollectionSnapshot stay in ExperimentCollectionStore.fs, because SolverHandoffView consumes them until S11.5 deletes the hand-off; ExperimentCollectionError and CollectionName.tryCreate go with their only users.\n6. Writes are transactional in the model: the collection changes only when the kit write succeeded; a failure is shown in kitStatus. A removal treats MissingKitFileErr as done. Removal snapshots nothing and deletes no snapshot.\n7. Resolution on open is wired here (step 156) because the S4.2 mapper named S4.3's opener as its first caller and neither the S4.3 nor the S5.2 brief carries it; S5.2's start screen calls the same openKitAt and the same dialog flow.\n8. The kit id is minted in openKitAt (Guid.NewGuid) and the system clock is ClockProvider.system in KitOpening.fs, the code that first opens a kit (S4.1 interpretation 10). The kit's author on New is Environment.UserName.\n9. Test scenes and the TestWindows heads work in a scratch in-memory kit (KitContext.createInMemory), so initWith / initMainWith / initInverse keep their signatures and their many test consumers stay untouched; recording into it snapshots through the model's catalogueImports. SolverHandoffWindowTests binds presets over an otherwise empty import seam, so it takes the app library's seam (TestAppScope.freshAppContext).\n10. Scene names keep the lab's characters (step 24's FileStem.ofText); two names differing only in characters Windows forbids share one file, the later save replacing it. The name is stored in the file.\n11. The S4.4 invariant \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" becomes true at step 152 (stated in its acceptance and restated in 156); it is not declared on this section (.user-md: never on the section that makes it true).\n12. Names: every new name was checked unused in the tree, STL and the spec (specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py). KitFolder.namedKitFile avoids the step-125 test helper newKitFile. Field- and case-level contract symbols were resolved in the inventory (specs/0050/.artifacts/s43/symcheck.py) to keep each consumer census exact.\n13. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s43/seam.json).\n    - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered; whole_suite light) on every step; ui-smoke (all_discovered; light) on 150-156.\n    - ui-tests on 151-156 adopts seam-plan's classes: 151-153 change the constructor model, initWith and the commit path under nearly every model test (ExperimentControlsTests commits 12 times), so the selection is broad. WireUiFinalCompositionTests is dropped from 152-156 because its only ui-tests fact is deleted at 152 (an empty selector arm).\n    - Seam-plan's kit-acceptance on 151-156 is the shared-test-project artefact; KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1 (brief). unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these files.\n14. Budget: 12 steps against a soft 12-22.\n15. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: Storage KitContentFiles.fs, schema/experiment.schema.json, schema/setup.schema.json; Ui KitOpening.fs; Tests KitContentFileJsonTests.fs, KitOpeningTests.fs; Ui.Tests SceneSaveLoadTests.fs.\n16. Validation.\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only \"SELECTION_REQUIRED step 156 [unit-tests]\": step 156 is a WIRE_UI step and, until the next section is appended, the spec's final step, so the whole-suite final-step rule applies to it. This is the mid-campaign artefact that replaced the earlier sec 9.3 note.\n    - A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes with no findings.\n    - A negative probe, AppContextTests.fs removed from step 152's edits, is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS on three retired symbols, so the consumer census is enforced.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s43/build_s43.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py; logs build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S4.4 (The .ocproj aggregate is deleted): appended steps 157-161 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (19 obligations, 5 acceptance bindings, 5 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 157 IMPLEMENT: Report.fs loses its two project-only modules.\n  - DesignHistory (ChangeKind, DiffIdentity, DiffItem, ProjectDiff, historyFolder, appendRevision, diffRevisions) and Report (ReportFormat, generate) are deleted, with ExportImportTests' AC-I11 fact.\n  - The Storage project's Giraffe.ViewEngine.StrongName reference goes; the report HTML was its only use.\n  - MaterialLibrary stays.\n- 158 IMPLEMENT: History.fs (EditHistory: ofPresent, push, undo, redo) is deleted with HistoryTests' two AC-I7 facts.\n- 159 IMPLEMENT: the project file and the autosave go.\n  - ProjectFile.fs (extension, saveProject, openProject) and RecentFiles' Autosave module are deleted. RecentFiles keeps its recent-files list for S5.1, and its doc drops .ocproj.\n  - DELETE_TEST RoundTripTests -> KitContentFileJsonTests: its three storage facts hold for kit files in step 146's facts.\n  - HistoryTests' AC-I6 fact goes. The R-1 bump fact stays, its paths written as kit folders.\n  - The .gitignore *.autosave rule goes.\n  - ExperimentDataStore's doc drops any sentence that still points at ProjectFile.\n- 160 IMPLEMENT: the project codec, the project schema and the record go.\n  - Deleted: ProjectJson.fs; SchemaValidation's project schema, its lazy and validate; schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json; Domain Project.fs.\n  - MaterialLibrary's materialEntry check moves with what it reads. New schema/material-metadata.schema.json holds the materialEntry closure (materialEntry, dispersionModel, thermoOptic, unitOfMeasure) verbatim. validateEntryElement answers validateWith over it.\n  - DELETE_TEST ProjectJsonRoundtripTests -> TableViewTests: the fresh-table fact moves unchanged.\n  - PlacementTests' AC-A6 fact goes; SceneRoundTripTests holds the placement round trip since step 148.\n  - StackEditTests drops its unused open of Domain.Project.\n  - New fact: ExportImportTests' 'a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr'.\n  - The docs of Sidecar and SidecarTests stop naming the record.\n- 161 IMPLEMENT: no 'ocproj' under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/ (001 sec T 'From section 4').\n  - The .ocproj wording goes from GroupsLibrary's and Groups.fs' docs, the groups schema description and GroupsRoundTripTests' doc.\n  - EnvironmentRoundTripTests' two old-file facts graft kit-folder literals.\n  - Any wording steps 151/152 left in Scene.fs, ExperimentCollectionStore.fs or the Domain.fsproj comments goes.\n  - The .gitignore *.binz comment drops its .ocproj sentence; the rule stays.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Report.fs keeps its MaterialLibrary module.\n   - The metadata-only material file is a live surface of its own: S1.2 step 11 and S1.7 step 46 maintain it, and ExportImportTests proves it.\n   - It read the project schema's $defs (Report.fs:materialEntrySchema), so its materialEntry closure moves to its own schema file in the same step that deletes the project schema. That is a move, never a transient copy.\n   - validateEntryElement reuses step 29's validateWith, the one evaluation body. Its refusal now carries the evaluation messages; no fact asserted the old fixed text.\n   - Report.fs keeps its file name; renaming it is outside the brief.\n2. Export's ChartHandle and exportChartImage lose their only caller, Report.generate. They stay as Export's own sec I.7 chart-image surface, which the aggregate does not own.\n   - The root Directory.Build.targets PackageVersion for Giraffe.ViewEngine.StrongName is not touched.\n3. The brief asked to check six modules:\n   - Sidecar stays: SynthesisFitPage and JobRunnerCancelTests use it. It loses only its doc sentence about the project.\n   - GroupsLibrary keeps its surface and loses only wording.\n   - Localization.fs and UserEnvironment.fs need no edit: after step 21 they read CanonicalJson.options and name nothing of the aggregate.\n   - History.fs is deleted: its only consumer was HistoryTests, and .spec-md sec 8 adds no undo history.\n   - Report.fs is item 1.\n4. BeamTree, SourceSpec, Placement and Table stay; other code uses them.\n5. StackEditTests.fs opens OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project without using it. The record's census does not list it, so step 160 names it to keep the build green.\n6. Census-only scope in step 160.\n   - The record's baseline census also names History.fs (deleted at 158), ProjectFile.fs and RoundTripTests.fs (deleted at 159), and RecentFiles.fs and HistoryTests.fs (emptied of the record at 159).\n   - They are in 160's edits only so the retirement covers its whole census; the how_to says nothing more changes in them.\n   - The alternative was one step deleting every consumer with the record, about 22 paths.\n7. Conditional wording scope.\n   - ExperimentDataStore.fs (159) is in scope because step 135 rewrote its doc and may have kept the ProjectFile precedent sentence.\n   - Scene.fs, ExperimentCollectionStore.fs and OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj (161) are in scope because steps 151 and 152 rewrote their .ocproj wording.\n   - Each step's closing grep makes the outcome checkable.\n8. The *.autosave rule goes with the Autosave module (159). The *.binz comment's .ocproj sentence goes in the sweep (161), since Sidecar stays.\n9. EnvironmentRoundTripTests' two old-environment-file facts keep their assertions; only the grafted array's .ocproj names change. The brief said to delete or re-point; re-pointing keeps coverage of the total load.\n10. The S4.4 invariant 's19-t4-no-ocproj' (001 sec T 'From section 4') becomes true at step 161. It is not declared on this section (.user-md: never on the section that makes it true).\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s44/seam.json).\n    - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests run on every step; constructor-unit-tests is all_discovered (whole_suite light, measured 13 s).\n    - No step edits Ui, Ui.Tests or App, which is ui-tests' and ui-smoke's applies_to. So no ui-tests class is touched and none is selected; the brief's 'ui-tests by touched class' selects nothing.\n    - seam-plan proposes exactly build, constructor-unit-tests and elevation for 157-160. Its full roster on 161 is the current-final-step artefact.\n    - unit-tests' and kit-acceptance's applies_to cover none of these paths.\n12. Budget: 5 steps against a soft 6-12. Each step is one green, self-contained deletion; splitting further would only add census-only scope.\n13. New artifact the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: Storage schema/material-metadata.schema.json, read by MaterialLibrary.validateEntryElement. Sec 0.1's ProjectJson / ProjectFile row could also name Report.fs (DesignHistory and Report deleted) and History.fs (deleted).\n14. Names: schema/material-metadata.schema.json, its $id https://berreman/schema/material-metadata.json, and the new fact's name are unused in the tree and in STL.\n15. Validation.\n    - On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 161, is not WIRE.\n    - A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes with no findings.\n    - A negative probe, HistoryTests.fs removed from step 160's edits, is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS on OpticalConstructorProject, so the consumer census is enforced.\n    - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s44/build_s44.py (stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py, symcheck.py; logs build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S5.1 (The kit history over the per-user preferences): appended steps 162-169 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (23 obligations, 8 acceptance bindings, 8 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 162 IMPLEMENT: Domain WorkbenchSettings gains KitHistoryLimit (value, defaultValue 100, tryCreate) and WorkbenchSettingsError.NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr. The record is unchanged here.\n- 163 IMPLEMENT: the settings carry the limit.\n  - WorkbenchSettings.kitHistoryLimit, 100 in defaults.\n  - ConfigKey.kitHistoryLimit (\"KitHistoryLimit\").\n  - The KitHistoryLimit door. The three existing count doors' shared body moves into one private extension member, AppSettings.ConfigValue.tryPositiveCount, which all four doors call.\n  - loadWorkbenchSettings reads the key, writing the default back.\n  - Tests: WorkbenchSettingsTests (two literals gain the field, one new fact) and an AppConfigTests door fact.\n- 164 IMPLEMENT: new Domain KitHistory.fs (after KitFolders.fs).\n  - KitStar (StarredKit / UnstarredKit, tags 1 and 2, tryOfWire).\n  - KitHistoryEntry { folder; kitId; name; lastOpened; star }.\n  - KitHistory { schemaVersion; entries } with empty, star, unstar, forget, evict and displayOrder.\n  - ADD_TEST KitHistoryTests.\n- 165 ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:KitHistoryProxy>: KitFolderPresence, KitHistoryError (KitHistoryWriteErr), KitHistoryProxy { readHistory; writeHistory; probeFolder } and createInMemory (presentFolders).\n  - KitHistoryProxyContract with KitHistoryProxyTests (in memory). ADD_TEST KitHistoryProxyTests.\n- 166 IMPLEMENT: CanonicalJson.options gains the KitStar int-tag converter (step 28's rule). CanonicalJsonTests' two int-tag facts cover it.\n- 167 IMPLEMENT: the history file's text.\n  - schema/kit-history.schema.json and SchemaValidation.validateKitHistory.\n  - New Storage KitHistoryStore.fs (after KitContentFiles.fs) with KitHistoryText, KitHistory.fileName (kit-history.json), KitHistory.fileText and KitHistoryText.parseKitHistory over step 124's parseVersionedText.\n  - ADD_TEST KitHistoryJsonTests.\n- 168 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <STORE:KitHistoryProxy>: KitHistoryProxy.create (preferences : FolderName).\n  - A missing or unreadable file reads as the empty history, with Logger.logWarn.\n  - Writes are atomic through FileName.writeBytesAtomically, creating the folder; a failure is KitHistoryWriteErr.\n  - The probe is Directory.Exists.\n  - KitHistoryProxyFolderTests runs the contract facts plus four of its own under the test output. ADD_TEST KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.\n- 169 IMPLEMENT: RecentFiles.bump moves into KitHistory.bump (limit, clock, folder, kitFile).\n  - RecentFiles.fs is deleted whole (maxRecent, prefsPath, loadRecent, pushRecent, recent.json).\n  - DELETE_TEST HistoryTests -> KitHistoryTests: the R-1 fact moves as the MRU fact, and three bump facts are added.\n  - UserEnvironment.fs' and EnvironmentRoundTripTests' docs name the kit history instead.\n  - Afterwards nothing under Berreman/ names RecentFiles, recent.json, maxRecent, pushRecent, loadRecent or prefsPath.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The move of bump lands last (169), in the same step that deletes RecentFiles.fs whole.\n   - A move creates the new home and deletes the old body in one step. pushRecent calls bump, so bump cannot leave while RecentFiles' IO stays.\n   - recent.json's IO goes in the change that completes its replacement: the store exists from 168.\n   - Nothing in the product ever called loadRecent or pushRecent.\n2. KitHistory.bump takes the opened kit's KitFile (its id and name fill the entry's kit id and name cache) and the ClockProvider (001 sec F 'over a clock provider'), reading the clock once.\n   - A reopened kit keeps its star; its folder text, id, name and time are refreshed.\n3. Eviction is the history's ceiling. When every other entry is starred, the just-opened kit is the only unstarred entry, and bump evicts it, so the history never exceeds the limit through a bump.\n   - 001 sec F: 'up to KitHistoryLimit', and the cap evicts the oldest UNSTARRED entry and never a starred one.\n   - The alternative, never evicting the entry just pushed, would let a bump exceed the cap.\n   - Fact 'a bump into a full starred history never drops a star' pins this.\n4. 'Oldest' means the earliest lastOpened, the entry later in the list winning a tie.\n   - The display order sorts each group by lastOpened, newest first, with a stable sort, so equal times keep the stored order.\n   - Star, unstar and forget never evict.\n5. readHistory is total (unit -> KitHistory), as loadRecent was. The brief says a missing or unreadable file gives an empty history and a logged warning, read literally: both cases log one Logger.logWarn naming the file and the cause.\n   - A read never changes the file. The next write replaces an unreadable file; there is no migration (.spec-md sec 7: the kit history starts empty).\n6. The history file follows the kit file's stack (step 124), as one file of its own: canonical JSON, schemaVersion 1, its own schema, and parseVersionedText.\n   - FileExtension \".json\" names it in UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr.\n   - The star is stored as its int tag through a CanonicalJson converter, step 28's rule (AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is an int).\n   - KitHistoryText mirrors KitFileText.\n   - KitHistory.fileName (\"kit-history.json\", the brief's name) is a Storage extension, because only the store uses it.\n7. The probe answers KitFolderPresence (KitFolderPresent / KitFolderMissing), a named two-case union and never a bool.\n   - The in-memory probe answers Present for a folder equal to one of the folders it was given.\n   - S5.2 renders the missing state; S5.1 adds no row type.\n8. Folder identity is the moved rule, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase over the folder text, written once as a private member of KitHistory.\n   - ELEV010 checks public members as well as module functions (Softellect Analyzers/NoPrimitiveBesideElevated.fs: only private ones are sanctioned), so no public member answers a bool beside our types.\n9. The KitHistoryLimit door reuses the existing count-door body instead of adding a fourth copy (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy').\n   - The body moves to a private extension member of AppSettings.ConfigValue. Members are exempt from ELEV003 and private members from ELEV010, so no boundary mark is needed.\n   - The three existing doors keep their texts and answers. The new AppConfigTests fact proves all four doors share the body.\n10. Census-only scope at 163, step 160's precedent.\n   - The inventory census of WorkbenchSettings is AppConfig.fs, WorkbenchSettings.fs, WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs, Ui/AppContext.fs and seven Ui.Tests files (AppContextTests, LauncherTests, TableAndElementRotationTests, WindowLauncherTests, WireUi0040CompositionTests, WireUiCompositionTests, WireUiFinalCompositionTests).\n   - Those that build no record literal are in the edits only so the change_shape covers its census; the how_to says nothing changes in them.\n   - A negative probe dropped AppContext.fs from 163 and HistoryTests.fs from 169. It is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS, so the census is enforced.\n11. Gates.\n   - The brief listed build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests. .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' adds ui-smoke on steps that touch Ui or App code, and ui-tests by touched class.\n   - So 163 (AppConfig.fs, the AppContext.fs census and AppConfigTests) runs ui-smoke whole and ui-tests over AppConfigTests, AppContextTests, LauncherTests, TableAndElementRotationTests and WindowLauncherTests.\n   - 169 (UserEnvironment.fs docs) runs ui-smoke whole. seam-plan proposes no ui-tests class there.\n   - Every step runs constructor-unit-tests all_discovered (whole_suite light, measured 13 s). ui-smoke is also whole_suite light (27 s).\n   - seam-plan proposed kit-acceptance at 163 because the step edits Ui.Tests facts. It is not adopted: kit-acceptance cannot run before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs (the brief; steps 154 and 156 did the same).\n   - seam-plan also proposed WireUiFinalCompositionTests for 163's ui-tests. It and the other two WireUi*Composition classes are left out: the checker reports SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM, because their facts carry the ui-smoke trait, and ui-smoke runs whole.\n   - unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these paths.\n12. A request to the S5.2 mapper: compose KitHistoryProxy.create over locations.preferencesFolder (DataLocations, step 81) where the start screen's proxies are built, and pass settings.kitHistoryLimit to KitHistory.bump.\n   - .spec-md sec 0.2 names AppContext.create and the start screen as KitHistoryProxy's invokers. The S5.2 brief injects the history and kit proxies into the start-screen model.\n   - S5.1 adds no AppContext field, because no S5.1 surface reads one.\n13. The S5.2 invariant s20-no-recent-json becomes true at 169. It is not declared on S5.1 (.user-md: never on the section that makes it true). Step 169 rewrites UserEnvironment.fs' recent.json wording so the invariant holds.\n14. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n   - Domain KitHistory.fs.\n   - Storage KitHistoryStore.fs.\n   - Storage schema/kit-history.schema.json.\n   - Sec 0.1's RecentFiles row can read: RecentFiles.fs is deleted whole, and bump moves to KitHistory.bump.\n15. Names checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the section plan:\n   - Types and cases: KitStar, StarredKit, UnstarredKit, KitHistoryEntry, KitHistory, KitFolderPresence, KitFolderPresent, KitFolderMissing, KitHistoryError, KitHistoryWriteErr, KitHistoryProxy, KitHistoryLimit, NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr, KitHistoryText.\n   - Members and modules: KitHistoryStore, validateKitHistory, parseKitHistory, tryPositiveCount.\n   - STL's probeFolder and readHistory are private STL locals, not namesakes the rules see.\n16. Budget: 8 steps against a soft 8-14.\n17. Validation.\n   - On the real folder, executability check reports only the expected notes: the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note (169 is not WIRE) and the two unresolved <STORE:KitHistoryProxy> placeholders the cycle mints, as S4.1 did.\n   - A deep copy with the placeholder neutralised, plus a bound placeholder final WIRE step, passes with no findings.\n   - Build script: specs/0050/.artifacts/s51/build_s51.py (stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py, symcheck.py).\n   - Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-baseline.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-deep.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log, seam-wired.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S5.2 (The kit start screen and the Launcher): appended steps 170-180 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (27 obligations, 11 acceptance bindings, 11 behavior seams, 1 closing scope). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 170 IMPLEMENT (Domain KitHistory.fs): KitHistoryFilter (none), KitHistory.entriesMatching (displayOrder narrowed by name or folder, trimmed, ignoring case), KitHistoryRow { entry; presence } and KitHistory.rowsMatching filter probe.\n- 171 IMPLEMENT (Domain): KitHistory.relocate missing found (keeps id, name, time, star and place; one entry per folder) and KitHistoryProxy.changeHistory (read, change, write, answer). A new KitHistoryProxyContract fact runs over both stores; the folder suite adds a failed-write fact.\n- 172 IMPLEMENT (Ui KitOpening.fs): openExistingKitAt (open read-write, never initialise; NotAKitFolderErr and KitLockedErr write nothing). openKitAt's post-open body moves into one private openedOver that both call.\n- 173 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryError.openFailedCaption and KitLockHolder.openElsewhereCaption in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain, moved from the launcher's literals (steps 154, 155), which the launcher now renders.\n- 174 IMPLEMENT: KitFolderPicker.pickThen (step 154's Async.StartImmediate start) and OpenedKit.resolveAndShow (step 156's resolution on open: import dialog, re-binding, close on cancel) move from Program.fs into KitOpening.fs; the launcher calls them.\n- 175 IMPLEMENT: AppContext.kitHistory = KitHistoryProxy.create locations.preferencesFolder in compose (the S5.1 mapper's request 12).\n- 176 IMPLEMENT: new Ui KitStartView.fs (after TableAndElementRotationView.fs): KitStartContext { kitHistory; limit; clock; author; imports; picker; showKit }, KitStartOffer (NoKitStartOffer / MakeKitOffer / ReadOnlyKitOffer), KitRelocation, KitStartModel, KitStartMsg (StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit, LocateKit, FilterKitHistory), initKitStart and updateKitStart; KitHistoryError.notSavedCaption. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.\n- 177 IMPLEMENT: the open messages CreateKit (openKitAt read-write: initialise or open), OpenKit (openExistingKitAt), OpenKitReadOnly, DismissKitStartOffer and KitOpenFailed. A successful open bumps the history through changeHistory (limit, clock, folder, kit file) and calls showKit once; KitLockedErr becomes the read-only offer, NotAKitFolderErr the Make this a kit offer, any other error the status.\n- 178 IMPLEMENT: kitStartView (New kit…, Open kit…, status, offer pair on one row, filter box, history rows with name, folder, last open, star; missing rows greyed with Locate… and Remove from history), the start-screen ConstructorUiId group (9 fixed + 4 positional ids), KitHistoryEntry.lastOpenedCaption and KitFolder.notAKitCaption. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.\n- 179 IMPLEMENT: new Ui KitStartWindow.fs (after AppContext.fs): KitStartWindow(context, mode, pickerFor, showConstructor), titled by mode, keepOnScreen, its hand-off through resolveAndShow, closing itself once the constructor opens; ConstructorUiId.kitStartWindow; ScrollExtentTests joins it.\n- 180 WIRE_UI (Program.fs): Main and Inverse open KitStartWindow in the forward and inverse mode through KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn; the launcher's kit-open function, error text, read-only row and the ids launcherKitErrorText, launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton and launcherCancelKitOpenButton are deleted. LauncherTests' kit facts are re-pointed through the start screen (one renamed), and WireUiFinalCompositionTests renders the screen in both modes.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The open flow moves from the launcher to the start screen without a copied body.\n   - The two failure texts (173) and the picker start and resolution on open (174) first move to reusable homes, and the launcher calls them.\n   - The launcher's remaining open function, its error text, its read-only row and their three ids are deleted at 180, the change that replaces them (.spec-md sec 4).\n   - The start screen owns the open-time read-only offer from 180 on. S5.3 adds the read-only title marker and the disabled writes (step 155's note).\n2. Open kit… is open-only through a NEW function, openExistingKitAt, not a flag on openKitAt (the spec rule: introduce a new function rather than a flag). Both share one private body.\n   - NotAKitFolderErr becomes the Make this a kit offer. Its accept sends CreateKit, whose initialise-or-open keeps the folder's files (001 sec F).\n3. New kit… on a folder that is already a kit opens that kit, because step 145's openOrInitialise keeps an existing kit file; nothing is refused.\n4. Locate… re-points the history entry only (KitHistory.relocate); it does not open the kit. The row is listed present again and opens on a press.\n   - Remove from history is offered on missing rows, as 001 sec F lists it; ForgetKit itself works for any folder.\n5. A successful open bumps the history before the hand-off, read-only opens included.\n   - A cancelled import dialog leaves the bump, because the user chose the kit.\n   - A failed history write does not block the open; the status shows it.\n6. The start screen closes once the constructor opens, and the Launcher stays. Each Main or Inverse click opens a new screen; one-window-per-kit is S5.3's.\n7. History row ids are positional (ConstructorUiPosition, 0 first). A folder's text is not a safe id, and a copied kit folder carries the same kit id.\n8. Last-open times render in UTC, \"Last opened yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm UTC\", as KitLockHolder.describe renders a time (step 129), so the captions are deterministic under test.\n9. The screen's buttons reuse MaterialsWindowView.verbButton and actionButton (public since step 107, one look). Their ids are AutomationIds, so the tests press boxes at their centre (LibraryWindowTests.clickOn).\n10. KitStartWindow takes the app scope plus showConstructor, because the constructor windows live in OpticalConstructor.App, which Ui cannot reference. Program.fs passes KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn.\n11. Tests.\n   - The pure update facts live in OpticalConstructor.Tests (KitStartTests, gate constructor-unit-tests), as KitOpeningTests covers Ui's KitOpening (step 150).\n   - The headless view and window facts live in Ui.Tests KitStartWindowTests.\n   - LauncherTests keeps the composition facts through the launcher, re-pointed in place. One is renamed, because its name said \"launcher\".\n   - WireUiCompositionTests and WireUi0040CompositionTests build constructor windows directly, so they keep their code.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s52/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered; whole_suite light) run on every step. ui-smoke (all_discovered; light) runs on 172-180, the steps touching Ui or App code.\n   - ui-tests runs by class: LauncherTests on 173, 174 and 180 (Program.fs), AppContextTests on 175, KitStartWindowTests on 178, and KitStartWindowTests plus ScrollExtentTests on 179.\n   - seam-plan proposed every Ui.Tests class at 178 because the fsproj gains a compile line. Following steps 82 and 107, only the new class is selected.\n   - seam-plan's WireUiFinalCompositionTests ui-tests arm at 180 is not adopted, because all its facts carry the ui-smoke trait (an empty arm, S5.1 note 11). ui-smoke covers it whole.\n   - kit-acceptance is not adopted: it cannot run before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs (the brief). unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these paths.\n13. Budget: 11 steps against a soft 12-22. Each step is one move or one surface (filter, verbs, open-only, captions, hand-off, app history, model, open messages, view, window, wire). Splitting further would add gate runs without isolating any risk.\n14. Requests to later mappers:\n   - S6: Open kit from zip… adds OpenKitZip to KitStartMsg and openKitZipButton to the start-screen group. After extraction it opens the target folder through the same path (OpenKit).\n   - Close: the committed kits open from the start screen read-only through OpenKitReadOnly, which writes nothing to the kit.\n15. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2: Ui KitStartView.fs, KitStartWindow.fs; Tests KitStartTests.fs; Ui.Tests KitStartWindowTests.fs. Sec 0.1's Program.fs row holds: Main and Inverse open the kit start screen.\n16. Names were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec, with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py. Types and cases: KitHistoryFilter, KitHistoryRow, KitStartContext, KitStartOffer, NoKitStartOffer, MakeKitOffer, ReadOnlyKitOffer, KitRelocation, KitStartModel, KitStartMsg, CreateKit, OpenKit, OpenKitReadOnly, DismissKitStartOffer, StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit, LocateKit, FilterKitHistory, KitOpenFailed, KitStartWindow. Members and functions: entriesMatching, rowsMatching, relocate, changeHistory, openExistingKitAt, openedOver, openFailedCaption, openElsewhereCaption, pickThen, resolveAndShow, notSavedCaption, lastOpenedCaption, notAKitCaption, initKitStart, updateKitStart, kitStartView, showConstructorIn, KitConstructorWindows, and every new ConstructorUiId member.\n17. Validation.\n   - On the real folder, executability check reports only \"SELECTION_REQUIRED step 180 [unit-tests]\". Step 180 is a WIRE_UI step and, until the next section is appended, the spec's final step, so the whole-suite final-step rule applies to it (S4.3 note 16).\n   - A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes with no findings.\n   - A negative probe, LauncherTests.fs removed from step 180's edits, is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS on OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow, so the census is enforced.\n   - The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s52/build_s52.py and s52_steps.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-baseline.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S5.3 (The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations): appended steps 181-195 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (31 obligations, 15 acceptance bindings, 15 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 181-195). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 181 IMPLEMENT (Domain): KitFolder.canonical (backslashes to '/', trailing '/' removed, upper-cased). KitHistory's private folder comparison moves onto it, and its OrdinalIgnoreCase text compare is deleted, so the history and the window key share one rule.\n- 182 ADD_CONTRACT <SVC:ExplorerProxy> (Domain KitFolders.fs): ExplorerError (MissingFolderErr, ExplorerLaunchErr) with describe; ExplorerProxy { showFolder }; createInMemory (record). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests.\n- 183 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <SVC:ExplorerProxy> (Ui KitOpening.fs): ExplorerProxy.system. A missing folder is MissingFolderErr and nothing starts; otherwise explorer.exe starts with the full path; exceptions are ExplorerLaunchErr.\n- 184 IMPLEMENT: OpenedKit.folder (set through openedOver); the model's kitFolderOpt, kitCaption and kitWindowTitle ('<name>[ (read-only)] — <folder> — Optical Constructor — Main|Inverse'). ConstructorScene.mount sets the window title from the model. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.\n- 185 IMPLEMENT: read-only disables the write messages.\n  - model.kitWrites (ControlAvailability). Under ReadOnlyKitAccess, ExpCommit, ExpRemove, AttachDataFileTo and SceneSave answer 'The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.' through one guard and call no proxy.\n  - The view withholds Add/Update, Remove (new ExperimentControlsState.removalAvailability; rowActionButton gains an availability), Attach data file… and Save scene (availableWorkbenchButton).\n  - InverseConstructorTests' 'a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why' keeps ReadWriteKitAccess over the readOnlyView proxy, so the proxy's error is still what it shows.\n- 186 IMPLEMENT: the KitWindowShell { explorer; requestClose } seam (inert default) and the model's kitShell. Messages SwitchConstructorMode (sets constructorMode alone), ShowKitInExplorer and CloseKit.\n- 187 IMPLEMENT: reload.\n  - KitCheckOrigin (KitCheckOnActivation / KitCheckOnRequest); kitChanges : FileName list.\n  - CheckKitChanges, ReloadKitChanges (re-read the kit file, experiments and scene names, then recordStamps) and KeepMyKitChanges (recordStamps).\n  - loadKit's content body becomes one private function that the reload shares.\n- 188 IMPLEMENT: new Ui KitWindowView.fs (after KitStartView.fs).\n  - kitWindowView is the kit bar docked above mainView. The bar holds: 'Kit:' and the caption; the Kit menu verbs Show in Explorer, Reload changes and Close kit; the mode text and switch; the changes offer, Reload and Keep mine on one row; and kitStatus.\n  - kitStatus moves out of collectionBuilderView. Ten new ConstructorUiId members; ScrollExtentTests joins.\n- 189 WIRE_UI (Program.fs): ConstructorScene.mount runs mkProgram, capturing the dispatch. It seeds kitShell with ExplorerProxy.system and window.Close, renders kitWindowView, and dispatches CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation on every Activated.\n- 190 IMPLEMENT: one window per kit, the Ui half.\n  - WindowKey gains KitWindowKey of KitFolder. KitOpening gains KitWindowPresence (KitWindowActivated / NoKitWindowOpen), KitFolder.windowKey and KitFolder.activateKitWindow, which goes through WindowLauncher and only activates.\n  - KitStartContext.activateKitWindow is consulted first by CreateKit, OpenKit and OpenKitReadOnly. KitStartWindow closes itself after an activation.\n  - WireUiFinalCompositionTests' exhaustive root factory answers KitWindowKey with a typed error.\n- 191 WIRE_UI (Program.fs): KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn opens the window through WindowLauncher under opened.folder.windowKey. When a window already holds the kit, or the factory fails, the opened kit is closed again. LauncherTests gains the one-window acceptance.\n- 192 IMPLEMENT: Domain DataLocationKind (seven cases, all in field order) and Storage LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf. tryFileOf is moved out of recreate (step 87), which now calls it.\n- 193 IMPLEMENT: new Ui DataLocationsView.fs (after KitWindowView.fs) and the ids.\n  - DataLocationRow, DataLocations.rows (an in-memory library has no folder), DataLocationsContext { locations; explorer }, the model, OpenDataLocationFolder, init / update / view.\n  - Captions, uiKeys and three per-kind ids in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain; dataLocationsStatusText in UiIds.\n  - ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.\n- 194 IMPLEMENT: new Ui DataLocationsWindow.fs (after KitStartWindow.fs), titled 'Data locations', with keepOnScreen. WindowKey gains DataLocationsWindowKey. The root factory renders the window, and ScrollExtentTests joins it.\n- 195 WIRE_UI (Program.fs): the Launcher footer gains launcherDataLocationsLink, always enabled, which opens DataLocationsWindow(locations, ExplorerProxy.system) single-instance.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The lock warning is S5.2's. The start screen's ReadOnlyKitOffer (steps 177, 178, 180) already shows KitLockHolder.describe (user, machine, process, time, step 129) with Open read-only / Cancel on one row. S5.3 adds what step 155 left to it: the '(read-only)' title marker (184) and the disabled write messages (185).\n2. 'Disables every write message' means two things. The update refuses ExpCommit, ExpRemove, AttachDataFileTo and SceneSave under ReadOnlyKitAccess before any proxy call, and their controls are withheld. Nothing is hidden; later sections' write messages join the same guard.\n3. The Kit menu is the kit bar's verb row, not an Avalonia Menu and not a ribbon bay. A popup is not provable headless (the element-menu precedent, TableAndElementRotationView.fs:117), and the ribbon's order is operator-ruled (Add first, Details last, spec 0046). The bar sits outside the page's ScrollViewer, in its own file (.spec-md sec 4), so it is always in view.\n4. The mode switch uses the existing two-case ConstructorMode (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:246). WindowMode.fs's LibraryWindowMode is Browse / Select and does not fit. The switch keeps the window's type (MainConstructorWindow / InverseConstructorWindow); the title, the chart gate and the Data files section follow the mode.\n5. Reload re-reads the kit file, experiments and scene names, not only the changed files, through loadKit's body. The draft starts fresh as an open's does. Keep mine records the stamps, so the same changes are not offered again. A scratch kit is never checked. A read-only kit is checked and reloads, because neither verb writes.\n6. One window per kit reuses the host WindowRegistry (WindowLauncher.fs:108), keyed by the canonical folder; no second registry is written. Activation bumps nothing, because the history entry was bumped when the window opened. Choosing an open kit from another mode's screen activates the window in its current mode; the bar's switch changes it.\n7. The folder identity rule moves into KitFolder.canonical, used by the history and the window key. Two spellings of one folder (case, separators, trailing slash) are one kit.\n8. ExplorerProxy is one seam for Show in Explorer and Open folder. The system proxy refuses a missing folder (MissingFolderErr) and never creates one. No test asks it to show an existing folder. Real windows use the system proxy, so the headless window facts never press Show in Explorer or Open folder.\n9. Data locations lists the seven DataLocations fields. The library row shows the database file through LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf, the in-memory case without Open folder. The window is single-instance (DataLocationsWindowKey). The footer link is enabled even when the library fails to open.\n10. The title format is '<kit name>[ (read-only)] — <folder> — Optical Constructor — Main|Inverse'; the scratch kit omits the folder. kitCaption is the one body shared by the bar and the title.\n11. Tests.\n   - Pure model facts are in OpticalConstructor.Tests: KitWindowModelTests, DataLocationsTests and ExplorerProxyTests, plus KitTests, KitHistoryTests, KitOpeningTests, KitStartTests, LibraryDatabaseTests and WorkbenchSettingsTests.\n   - Headless facts are in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: KitWindowTests, DataLocationsWindowTests, LauncherTests, ScrollExtentTests and KitStartWindowTests.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s53/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, light) run on every step; ui-smoke on every step touching Ui or App code (183-191, 193-195).\n   - ui-tests runs by class: the new classes and the classes holding the facts of the code a step changes. InverseConstructorTests and SceneSaveLoadTests are selected where loadKit, the write arms or collectionBuilderView change (184, 185, 187, 188); ExperimentControlsTests at 185.\n   - At 184 and 193, seam-plan proposed every Ui.Tests class, because the fsproj gains a compile line. Following steps 82, 107 and 178, only the touched classes are selected.\n   - WireUiFinalCompositionTests is never a ui-tests arm: after step 152 all its facts carry the ui-smoke trait (S5.2 note 12).\n   - kit-acceptance is not adopted (not runnable before S12.1), and unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these paths.\n13. Contract effects follow earlier sections. New members, cases and fields are 'create'. MainConstructorWindow / InverseConstructorWindow (184, 189) and LauncherWindow (191, 195) are change_behavior, with their inventory consumers in the authorized edits.\n14. Budget: 15 steps against a soft 10-18.\n15. Requests to later mappers:\n   - S6: Send kit… and Copy experiments from another kit… join the kit bar's verb row in KitWindowView.fs, each a verbButton with a ConstructorUiId of the kit-bar group, sending a TableAndElementRotationMsg. Their kit writes go through the read-only guard of step 185.\n   - S7.2 (the flow strip) and later surfaces: kitWindowView docks the bar above mainView; a new surface keeps the bar outside its own ScrollViewer.\n   - Close: a whole-suite final step owns the SELECTION_REQUIRED finding below.\n16. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n   - Ui: KitWindowView.fs, DataLocationsView.fs, DataLocationsWindow.fs.\n   - Tests: ExplorerProxyTests.fs, KitWindowModelTests.fs, DataLocationsTests.fs.\n   - Ui.Tests: KitWindowTests.fs, DataLocationsWindowTests.fs.\n   - Sec 0.1's UiIds.fs and Program.fs rows hold: the kit bar, Data locations and the footer link.\n17. Names were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec, with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py.\n   - Types and cases: ExplorerProxy, ExplorerError, MissingFolderErr, ExplorerLaunchErr, KitWindowShell, KitCheckOrigin, KitCheckOnActivation, KitCheckOnRequest, KitWindowPresence, KitWindowActivated, NoKitWindowOpen, KitWindowKey, DataLocationsWindowKey, DataLocationKind and its seven cases, DataLocationRow, DataLocationsContext, DataLocationsModel, DataLocationsMsg, OpenDataLocationFolder, DataLocationsWindow, SwitchConstructorMode, ShowKitInExplorer, CloseKit, CheckKitChanges, ReloadKitChanges, KeepMyKitChanges.\n   - Members and functions: windowKey, activateKitWindow, kitWindowTitle, kitWrites, tryFileOf, kitWindowView, initDataLocations, updateDataLocations, dataLocationsView, kitShell, kitChanges, kitFolderOpt, and every new ConstructorUiId member.\n   - The ExperimentControlsState field is removalAvailability, because removeAvailability is already ElementPaletteControls' field.\n18. Validation.\n   - On the real folder, executability check reports only the two unresolved '<SVC:ExplorerProxy>' placeholders (steps 182, 183), which the cycle's minting step resolves.\n   - A deep copy, with the placeholder neutralised as S5.1's deep_stage.py does, reports only 'SELECTION_REQUIRED step 195 [unit-tests]'. Step 195 is the spec's final step until the next section is appended (S4.3 note 16, S5.2 note 17).\n   - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step, the copy passes with no findings.\n   - A negative probe (LauncherTests.fs removed from step 195's edits) is reported as SCOPE_CONSUMERS on OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow and SCOPE_TEST, so the census is enforced.\n   - The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s53/build_s53.py and s53_steps.py (with stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-deep.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S6 (Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits): appended steps 196-211 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (32 obligations, 16 acceptance bindings, 16 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 196-211). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 196 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs, new KitArchive.fs after KitHistory.fs): the send rule.\n  - KitPathRole (KitAppCachePath / KitContentPath); KitRelativePath.appCacheFolder (.oc), pathRole, parentOpt, leafName. The lock code of KitFolderStore.fs and InMemoryKitFolder names .oc through appCacheFolder, so .oc is written once.\n  - GlobPathMatch; SendExcludeGlob.matchOf (** whole segments, * and ? inside a segment, ignoring case, anchored at the kit root; no regex, no package).\n  - KitSendChoice (SentWithKit / LeftOutOfSend), KitTreeEntry (KitTreeFile / KitTreeFolder), KitFile.sendChoiceOf, KitFile.sentEntries, KitName.zipFileName.\n  - ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.\n- 197 ADD_CONTRACT <FILE:KitArchiveProxy> (Domain): KitArchiveError (five *Err cases), KitTreeEntry.tryOfZipEntryName / zipEntryName, KitArchiveFileCount, KitArchiveProgress, KitArchiveObserver (unobserved), KitArchiveOutcome, KitZipJob, KitUnzipJob, KitArchiveProxy { listKitTree; writeKitZip; listZipEntries; extractKitZip }, InMemoryArchiveDisk and createInMemory. KitArchiveProxyContract with KitArchiveProxyTests (in memory). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.\n- 198 IMPLEMENT (Domain): KitArchiveProxy.sendKit (a zip inside the kit refused; the kit file's sentEntries zipped) and receiveKit (a zip without a root .kit-json refused; .oc entries never extracted); KitZipPicker { pickZipToWrite; pickZipToOpen } with none.\n- 199 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <FILE:KitArchiveProxy> (new Storage KitArchiveStore.fs after KitHistoryStore.fs): KitArchiveProxy.create () over System.IO.Compression. KitArchiveProxyFolderTests runs the contract facts and four of its own. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.\n- 200 IMPLEMENT (new Ui KitArchiveJob.fs after KitOpening.fs): KitArchiveJobHost (posting through JobRunner.startBackground, onUiThread, immediate, inert), KitArchiveJobState over JobRunner's JobModel, kitArchiveProgressView, KitZipPicker.ofWindow with pickZipToWriteThen / pickZipToOpenThen. KitFolderPicker.pickThen's body moves into KitOpening.startPick. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.\n- 201 IMPLEMENT (TARV): KitWindowShell gains zipPicker, archive, archiveJobs (inert defaults; Program.fs's mount builds its shell as an update of inert); model kitSend; SendKit, SendKitProgressed, SendKitEnded, CancelSendKit.\n- 202 IMPLEMENT (KitWindowView, UiIds): Send kit… first in the Kit menu (sendKitButton = SendKitButton) and the progress row (sendKitProgressBar, sendKitProgressText, sendKitCancelButton).\n- 203 IMPLEMENT (Domain): Experiment.renumberedFor; KitLibrary.referenceClosure, the walk moved out of snapshotReferences (which calls it).\n- 204 IMPLEMENT: KitProxy.readLabFile (absolute name in the kit and the bytes as stored), both implementations, passed through readOnlyView.\n- 205 IMPLEMENT (Storage KitContentFiles.fs): ExperimentCopyReport and KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.\n- 206 IMPLEMENT (TARV): KitWindowShell.kitPicker; KitCopySource; model kitCopyOpt; OpenCopySource, ToggleCopiedExperiment, CopyChosenExperiments, CloseCopySource.\n- 207 IMPLEMENT (KitWindowView, UiIds, ConstructorUiIdOfDomain): Copy experiments from another kit… and its panel (five fixed ids and kitCopyExperimentToggle of an ExperimentId); ScrollExtentTests' kit-window fact at the bar's tallest.\n- 208 IMPLEMENT (KitStartView): KitStartContext gains zipPicker, archive, archiveJobs (KitStartWindow composes none, KitArchiveProxy.create () and onUiThread); KitZipOpening; model zipJob, zipOpeningOpt; OpenKitZip, OpenKitZipProgressed, OpenKitZipEnded, CancelOpenKitZip.\n- 209 IMPLEMENT (kitStartView, UiIds): Open kit from zip… (openKitZipButton = OpenKitZipButton) and its progress row.\n- 210 WIRE_UI: KitStartWindow takes zipPickerFor; the launcher passes KitZipPicker.ofWindow over locations.exportsFolder; acceptance on a real start screen.\n- 211 WIRE_UI: AppContext.locations; ConstructorScene.mount composes the real zip dialog, archive, job host and kit folder dialog.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. 'S4.1's suffix rule' for a copied experiment. S4.3 stores an experiment under its id (E<n>.experiment-json, step 146), and no kit-file suffix rule exists in S4.1. A clash is therefore an id clash: a clashing experiment takes the next free id (Experiment.renumberedFor), and every other keeps its id. Data files use S4.2's copyTargetFor suffix rule unchanged.\n2. 'Its setup files'. An S4.3 experiment carries its setup inside its own file (the setup array, step 146) and references no .setup-json, so copying the experiment file copies its setup. Bringing a referenced setup file belongs to the section that makes experiments reference one (request 15).\n3. The copy pins nothing. Snapshots arrive byte for byte as the source's, as a received kit's do. A version the target holds keeps the target's snapshot (step 139's rule). A copied snapshot the library lacks is resolved by the kit's import dialog when the kit is next opened (step 141), because the window's library overlay is composed when the window opens (step 154).\n4. Data files are copied as bytes. readDataFile decodes text, so step 204 adds KitProxy.readLabFile.\n   - Each distinct source path is copied once, into its own data folder when that folder is data or inside it, otherwise into data.\n   - A clash takes the next free suffix, and the attachment records the hash of the bytes now held, even when the source changed since attach.\n   - Everything is read before anything is written, so a missing data file or snapshot refuses the whole copy.\n   - attachLabFile is not reused for the copy: two in-memory kit folders share one kitFolder text (step 133), so its in-place test would misfire.\n5. The archive.\n   - Entries sit at the zip root, kit-relative and forward-slashed, folders as '<path>/' entries, so empty data and library come back.\n   - The zip streams into <zip>.tmp and is moved in place only when whole; a zip inside the kit it holds is refused.\n   - Extraction goes only into a new or empty folder (no merge or overwrite), and a cancel or failure removes what it created.\n   - Receiving never extracts .oc, because a foreign .oc/lock would lock the received kit. A zip without a root .kit-json is refused.\n6. Glob semantics: anchored at the kit root, '\\' read as '/', ** over whole segments, * and ? inside one segment, case-insensitive. A glob that matches a folder leaves out everything in it. No glob editor is added; the globs live in .kit-json (step 122).\n7. Progress and Cancel through JobRunner (.spec-md §10.2). JobRunner.startBackground runs the job; JobModel / updateJob hold its running state and progress. The archive's own loop reads the token before each file, the runLoop rule.\n   - The end returns the state to idle and the surface's status tells the outcome. JobStatus Completed / Failed are not used, because a KitArchiveError is not an exn.\n   - The windows' callbacks arrive on the UI thread through Dispatcher.UIThread.Post (KitArchiveJobHost.onUiThread). Each surface runs one job at a time.\n8. Send kit writes no kit file, so it is not behind the read-only guard (step 185): a read-only kit can be sent (001 §E review round-trip). Copy experiments is behind the guard, and its verb is withheld for a read-only kit.\n9. One dialog start. KitFolderPicker.pickThen's body moves into KitOpening.startPick, which pickThen and the two zip dialogs call.\n10. Dialog locations.\n   - AppContext gains locations, so the constructor windows' dialogs start in the exports and kits folders. Step 189's mount takes the AppContext.\n   - KitStartWindow gains zipPickerFor, mirroring pickerFor, so the real-window acceptance (step 210) can substitute it.\n   - The constructor windows' Send kit and Copy dialogs are the system's and are never pressed headless (the S5.3 Show in Explorer precedent).\n11. The copy panel lives in the kit bar (KitWindowView.fs), the S5.3 mapper's request. Its experiment list scrolls inside MaxHeight 160, because the bar sits outside the page's ScrollViewer (step 188). ScrollExtentTests' kit-window fact runs it at the bar's tallest.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s6/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (all_discovered, light) run on every step; ui-smoke on every step touching Ui or App code (200-202, 206-211).\n   - ui-tests runs by class: KitWindowTests (201, 202, 206, 207), ScrollExtentTests (207, 210), KitStartWindowTests (208-210), LauncherTests (210, 211), and AppContextTests and TableAndElementRotationTests (211).\n   - seam-plan proposed kit-acceptance, which is not adopted (not runnable before S12.1). It proposed whole ui-tests at 201, 206 and 208; class selections are kept (.user-md: whole at the final step only).\n   - WireUiFinalCompositionTests is never a ui-tests arm (S5.2 note 12, S5.3 note 12). unit-tests' applies_to covers none of these paths.\n13. Contract effects follow earlier sections: new members, cases and fields are 'create'. LauncherWindow (210) and MainConstructorWindow / InverseConstructorWindow (211) are change_behavior, with their inventory consumers in the authorized edits.\n14. Budget: 16 steps against a soft 12-22.\n15. Requests to later mappers:\n   - S7.2 (item mapping on copy): KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom gains the item mapping (map onto an existing item where the user says so, otherwise add it), and the kit bar's copy panel (KitWindowView.fs, step 207) gains its choice. The copy's read-then-write order and its report stay.\n   - S8.2 / S9.1 (experiments reference a setup by name + revision, .spec-md §5): copyExperimentsFrom brings each referenced .setup-json, with a clash rule for setup names. S8.3 / S9.1 (template names) carry Experiment.renumberedFor's rule over to names.\n   - S7.1, S11 (new kit file kinds): Send kit zips the whole tree, so items, studies and fit runs travel without a change.\n   - S12 (AT-1 / AT-2 Send round trip): send through KitArchiveProxy.sendKit or the SendKit message, and reopen through receiveKit or OpenKitZip.\n   - Close: a whole-suite final step owns the SELECTION_REQUIRED finding below.\n16. New artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n   - Domain: KitArchive.fs. Storage: KitArchiveStore.fs. Ui: KitArchiveJob.fs.\n   - Tests: KitArchiveTests.fs, KitArchiveProxyTests.fs, KitArchiveJobTests.fs, ExperimentCopyTests.fs.\n   - Sec 0.1's UiIds.fs, Program.fs and AppContext.fs rows hold: the Send / Copy / Open-from-zip ids, the real dialogs, and AppContext.locations.\n17. Names were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec, with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py.\n   - Types and cases: every new type and case of KitArchive.fs, KitArchiveJob.fs and KitStartView / TARV, among them KitArchiveProxy, KitArchiveError and its five cases, KitTreeEntry, KitTreeFile, KitTreeFolder, KitSendChoice, SentWithKit, LeftOutOfSend, GlobPathMatch, KitPathRole, KitAppCachePath, KitContentPath, InMemoryArchiveDisk, KitZipPicker, KitArchiveJobHost, KitArchiveJobState, KitCopySource, KitZipOpening, ExperimentCopyReport and every new message case.\n   - Members and functions: sendKit, receiveKit, listKitTree, writeKitZip, listZipEntries, extractKitZip, sendChoiceOf, sentEntries, matchOf, zipFileName, tryOfZipEntryName, zipEntryName, readLabFile, referenceClosure, renumberedFor, copyExperimentsFrom, startPick, kitArchiveProgressView, and every new ConstructorUiId member.\n   - InMemoryArchiveDisk's read member is tryDiskFile, because tryReadFile is an STL name. The pathRole member is not named role (447 hits).\n18. Validation.\n   - On the real folder, executability check reports only the two unresolved '<FILE:KitArchiveProxy>' placeholders (steps 197, 199), which the cycle's minting step resolves.\n   - A deep copy, the placeholder neutralised, reports only 'SELECTION_REQUIRED step 211 [unit-tests]'. Step 211 is the spec's final step until the next section is appended (S5.3 note 18).\n   - With a bound placeholder final WIRE step, the copy passes with no findings.\n   - Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: ExperimentCopyTests.fs removed from step 205's edits gives SCOPE_TEST, and LauncherTests.fs removed from step 210's gives SCOPE_CONSUMERS on OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow.\n   - The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s6/build_s6.py and s6_steps.py (with stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-deep.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S7.1 (Items, parameters and item models): appended steps 212-229 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (34 obligations, 18 acceptance bindings, 18 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 212-229). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 212 IMPLEMENT: new Domain ItemModels.fs (module ItemModels, compiled after ElementId.fs and before LibraryEntryFiles.fs). ParameterName moves from MuellerInverse.fs and DialSign from MuellerReconstruction.fs, both unchanged; their consumers open the module. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests. unit-tests over OptimizationTests and MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 213 IMPLEMENT: AngleUncertainty, ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty and NoiseParam (decentLab, noiseless) move from BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs into ItemModels.fs. The harness keeps NoiseSeed, UniformDeviateProvider and the noise functions (S10.1's). unit-tests over MuellerInverseTests.\n- 214 IMPLEMENT: ParameterValue, ParameterKind (seven cases, never stored), ItemParameterAxis { name; kind; defaultValue }.\n  - Noise types gain parameterValue; NoiseParam.parameterAxes publishes the three uncertainties.\n  - SourcePreset.parameterAxes: azimuth, ellipticity, degreeOfPolarization 0, intensityScale 1.\n  - PolarizerPreset.parameterAxes: none. Sample.parameterAxes: film<k>.thickness, film<k>.layer<j>.thickness, substrate.thickness. Thickness.parameterValueOpt.\n- 215 IMPLEMENT: PolarizerLeakage, RetardanceDispersion, BlackBoxNormalisation, OpticalForm (real LP, retarder, black box, compound of CompoundComponent { form; offset } in light order) and ItemModelForm (OpticalElementModel, EmptySlotModel, IntensityDetectorModel / MuellerPolarimeterModel / EllipsometerModel of NoiseParam). Each publishes parameterAxes; compound axes are c<k>.-prefixed.\n- 216 ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:ItemModelProxy>: ItemModelId, ItemModelVersionId, ItemModelEntry, ItemModelVersion, ItemModelIds (eight frozen GUIDs), ItemModelError, ItemModelProxy { listItemModels; resolveItemModelVersion; saveItemModel } and createInMemory. ItemModelProxyContract with ItemModelProxyTests. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests.\n- 217 IMPLEMENT: the library kind and the built-ins, in one step.\n  - LibraryEntryKind gains ItemModelEntryKind (tag 7, .item-model-json); LibraryEntryPayload gains ItemModelPayload; ofItemModel / toItemModel; ItemModelId.toLibraryEntryId; ItemModelVersionId.entryReference.\n  - Every incomplete match gains the case (import order, schema file, facet rows, the 'Item model' caption).\n  - InMemoryCatalogueStores gains itemModels, and the in-memory import pushes item models through saveItemModel.\n  - schema/library-item-model.schema.json.\n  - A throw-away Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx writes the eight built-ins into Catalogue/Builtin/ through ofItemModel, sealed and writeCatalogue, and rewrites the manifest.\n  - BuiltinCatalogue gains itemModels / itemModel. The integrity counts gain 8 item models.\n  - ui-smoke; ui-tests over ImportDialogTests and AppContextTests.\n- 218 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT <STORE:ItemModelProxy>: new Storage ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs (after PresetDatabaseStore.fs) with ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase. ItemModelProxySqliteTests runs the contract and three facts of its own. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.\n- 219 IMPLEMENT: the export tool is deleted. EntryFileJsonTests round-trips every form; the import contract's ImportStoreSet gains itemModels and its fill / resolve facts cover item models on both stores.\n- 220 IMPLEMENT (Kit.fs): ItemError, ItemId, ItemLabel (tryCreate, fileStem), ItemNotes, ItemRevision, and ItemModelInstance (PresetInstance / SampleInstance / ItemModelVersionInstance) with entryReferenceOpt. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.\n- 221 IMPLEMENT (Kit.fs): ParameterInterval, ParameterSigma, ParameterPrior, UnknownParameterData, FitRunName, CalibratedParameterData, ParameterState (KnownParameter / UnknownParameter / CalibratedParameter), and Parameter with knownAtDefault and validate.\n- 222 IMPLEMENT (Kit.fs): ItemDial (DialMounted of DialSign / FixedMounting; a dialZero axis), ItemRevisionRecord, and Item with libraryReferences and tryFindParameter.\n- 223 IMPLEMENT: AddItem as ItemModelChoice (instance, parameterAxes) and ItemDraft (toItem, addTo).\n- 224 IMPLEMENT: SetParameterState as Item.withParameterState.\n- 225 IMPLEMENT: publishing a revision as Item.publishRevision.\n- 226 IMPLEMENT: the item kit file. ItemFile with schemaVersion 1, schema/item.schema.json, SchemaValidation.validateItemFile, ItemFile.fileText and KitFileText.parseItemFile.\n- 227 IMPLEMENT: KitProxy.writeItem / readItems over the per-kind verbs. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests (over a kit folder).\n- 228 IMPLEMENT: KitLibraryContext.recordItem snapshots and pins the item's model reference, then writes the file. KitLibraryTests facts.\n- 229 WIRE: AppContext.itemModels = ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase over the app's library database. AppContextTests fact.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. ParameterName and DialSign MOVE into a new early Domain file, ItemModels.fs. The brief REUSES both, but MuellerInverse.fs and MuellerReconstruction.fs compile last, after LibraryEntryFiles.fs and Kit.fs, which must name them. Kit.fs cannot move later, because Experiments.fs opens it (step 135); the S4.1 mapper's note 12 allowed a later file but none is possible here. The noise data types join them (.spec-md §3.23). One declaration of each type exists, and BerremanTests' numbers are unchanged.\n2. Item, ItemId, ItemLabel, Parameter and ParameterState live in Kit.fs as .spec-md §5 says. The item-model vocabulary (ParameterValue, ParameterKind, ItemParameterAxis, the forms, ItemModelEntry, ItemModelProxy, ItemModelIds) lives in ItemModels.fs. It must compile before LibraryEntryFiles.fs, because LibraryEntryPayload carries the item-model form.\n3. The light-source row. .spec-md §3.14 makes the source preset a model in its own right, and the brief's built-in list has no light-source item model. So the light-source parameters (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization 0, intensity scale 1) are published by the source preset over its λ (SourcePreset.parameterAxes). An item instantiating a source preset gets them, and no light-source item-model entry exists. Detector presets are not instantiated as items; the three detector item models are.\n4. The payload union is two-level. OpticalForm holds the forms a compound may compose (real LP, retarder, black box, compound). ItemModelForm adds the empty slot and the three detectors. So a detector or an empty slot cannot sit inside a compound, by type and with no validation. The ideal LP / CP presets and the stack sample get no wrapper.\n5. A detector's noise model is its parameters' defaults. Each detector form carries a NoiseParam, published as rotationUncertainty, elementUncertainty and throughputUncertainty, so each detector item holds its own values. The built-in detectors carry NoiseParam.decentLab, which lets AT-2's polarimeter use the built-in as shipped. The intensity detector's gain is session-scoped in a study (S11.1); here it is an ordinary axis.\n6. 'CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel' is realised on step 94's kind-neutral seam. The in-memory InMemoryCatalogueStores gains an itemModels store, and its put adapter pushes decoded item models through ItemModelProxy.saveItemModel. The database seam stores every kind's envelope already (step 95) and is unchanged.\n7. The item-model store is minimal. saveItemModel stores a NEW item model at a given version and refuses a held id, because no item-model editor is in scope (.spec-md §8); a later version arrives through the import seam. The in-memory store holds what it is given, built-ins included; the database store saves user item models only.\n8. The kind, its built-ins and the integrity facts land in one step (217). BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests requires every kind of LibraryEntryKind.all to have rows, so the kind cannot land before its files (step 57's rule).\n   - The built-ins go through the export path once: ofItemModel, sealed, CatalogueData.tryCreate and writeCatalogue in a throw-away .fsx, as step 35.\n   - The tool is deleted in step 219, after the files and their facts are green. It is folded into 219 because a step deleting only an uncompiled .fsx has no gate seam.\n   - The catalogue keeps version 1, because no release exists; its manifest hash changes.\n9. The eight built-in item models: Real linear polarizer (extinction ratio), Retarder plate (constant), Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder: real LP at 0 deg, retarder at 45 deg), Black-box Mueller matrix (sixteen elements), Empty slot (air), Intensity detector (gain, dark offset and noise), Mueller polarimeter, and Ellipsometer (noise budget). Their names avoid the detector presets' file stems; ItemModelIds holds their GUIDs (.spec-md §3.3).\n10. Material parameters as unknowns. The item half is negative: a stack sample's item publishes its layer thicknesses only, and its materials publish nothing as item parameters. A study opens a material version and owns its unknowns (001 §I; S11.1). An orientation unknown of a mounted sample is its dialZero.\n11. Dial mapping. ItemDial is DialMounted of DialSign or FixedMounting, chosen when the item is added. A dial-mounted item gets an ordinary dialZero parameter (AngleParameter, 0), and the physical angle is sign · (reading − dialZero), MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle's rule. Experiments record raw readings (S9.1).\n12. Revisions. Item.revision starts at 1. Item.history holds every earlier revision's parameter values, oldest first: 'short' because a fit run keeps the full vectors (001 §I). Only publishRevision moves the revision; withParameterState edits the working revision. CalibratedParameter names its fit run by FitRunName, the fit run file's stem <study>@<stamp> (001 §A).\n13. Validation of a state: every number finite; an unknown's lower < upper with start inside, ends included; a prior's and a calibration's sigma above zero. No per-kind range is checked (a kind's range is the run law's, S8.1).\n14. Labels. An item file is <label>.item-json through FileStem.ofText. AddItem refuses a label whose file stem equals a held one ignoring case, because the kit root is one folder on Windows; readItems refuses a file whose stem is not its label's or that repeats an ItemId. No rename or delete verb is added (not in the brief).\n15. ParameterKind and the new fieldless unions carry no int tag. Kinds are generated and never stored; the stored unions use the serializer's case-name form, as step 28 keeps every union it does not tag and step 146 stores the experiment's.\n16. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates', adjusted after executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s71/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on every step but 229, which runs build, elevation, ui-smoke and ui-tests (AppContextTests).\n   - Step 217 adds ui-smoke and ui-tests (ImportDialogTests, AppContextTests) for the caption and the shipped catalogue.\n   - unit-tests by class only where its applies_to matches (212, 213).\n   - seam-plan proposed unit-tests over every class whose file gains an 'open' at 212 (seven classes, about 67 min) and three at 213 (with BiaxialInverseTests and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests, about 25 min each). The brief's 'cheapest classes that compile and exercise them' is adopted instead: OptimizationTests and MuellerReconstructionTests (about 2 s) at 212, MuellerInverseTests (about 11 min) at 213. The build compiles every edited class, and a new constructor fact pins the moved values.\n   - seam-plan's final-step 'every planned gate' and kit-acceptance (not runnable before S12.1) are not adopted.\n17. Contract effects: moved symbols are 'retire' (with preserves_obligations) at their old qualified names, with every inventory consumer in the authorized edits, plus 'create' at the new home; every new type, case, member and field is 'create' (earlier sections' convention).\n18. Budget: 18 steps against a soft 16-28.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S7.2 (Items panel, flow strip, item mapping on copy):\n  - offer AppContext.itemModels.listItemModels and the source / polarizer presets and sample versions as ItemModelChoice;\n  - mint the ItemId through an injected provider;\n  - send AddItem and SetParameterState through ItemDraft.addTo / Item.withParameterState and persist through KitLibraryContext.recordItem;\n  - read KitProxy.readItems on open. Copying experiments maps items by ItemId or label.\n  - A remove, rename, photo or notes edit, if S7.2 needs it, is its own member.\n- S8.1 (run law): evaluate OpticalForm / ItemModelForm, a source preset's light-source parameters and the dial mapping from an item's parameters.\n  - The default source parameters are unpolarized at unit scale.\n  - Black-box elements are m<row><column>, row-major, at reference orientation. Compound axes are c<k>.-prefixed.\n  - A ParameterValue -> elevated conversion belongs on ParameterValue, and no reverse member may be added (ELEV006).\n- S8.2 (setups as slots): slots hold ItemId references; an item's dial is ItemDial.\n- S10.1: the noise functions move into Optimization and open OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels for NoiseParam. The harness's measurement-error banner moves with them.\n- S11.1 / S11.3 / S11.5:\n  - ParameterState and ItemParameterAxis feed the generated fit axes; material components stay the study's (MaterialScope).\n  - FitRunName is the fit run's file stem; S11.3 MUST reuse it, not declare a second fit-run name.\n  - Publish calibration calls Item.publishRevision with CalibratedParameter states, then KitLibraryContext.recordItem.\n- S12 (AT-1 / AT-2): the CPL items instantiate ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId; QZ / LR blackBoxMuellerModelId; the phone intensityDetectorModelId; AT-2's polarimeter muellerPolarimeterModelId, whose defaults are NoiseParam.decentLab.\n- Close: a whole-suite final step owns the two SELECTION_REQUIRED findings below.\n\nNew artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n- Domain: ItemModels.fs. Storage: ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs, schema/library-item-model.schema.json, schema/item.schema.json.\n- Catalogue: Builtin/*.item-model-json (eight files).\n- Tests: ItemModelsTests.fs, ItemModelProxyTests.fs (ItemModelProxyTests, ItemModelProxySqliteTests), KitItemTests.fs, KitItemFileTests.fs.\n- Sec 0.1's MuellerInverse.fs / MuellerReconstruction.fs rows: ParameterName and DialSign moved to ItemModels.fs. The InverseFitHarness row: the noise data types moved to Domain in S7.1.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec, with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py.\n- Types and cases: every new type and case of ItemModels.fs and Kit.fs, among them ParameterValue, ParameterKind, ItemParameterAxis, OpticalForm, ItemModelForm, ItemModelProxy, ItemModelError, ItemId, ItemLabel, ParameterState, Parameter, ItemDial, Item, ItemError, ItemModelChoice, ItemDraft and ItemFile.\n- Members: parameterAxes, parameterValue, parameterValueOpt, withParameterState, publishRevision, addTo, toItem, itemFile, parseItemFile, writeItem, readItems, recordItem, validateItemFile, ofItemModel, toItemModel, listItemModels, resolveItemModelVersion, saveItemModel, and the ItemModelIds members.\n- Renames made: the search bounds are ParameterInterval, because ParameterBounds is OptimizationInterface's; the default maker is Parameter.knownAtDefault, because ofAxis is a BerremanTests local.\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the two unresolved '<STORE:ItemModelProxy>' placeholders (steps 216, 218), which the cycle's minting step resolves.\n- A deep copy, the placeholder neutralised, reports only 'SELECTION_REQUIRED step 229 [constructor-unit-tests]' and '[unit-tests]'. Step 229 is the spec's final step until the next section is appended (S6 note 18).\n- With a bound placeholder final WIRE step, the copy passes with no findings. An earlier run had found that the pure move step needs a test effect, so step 212 gained ItemModelsTests' first fact.\n- Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs removed from step 212's edits gives SCOPE_CONSUMERS on MuellerInverse.ParameterName, and KitItemFileTests.fs removed from step 227's gives SCOPE_TEST.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s71/build_s71.py, s71_common.py and s71_steps_a/b/c.py (with stage_all.sh, deep_stage.py, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-deep.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S7.2 (The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy): appended steps 230-243 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (30 obligations, 14 acceptance bindings, 14 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 230-243). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 230 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs): ItemError gains UnknownKitItemErr; Item.withNotes, Item.withPhoto (None drops the reference, never a file), Item.relabelledAmong (DuplicateItemLabelErr on another item's file stem, own label ignored); ItemIdProvider { mintItemId }.\n- 231 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs, Experiments.fs): ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong; ItemCopyChoice (MapOntoKitItem / AddCopiedItem); ItemCopyRow; Item.defaultCopyChoice; ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor and itemsToAdd; Experiment.itemsUsedBy.\n- 232 IMPLEMENT (Storage KitContentFiles.fs): KitLibraryContext.recordRelabelledItem previous relabelled (new file then old deleted; a case-only change deletes then writes; each failure rolls back).\n- 233 IMPLEMENT (Domain KitLibrary.fs): ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith, step 142's overlay rule for item models.\n- 234 IMPLEMENT (Ui KitOpening.fs, TARV): OpenedKit.items read at open; the model's kitItems, set by loadKit and ReloadKitChanges.\n- 235 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ConstructorFlowStep (Items, Setups, Experiments), the model's flowStep, ShowFlowStep; SelectBay keeps the strip on Setups or Experiments.\n- 236 IMPLEMENT (KitOpening.fs, TARV): ItemIdProvider.system; AddItemForm; the model's itemModels, itemIds, selectedItemOpt, addItemFormOpt (DefaultStores carries the imported item models); SelectKitItem, OpenAddItemForm, ChooseNewItemModel, SetNewItemLabel, SetNewItemDial, CancelAddItemForm, AddItem. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.\n- 237 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ParameterStateChoice, ParameterEditField, ParameterEditDraft (ofParameter, withFieldText, tryState); parameterEditOpt; SetParameterState, EditItemParameter, SetParameterEditChoice, SetParameterEditText, CancelParameterEdit, RelabelKitItem, SetKitItemNotes, SetKitItemPhoto, RemoveKitItemPhoto.\n- 238 IMPLEMENT: new Ui ItemsPanelView.fs (after KitStartView.fs, before KitWindowView.fs); the Items-panel ConstructorUiIds; ConstructorUiIdOfDomain ids and captions (kitItemRow, addItemOffer, newItemDialChoice, itemParameterRow, itemRevisionRow, ParameterGridCells / Parameter.gridCells); pickDataFile public with a title; model.itemModelCaption. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests.\n- 239 IMPLEMENT: new Ui FlowStripView.fs (after ItemsPanelView.fs); flow ids; ConstructorFlowStep.flowUiId; kitWindowView docks the strip left of a keyed surface (Items panel or mainView). ScrollExtentTests covers the Items step.\n- 240 IMPLEMENT (KitLibrary.fs, KitContentFiles.fs, TARV): KitLibraryError gains KitLibraryItemErr; ExperimentCopyReport gains items; copyExperimentsFrom takes the item rows, adds the used items it should (model snapshots through the closure, photos as lab files) and maps the rest; the window's copy passes no row (defaults) and re-reads kitItems.\n- 241 IMPLEMENT (TARV): KitCopySource gains items and itemRows; ChooseCopiedItem; the toggles keep the rows; the copy passes them and names the added items.\n- 242 IMPLEMENT (UiIds, ConstructorUiIdOfDomain, KitWindowView): kitCopyItemList and kitCopyItemChoice; the mapping table inside the copy panel's existing scroller.\n- 243 WIRE_UI (Program.fs): the windows thread itemModels = context.itemModels.overlaidWith opened.overlay; the real-window acceptance adds CPL1 and reopens the kit.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The items the copied experiments use. An S4.3 experiment names no item; its setup binds presets by entry id and samples by version. So at S7.2 an experiment uses the items whose model it binds: Experiment.itemsUsedBy matches Item.libraryReferences (step 222) against Experiment.libraryReferences (step 137), one rule over existing members. An item-model item is used by no experiment until S8.2's slots name items. A mapping therefore changes no experiment file; it decides whether the source item is added.\n2. The default mapping: the kit's item of the same ItemId first (one id is one physical piece; the S7.1 request 'by ItemId or label'), then an item of identical model and label (the brief), otherwise add. An Add of an item whose id the kit holds is DuplicateItemIdErr; a mapping onto a missing id is the new UnknownKitItemErr; an added item whose label the kit holds takes the next free ' (2)' suffix (the form of KitDataFolder.copyTargetFor, step 132).\n3. Added items travel whole: their model snapshots come through the copy's closure (pinning nothing, as S6 decided), their photos as lab files under S6's folder and suffix rule, photoOpt re-pointed. A refusal is KitLibraryItemErr of ItemError (new case), answered before anything is written.\n4. copyExperimentsFrom takes the rows; an item no row names takes its default. Step 240 passes no row from the window (the defaults); step 241 passes the panel's rows. The window's status keeps step 206's text when no item was added.\n5. The flow strip. ConstructorFlowStep is window state in TARV with no wire tag; ConstructorFlowStep.all is 001 sec O's order. Setups is the table (mainView); Experiments is mainView with the Experiments bay open; Setups leaves the Experiments bay for Add; SelectBay keeps the strip on Setups or Experiments. A window opens on Setups with the Add bay, as today. The strip is the same in both modes.\n6. Messages live in TARV (the S5.3 / S6 precedent); the panel and the strip are views in their own files, compiled after KitStartView.fs and before KitWindowView.fs; kitWindowView keys its surface items / workbench.\n7. AddItem carries the ItemDraft, so the button and a test send the same message; the form mints the ItemId through ItemIdProvider when it opens (system instance beside ClockProvider.system). The offers are the item models (overlaid in the windows), the source presets, the polarizer presets and the samples at SampleVersionId.firstOf, the version TableAndElementRotationView.fs:descriptorBinding pins, so an item and an experiment name one entry. A failing library listing offers nothing of its kind (allowedEntryIds precedent); a failing item-model store is told in kitStatus.\n8. Parameter editing is one editor for the selected parameter: Known or Unknown by hand (a calibration comes from a fit, S11.5). Texts are raw captions read with the invariant culture at Set; a prior is centred on the start; values stay in the parameter's own unit (radians for angles). Provenance in the grid: Given, To be fitted, Fit run <name>.\n9. Label, notes and photo. relabelledAmong plus recordRelabelledItem (write, then delete the old file; a case-only change deletes, then writes; each failure rolls back so readItems never sees two files of one id). The photo is attached through the window's attachDataFile (step 135), in place or copied into data/, and shown by its kit path, not as an image; removing it keeps the file. pickDataFile becomes public with a title (reused for the photo, not copied); its options builder is unchanged.\n10. The six item writes pass step 185's read-only guard; their controls are absent or disabled under a read-only kit. Every outcome is told in kitStatus, the kit bar's one status line.\n11. ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith follows step 142's rule; KitLibraryStores is unchanged, the windows compose the overlaid item-model store beside it, so a kit's item models resolve on any machine.\n12. The dial is shown, not edited: it is chosen when the item is added (step 222); its zero is the dialZero row of the grid.\n13. The mapping table shares the copy panel's existing scroller (MaxHeight 160), so the kit bar's tallest height is unchanged and ScrollExtentTests keeps passing at 1000 x 540.\n14. No new window is added; ScrollExtentTests gains the kit window's Items step.\n15. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s72/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on every step; ui-smoke (whole, light) on every step touching Ui or App code (234-243), which seam-plan did not propose for 234-237.\n   - ui-tests by class: ItemsPanelTests and DataFilePickerFolderTests (238, the picker code changes), KitWindowTests and ScrollExtentTests (239, 242), KitWindowTests (241), AppContextTests, KitWindowTests, LauncherTests and TableAndElementRotationTests (243).\n   - Not adopted: kit-acceptance (not runnable before S12.1); the every-class or whole-suite selections seam-plan derives from the fsproj edits (236, 238) and from 241's edits; the final step's 'every planned gate'. unit-tests applies to no step.\n16. Contract effects: new members, cases and fields are 'create'; copyExperimentsFrom is 'change_shape'; kitWindowView and the two constructor windows are 'change_behavior', the windows' inventory consumers in 243's authorized edits.\n17. Budget: 14 steps against a soft 10-18.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S8.2 (setups as slots): slots hold ItemIds; Experiment.itemsUsedBy is re-pointed to the items a referenced setup's slots name (one rule, not a second); the copy then rewrites a copied setup's slot ItemIds by the mapping (MapOntoKitItem to the kit's id, AddCopiedItem to the added item's id) beside bringing each referenced .setup-json (S6 request). The Add-item sample offer's pinned version (SampleVersionId.firstOf, as descriptorBinding) is re-decided with the slots.\n- S8.4 (slot bar): its chips list the model's kitItems; the Setups flow step stays the table.\n- S9.3 (Data step): insert DataFlowStep into ConstructorFlowStep.all after Experiments (001 sec O), with its surface in kitWindowView's switch and an id beside flowExperimentsStep.\n- S11 / S14: Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish join ConstructorFlowStep.all at 001 sec O's positions (Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results, Publish). Publish calibration records through KitLibraryContext.recordItem and refreshes kitItems; the grid's Calibrated provenance already names the fit run.\n- S12 (AT-1 / AT-2): items are added through AddItem of an ItemDraft and set through SetParameterState; the copy and Send round trips carry item files without change.\n- Close: a whole-suite final step owns the SELECTION_REQUIRED finding below.\n\nNew artifacts the planner may add to .spec-md sec 0.2:\n- Ui: ItemsPanelView.fs, FlowStripView.fs. Tests: ItemsPanelModelTests.fs, ItemsPanelTests.fs.\n- Sec 0.1 rows: TableAndElementRotationView.fs hosts the flow strip's and the Items panel's messages; KitLibrary.fs gains ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith and KitLibraryItemErr; KitContentFiles.fs copies items with experiments; Program.fs threads the overlaid item-model store; UiIds.fs gains the Items-panel, flow-strip and copy-mapping ids.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec, with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py.\n- Types and cases: ConstructorFlowStep, ItemsFlowStep, SetupsFlowStep, ExperimentsFlowStep, ItemIdProvider, AddItemForm, ParameterEditDraft, ParameterStateChoice, KnownStateChoice, UnknownStateChoice, ParameterEditField, ValueEditField, LowerEditField, UpperEditField, PriorSigmaEditField, ItemCopyChoice, MapOntoKitItem, AddCopiedItem, ItemCopyRow, ParameterGridCells, UnknownKitItemErr, KitLibraryItemErr and every new message case.\n- AddItem (001 sec P's name) is a DU case here; ElementPaletteControls.AddItem is a record type, and ELEV016 compares union cases only (STL Analyzers/NoDuplicateDuCase.fs), so the two do not collide.\n- Renames made: copyRowsFor (rowsFor has STL hits), itemDraftOpt (draftOpt), withFieldText (withText), flowUiId (uiId has 75 STL hits).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only 'SELECTION_REQUIRED step 243 [unit-tests]'. Step 243 is the spec's final step until the next section is appended (S6 note 18, S7.1 validation).\n- With a bound placeholder final WIRE step, the copy passes with no findings.\n- Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: ItemsPanelTests.fs removed from step 238's edits gives SCOPE_TEST, and LauncherTests.fs removed from step 243's gives SCOPE_CONSUMERS on OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow and InverseConstructorWindow.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s72/build_s72.py, s72_common.py, s72_steps_a.py and s72_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S8.1 (The run law walks every object; the source is real): appended steps 244-254 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (27 obligations, 11 acceptance bindings, 11 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 244-254). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 244 IMPLEMENT (ItemModels.fs, Kit.fs): every parameter name a model publishes becomes one ParameterName member (azimuth ... dialZero, blackBoxScale = 'scale', substrateThickness, muellerElement row column, filmThickness k, repeatedLayerThickness k j, inComponent k); SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes; steps 214/215/222's parameterAxes name the members. No text, order, kind or default changes.\n- 245 IMPLEMENT: new Domain ItemEvaluation.fs (module ItemEvaluation, directly after MuellerInverse.fs): ItemEvaluationError (MissingParameterValueErr, ParameterOutOfRangeErr); ParameterValues (ofParameters, defaultsOf, withValue, valueOf, checkedFor with the kinds' ranges). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.\n- 246 IMPLEMENT: SourceEmission { azimuth; ellipticity; degreeOfPolarization; intensityScale } in ExperimentRun.fs with stokes; SourceEmission.ofValues, ParameterValue.angle, ItemModelChoice.emissionWith, NotALightSourceErr.\n- 247 IMPLEMENT: ElementOrientation { rotation; incidence; branch } (transmittingAt); BoundOpticalElement = BoundPolarizerPreset | BoundEmptySlot; muellerAt (behaviorMueller exactly; identity); UnmodelledBranchErr.\n- 248 IMPLEMENT: BoundOpticalForm + ofOpticalForm; ParameterValues.forComponent; ParameterValue.retardanceAt; real LP (rotated linear diattenuator), retarder (retarderMueller), black box (rotateMueller), compound (rotateMueller of compoundMueller).\n- 249 IMPLEMENT: Sample.withThicknessValues, ParameterValue.thickness; BoundStackSample + ofStackSample (resolved once); muellerAt = sampleMuellerSpun; SampleMaterialErr of MaterialError.\n- 250 IMPLEMENT: CutPlate { cut; thickness; predict } with ofForward over MuellerInverse's ForwardModelProxy; ElementOrientation.sampleAzimuth / observable; BoundCutPlate; CutPlateSolveErr.\n- 251 IMPLEMENT: ItemModelChoice.boundWith (presets, stack samples, optical forms, empty slot; NotAnOpticalElementErr for detectors and sources, no wildcard).\n- 252 IMPLEMENT: the run law. RunStep = ElementStep | ObjectStep of MuellerMatrix; SourceEmission.emittedInto; detectorStokes / read take the emission; the prepared flag, Propagation.behaviorInputStokes and TARV's unused runInputStokes are deleted; chartForRun builds its steps through BoundOpticalElement and reads with the default emission; docs and AGENTS.md's run-law gotcha. ExperimentRunTests (one rename, two re-pointed, four new), PolarizerBehaviorTests (two behaviorInputStokes facts deleted), ExperimentControlsTests (two samples in series).\n- 253 IMPLEMENT (BeamLayout.fs): DetectorCapture and detectorCaptures scene detectors varied objects, the per-object capture rule. Two BeamLayoutTests facts.\n- 254 IMPLEMENT: detectedBranches takes objects; TARV measuredElementOf deleted, model.objectIds, captureDetectors and availableCaptures read the rule; AGENTS.md names it. BeamLayoutTests re-pointed; ElementMenuTests fact (a detector on a second sample's reflected ray offers R).\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. 'Unit scale after the first polarizer' is a reference, not a fold arm. The source emits stokes = I·[1, p cos2χ cos2ψ, p cos2χ sin2ψ, p sin2χ]; the run starts from emittedInto steps = stokes × r, where r = 1 / S0 of the first ElementStep in front of the first ObjectStep applied to unpolarized light (1 when there is none, or it passes nothing). The fold applies every step's matrix uniformly. For ideal polarizers r = 2 and every product is exact, so every existing chart (all ComputedIdeal) is bit-identical; ExperimentRunTests' new fact compares against inputStokes over every kind and sampled orientation.\n2. Departure: a ConstantMueller first polarizer now passes unit S0 like every other polarizer (today it was un-normalized through behaviorInputStokes). No seed, catalogue entry or editor produces a ConstantMueller (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:idealKindOpt says so), so no chart changes; the same rule gives a CPL item at its defaults unit S0 after it, as the ideal CPL preset has. PolarizerBehaviorTests loses its two behaviorInputStokes facts with the function; the remaining facts are numerically unchanged, as the brief asks.\n3. Captures per object: a lit detector that sees the varied element captures the branch by which its path leaves the LAST object on it (the object whose light it receives); with no object on its path, transmitted light of the varied element only (today's no-sample rule). With one bound sample this is today's rule, so every existing capture and chart is unchanged. The rule is Domain (BeamLayout.detectorCaptures), shared by captureDetectors and availableCaptures.\n4. In S8.1 the table binds presets, not items, so every chart reads the source's DEFAULT parameter set (SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes); S8.2's source slot passes a source item's values through ItemModelChoice.emissionWith.\n5. The evaluator lives in a new Domain file after MuellerInverse.fs, because it calls MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller and MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (compiled last); ExperimentRun.fs keeps the pure fold and SourceEmission. Evaluation is two-phase (bind once: values checked, sample materials resolved; then muellerAt per orientation and wavelength), so the host still resolves a sample once per run.\n6. Step 244 refactors S7.1's publishers so every published name is written once (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'); the evaluator reads values under those members. Positions stay int on ParameterName members (members are exempt).\n7. Step 221 said 'a kind's range is its model's (S8.1)': checkedFor enforces finite numbers, FractionParameter in [0, 1], ScaleParameter and ThicknessParameter >= 0; other kinds take any finite number.\n8. A cut plate is a CutPlate built from MuellerInverse's ForwardModelProxy and a parameter record (no crystal-parameter material exists before S11.1); its muellerAt maps the orientation to a MeasurementConfiguration (rotation as SampleAzimuth, branch as Observable). The test builder uses OpticalProperties.fromRefractionIndex over MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters.\n9. Detectors are not evaluated here: boundWith answers NotAnOpticalElementErr for the three detector models (gain, dark and noise are S11.2's forward model); ParameterName.gain / darkOffset / noise names exist for it.\n10. A non-material evaluation error at the host (never raised by its own inputs) shows the title 'The run cannot be evaluated'; SampleMaterialErr keeps today's 'Sample materials failed to resolve' chart and runFailureCaption text.\n11. BoundElement was renamed BoundOpticalElement before writing: ElementRenderer.fs has a BoundElement union case that the host can see beside it.\n12. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s81/seam.json).\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on every step; ui-smoke (whole, light) and ui-tests on 252 and 254, which touch TableAndElementRotationView.fs.\n   - ui-tests by class on 252 and 254: FsxAcceptanceTests, ExperimentControlsTests and MainWorkbenchTests (the brief), plus ElementMenuTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests and InverseConstructorTests (the classes that drive charts and captures). seam-plan proposed ExperimentControlsTests alone for 252.\n   - Not adopted: kit-acceptance (ExperimentRun.fs is in its applies_to, but KitAcceptanceTests.fs is not created before S12.1); the final step's 'every planned gate' (254 is final only until the next section is appended). unit-tests applies to no step: MuellerInverse.fs and MuellerReconstruction.fs are called, never edited.\n13. Budget: 11 steps against a soft 12-22; the evaluator steps are one model family each, and the run law is one step because RunStep's reshape forces the host and its tests together.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S8.2 (setups as slots): the run law reads the slots in light order. Prep and Analyzer slots become ElementSteps and Object slots ObjectSteps through ItemModelChoice.boundWith / BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt at the slot's R1 (a dial reading through ParameterName.dialZero and the item's DialSign), its drawn incidence and its path branch; the source slot's item emits through emissionWith (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters); TARV's model.objectIds becomes the setup's Object slots. Its invariant no-measured-element-of holds from step 254.\n- S11.2 (forward model): build on ItemModelChoice.boundWith, BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt, SourceEmission and ExperimentRun.detectorStokes; read gain and darkOffset through their ParameterName members.\n- S10.1 / S11.1: a crystal-parameter material evaluates as CutPlate.ofForward over createBerremanForward of the promoted builders.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add ItemEvaluation.fs (Domain, the item-model evaluator, invoked from the run host and S11's forward model) and ItemEvaluationTests.fs; sec 0.1's ExperimentRun.fs row may name BeamLayout.fs (detectorCaptures) and Propagation.fs (behaviorInputStokes deleted).\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py: SourceEmission, ItemEvaluation, ItemEvaluationError, ParameterValues, ElementOrientation, CutPlate, BoundOpticalElement, DetectorCapture, ElementStep, ObjectStep, every new *Err case and Bound* case, detectorCaptures, lightSourceAxes, emittedInto, emissionWith, boundWith, ofStackSample, ofOpticalForm, ofForward, withThicknessValues, forComponent, retardanceAt, transmittingAt, inComponent, muellerElement, repeatedLayerThickness, substrateThickness, blackBoxScale, objectIds, checkedFor, defaultsOf, ofParameters, withValue, sampleAzimuth, ofValues. filmThickness, valueOf and observable match only test-local values, STL test locals and a record field, none of them our member on the same receiver.\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 254, is not WIRE.\n- step_compiler check_spec reports the same note on the staged copy and nothing on the wired copy.\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings.\n- Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs removed from step 252's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its two deleted facts and SCOPE_CONSUMERS on Propagation.behaviorInputStokes; ElementMenuTests.fs removed from step 254's gives SCOPE_TEST and SCOPE_CONSUMERS on availableCaptures.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s81/build_s81.py, s81_common.py, s81_steps_a.py and s81_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S8.2 (Setups as slots): appended steps 255-266 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (29 obligations, 12 acceptance bindings, 12 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 255-266). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 255 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs, ItemModels.fs, MuellerReconstruction.fs): SetupError (seven *Err cases), SetupName (tryCreate, fileStem, nextFreeAmong, firstFree = the first free 'Setup <n>'), SetupRevision, SetupReference; FileStem.firstFreeText (the suffix sequence moved out of ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong, which calls it); DialSign.physicalAngleOf (the rule moved out of MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle, which calls it) and DialSign.readingOf. unit-tests over MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 256 IMPLEMENT: new Domain Setups.fs (module Setups, directly after BeamLayout.fs): SlotTurn (PlacementTurn | DialTurn of reading : Angle), SlotContent (EmptySlotContent | ItemInSlot), SetupSlot { id; placement; zoom; beam; content } with layoutElement, SetupRevisionRecord, Setup { name; revision; slots; history } with reference, slotsAt, heldItems, create (DuplicateSetupNameErr by file stem) and revisedWith over Lifecycle.decideVersioning. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.\n- 257 IMPLEMENT: SlotPosition, SlotRole (Source / Prep k / Obj k / Analyzer k / Detector k, with text, never stored), RoledSlot, SetupSlot.inLightOrder and Setup.lightOrder, derived from the kind and the BeamLayout path.\n- 258 IMPLEMENT: ParameterState.currentValue (moved out of ParameterValues.ofParameters), ParameterValue.angle (moved into ItemModels.fs), Item.dialZeroAngle; ItemModelChoice.libraryEntryOpt and slotKinds; SetupSlot.withItem / withoutItem / drawnWith / recordedWith; SetupSwap and Setup.swapTarget.\n- 259 IMPLEMENT: TableAndElementRotationView.TestElement is deleted; the model's elements are Setups.SetupSlot list (the lower type), every element placed empty; layoutElements maps layoutElement; the TestWindows view and every test that named TestElement re-pointed. MainSceneMsgTests gains one fact.\n- 260 IMPLEMENT: the setup file replaces the scene file. SetupFile and Setup.libraryReferences (moved from SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences); Scene.fs keeps SnapMode alone; setup.schema.json describes { schemaVersion; setup { name; revision; slots; history } }; validateSetupFile, SetupFile.fileText, KitFileText.parseSetupFile, KitProxy.writeSetup / readSetups, KitLibraryContext.recordSetup; OpenedKit.setups; the model's setupName, kitSetups, activeSetupOpt; SetSetupName, CreateSetup and ActivateSetup replace SceneSetName / SceneSave / SceneLoad; captureScene / restoreScene deleted; the setup row and ids. RENAME_TEST SceneRoundTripTests -> SetupRoundTripTests and SceneSaveLoadTests -> SetupSaveLoadTests; ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.\n- 261 IMPLEMENT: experiments reference setups. ElementBinding, PlacementSummary, ElementDescriptor and Lifecycle.VersionRef deleted; VariedElement.label; Experiment.setup : SetupReference; Setup.pinFor, Experiment.slotsIn, Experiment.itemsUsedBy (moved, now the referenced revision's slot items); ExperimentDataLoad reads the slots; ExperimentCollectionSnapshot.setups; KitLibrarySetupErr; experiment.schema.json setup { name; revision }; recordExperiment refuses an unheld revision and snapshots nothing; copyExperimentsFrom brings the setups (items mapped, same content not rewritten, a clash renamed by nextFreeAmong with its experiments following); ExpCommit records the active setup (revisedWith over pinFor, or a new first-free setup) before the experiment; the solver hand-off reads slots in light order; AGENTS.md gotcha 'The table is the active setup'.\n- 262 IMPLEMENT: SaveSetup (in place until an experiment references the revision, then the next revision; nothing written with no active setup or an unchanged table; refused read-only); activeSetupText and saveSetupButton.\n- 263 IMPLEMENT: model.tryItemModelChoice (itemModelCaption reads it) and AssignSlot (writes nothing; refusals told).\n- 264 IMPLEMENT: SwapSlot (switches to the held setup with the swapped content, else creates and activates '<active> (2)' or 'Setup <n>'; the swapped-from setup never written; creates nothing read-only).\n- 265 IMPLEMENT: chartForRun evaluates a slot holding an item through boundWith over the item's own parameters (ObjectStep for a Sample slot, ElementStep otherwise); objectIds counts sample items; the no-analyzer and bound checks count items.\n- 266 IMPLEMENT: model.runEmission, the source slot's item emitting through emissionWith over its own parameters (default parameter set without one); chartForRun reads with it.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Setup gains history (earlier revisions, oldest first) beyond the brief's { name; revision; slots }: an experiment that references an earlier revision must still resolve its slots, and 001 sec A names one <name>.setup-json per setup, so the revisions live in that one file, as an item file keeps its value history (step 222). The revision rule is Lifecycle.decideVersioning (.spec-md sec 6 'Version rule') with metadata (), the pin being 'an experiment of the window references the current revision'.\n2. Roles are derived, never stored: LightSource slots are the source, Sample slots objects, Detector slots detectors, any other slot (polarizers, lenses, mirrors) a prep when its BeamLayout path crosses no Sample slot and an analyzer otherwise (an element on an object's reflected ray included); each role ordered by light depth then table order. Departure: 001 sec J lists one Detector; the table captures T and R through a detector on each branch (step 254), so detectors are numbered too. Without a sample every optical element is a prep; an empty object is a Sample slot holding nothing or the Empty slot (air) item.\n3. The table's elements are the active setup's slots: TestElement had SetupSlot's fields without the content, so it is collapsed into the lower type (AGENTS.md 'A bijection is collapsed, not bridged'), and no capture / restore mapping remains.\n4. A setup is the optical path: the table view, the snap mode and the rotation pivot that step 147's scene file held are the window's. Loading a setup keeps them; Scene.fs keeps SnapMode alone. The setup file keeps schema version 1 in its new shape: no kit of the old shape exists outside test output (.spec-md sec 7).\n5. A dial reading is an Angle on the dial's scale (DialTurn of reading : Angle), as MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle already takes it, so no reading type, wrap or bijection is added (ELEV001, ELEV006). The one rule sign · (reading − zero) moved onto DialSign.physicalAngleOf. The table works in physical R1: SetupSlot.drawnWith maps readings through the item's current dialZero when a setup is drawn, and recordedWith maps R1 back when the table is recorded, so a recalibrated zero moves the element.\n6. A slot holding a preset or sample item is bound to that library entry (valueId and placementEmissionForEntry, as the table binds an entry), so drawing, Details and the bound source's wavelength agree with the item. An item-model item leaves the binding: a detector slot holding a detector item reads the kind of its bound detector preset, the gain, dark offset, noise and Mueller-polarimeter matrix being S11.2's forward model.\n7. Slot fit: library entries by LibraryEntry.forKinds; item models by form: real LP -> LinearPolarizer; retarder -> LinearPolarizer, CircularPolarizer, Sample; black box -> Sample; compound -> both polarizer kinds (as the compound presets); empty slot -> both polarizer kinds and Sample; the three detector models -> Detector.\n8. Writes are explicit: CreateSetup, SaveSetup, ExpCommit and a swap that creates a setup write the active setup; table edits (drags, rotations, AssignSlot) write nothing, so a turn never mints a revision by itself. A table that is no setup yet takes 'Setup <n>' (SetupName.firstFree) at a commit or a swap; a swap from an active setup takes '<name> (2)' (nextFreeAmong); a copied setup whose name the target holds with other content takes nextFreeAmong too, its experiments following. S8.3's template replaces these names.\n9. Experiment.libraryReferences goes: an experiment references a setup revision, whose library versions recordSetup snapshots, so recordExperiment snapshots nothing and refuses a revision the kit lacks (KitLibrarySetupErr). VariedElement carries the varied slot's label, so a row outlives the slot; a dark line describes its setup reference.\n10. Lifecycle.VersionRef is deleted with ElementBinding: step 65 kept it for that binding alone. LifecycleTests' 'version ref distinguishes a material version from a sample version' goes with it; SampleProxyTests and MaterialProxyTests are authorized in case a fixture still names it.\n11. Contract effects are omitted where the baseline census names files earlier steps delete or rewrite (the S2.2 precedent, interpretation 8): Scene.SceneSnapshot / SceneElement / SceneName / SceneStoreError (SceneProxyTests.fs, deleted by step 151); ElementBinding / PlacementSummary / ElementDescriptor / Experiment / VariedElement / ExperimentCollectionSnapshot (ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs, deleted by step 152); VersionRef (MaterialStore.fs / SampleStore.fs uses removed by step 65); updateTableAndElementRotation (census of every caller) and objectIds (spec-created, no census). Each step's closing grep and the build (FS0025 as an error) prove them. Census-only readers that compile as they are are authorized edits whose how_to says nothing changes in them (step 259: PlacedSampleEmissionTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, LibraryWindowTests, LightSourceEditorTests, ScrollExtentTests).\n12. ExperimentProxyTests deletes five facts whose subject is gone (E2's chain, versionRefs, the two pin facts, an experiment's library references); the pin rule is SampleProxyTests' (step 65) and the setup's references KitContentFileJsonTests' (step 260). Counts: constructor 255 +5, 256 +5, 257 +3, 258 +5, 259 0, 260 0, 261 +1, 262 +2, 263 +3, 264 +3; ui-tests 259 +1, 261 +1, 262 +1, 265 +3, 266 +2; ui-smoke unchanged.\n13. ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate takes the experiment's slots; detectorKindOf reads the first Detector slot's preset binding, its rule unchanged. The solver hand-off (retired by S11.5) reads the snapshot's setups and lists role texts.\n14. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s82/seam.json):\n   - build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on every step; unit-tests over BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests on 255 (MuellerReconstruction.fs is in its applies_to; seam-plan proposed none);\n   - ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests by class on 259-266, which edit Ui code; 260 adopts seam-plan's every-class list (its Ui.Tests.fsproj edit for the renamed SetupSaveLoadTests.fs reaches every class) plus KitWindowTests, less WireUiFinalCompositionTests, whose facts are all ui-smoke (SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM); 261's WireUiFinalCompositionTests and two KitWindowTests copy facts are ui-smoke facts;\n   - not adopted: kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1) and seam-plan's 'final step runs every planned gate' row for 266 (266 is final only until the next section is appended).\n15. Budget: 12 steps against a soft 12-22. 261 is one step because Experiment.setup's type changes every consumer at once (the step 135 precedent).\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S8.3 (naming template, grid generator): format from Setup.lightOrder / SetupSlot.inLightOrder (SlotRole.text, the slot items' labels, a DialTurn reading or the placement R1 as phi); parse names into slot items and angles; GenerateSetupGrid builds setups through Setup.create and SetupSlot.withItem; the template replaces SetupName.firstFree / nextFreeAmong where a setup is named; MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle now calls DialSign.physicalAngleOf.\n- S8.4 (slot bar): one chip per RoledSlot of SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements; a chip's compatible items are the kit items whose model.tryItemModelChoice has the slot's kind in slotKinds; choosing one sends SwapSlot; RecordExperiment is ExpCommit's flow over the active setup (step 261).\n- S9.1 (experiments v2): Experiment.setup is a SetupReference and a varied element is a slot id with its label; CorrectSetup re-points the reference; dial scans record readings (DialTurn).\n- S11.2 (forward model): read the referenced revision's slots (Experiment.slotsIn), a DialTurn reading through DialSign.physicalAngleOf and the item's dialZero (an ordinary, possibly unknown, parameter).\n- S12.1 / S12.2: build setups through CreateSetup, AssignSlot and SwapSlot.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.1 may add rows for Lifecycle.fs (VersionRef deleted), ExperimentDataLoad.fs, ExperimentCollectionStore.fs, SolverHandoffView.fs and KitContentFiles.fs; sec 0.2 may add Setups.fs (Domain; invoked from the constructor window, KitProxy and the copy), SetupTests.fs and SetupModelTests.fs, and the renamed SetupRoundTripTests.fs and SetupSaveLoadTests.fs.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py: Setups, SetupSlot, SetupName, SetupRevision, SetupReference, SetupError, SetupRevisionRecord, SetupFile, SlotTurn, PlacementTurn, DialTurn, SlotContent, EmptySlotContent, ItemInSlot, SlotPosition, SlotRole and its five cases, RoledSlot, SetupSwap, SwitchToHeldSetup, CreateSwappedSetup, the seven SetupError cases, KitLibrarySetupErr, firstFreeText, firstFree, physicalAngleOf, readingOf, currentValue, dialZeroAngle, libraryEntryOpt, slotKinds, withItem, withoutItem, drawnWith, recordedWith, swapTarget, inLightOrder, lightOrder, slotsAt, slotsIn, pinFor, revisedWith, heldItems, layoutElement, setupFile, writeSetup, readSetups, recordSetup, parseSetupFile, validateSetupFile, SetSetupName, CreateSetup, SaveSetup, ActivateSetup, AssignSlot, SwapSlot, setupName, kitSetups, activeSetupOpt, setupNameField, createSetupButton, saveSetupButton, savedSetups, savedSetup, activeSetupText, tryItemModelChoice, runEmission, SetupTests, SetupModelTests, SetupRoundTripTests, SetupSaveLoadTests. Renamed before writing: physicalAngle -> physicalAngleOf (MuellerReconstruction's free physicalAngle), assigned -> withItem and emptied -> withoutItem (generic hits), swapTo -> swapTarget (Groups.fs), itemIds -> heldItems (the model's itemIds field), dialZero -> dialZeroAngle (ParameterName.dialZero).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 266, is not WIRE.\n- step_compiler check_spec reports the same note on the staged copy and nothing on the wired copy.\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings. Earlier runs found the census gaps fixed in interpretation 11, the ui-smoke facts of 261 and the test effect step 259 needed.\n- Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: KitContentFileJsonTests.fs removed from step 260's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its five facts; LibraryWindowTests.fs removed from step 259's gives SCOPE_CONSUMERS on TestElement and TableAndElementRotationModel.elements.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s82/build_s82.py, s82_common.py, s82_steps_a.py, s82_steps_b.py and s82_steps_c.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S8.3 (The naming template and the grid generator): appended steps 267-276 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (27 obligations, 10 acceptance bindings, 10 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 267-276). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 267 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs, Storage kit.schema.json): NamingTemplate of string (.value; standard = 001 sec J's '{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}'), declared before KitFile; KitFile gains namingTemplate after sendExclude; KitFile.create sets the standard template; kit.schema.json requires it as a string (schema version 1 kept).\n- 268 IMPLEMENT: new Domain NamingTemplates.fs (module NamingTemplates, directly after Setups.fs): NamePart, NameAlias { label : ItemLabel; part }, PlaceholderNeed, TemplatePlaceholder (SlotPlaceholder of SlotRole | AnglePlaceholder of SlotPosition | NotePlaceholder) with text and need, TemplateValue, TemplatePiece, NamingTemplateError (seven *Err cases), NamingTemplate.pieces and tryCreate. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.\n- 269 IMPLEMENT: NameText, SlotPart, ObjectAngle, NameReading (tryFindPart, tryFindAngle); NamingTemplate.writeName and readName (the ways of leaving out optional groups tried in a fixed order; each value runs to the first following owned text at least one character on). The lab's label cases are the engine's first tests.\n- 270 IMPLEMENT (MuellerReconstruction.fs, BerremanTests): experimentRegex, objectRegex, MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed, ParsedExperiment, ParsedObject, MuellerLabelToken and the RegularExpressions open deleted; MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText; NameReading.family / objectRotation / matrixKind / objectPhi moved with their rules; buildDesign reads labels through NamingTemplate.standard. MuellerReconstructionTests' label fact renamed and re-pointed, section 7.2's prepareRow re-pointed, numbers unchanged. 001 sec T 'From section 8' (experimentRegex) holds from here. unit-tests over MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 271 IMPLEMENT: ItemLabel.namePart, NameText.toSetupName (one way), SlotItem; NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf (slots in light order, aliases, Obj k's DialTurn reading or R1), itemsOf, setupNameOf, setupNameAmong (the template's name made free by nextFreeAmong, else the given name).\n- 272 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ExpCommit on a table that is no setup yet and SwapSlot's CreateSwappedSetup name the new setup by the kit's template (setupNameAmong), S8.2's names kept when the template cannot name the table.\n- 273 IMPLEMENT (TARV, KitWindowView, UiIds, ConstructorUiIdOfDomain): NamingTemplate.caption; namingTemplateField, saveNamingTemplateButton; model namingTemplateText; SetNamingTemplateText and SaveNamingTemplate (read-only guard, tryCreate, unchanged told, KitContext.saveKitFile); the kit bar's 'Naming template:' row.\n- 274 IMPLEMENT: SetupError gains SlotItemTwiceErr; new Domain SetupGrids.fs (module SetupGrids, directly after NamingTemplates.fs): SlotChoice { itemOpt; r1 }, SlotOptions, SlotPick, GridCombination with slotsOver, SetupGrid { axes; unticked } with combinations, ticked, untick, tick, create (impossible combinations unticked) and generate. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.\n- 275 IMPLEMENT (Experiments.fs): commitOverSetups, folding commit over each setup reference from a draft editing nothing.\n- 276 IMPLEMENT (TARV, AGENTS.md): GenerateSetupGrid of SetupGrids.SetupGrid (read-only guard; generate; new setups recorded; the draft committed over every generated setup and recorded as ExpCommit records; 'Generated <n> setups (<m> new) and <k> experiments.'); AGENTS.md gotcha 'Names come from the kit's naming template'.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The template speaks the polarimeter's words: {source} / {source<k>} is the polarization source, S8.2's Prep k slot; {light} is S8.2's Source slot (the light source); {obj<k>} / {phi<k>} the objects and their angles; {analyzer<k>}, {detector<k>}, {note}; no number is 1. Reason: 001 sec J's example, sec A's kit layout (items CPL1 / CPL2 beside the setup CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.setup-json) and sec O's experiment matrix ('rows source x objects x phi, columns analyzer') all call the prep polarizer the source; with {source} as the laser, 001's own example could not name its own kit.\n2. Optionality is by placeholder kind, not by new syntax: a second or later slot of a role (with its angle) and the note are optional and are left out with the literal text they own; everything else is required. 001's literal template therefore reads every science label of the lab archive verbatim (checked against the distinct labels of Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip), and rejects Darkness, BullshitCheck and LP-(Darkness)-CPL2.\n3. Item aliases live in the template's text ({source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}), keyed by placeholder and item label, so CPL1 at the source and CPL2 at the analyzer both write CPL and read back to the right item. The template stays one string in .kit-json and one field in the kit bar.\n4. NamingTemplate (the text) is declared in Kit.fs before KitFile; the engine is NamingTemplates.fs after Setups.fs because placeholders name SlotRole / SlotPosition. The text is validated by tryCreate when it is saved, not on read: every use answers a Result, and a template that cannot name a table leaves S8.2's name (no default-on-read, no up-converter).\n5. NamingTemplate.standard is the one literal of 001's template: every new kit's default and the reference pipeline's label grammar.\n6. readName is a fixed-order, regex-free scan. The only reading that differs from parsed is a darkness label (parsed: Air; the template: no reading); buildDesign never keeps such a row and no design selects Air, so every MuellerReconstructionTests number is unchanged.\n7. ELEV009 / ELEV010 check members too, and private module-level signatures are enforced (STL Analyzers/NoPrimitiveOnResultHappyPath.fs, NoPrimitiveBesideElevated.fs; enforcePrivateSignatures defaults on). So a whole name is NameText and a piece NamePart, no member mixes string with our types or returns Result<string, _> (tryCreate excepted, as the analyzers sanction it), cross-type conversions are one-way members on the source type (MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText, ItemLabel.namePart, NameText.toSetupName, NamingTemplate.caption), and the scanning helpers are locals inside members.\n8. MuellerReconstructionTests' fact 'parseExperiment decodes CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)' keeps its assertions under a new name; its decode cases, with the AIR rows, the note suffix and the non-matching labels, are NamingTemplateTests' first facts (269) and the family / kind / phi cases NamingTemplateTests' fact of 270. unit-tests' count is unchanged.\n9. Only setups the window or the grid makes are named by the template (a commit on a table that is no setup yet, a swap that creates a setup, the grid); CreateSetup keeps its typed name and copied setups keep theirs. Nothing is renamed when the template changes. Step 261's and 264's facts keep 'Setup 1' / 'Bench A (2)' because their tables hold no item in Prep 1, Obj 1 or Analyzer 1.\n10. 001 sec O gives the template no home; it is edited in the kit bar (a kit property). Save template is absent under a read-only kit, as Copy experiments is (step 207), and refused by step 185's guard.\n11. Grid options are (item or nothing, R1) per slot. A combination equal to a held setup's slots is that setup; Setup.swapTarget is not reused because it compares content and ignores R1. SetupError gains SlotItemTwiceErr (one physical piece cannot sit in two slots). create starts the impossible combinations unticked; generate refuses the whole grid when a ticked one cannot be made.\n12. The grid's experiments are the window's draft committed over each generated setup (commitOverSetups folds commit); experiments keep ExperimentId names until S9.1 names them by the template and adds scans.\n13. Contract effects: step 272 declares none (an arm change of updateTableAndElementRotation, whose census lists every caller; S8.2 interpretation 11's precedent). Step 267's KitFile.create and SchemaValidation.validateKitFile behaviour effects were dropped after SYMBOL_CENSUS_UNKNOWN / SCOPE_CONSUMERS findings: KitFile's change_shape covers create, and the validator's code is unchanged (only its schema file is edited).\n14. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s83/seam.json): build, elevation and constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on every step; unit-tests over BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests on 270 only (MuellerReconstruction.fs and BerremanTests are in its applies_to); ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests by class on 272 (ExperimentControlsTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, InverseConstructorTests, SetupSaveLoadTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests), 273 (KitWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests) and 276 (InverseConstructorTests, SetupSaveLoadTests). Not adopted: seam-plan's kit-acceptance on 273 (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1) and its 'final step runs every planned gate' row for 276 (final only until the next section is appended).\n15. Counts: constructor-unit-tests 267 +1, 268 +5, 269 +4, 270 +1, 271 +4, 272 +2, 273 +2, 274 +4, 275 +1, 276 +4; ui-tests 273 +1; unit-tests 0 (one rename); ui-smoke unchanged.\n16. Budget: 10 steps against a soft 10-18.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S8.4 (slot bar, grid UI): SetupGridGenerateButton builds a SetupGrid through SetupGrid.create over the chips' options (each a SlotChoice) and sends GenerateSetupGrid; untick / tick are the grid's own members.\n- S9.1 (experiments v2): name experiments by the kit's template through nameReadingOf slots items (Some note) and writeName (a NameText); give the experiment name type a one-way member from NameText or to it, never both (ELEV006); extend commitOverSetups and GenerateSetupGrid to scans.\n- S9.3 (split and match): a split group's key is a NameText born at the import profile; match it by readName and itemsOf (or compare with writeName of the kit's setups); an unmatched group's setup comes from itemsOf and the reading's angles.\n- S12.1 (AT-1): the lab template is '{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL,LP2=LP}-{note}' (001's text with the item aliases), set through SetNamingTemplateText and SaveNamingTemplate; the AIR setups put an item labelled AIR (the Empty slot model) in Obj 1, because {obj1} and {phi1} are required; Darkness and BullshitCheck labels do not read through the template.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add NamingTemplates.fs and SetupGrids.fs (Domain; invoked from the window's setup naming, GenerateSetupGrid and MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign), NamingTemplateTests.fs and SetupGridTests.fs; sec 0.1's MuellerReconstruction.fs row (experimentRegex, objectRegex, parsed deleted) is met by step 270.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (log specs/0050/.artifacts/s83/namecheck1.log): NamingTemplate, NamingTemplates, NamingTemplateError and its seven cases, NamePart, NameAlias, NameText, PlaceholderNeed, RequiredPlaceholder, OptionalPlaceholder, TemplatePlaceholder, SlotPlaceholder, AnglePlaceholder, NotePlaceholder, TemplateValue, TemplatePiece, LiteralPiece, ValuePiece, SlotPart, ObjectAngle, NameReading, SlotItem, tryFindPart, tryFindAngle, readName, writeName, nameReadingOf, itemsOf, setupNameOf, setupNameAmong, toSetupName, SetupGrids, SetupGrid, SlotChoice, SlotOptions, SlotPick, GridCombination, slotsOver, untick, SlotItemTwiceErr, commitOverSetups, GenerateSetupGrid, SetNamingTemplateText, SaveNamingTemplate, namingTemplateText, namingTemplateField, saveNamingTemplateButton, NamingTemplateTests, SetupGridTests. Renamed before writing: read / write -> readName / writeName (generic hits), readingOf -> nameReadingOf (DialSign.readingOf, step 255). Kept on purpose: family, matrixKind, objectRotation, objectPhi (moved from ParsedExperiment, deleted in the same step), nameText (STL hits are locals), namePart (one STL local).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 276, is not WIRE.\n- step_compiler check_spec reports the same note on the staged copy and nothing on the wired copy.\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings. The earlier run's two step-267 findings are interpretation 13.\n- Negative probes on the wired copy are reported: NamingTemplateTests.fs removed from step 269's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its four facts; MuellerReconstructionTests.fs removed from step 270's gives SCOPE_TEST on the renamed fact and SCOPE_CONSUMERS on MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed, ParsedExperiment and buildDesign.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s83/build_s83.py, s83_common.py, s83_steps_a.py and s83_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S8.4 (The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem): appended steps 277-284 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (26 obligations, 8 acceptance bindings, 8 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 277-284). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 277 IMPLEMENT (Domain Setups.fs, NamingTemplates.fs): PickLetter of char (tryCreate: first character, upper-cased invariant, letter or digit only); SetupSlot.turnAngle (a DialTurn slot's reading, else R1), moved out of NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf's AnglePlaceholder arm, which calls it; SetupSlot.fittingItems (the items whose resolved choice's slotKinds hold the slot's kind, step 258's withItem rule applied first); SetupSlot.pickedByLetter (the next fitting item whose label starts with the letter after the held one, wrapping; never the held item). Three SetupTests facts.\n- 278 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ExpCommit's two halves (the table recorded as the active setup; the appended experiments recorded) become one private function each, called by ExpCommit, GenerateSetupGrid and the new RecordExperiment. RecordExperiment: read-only guard; 'Not recorded — …' for a draft that cannot commit or has no capture; otherwise the table recorded as ExpCommit records it and commitOverSetups [setup.reference] appends a NEW experiment (never editing the draft's own); 'Recorded <id> over <reference.describe>.'. Four SetupModelTests facts; the KitWindowModelTests read-only fact also sends it.\n- 279 IMPLEMENT (TARV): model slotChipOpenOpt; model.slotChipItems; ToggleSlotChip (one list open at a time, writes nothing); SwapSlot closes the list on every outcome. Two SetupModelTests facts.\n- 280 IMPLEMENT: new Ui SlotBarView.fs, compiled directly before TableAndElementRotationView.fs: SlotChipState, SlotBarState, SlotBarHandlers, slotBarView. UiIds slotBar, slotChipChoiceList, recordExperimentButton; ConstructorUiIdOfDomain SlotRole.uiKey, slotChip (SlotChip_<role>, e.g. SlotChip_Obj1), slotChipChoice, ItemLabel.caption, Angle.degreeCaption, RoledSlot.chipCaption ('Obj 1: QZ @ 45°'). TARV: model.slotBarState, private slotBarHandlers (pickByLetter resolved against the model into SwapSlot); mainView's tableSurface docks the bar above the table. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests (four ui-tests facts incl. Tab and typed letters, two ui-smoke presses: a chip and an item; Record experiment twice). KitWindowTests' read-only fact finds no recordExperimentButton.\n- 281 IMPLEMENT (Domain SetupGrids.fs): GridSlotDraft { slot; items; angles } and SetupGridDraft { slots; unticked } with empty, slotDraft, withItemToggled, withGridAngle, withoutGridAngle, withCombinationToggled and gridOver (axes in light order, each item at each angle, SetupGrid.create, the user's unticks kept while listed). Three SetupGridTests facts.\n- 282 IMPLEMENT (TARV): model setupGridOpt and model.setupGrid; OpenSetupGrid, CloseSetupGrid, ToggleSetupGridItem, AddSetupGridAngle (BarDegrees, wrappedAngle), RemoveSetupGridAngle, ToggleSetupGridCombination, none writing; GenerateSetupGrid (step 276) unchanged, sent with model.setupGrid. Three SetupModelTests facts.\n- 283 IMPLEMENT: new Ui SetupGridView.fs after SlotBarView.fs: GridCombinationMark (CombinationTicked / CombinationUnticked / CombinationImpossible of reason), GridCombinationState, SetupGridSlotState, SetupGridState, SetupGridHandlers, setupGridView. UiIds setupGridOpenButton, setupGridPanel, setupGridCombinationList, setupGridGenerateButton (001 sec O), setupGridCloseButton, setupGridCombination; ConstructorUiIdOfDomain setupGridItemChoice, setupGridAngleField, setupGridAngle, GridCombination.caption. SlotBarHandlers gains openSetupGrid ('Setup grid…'); TARV model.setupGridState (impossible marked by slotsOver's error) and setupGridHandlers; the panel docks between the bar and the table. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests (four ui-tests facts, one ui-smoke press flow); ScrollExtentTests gains the Main page with the grid open; SlotBarTests' id fact checks setupGridOpenButton.\n- 284 IMPLEMENT (Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md): KitWindowTests ui-smoke acceptance through kitWindowView over a kit folder (Record experiment twice over 'Bench', a chip swap creating 'Bench (2)', Record again; the reopened folder lists both setups and E1-E3); AGENTS.md gotcha 'The slot bar is the quick swap'.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. One dropdown per chip, the item's. The brief writes the chips as 'Source: Laser | Prep: CPL1 | Obj 1: QZ @ 45 deg | ...' and says 'Each dropdown lists compatible items only'; 001 sec J's '@ 45° ▾' is read through it. An object's chip shows its angle (the slot's turnAngle: a dial reading, else R1, the angle the naming template writes); the angle is turned in the Rotate bay as every R1 is, and the grid generator varies it. No angle-swap message is added.\n2. Every chip opens its list, the source's and the detector's included; 001's example marks no ▾ on them because its kit holds one of each. Chips read SlotRole.text (S8.2's chip names: 'Prep 1', 'Detector 1').\n3. A chip is a focusable Border in the codebase's box look (no Avalonia Button is used anywhere in the views), and its open list is model state (slotChipOpenOpt) drawn inline under the chips, not a Popup, Flyout or ComboBox: deterministic for headless tests, portable to WinForms (AGENTS.md), and free of ComboBox's selection re-entrance on re-render. Letters pick through the pure Domain rule pickedByLetter, not Avalonia's text search; a letter never swaps a slot to its own content (that would create a setup out of nothing on a table that is no setup yet). The open list marks the held item, whose press only closes the list.\n4. The bar sits inside the main page directly above the table, so SlotBarView.fs and SetupGridView.fs compile before TableAndElementRotationView.fs as projections of their own state and handler records (the Experiments bay's ExperimentControlsState / ExperimentControlsHandlers shape); TARV builds them (model.slotBarState, model.setupGridState, private slotBarHandlers, setupGridHandlers) and docks them. The Items panel and the flow strip, which surround the page, compile after TARV (steps 238, 239). mainView's signature is unchanged, so every test mounting it sees the bar.\n5. Chip ids are role-based (SlotChip_Source, SlotChip_Prep1, SlotChip_Obj1, …, via SlotRole.uiKey): the role is what a chip is and tests name 'the Obj 1 chip' by meaning; roles come from the one ray law (step 257). Choice ids add the item's GUID.\n6. RecordExperiment always appends a new experiment over the active setup (commitOverSetups of one reference, step 275), while ExpCommit edits the experiment its draft edits. The table-to-setup rule is ExpCommit's (step 261 (8)(b), 272), shared through one private function, so Record works on a table that is no setup yet (template name, else Setup n) and mints the next revision over a changed table an experiment pins. Several experiments over one setup, each its own <id>.experiment-json, is the direct problem.\n7. The grid's editable options are Domain (SetupGridDraft), so the panel holds no rule. Options are kit items only (an empty slot is an item of the Empty slot model, S8.3's request for AIR); angles are R1 in the table's convention (BarDegrees.wrappedAngle, [0, 360)), entered one at a time through the rotation bar's own parser (BarDegrees.tryCreate), each removable. Axes follow light order whatever the edit order; a slot with no angle is tried at its own R1. An untick lasts while its combination is listed. Generate is offered only for a writable kit with an axis and a ticked combination; the grid's edits write nothing, so Setup grid… is offered read-only too. GenerateSetupGrid (step 276) is unchanged and the panel stays open after it.\n8. Contract effects: mainView declares none (its signature is unchanged and the census lists every test that mounts it, as SCOPE_CONSUMERS reported when change_behavior was declared; S8.3 interpretation 13's precedent). NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf declares none for the moved angle rule (steps 255 and 258's precedent: a moved rule's caller keeps its contract).\n9. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates': build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on 277-283; ui-smoke (whole) on 278-280 and 282-284; ui-tests by class on 278 (ExperimentControlsTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, InverseConstructorTests, ScrollExtentTests, SetupSaveLoadTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, ExpCommit's UI users), 279 (SetupSaveLoadTests), 280 and 283 (every class that mounts mainView — AppContextTests, ElementMenuTests, ExperimentControlsTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, InverseConstructorTests, KitWindowTests, LayerBandsControlsTests, LibraryControlsTests, LibraryWindowTests, LightSourceEditorTests, MainSceneMsgTests, MainWorkbenchTests, MaterialsWindowTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, ScrollExtentTests, SourceAndDetectorMoveTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests — plus SlotBarTests, and SetupGridPanelTests on 283), 282 (InverseConstructorTests, SetupSaveLoadTests) and 284 (KitWindowTests). WireUiCompositionTests was dropped after SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM (it holds no ui-tests fact). Not adopted from executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s84/seam.json): kit-acceptance on 280, 283 and 284 (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1), its project-wide ui-tests / ui-smoke class lists (the Ui project's every dependent; the bar changes the main page only), constructor-unit-tests by class (the suite is light, whole), and its 'final step runs every planned gate' row for 284 (final only until the next section is appended).\n10. Counts: constructor-unit-tests 277 +3, 278 +4, 279 +2, 281 +3, 282 +3; ui-tests 280 +4, 283 +5; ui-smoke 280 +2, 283 +1, 284 +1; unit-tests 0.\n11. Budget: 8 steps against a soft 8-16.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S9.1 (experiments v2): RecordExperiment appends through commitOverSetups; extend it with commitOverSetups to scans, and name its experiment by the kit's template as S8.3 asks; keep RecordExperiment the slot bar's button (recordExperimentButton) and ExpCommit the bay's.\n- S9.3 (split and match): an unmatched group's setup can be created as the grid creates one (SetupGrid / SetupGridDraft are pure); the slot bar shows any setup the match activates.\n- S12.1 (AT-1, AT-2): build the kits through these messages: AssignSlot / SwapSlot for quick swaps, RecordExperiment for the direct problem, OpenSetupGrid … GenerateSetupGrid for the lab's grid; the chips are found by ConstructorUiId.slotChip of a SlotRole.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add SlotBarView.fs and SetupGridView.fs (Ui, docked by mainView above the table), SlotBarTests.fs and SetupGridPanelTests.fs.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (log specs/0050/.artifacts/s84/namecheck1.log, 61 names, no hit outside these steps): PickLetter, pickedByLetter, fittingItems, turnAngle, ToggleSlotChip, slotChipOpenOpt, slotChipItems, RecordExperiment, SlotBarView, slotBarView, SlotChipState, SlotBarState, SlotBarHandlers, slotBarState, slotBarHandlers, slotBar, slotChip, slotChipChoice, slotChipChoiceList, recordExperimentButton, chipCaption, degreeCaption, GridSlotDraft, SetupGridDraft, slotDraft, withItemToggled, withGridAngle, withoutGridAngle, withCombinationToggled, gridOver, setupGridOpt, setupGrid, OpenSetupGrid, CloseSetupGrid, ToggleSetupGridItem, AddSetupGridAngle, RemoveSetupGridAngle, ToggleSetupGridCombination, SetupGridView, setupGridView, GridCombinationMark, CombinationTicked, CombinationUnticked, CombinationImpossible, GridCombinationState, SetupGridSlotState, SetupGridState, SetupGridHandlers, setupGridState, setupGridHandlers, setupGridPanel, setupGridOpenButton, setupGridGenerateButton, setupGridCloseButton, setupGridCombinationList, setupGridCombination, setupGridItemChoice, setupGridAngleField, setupGridAngle, SlotBarTests, SetupGridPanelTests. Renamed before writing: withAngle / withoutAngle -> withGridAngle / withoutGridAngle (a SampleEditorView.fs hit); the handler fields generate / close -> generateGrid / closeGrid. ELEV013 was read (STL Analyzers/NoSingleParameterFunction.fs): setupGridHandlers (dispatch) takes a function, not one of our types, so it stays a private function.\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 284, is not WIRE; step_compiler check_spec reports the same note.\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check and check_spec with no findings. Earlier runs' SCOPE_CONSUMERS (mainView change_behavior, steps 280 and 283) and SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM (WireUiCompositionTests, step 280) are interpretations 8 and 9.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy is reported: SlotBarTests.fs removed from step 280's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its six facts.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s84/build_s84.py, s84_common.py, s84_steps_a.py and s84_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S9.1 (Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments): appended steps 285-297 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (31 obligations, 13 acceptance bindings, 13 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 285-297). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 285 IMPLEMENT (Experiments.fs, CanonicalJson.fs): ExperimentRole (ScienceRun ... PlannedRun, value 1-7, tryOfWire, text, all), SessionName (tryCreate, None for blank), ExperimentNotes (free text, none); CanonicalJson.options writes the role as its int tag (step 166's KitStar converter pattern). Two ExperimentProxyTests facts; CanonicalJsonTests' two int-tag facts changed.\n- 286 IMPLEMENT (Experiments.fs, NamingTemplates.fs): ExperimentError moved up, + InvalidExperimentNameErr and describe; ExperimentName (tryCreate, fileStem, nextFreeAmong via FileStem.firstFreeText); ExperimentId.defaultName = E<n>; NameText.toExperimentName (one way); NamingTemplate.experimentNameAmong (writeName of nameReadingOf, made free, else the given name).\n- 287 IMPLEMENT (Experiments.fs): VariableRange.sweptValues (chartForRun's grid); ScanAxis { elementId; label; variable; range } with describe; ScanSetting; ScanPoint; ScanBlock { axes; capture } with points (product, first axis outermost, a block of no axis = one point); ExperimentScan { blocks; sourceWaveLengthOpt } with points, axes, oneAxis, darkLine.\n- 288 IMPLEMENT (record switch 1): Experiment = { id; setup; scan; role; sessionOpt; notes; dataFileOpt }; VariedElement and variedLabel deleted; description keeps today's one-axis and dark-line texts; ExperimentDraft gains outerAxes, closedBlocks, axisOpt, scanOpt; addScanAxis, addScanBlock; commit from scanOpt (new = ScienceRun, no session, no notes); edit splits the scan back; requestedWavelengthsOf spans the wavelength axes; loadAndValidate validates one-axis and dark-line scans as before and refuses an X,Y file for any other scan (DataRangeMismatchErr); experiment.schema.json (version 1 kept); chartForExperiment draws one-axis scans until 293.\n- 289 IMPLEMENT: VariableParameter.VaryDialReading (0-360 over 19 points); SetupSlot.scanVariablesWith (R1 replaced by the dial reading for a dial-mounted item); the Controls mirror VariableChoice gains it; chartForRun evaluates each reading at sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle.\n- 290 IMPLEMENT (record switch 2): Experiment.name; ExperimentId.fileStem deleted; ExperimentTarget { setup; name }; commit / commitOverSetups take targets (an edit keeps the name); Experiment.renamedFor; NamingTemplate.experimentTargets; KitContentFiles writes, reads, deletes and copies by name; ExpCommit, RecordExperiment and GenerateSetupGrid name experiments by the template; ExpRemove deletes by name.\n- 291 IMPLEMENT (record switch 3): Kit.fs ImportProfileName (intensitySeries 'Intensity series', ellipsometricSeries 'Ellipsometric series'), DataRowKey, DataRowSelection (AllDataRows | KeyedDataRows), MappedAttachment { attachment; profile; rows }; Experiment.dataOpt; DetectorKind.builtInProfile; loadAndValidate reads by the profile (another name, or a key selection, is MalformedDataFileErr reading nothing); the attach arm records the detector's built-in profile over every row; schema, copy and the solver hand-off follow.\n- 292 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ExpAddScanAxis, ExpAddScanBlock (draft messages, no kit write). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests (folder kit, two facts).\n- 293 IMPLEMENT (TARV): chartForRun (model) (scan): per block, x = its last axis, one series group per point of the other axes, each path step built from the settings touching it; a one-axis scan gives today's chart exactly; chartForParams (uncalled) deleted; experimentResult, chartForExperiment and Export data read the scan; AGENTS.md run-law gotcha names it. Three ExperimentControlsTests facts.\n- 294 IMPLEMENT: Experiment.withRole / withSessionOpt / withNotes, ExperimentCollection.withStoredExperiment; SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession (blank clears), SetExperimentNotes (read-only guarded, recorded through recordExperiment). Two ExperimentModelTests facts; KitWindowModelTests' read-only fact sends them.\n- 295 IMPLEMENT: ExperimentDataLoad.fs ExperimentDataBadge (NoDataBadge, MappedDataBadge of problemOpt, ValidatedDataBadge of points, DataChangedBadge of attachment * currentOpt, OutOfRangeBadge of problem) with text and the one rule ofCheck; TARV's ExperimentFileStatus moves into it and is deleted (every caption kept by ExperimentDataBadge.caption); a refused attach is told in kitStatus; model.dataBadgeOf. InverseConstructorTests' attach facts re-pointed, the attach-failed fact renamed.\n- 296 IMPLEMENT: the bay reads v2: scan summary, Add variable / Add block, the loaded experiment's role row, session and notes fields, each row's name, role and badge; ExperimentRoleMark, ExperimentRoleOption; seven UiIds (ExperimentScanSummary, ExperimentAddScanAxisButton, ExperimentAddScanBlockButton, ExperimentRole_<key>, ExperimentSessionField, ExperimentNotesField, ExperimentBadge_<key>); ExperimentRole.uiKey / caption. Four ui-tests facts, one ui-smoke press.\n- 297 IMPLEMENT (Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md): KitWindowTests ui-smoke acceptance through kitWindowView over a folder kit (a two-axis experiment with role, session and notes read back after reopening); AGENTS.md gotcha 'An experiment is a scan over a setup revision'.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. A scan is a list of blocks, each a product of axes read on one capture (T, R or both, the observable innermost). 001 sec Q AT-2 needs it: the optic-axis plate's one experiment joins A1 (four azimuths, T) and A2 (incidence x azimuth, T and R), and every AT-2 design is evenly spaced, so VariableRange (min, max, points) stays the axis's values and no list-of-values form is added. A dark line is a block of no axis (one point).\n2. Generalised, not duplicated: VariedElement plus its range becomes ScanAxis (VariedElement deleted); VariableParameter gains VaryDialReading; the tunable source's sourceWaveLengthOpt moves onto ExperimentScan (the draft keeps its field for the bay's clamp). The capture stays MeasurementMode, now per block.\n3. Raw dial readings (001 sec I): a dial-mounted item's slot scans VaryDialReading in place of VaryR1; the chart maps readings through DialSign.physicalAngleOf and the item's dialZero (steps 255, 258).\n4. ExperimentId stays the in-window identity (messages, rows, status maps); the experiment's name is its file stem. A new experiment is named by the kit's template over its setup's slots (no note), made free by nextFreeAmong, else E<n> (ExperimentId.defaultName), so every table the template cannot name keeps today's E<n> files and texts. An edit never renames; copies rename on a clash (renamedFor) as well as renumbering ids.\n5. The data attachment is MappedAttachment { DataAttachment; ImportProfileName; DataRowSelection } in Kit.fs, where S9.2's profiles will live. Until S9.2 the profile name is real: loadAndValidate picks the parser by it ('Intensity series' / 'Ellipsometric series'), refuses any other name and a key selection with typed errors, and an attach records the detector's built-in profile over every row.\n6. A multi-variable scan cannot be validated by an X,Y file (one abscissa), so loadAndValidate refuses it with DataRangeMismatchErr; a dark line validates with VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1, the range every dark line held (step 50).\n7. Badges: 'mapped' means a mapped attachment whose points are not validated (not yet loaded, or the file did not read, the reason kept). The window's ExperimentFileStatus was the same concept, so it moves into Domain as ExperimentDataBadge (one rule, ofCheck) and is deleted, every caption kept. The excluded-points badge needs exclusions, which S9.3 adds; a case nothing could produce is not added here (see the request below).\n8. Role, session and notes are set on a recorded experiment (SetExperimentRole / SetExperimentSession / SetExperimentNotes write its file at once); a new experiment is a ScienceRun with no session and empty notes. The bay shows them while an experiment is loaded in a writable kit. The session is a name set by hand; S11.1's auto-split and gain models are the study's.\n9. The schema stays version 1 for the new experiment shape: no kit of the old shape exists outside test output (.spec-md sec 7; S8.2 interpretation 4's precedent).\n10. Contract effects: VariableParameter's change_shape is omitted because its baseline census names ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs, which step 152 deletes (S8.2 interpretation 11's precedent); the build with FS0025 as an error proves every match gains the case. Census-only readers are authorized edits whose how_to says nothing changes in them: SolverHandoffView.fs (288); ElementMenuTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, InverseConstructorTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests (289); ElementMenuTests, InverseConstructorTests (296).\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s91/seam.json): build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on 285-296; ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests by class on 288-297, the classes being the brief's (FsxAcceptanceTests, ExperimentControlsTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests) plus the classes whose files the step edits (InverseConstructorTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests, KitWindowTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, ElementMenuTests, MainWorkbenchTests, SlotBarTests, SetupGridPanelTests, DataFilePickerFolderTests as applicable). Not adopted: kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1), seam-plan's narrower or absent ui selections on 292-296 (those steps change TARV's experiment code, which the brief's classes drive), and its 'final step runs every planned gate' row for 297 (final only until the next section is appended).\n12. Counts: constructor-unit-tests 285 +2, 286 +3, 287 +3, 288 +3, 289 +1, 290 +3, 291 +3, 292 +2, 294 +2, 295 +1; ui-tests 289 +1, 293 +3, 296 +4; ui-smoke 296 +1, 297 +1; unit-tests 0.\n13. Budget: 13 steps against a soft 12-20.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S9.2 (import profiles): name the two built-in X,Y profiles ImportProfileName.intensitySeries / ellipsometricSeries ('Intensity series', 'Ellipsometric series'), as attachments already record them; store ImportProfile { name : ImportProfileName; ... } in KitFile; make loadAndValidate's parser choice (step 291) read the kit's profiles and map multi-variable scans (ScanAxis / ScanSetting) instead of step 288's refusal; KeyedDataRows selects by the profile's experiment-key column.\n- S9.3 (split, exclusions, corrections, matrix): add the experiment's exclusions and the ExcludedPointsBadge case to ExperimentDataBadge with its branch in ofCheck; a split group is a KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey) of one MappedAttachment; name experiments made from groups with experimentNameAmong's noteOpt from the read name, or the key; CorrectSetup re-points Experiment.setup (an edit keeps the name); the matrix's per-cell badge is model.dataBadgeOf.\n- S11.1 / S11.2 (studies, forward model): an experiment's points are ExperimentScan.points (ScanSetting per axis, capture per point); a VaryDialReading setting maps through DialSign.physicalAngleOf and the item's dialZero (an ordinary, possibly unknown, parameter); roles (IgnoredRun, DarkRun, CalibrationRun, DiagnosticRun) and sessionOpt are the study's inputs.\n- S12.2 (AT-2): one experiment per plate whose scan blocks are A1 / A2 / A3's (incidence R2, azimuth R1 on the plate's slot, capture per block), built through ExpAddScanAxis / ExpAddScanBlock and checked against fullConfigurations via ExperimentScan.points.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.1's Experiments.fs row is met by steps 285-296; sec 0.2 may add ExperimentModelTests.fs; sec 5's 'Experiment v2, ExperimentRole, scans, sessions' row may name ExperimentScan / ScanBlock / ScanAxis, ExperimentName and MappedAttachment (Kit.fs).\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (logs specs/0050/.artifacts/s91/namecheck2.log and this cycle's first run): ExperimentRole and its seven cases, SessionName, ExperimentNotes, ExperimentName, InvalidExperimentNameErr, defaultName, toExperimentName, experimentNameAmong, experimentTargets, ExperimentTarget, renamedFor, ScanAxis, ScanBlock, ScanSetting, ScanPoint, ExperimentScan, sweptValues, VaryDialReading, scanVariablesWith, ImportProfileName, DataRowKey, DataRowSelection, AllDataRows, KeyedDataRows, MappedAttachment, builtInProfile, ExperimentDataBadge and its five cases, dataBadgeOf, addScanAxis, addScanBlock, outerAxes, closedBlocks, axisOpt, scanOpt, ExpAddScanAxis, ExpAddScanBlock, SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession, SetExperimentNotes, withRole, withSessionOpt, withStoredExperiment, ExperimentRoleMark, RoleChosen, RoleNotChosen, ExperimentRoleOption, scanAvailability, bookkeepingAvailability, roleOptions, the seven experiment UiIds, ExperimentModelTests. Renamed before writing: Scan -> ExperimentScan (an STL type), ExperimentData -> MappedAttachment (the ExperimentData module), values -> sweptValues, ofAxis -> oneAxis. ellipsometricSeries / intensitySeries have only test-local hits (outside ELEV scope).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check reports only the mid-campaign sec 9.3 note: the final step, 297, is not WIRE; step_compiler check_spec reports the same note on the staged copy and nothing on the wired copy.\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings. The first wired run's SCOPE_CONSUMERS (loadAndValidate 288, VariableParameter and VariableChoice 289, ExperimentControlsState 296) are interpretation 10.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy is reported: ExperimentModelTests.fs removed from step 292's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its two facts.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s91/build_s91.py, s91_common.py, s91_steps_a.py and s91_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py and bind_wire.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S9.2 (Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard): appended steps 298-312 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (33 obligations, 15 acceptance bindings, 15 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 298-312). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 298 IMPLEMENT (Domain Kit.fs, Storage CanonicalJson.fs): ImportProfileName moves directly before NamingTemplate and gains phoneRoiCsv ('Phone ROI CSV'), muellerObservations ('Mueller-matrix observations') and builtIns; DataDelimiter, HeaderRowChoice, ByteOrderMark, ScanColumnUnit (deg, rad, nm, um, eV, cm-1; spectralUnitOpt), ScanReading (raw dial / physical), each with a 1-based int value, tryOfWire, text, all, written by CanonicalJson.options as tags (step 166's converter form); DataColumnNumber (from 1, index).\n- 299 IMPLEMENT (Kit.fs, kit.schema.json): ScanColumn { column; valueUnit; reading }, ReadingColumns (SignalColumns of signal * sigmaOpt | MuellerElementColumns of elements * throughputOpt), ColumnRoles { scan; reading; timestampOpt; captureIndexOpt; observableOpt; keyOpt }, ImportProfileError (seven *Err cases), ImportProfile { name; delimiter; header; bom; roles }, ImportProfileName.availableAmong (built-in and held names refused), KitFile.importProfiles (after namingTemplate, empty on create) and KitFile.withImportProfile (append, never replace); schema version 1 kept.\n- 300 IMPLEMENT: new Domain ImportProfiles.fs after ItemEvaluation.fs: Observable.value/tryOfWire/tryOfCell and SampleCut.value/tilt/tryOfWire (members here, MuellerInverse.fs untouched); BuiltInImportProfile; ChosenImportProfile (built-ins first); MeasuredSigma, RowTimestamp, ScanCell.displayValue, MappedReading, MappedRow, KeyedObservation, MappedPoints (SeriesPoints | CapturePoints | ObservationPoints | ColumnPoints) with pointCount; MuellerElementIndex, ColumnRoleChoice, ColumnChoice, ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.\n- 301 IMPLEMENT: new Storage LabFileImport.fs after MuellerDataStore.fs: KeyedObservation.observationFileText and KitFileText.parseMuellerObservations (the 25-column observation file). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.\n- 302 IMPLEMENT: one private CsvFile.Parse read and ImportProfile.mapText (a kit profile's column mapping into MappedRow list).\n- 303 IMPLEMENT: ChosenImportProfile.mapText, the one read: the X,Y built-ins call the MeasuredData parsers, Phone ROI CSV calls parseMuellerCsv (errors mapped), the observation profile parseMuellerObservations, a kit profile its mapping; each built-in reads its fixture exactly as its parser did; MeasuredData.fs's doc names the parsers as the profiles' bodies.\n- 304 IMPLEMENT: ExperimentDataProxy.fs and ExperimentDataLoad.fs compile after ImportProfiles.fs; ScanQuantity, ExperimentScan.quantities, MappedPoints.validatedFor (step 288's series rule moved; Phone ROI rows and mapped rows against the scan's quantities and the detector; observations pass); loadAndValidate and ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck carry mapped points; the solver hand-off counts their points.\n- 305 IMPLEMENT: MappedPoints.selectedBy; ExperimentDataProxy = { readPickedFile; attachDataFile; attachmentStatus; readMapped }, tryLoadIntensity / tryLoadEllipsometric deleted; loadAndValidate = readMapped then validatedFor; ExperimentDataStore.fs after LabFileImport.fs, createFileBacked resolving the profile from the kit file (DataFileKind, loadThrough deleted); every proxy built in tests follows.\n- 306 IMPLEMENT: ImportProfileName.nextFreeAmong; copyExperimentsFrom brings the kit profiles its experiments are mapped by (equal reused, different renamed with its experiments following, saved before any experiment); ExperimentCopyReport gains profiles and kitFile; the window takes the copy's kit file.\n- 307 IMPLEMENT: FileByteContent.kitFileText (the kit's one decode, the stores' decode bodies call it) and byteOrderMark; LabFileSniff, PreviewCell, PreviewRow, LabFilePreview, LabFileSource.sniffedLayout (Domain); KitFileText.previewWith through the mapping's CSV read (Storage).\n- 308 IMPLEMENT: new Ui ImportWizardView.fs after SetupGridView.fs: the wizard's MVU (ImportWizardRequest, ImportWizardApplied, ImportWizardContext, WizardProfileChoice, ImportWizardModel, ImportWizardMsg, initImportWizard, updateImportWizard). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.\n- 309 IMPLEMENT: importWizardView; fifteen ImportWizard ConstructorUiIds; uiKey / caption members in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.\n- 310 IMPLEMENT (TARV): KitWindowShell.openImportWizard (inert ignore); AttachDataFileTo renamed AttachDataFile carrying the profile name; OpenImportWizard; SaveImportProfile; ImportWizardApplied.messages (save, then attach); all behind the read-only guard; the Attach data file button sends OpenImportWizard.\n- 311 IMPLEMENT: new Ui ImportWizardWindow.fs after KitWindowView.fs: ImportWizardWindow (keepOnScreen) and module ImportWizardOpening's KitWindowShell.withImportWizard; ScrollExtentTests joins (the window and a hosted mapped model); a ui-smoke window acceptance.\n- 312 WIRE_UI (Program.fs, KitWindowTests, AGENTS.md): ConstructorScene.mount's shell .withImportWizard window dispatch; a ui-smoke end-to-end fact over a folder kit (OpenImportWizard, the wizard window, Phone ROI CSV, Attach: copied into data, mapped and validated); AGENTS.md gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles'.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. A profile is stored in Kit.fs before KitFile (ImportProfileName moved there from step 291's place). The four built-ins are code (BuiltInImportProfile), never stored; a kit profile, once saved, is never replaced (availableAmong refuses built-in and held names), because experiments name it and 001 sec K makes raw data immutable.\n2. Column roles: the scan columns, in column order, give the experiment's scan quantities in order (the distinct slot variables of its axes in first appearance, so A1's and A2's azimuth is one quantity); each carries its unit and raw dial vs physical. A custom Mueller mapping's configuration columns are its scan columns (incidence, azimuth as scan variables), the observable and the key.\n3. The observation file holds the key and all six MeasurementConfiguration fields (cut tag and tilt, thickness m, incidence and azimuth rad, observable tag, wavelength nm), the normalized m00..m33 and the throughput: the brief's 'incidence, azimuth, observable, cut / sample' plus the thickness and wavelength the 0044 shape needs to read back with no kit lookup. Numbers are written 'R' in the engine's own units, so the read is bit-exact; measured is rebuilt as throughput x normalized, misreadAbsolute's arithmetic, which gives such matrices back exactly (checked on over four million random product pairs and on the fixture values). A micrometre wavelength and an infinite thickness are refused, not converted. The key ('sample') is what splits a seed's file into its plates' experiments.\n4. Placement: CSV parsing reuses FSharp.Data, so the one read, the custom reader and the preview live in Storage LabFileImport.fs (after MuellerDataStore.fs, whose parseMuellerCsv it calls); shapes, selection and validation live in Domain ImportProfiles.fs after ItemEvaluation.fs (they hold MuellerRawRow and MuellerObservation), so ExperimentDataProxy.fs and ExperimentDataLoad.fs move after it and ExperimentDataStore.fs after LabFileImport.fs. parseMuellerCsv itself is not moved.\n5. Mapped points reuse MeasuredSeries for the X,Y built-ins (SeriesPoints), so no case is duplicated; the badge counts pointCount. Observations pass validation as read, because each carries its own configuration and S11.2 pairs them with the experiment; Phone ROI rows validate against at most one quantity (a dark line has none).\n6. The proxy resolves the profile name at read time from the built-ins and the kit file it reads, so no profile list threads through loadAndValidate, the solver hand-off or the window; readPickedFile lets the wizard read the picked file before anything is copied in, so Cancel leaves the kit untouched.\n7. Attach-with-profile: AttachDataFileTo is renamed AttachDataFile (001 sec P) and carries the profile; the button sends OpenImportWizard after its file dialog; the wizard's Attach sends SaveImportProfile then AttachDataFile; the shell opens the window (KitWindowShell.openImportWizard, inert ignore), composed by withImportWizard over the window's dispatch in Program.fs.\n8. Copy carries profiles (not in the brief): a consequence of profiles living in the kit file; without it a copied experiment would lose its mapping. S6's rename-on-clash rule applies (nextFreeAmong over FileStem.firstFreeText).\n9. The byte-order mark is sniffed from the bytes and recorded, but no read needs it, because the kit drops a leading mark (step 128); FileByteContent.kitFileText becomes the kit's one decode.\n10. Contract effects: SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment is not declared changed (its answers are the same); census-only consumers of ExperimentDataProxy, loadAndValidate and createFileBacked (AppContext.fs, SolverHandoffView.fs, SolverHandoffWindow.fs, TARV) are authorized edits at step 305 whose how_to says nothing changes in them (S9.1 interpretation 10's precedent).\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s92/seam.json): build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (light, whole; applies to OpticalConstructor/**) on every step; ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests by class on the steps touching Ui, Ui.Tests or App: InverseConstructorTests and SolverHandoffWindowTests (304), with ScrollExtentTests (305), KitWindowTests (306, 312), DataFilePickerFolderTests, InverseConstructorTests and KitWindowTests (310, the attach button's picker path is DataFilePickerFolderTests'), ImportWizardTests (308, 309), ImportWizardTests and ScrollExtentTests (311). Not adopted: kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1), seam-plan's narrower ui-smoke selections (the suite is light), unit-tests (no step touches BerremanTests, Optimization, MuellerInverse.fs or MuellerReconstruction.fs), and its final-step row for 312 (final only until the next section is appended).\n12. Counts: constructor-unit-tests 298 +1, 299 +2, 300 +5, 301 +3, 302 +3, 303 +3, 304 +2, 305 +4, 306 +2, 307 +2, 310 +3; ui-tests 308 +6, 309 +4, 311 +1; ui-smoke 311 +1, 312 +1; unit-tests 0.\n13. Budget: 15 steps against a soft 12-22.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S9.3 (split, exclusions, corrections, Data step): a split group is KeyedDataRows of one MappedAttachment and MappedPoints.selectedBy is the selection (Phone ROI experiment labels, observation keys, a mapping's key column); the Data step hosts the Data files section, whose Attach data file opens the wizard (OpenImportWizard); MappedRow carries no row number, so exclusions keyed by row add one; ExcludedPointsBadge joins ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck.\n- S9.4 (lab files into the kit): LabFileImport.fs calls MuellerDataStore.fs's parseMuellerCsv and maps its two archive MuellerDataError cases; when the archive store goes, keep the parser (or move it into LabFileImport.fs with its tests) and drop those two arms; MuellerReconstructionTests can read the kit's CSVs through ChosenImportProfile.mapText (BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile).\n- S11.2 (forward model): ObservationPoints carry complete configurations; ColumnPoints rows carry scan cells in ExperimentScan.quantities order with displayValue; CapturePoints feed the staged path.\n- S12.1 (AT-1): attach the lab CSVs by 'Phone ROI CSV' through AttachDataFile, recorded in place inside the kit (step 134).\n- S12.2 (AT-2): write each seed's file through KeyedObservation.observationFileText (keyed by the plates), copy it in, and attach each plate's experiment by 'Mueller-matrix observations' with KeyedDataRows of its key; nm wavelengths only; data identity holds bit for bit for misreadAbsolute matrices.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add ImportProfiles.fs, LabFileImport.fs, ImportWizardView.fs and ImportWizardWindow.fs; sec 5's ImportProfile row lives in Kit.fs (the kit file holds it).\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (logs specs/0050/.artifacts/s92/namecheck1.log, namecheck2.log): every new type, case, module and member, among them ImportProfiles, ImportProfile, ImportProfileError and its seven cases, DataDelimiter, HeaderRowChoice, ByteOrderMark, ScanColumnUnit, ScanReading and their cases, DataColumnNumber, ScanColumn, ReadingColumns, ColumnRoles, BuiltInImportProfile, ChosenImportProfile, MappedPoints and its cases, MappedRow, MappedReading, KeyedObservation, ScanCell, ScanQuantity, MuellerElementIndex, ColumnRoleChoice and its cases, ColumnChoice, LabFileSniff, LabFilePreview, PreviewCell, PreviewRow, LabFileImport, ImportWizardView / Window / Opening and their types and messages, OpenImportWizard, AttachDataFile, SaveImportProfile, availableAmong, withImportProfile, mapText, observationFileText, parseMuellerObservations, sniffedLayout, previewWith, readMapped, selectedBy, validatedFor, withImportWizard, ImportProfileTests, LabFileImportTests, ImportWizardTests. readPickedFile has one STL hit (a BirdMessenger record field, not a module-level name); quantities has prose hits only; sniffed was renamed sniffedLayout (a MeasuredData.fs comment word).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check and step_compiler check_spec report only the mid-campaign final-step note SELECTION_REQUIRED step 312 [unit-tests] (step 312 is WIRE_UI and currently last; S3.2 and S3.3 carried the same note).\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings, and check_spec reports nothing on it. The first wired run's SCOPE_CONSUMERS (SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment 304; ExperimentDataProxy, loadAndValidate, createFileBacked 305) are interpretation 10.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy is reported: ImportProfileTests.fs removed from step 300's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its five facts.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s92/build_s92.py, s92_common.py, s92_steps_a.py and s92_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py and check_spec_run.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, stage-run.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S9.3 (One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix): appended steps 313-328 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (34 obligations, 16 acceptance bindings, 16 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 313-328). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 313 IMPLEMENT (record switch; Kit.fs, Experiments.fs, experiment.schema.json, KitContentFiles.fs, TARV, fixtures): MappedPointNumber (from 1), ExclusionReason (non-blank), PointExclusion; MappedAttachment.exclusions (point order, one per point) with withExclusion / withoutExclusion / tryFindExclusion; CorrectionNote (non-blank), SetupCorrection { previous; corrected; note }; Experiment.corrections (oldest first, [] on commit of a new experiment, kept on an edit); schema version 1 kept; copy keeps both; the AttachDataFile arm builds exclusions = [].\n- 314 IMPLEMENT: MappedPoints.keptBy (the one rule from exclusions to the points validated, and fitted in S11); loadAndValidate validates kept points; ExperimentDataBadge gains ExcludedPointsBadge of kept * excluded ('excluded points (<k> excluded, <n> validated)'), answered by ofCheck; caption 'Loaded — <n> point(s) kept, <k> excluded'.\n- 315 IMPLEMENT (TARV): ReviewedData, DataStepDraft, model reviewedDataOpt / dataDraft; ReviewExperimentData (reads through readMapped, writes nothing), SetExclusionReason, ExcludePoint and IncludePoint (read-only guarded, typed refusals, recorded through recordExperiment, badge and review refreshed). ExperimentModelTests +3.\n- 316 IMPLEMENT: Experiment.correctedTo; SetCorrectionNote, CorrectSetup (blank note, unknown setup, unchanged setup refused; name, scan and data kept; the lab file untouched). ExperimentProxyTests +1, ExperimentModelTests +2.\n- 317 IMPLEMENT: MuellerExperimentLabel.rowKey and MappedPoints.pointKeys (selectedBy reads it: one reading of a point's key); new Domain DataSplits.fs after ExperimentDataLoad.fs: SplitKeyColumn, ChosenImportProfile.splitKeyOpt (experiment / sample / column <n> / None), KeyedGroup, MappedPoints.splitGroups. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.\n- 318 IMPLEMENT: DataRowKey.nameText, DataSplitError (SplitKeyTextErr, SplitKeyNameErr, SplitKeySetupErr, SplitKeyTwiceErr), SplitSetupOffer, SplitGroupMatch (ExperimentForGroup, SetupOfferForGroup, GroupWithoutMatch), SplitGroup, DataSplit (matched / offered / unmatched), DataSplitParam, DataSplit.ofGroups.\n- 319 IMPLEMENT (TARV): DataSplitState, model dataSplitOpt; SplitByColumn (identify: resolve the profile, require its key column, read the picked file, map, split, match; writes nothing), ToggleSplitOffer, CancelDataSplit. ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.\n- 320 IMPLEMENT (TARV): MatchByTemplate (confirm: the file attached once; each matched experiment given KeyedDataRows of its key; each ticked offer's setup recorded when new and a new experiment of the draft's scan appended as RecordExperiment appends one; first failed write stops the run).\n- 321 IMPLEMENT: ImportWizardTarget (AttachWizardTarget of ExperimentId | SplitWizardTarget) in ImportWizardView.fs; request / applied carry target; heading and button name the target; ImportWizardApplied.messages answers AttachDataFile or SplitByColumn after SaveImportProfile; OpenSplitWizard (Phone ROI CSV default).\n- 322 IMPLEMENT: new Domain ExperimentMatrices.fs after DataSplits.fs: MatrixObject, MatrixRowKey { sources; objects }, MatrixColumnKey { analyzers }, MatrixCell, ExperimentMatrix (tryFindCell, ofExperiments; first-appearance order; unplaced). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests.\n- 323 IMPLEMENT: ConstructorFlowStep gains DataFlowStep and stepsOf (Inverse: all; Main: without Data); pickDataFile, attachDataFileButton and dataFileRow MOVE from TARV to new Ui DataStepView.fs (after FlowStripView.fs); the collection builder loses its Data files section; dataStepView holds the data-file rows and 'Split a file by key…' (OpenSplitWizard); KitWindowView shows it; FlowStripView shows stepsOf the mode; UiIds flowDataStep, dataStepPanel, dataSplitFileButton. ScrollExtentTests: two renames and the Data step fact.\n- 324 IMPLEMENT: the split panel (dataSplitKeyColumn heading 'Split <leaf> by '<key>' through '<profile>'', one row per group, offer toggles, Apply split / Cancel in one row). ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.\n- 325 IMPLEMENT: ExperimentControls PointMark, PlottedPoint, pointsChartView (the inline chart's frame reused; kept points dots, excluded points rings); MappedPoints.pointCaptions / chartPoints; Review verb per data-file row; the review panel with the reason field and Exclude / Include per point.\n- 326 IMPLEMENT: the correction block (current setup, audit note field, one Re-point choice per other kit setup, the audit trail).\n- 327 IMPLEMENT: the experiment matrix at the top of the Data step (MatrixRowKey / MatrixColumnKey captions, '<name> · <badge>' entries sending ReviewExperimentData, the unplaced line); ScrollExtentTests' Data step fact covers every panel.\n- 328 IMPLEMENT (KitWindowTests, AGENTS.md): a ui-smoke end-to-end fact over a folder kit (split, offer ticked, Apply, matrix entry, ExcludePoint, CorrectSetup, each read back; the lab file unchanged); AGENTS.md's Main ribbon gotcha names the Data step, and the gotcha 'The Data step never edits a lab file' is added.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. An exclusion lives on the MappedAttachment, not on the experiment: it numbers that attachment's points (MappedPointNumber = 1-based place among readMapped's answer, the row selection applied), so attaching a file anew starts with none and no exclusion outlives its points. A MappedRow carries no row number (the S9.2 mapper's note), and the point number serves every MappedPoints case.\n2. Validation (and later the study, S11) reads the kept points (MappedPoints.keptBy), so an excluded point is never out of range; the excluded-points badge carries the kept and the excluded counts.\n3. IncludePoint is added as ExcludePoint's undo (.spec-md §10.5: an action that moves user-visible state names its undo); 001 §P lists only ExcludePoint.\n4. A correction is { previous; corrected; note } on the experiment, oldest first, with no timestamp (the kit's file times and git carry when). It re-points Experiment.setup to a setup revision the kit holds; the name, the scan and the data stay, so a lab file keyed by the name still matches. The corrected revision is pinned by Setup.pinFor (step 261), which reads references.\n5. The data dialog is S9.2's wizard plus the Data step: the wizard keeps the preview, the column roles and the profile picker and gains a target (attach to one experiment, or split across the kit's experiments); the key split's matched / unmatched table and per-point exclusion live on the Data step, because they act on the kit window's state. SplitByColumn identifies and writes nothing; MatchByTemplate confirms (.spec-md §10.3). Offers start unticked: nothing is created unasked.\n6. Matching: a key matches the experiment of the same name (file-stem identity, ignoring case), then the experiment named as the template writes the key's reading back; otherwise the reading's items and angles are placed on the table through the grid generator (SetupGrid.generate over one-choice axes: every slot whose role the template names takes the reading's item or nothing, a dial-mounted item at the physical angle of the read reading, every other slot as the table holds it), held setups and earlier offers reused, and the experiment named by experimentNameAmong with the reading's note. A new experiment records the Experiments draft's scan, as RecordExperiment and GenerateSetupGrid do; a ticked offer with no draft scan refuses the whole apply. Two groups never share an experiment (SplitKeyTwiceErr).\n7. DataSplitKeyColumn is the split panel's heading naming the key column the profile splits by (experiment for Phone ROI CSV, sample for the observation file, column <n> for a kit mapping).\n8. The Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone (ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf), keeping spec 0046's rule pinned by ScrollExtentTests' 'the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone' (renamed '… Inverse window's Data step alone'); switching to Main from it lands on Experiments.\n9. The experiment matrix opens the Data step (its cells carry data badges). Rows are the Prep items (step 268: the source is the polarization source) and the objects at their turnAngle; columns the analyzer items; first-appearance order, no sort; experiments whose setup the kit lacks are listed apart.\n10. 'Stay visible in plots, marked': the review panel's chart plots every point of the reviewed experiment against its number, a kept point a dot and an excluded one a ring (pointsChartView, which calls the inline chart's private frame helpers in ExperimentControls.fs, not a copy); the point list marks it with its reason. Captions and chart points per MappedPoints case are Ui members (ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs).\n11. Domain-parameterised ids are ConstructorUiId extensions in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs (AGENTS.md; savedSetup and attachDataFile precedents); fixed ids and the position-keyed chart marks are UiIds members.\n12. Contract effects: loadAndValidate's census consumers (TableAndElementRotationView.fs, SolverHandoffView.fs) are authorized edits at step 314 whose how_to says nothing changes in them (S9.2 interpretation 10's precedent). Experiment and the window model are not declared change_shape (S9.1's precedent); step 313 enumerates the fixture files.\n13. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s93/seam.json): build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests (whole) on every step; ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests by class on the steps touching Ui, Controls or Ui.Tests: the classes whose files the step edits plus those that drive the changed code (InverseConstructorTests, KitWindowTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests, ExperimentControlsTests, ImportWizardTests, DataFilePickerFolderTests, DataStepTests as applicable). Not adopted: kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1), seam-plan's absent ui selections on 314-320 (those steps change the window or its data validation), its broad ui-tests selections on 324 (UiIds additions change no other class) and its final-step row for 328 (final only until the next section is appended). 328 is IMPLEMENT: nothing in the composition root changes.\n14. Counts: constructor-unit-tests 313 +2, 314 +2, 315 +3, 316 +3, 317 +3, 318 +4, 319 +3, 320 +3, 321 +1, 322 +2, 323 +1; ui-tests 321 +1, 323 +1, 324 +3, 325 +3, 326 +2, 327 +1; ui-smoke 323 +1, 324 +1, 325 +1, 327 +1, 328 +1; unit-tests 0.\n15. Budget: 16 steps against a soft 12-22.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S9.4 (lab files into the kit): the optics-mueller CSVs split through SplitByColumn (by 'experiment', Phone ROI CSV) and MatchByTemplate; nothing in S9.3 reads the archive.\n- S11.1 / S11.2 (studies, forward model): an experiment's points are readMapped data |> keptBy data.exclusions (excluded points never enter a residual); its setup is the corrected one, Experiment.corrections being audit only.\n- S11.5 (study view): Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish follow DataFlowStep in ConstructorFlowStep.all, and stepsOf decides per constructor.\n- S12.1 (AT-1): split data/raw/final/*.csv by 'experiment' (SplitByColumn + MatchByTemplate, offers ticked for the -BR / -2R / -2 repeats with the draft's scan set); 'Darkness' and 'BullshitCheck' do not read through the lab template, so their files attach whole (AttachDataFile) to DarkRun / DiagnosticRun experiments; the excluded frame (LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2, description 140°, capture index 17) is ExcludePoint of its MappedPointNumber among that experiment's keyed points with the reason 'likely contaminated frame'; the LR correction is CorrectSetup to the −45 / −90 setups with its audit note.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add DataSplits.fs, ExperimentMatrices.fs and DataStepView.fs; sec 5's Experiment v2 row may name MappedAttachment.exclusions and Experiment.corrections.\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (logs specs/0050/.artifacts/s93/namecheck1.log, namecheck2.log, namecheck3.log). nameText (DataRowKey) follows MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText (step 270) on another receiver; rowKey and stepsOf have STL hits only as record fields or test locals; exclusions and corrections are record fields.\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check and step_compiler check_spec report only the mid-campaign note: the final step, 328, is not WIRE (S9.1 carried the same note).\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings, and check_spec reports nothing on it. The first staged run's SCOPE_CONSUMERS (loadAndValidate at 314) is interpretation 12.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy is reported: DataSplitTests.fs removed from step 317's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its two facts.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s93/build_s93.py, s93_common.py, s93_steps_a.py and s93_steps_b.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py and check_spec_run.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-neg.log, seam.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S9.4 (The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder): appended steps 329-331 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (21 obligations, 3 acceptance bindings, 1 behavior seam, 1 closing scope over steps 329-331). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan:\n- 329 IMPLEMENT (BerremanTests): git mv README.md, the four reference scripts and the two summaries from Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/ to data/optics-mueller/data/reference/ (scripts and summaries byte for byte, no kit file written); the README says where it now is and names data.zip by its repository path, and gains the spec 0050 further-reading bullet; MuellerReconstructionTests' provenance comments name the summaries and README at their kit path. No code change; numbers and count unchanged.\n- 330 IMPLEMENT (BerremanTests): the 15 CSV entries of data.zip written byte for byte to data/optics-mueller/ + their archive paths (data/raw/final/*.csv, data/raw/*.csv) and the three data/shapes/*.json to data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/, each checked by SHA-256; .gitattributes gains data/optics-mueller/data/raw/** -text !eol and AGENTS.md's line-endings gotcha names the exception; data.zip, Berreman/Data/, the data.zip Content link and the stale Storage-reference comment in BerremanTests.fsproj deleted; the README describes the data in the kit. New BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs: CommittedKit = OpticsMuellerKit with tryFindFolder : KitFolder option (repository root = first folder above the test output holding Berreman/Berreman.slnx). loadDataSet (file : KitRelativePath) reads through (KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView.readDataFile and (BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile).mapText; seven test-local KitRelativePath values replace the data-set cases; the Stage-1 and section 7.2 facts load them with unchanged numbers; the createArchiveBacked row-count fact is renamed 'the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts' (209, 209, 209, 170, 57, 6, 2); new fact 'the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte' pins the 18 SHA-256 values. unit-tests +1.\n- 331 RETIRE_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0009 MuellerDataProxy (Domain, Storage, BerremanTests): MuellerDataSet, MuellerArchivePath, MuellerDataProxy and the ArchiveUnreadableErr / DataSetMissingErr cases deleted from MuellerReconstruction.fs (MuellerDataError keeps MalformedRowErr and EmptyFileErr); archiveEntryName, committedArchive, tryLoadFromArchive, createArchiveBacked and the System.IO / System.IO.Compression opens deleted from MuellerDataStore.fs (parseMuellerCsv unchanged); LabFileImport's Phone ROI arm loses its two archive arms; the Storage fsproj comment and MuellerInverseTests' comment naming the proxy are cleaned; the five seam facts and the mock fixtures deleted (unit-tests -5). Greps for the retired names, the data-set cases, Data/MuellerMatrix and DataFilePath under Berreman/ find nothing (001 sec T 'From section 9').\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Byte for byte needs a .gitattributes rule. The archive's CSVs are CRLF (all but cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv with a UTF-8 BOM); the catch-all '* text=auto eol=lf' would store them as LF, so a clone would hold other bytes than the archive and than the SHA-256 a kit records at attach (001 sec E), and S12.1's committed hashes would not hold on a fresh clone. A scratch-repository probe (under specs/0050/.artifacts/s94/, removed after) confirmed: without the rule the index holds LF; with 'data/optics-mueller/data/raw/** -text !eol' (the form of the existing *.nb rule) a checkout returns the CRLF bytes. AGENTS.md's 'Line endings: LF' gotcha gains one sentence naming the exception, because it states the LF rule absolutely and a later worker would otherwise convert the files. The shapes JSON, scripts and summaries are already LF, so they need no rule.\n2. Three steps against a soft 8-14. The data move is atomic with the test re-point and the zip deletion, so no second copy of the data exists between steps and every gate stays green (.spec-md sec 7 'There is no second copy'); the reference move comes first so the README is true at each step's end; and the retirement is one step because the Domain cases and the Storage / LabFileImport arms must go together to compile. Finer splits would leave a second copy, a red gate, or path churn in comments.\n3. MuellerDataProxy is STORE_XDUO_0009 (.contract-ids/XDUO-json, status active), so its retirement is a RETIRE_CONTRACT step, as step 59 retired STORE_XDUO_0007.\n4. The test read path is the product's: the folder KitProxy's readOnlyView (steps 126, 128, 131: it cannot write, not even .oc/) and ChosenImportProfile.mapText of BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile (step 303, which calls parseMuellerCsv). KitProxy.create reads any file of a folder by kit path without a .kit-json (step 128), so nothing kit-shaped is written before S12.1. The kit paths of the final files equal their archive paths (data/raw/final/*.csv).\n5. The locator is a one-case union, CommittedKit = OpticsMuellerKit, with tryFindFolder : KitFolder option (no environment variable, writes nothing), in BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs compiled before MuellerReconstructionTests.fs; it is declared as contract BerremanTests.CommittedKit (create) so S10.2's move is traceable. loadDataSet keeps its name (S10.3's brief lists it) and takes a KitRelativePath.\n6. The byte-for-byte guard is a fact over all 18 former archive entries (SHA-256 literals computed from data.zip at authoring time by build_s94.py), not only the seven read; it is a data-integrity fact, not an inverse-physics one (001 sec W).\n7. Stale comments go in the step that touches their file: BerremanTests.fsproj's Storage-reference comment (createFileBacked, gone since spec 0044; STORE_XDUO_0009) in 330, where that file is edited anyway; the Storage fsproj comment and MuellerInverseTests' 'MuellerDataProxy convention' comment in 331, so S10.1's invariant s33-no-archive-data-proxy (MuellerDataProxy|createArchiveBacked) holds; the last DataFilePath mentions (the two notes step 135 left for S9, and three in MuellerReconstructionTests) go with the text they sit in.\n8. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates' and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s94/seam-wired.json): build, elevation and unit-tests over BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests on every step; constructor-unit-tests (whole, light) on 331, which edits LabFileImport.fs (LabFileImportTests, step 301-303). Not adopted: seam-plan's every-class unit-tests selection on 330 (proposed because BerremanTests.fsproj changes; the new compile item is read only by MuellerReconstructionTests, the removed Content item was read only through createArchiveBacked by that class, a deleted comment changes nothing, and the whole suite runs at the final step); MuellerInverseTests on 331 (a comment-only edit; about 11 minutes per run in the TRX files under Berreman/BerremanTests/TestResults; step 212 edited that file without selecting it); kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests.fs does not exist before S12.1); seam-plan's final-step row for 331 (final only until the next section is appended). seam-plan does not propose constructor-unit-tests for 331 because LabFileImportTests is created by step 301 and is absent from the baseline census.\n9. Counts: unit-tests 329 0, 330 +1, 331 -5; constructor-unit-tests 331 0; ui-smoke and ui-tests not run.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S10.1: the invariants s33-t9-no-mueller-data-set, s33-t9-no-data-mueller-matrix and s33-no-archive-data-proxy hold from step 331.\n- S10.2: move Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs (CommittedKit, OpticsMuellerKit, tryFindFolder) to BerremanTestSupport; MuellerReconstructionTests opens it there.\n- S10.3: the test's inputs are loadDataSet (file : KitRelativePath) and the seven KitRelativePath values lpLpFile, lpCplFile, cplLpFile, cplCplDay1File, cplCplDay2File, darknessChecksFile, bullshitChecksFile; the row-count and byte-for-byte facts stay in MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- S12.1 (AT-1): the lab files are at kit paths data/raw/final/*.csv and data/raw/*.csv, the reference files at data/reference/ and the shapes at data/reference/shapes/; copy the committed data/ tree by bytes, never by text, so hashes hold; the -text rule keeps the committed bytes on every clone; the kit's .kit-json and the rest are built around these files.\n- S12.2 (AT-2): add AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit to CommittedKit (in BerremanTestSupport after S10.2); its observation files are written by the app as LF without a BOM (step 301), so they need no attribute rule.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.2 may add Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs (moved by S10.2), and sec 0.1 .gitattributes (the -text rule for data/optics-mueller/data/raw/).\n\nNames were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in the spec with specs/0050/.artifacts/s41/namecheck.py (log specs/0050/.artifacts/s94/namecheck1.log): CommittedKit, CommittedKits, OpticsMuellerKit, tryFindFolder, lpLpFile and the other file values. readLabFile was not used because KitProxy.readLabFile exists (step 204).\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check and step_compiler check_spec report only the mid-campaign note: the final step, 331, is RETIRE_CONTRACT, not WIRE (S9.3 carried the same note for 328).\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings, and check_spec reports nothing on it. The first wired run's SYMBOL_CENSUS_UNKNOWN on OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.MuellerDataSet.archiveEntryName was fixed with the inventory's name, OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.archiveEntryName.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy is reported: MuellerReconstructionTests.fs removed from step 330's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its two facts.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s94/build_s94.py, s94_common.py and s94_steps.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py and check_spec_run.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-spec-real.log, check-neg.log, seam.log, seam-wired.log.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S10.1 (The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization): appended steps 332-343 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (33 obligations, 12 acceptance bindings, no behavior seam, 1 closing scope over steps 332-343 on Domain, Optimization and BerremanTests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; gates build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests whole, unit-tests by class):\n- 332 (Domain, BerremanTests): UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties (the type_3_4_6_Crystal builder); MuellerInverseTests.buildUniaxialGyrotropic, its duplicate LangasiteInverseTests.buildLangasite and the fact-local buildUniaxial of BiaxialInverseTests deleted; MuellerInverse.fs opens OpticalProperties.Active and its module doc's \"Domain does not reference OpticalProperties\" sentence is corrected. unit-tests: LangasiteInverseTests.\n- 333: TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties (BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic deleted). unit-tests: FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 334: AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties (AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing deleted). unit-tests: AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 335 (Optimization, BerremanTests): new MuellerFitting.fs after MuellerInverseSolver.fs; MuellerFitError (ObservationForwardErr); configurationOf (incidence, azimuth : float<deg>); observeWith -> Result; InverseFitHarness gains expectOk. unit-tests: FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 336: residualFor, throughputResidualFor, residualJacobianAt, scalingAround into MuellerFitting unchanged. unit-tests: Feasible + AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 337: SearchBox; InverseFit<'Parameters> renamed MuellerFitData<'Parameters>; fitWithResidual / fitObservations / fitAbsorbingObservations -> Result (NonlinearFitErr). unit-tests: Feasible + AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 338: QuantityValue (new); RelativeError (between over QuantityValue); recoveryErrors. unit-tests: Feasible.\n- 339: new BenchNoise.fs after MuellerFitting.fs; NoiseSeed, UniformDeviate (new), UniformDeviateProvider (nextDeviate : unit -> UniformDeviate), disturb, misread -> Result (MuellerNormalizationErr), noisyObserveWith -> Result; the harness's measurement-error banner deleted (its narrative lives in specs/0044/.manual/011 and 019). unit-tests: MuellerInverseTests.\n- 340: misreadAbsolute, noisyObserveAbsoluteWith -> Result into BenchNoise; makes 001 sec T 'From section 10' true. unit-tests: AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests (the only class reaching them).\n- 341: new RecoveryEnsembles.fs after BenchNoise.fs; RecoveredQuantity (ParameterName, 'P -> QuantityValue), RecoveryStatistics (mean, absoluteScatter : QuantityValue), NoisyExperiment, EnsembleSize (new), statisticsFor, standardErrorOfMean (EnsembleSize), rowFor -> Result (UnknownQuantityErr). unit-tests: MuellerInverseTests.\n- 342: fitReportOf -> member MuellerFitData.report (ELEV013); new FitUncertainty.fs after RecoveryEnsembles.fs; ParameterWeights ([<NumericCarrier>] over float[]), PredictedVariance (new), predictedRelativeErrors, combinationVariance, differenceWeights -> Result (UnknownAxisErr). unit-tests: MuellerInverseTests.\n- 343: sumWeights -> Result, DirectionalSensitivity (new), directionalSensitivity into FitUncertainty; InverseFitHarness keeps only expectOk, describeErrors, describeColumnNorms, assertMuellerEqual, ensembleSeeds; BiaxialInverseTests' class doc names the four product modules. unit-tests: AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Errors are values in the product home. Every failwith the harness did (forward failure on ground truth or noisy data, normalization failure, solver failure, unknown row or axis name) becomes a case of one new MuellerFitError (cases ending in Err, each carrying the typed inner error or the ParameterName). The tests unwrap through one test-side assertion, InverseFitHarness.expectOk (failwith %A of the error, test code only). 001 sec Q's \"keeps only test assertions\" admits it; it is the fifth binding the harness keeps.\n2. ELEV-driven shapes, each traced to a rule, since the brief requires the moved code to meet every ELEV rule: configurationOf takes float<deg> (ELEV003/010; the ledger's precedent: SampleAzimuth.degree takes float<deg>); QuantityValue carries a recovered quantity's value (RelativeError.between took two doubles beside our type, ELEV010; RecoveredQuantity.valueIn and RecoveryStatistics.mean/absoluteScatter are record fields, ELEV008); UniformDeviate (the provider field unit -> double, ELEV008); names are ParameterName (derived, rowFor, sumWeights, differenceWeights: the brief's \"names are elevated\"); EnsembleSize (standardErrorOfMean's int beside our types, ELEV010); ParameterWeights is the [<NumericCarrier>] the brief names for float[] weight vectors; PredictedVariance and DirectionalSensitivity are the two scalar results (ELEV010); fitReportOf becomes the member MuellerFitData.report (ELEV013). Every number is computed by the same float operations in the same order, so BerremanTests stays bit-identical.\n3. InverseFit<'Parameters> is renamed MuellerFitData<'Parameters> (the brief: it collides with the module OpticalConstructor.Optimization.InverseFit; naming_conventions \"Data\").\n4. Four new files, one module each, compiled in this order directly after MuellerInverseSolver.fs: MuellerFitting.fs (error, configurations, observations, residuals, scaling, search box, fit record and runners, QuantityValue, RelativeError, recoveryErrors), BenchNoise.fs, RecoveryEnsembles.fs, FitUncertainty.fs. Names were checked unused in the tree, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in .spec-jsonl (specs/0050/.artifacts/s101/namecheck.py, log namecheck1.log); the harness names that exist today exist only in BerremanTests and move.\n5. The builders are instance members opticalProperties on the three records (.spec-md sec 3.16), so S11.1's toProperties calls record.opticalProperties. Two byte-for-byte duplicates of the uniaxial builder (LangasiteInverseTests.buildLangasite and a fact-local buildUniaxial in BiaxialInverseTests) are deleted with it (AGENTS.md \"Reuse, never copy\"), so ONE uniaxial builder exists.\n6. Gates follow the brief's \"cheapest class that exercises each moved function\": seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s101/seam.json) proposed the class of every edited test file, including BiaxialInverseTests (997 s) on nine steps and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests (946 s) on six. Adopted: BiaxialInverseTests never (every function it reaches is reached by a cheaper class; the final step's whole suite runs it); AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests on 340 only (misreadAbsolute and noisyObserveAbsoluteWith are reached nowhere else); MuellerInverseTests (about 456 s) on 339, 341 and 342; Feasible (104 s), AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests (177 s) and LangasiteInverseTests elsewhere. constructor-unit-tests (13 s whole) runs on every step because each edits Domain or Optimization (.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'), although seam-plan names no OpticalConstructor.Tests class for these files. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1.\n7. The generic scalingAround has no caller today: BiaxialSample.scalingAround, AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbingScalingAround and MuellerInverseTests.scalingAround build their own specialisations and shadow it. It moves because 001 sec Q lists it for the study engine; the build alone verifies it in S10.1.\n8. The measurement-error banner (InverseFitHarness.fs:59-110, which step 213 left beside the noise functions for S10.1) is not copied into product code: its narrative and sources are already specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md and 019 (AGENTS.md \"Document a decision once\"); BenchNoise's module doc points there. Stale test comments that place the driver or the noise model in InverseFitHarness are corrected in the step that makes them untrue (337, 339, 343).\n9. No new test is authored (001 sec Q AT-2, sec W; .spec-md sec 9 assigns the harness's coverage to BerremanTests). Contract effects are paired with change_expectation test effects on the selected classes' facts whose code paths change while their assertions stay (the step-109 precedent). Counts are unchanged on every step.\n10. Twelve steps, within the 12-20 soft budget; the noise move is split at the transparent / absorbing boundary so the 946 s class runs once.\n\nRequests to later mappers:\n- S10.2: BiaxialSample.fs and AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs (moving to BerremanTestSupport) no longer hold buildTriclinic / buildAbsorbing; after S10.1 they open OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting (configurationOf, SearchBox) and RecoveryEnsembles (RecoveredQuantity with ParameterName / QuantityValue), so BerremanTestSupport references OpticalConstructor.Optimization. The configuration helper there passes x * 1.0<deg>.\n- S11: the engine fits through MuellerFitting.fitObservations / fitAbsorbingObservations (Result<MuellerFitData, MuellerFitError>), observes through observeWith / BenchNoise.noisyObserveWith; materials holding a parameter record build through record.opticalProperties. AT-2's model identity compares with MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor.\n- S14: the Planner's layer 2 reuses FitUncertainty.predictedRelativeErrors, combinationVariance (ParameterWeights -> PredictedVariance), differenceWeights / sumWeights and directionalSensitivity, and MuellerFitData.report.\n- Planner: .spec-md sec 0.1's Optimization row may name the four files; sec 0.1's MuellerInverse.fs row is realised as the opticalProperties members.\n\nValidation.\n- On the real folder, executability check and step_compiler check_spec report only the mid-campaign note: the final step, 343, is IMPLEMENT, not WIRE (S9.4 carried the same note for 331).\n- A staged copy with a bound placeholder final WIRE step passes executability check with no findings, and check_spec reports nothing on it.\n- Negative probe on the wired copy: AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs removed from step 337's edits gives SCOPE_CONSUMERS on BerremanTests.InverseFit and InverseFitHarness.fitAbsorbingObservations.\n- The diff is append-only: .spec-jsonl +12 lines, .execution-contract-json +2232 / -0, LF only.\n- The build script and its inputs are specs/0050/.artifacts/s101/build_s101.py, s101_common.py and s101_steps.py (with stage_all.sh, wire_check.py, bind_wire.py and check_spec_run.py). Logs: build.log, build-stage.log, check-real.log, check-stage.log, check-wired-raw.log, check-wired.log, check-spec.log, check-spec-real.log, check-neg.log, seam.log, consumers.log, namecheck1.log, review.txt.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Mapper run, section 34/47: S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs. Appended steps 344-347 to .spec-jsonl (all tagged with the section name; no existing line touched; .spec-md not edited) and extended .execution-contract-json (26 obligations S102-*, 4 acceptance bindings, one closing scope 344-347; no behavior seam, since no test is created).\n\nSteps:\n- 344 IMPLEMENT (AC-S102a): create Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj (plain net10.0 x64 library, default assembly name BerremanTestSupport, Optimization.fsproj's property groups without AssemblyName, Domain reference, no comment), add it to Berreman.slnx after BerremanTests, git mv S9.4's CommittedKits.fs (step 330) into it under namespace BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests references it and drops the compile line, MuellerReconstructionTests opens BerremanTestSupport. Gates: build, elevation, unit-tests (BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests).\n- 345 IMPLEMENT (AC-S102b): git mv BiaxialSample.fs whole (namespace BerremanTestSupport, bodies unchanged as S10.1 leaves them); BerremanTestSupport gains the Optimization reference (RecoveredQuantity, QuantityValue); the five consumers open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample; BerremanTests.fsproj drops the compile line with its comment and the InverseFitHarness comment S10.1 made untrue; doc edits limited to what the move makes untrue plus one S10.2 citation. Gates: build, elevation, unit-tests (BiaxialInverseTests, FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests).\n- 346 IMPLEMENT (AC-S102c): git mv AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs whole (the constants, cuts, a1/a2/a3, fullConfigurations, perturbedStart, searchBox, absorbingScalingAround); open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness deleted; both absorbing suites open the new module. Gates: build, elevation, unit-tests (AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests).\n- 347 IMPLEMENT (AC-S102d): OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj references BerremanTestSupport (no comment, no source change). Gates: build, elevation, ui-smoke (all_discovered, light).\n\nDecisions recorded:\n- Namespace: the moved files take namespace BerremanTestSupport (the project's own), not BerremanTests; consumers change only their open lines.\n- The files move whole by git mv: everything left in them after S10.1 (including epsDiagonal, rhoImaginary, the optic-axis geometry and solverParameters) is the ground truth and its design, and 001 sec Q AT-2 / sec S10 name the two files. Docs keep their text except what the move makes untrue.\n- Elevation: Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151 scopes every solution .fsproj not ending in Tests.fsproj, so the driver analyzes BerremanTestSupport.fsproj; the analyzers apply no rule to it (assembly name matches neither inScopePatterns nor ownAssemblyPatterns, .elevation-analyzers.json:13-21; checked against STL Analyzers/ElevationAnalyzer.fs applicabilityWith and wireApplicabilityWith). Nothing under Elevation/ or in .elevation-analyzers.json changes.\n- unit-tests selections follow the brief ('classes opening the moved modules at low cost, e.g. BiaxialInverseTests and FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests') and the S10.1 rule that a ~1000 s class runs only where a moved declaration is reached nowhere else: BiaxialInverseTests (997 s) is selected at 345 because it alone reaches epsDiagonal, rhoImaginary, opticAxisFromLargest and recoveredQuantities; AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests (946 s) is not, since AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests reads every declaration it reads. The seam-plan proposal (every BerremanTests class, because the project file is edited) was not adopted, per .user-md 'unit-tests ... selected by class only; whole at the final step only'.\n- Step 347 runs ui-smoke whole and not ui-tests: no source file of the suite changes, so no ui-tests class holds a changed fact; the reference's effect (build and load) is what build and ui-smoke prove. kit-acceptance (proposed by seam-plan) is not runnable before S12.1.\n- Retired module symbols use the census keys BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.BiaxialSample and BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample, because a module type's census name is unqualified; BerremanTests.CommittedKit resolves through its step-330 creation.\n- Soft budget 6-12: four steps is the minimum the work divides into without an empty-project stub or a split that changes nothing on its own.\n\nVerification: a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step passes 'python -m ai_strategy_generator.executability ... check' (passed: true) and the step compiler's check_spec (0 findings); without the placeholder the only finding is the expected 'final step must be WIRE' (the Close section supplies it). A negative control (dropping AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs from step 345's edits) fails with SCOPE_CONSUMERS, so the module census key resolves. The real files equal the staged ones byte for byte; .spec-jsonl gained 4 lines and .execution-contract-json 860, with no deletion and no CR. Scratch work: specs/0050/.artifacts/s102/.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S10.3 (The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted): appended steps 348-352 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (27 obligations S103-*, 5 acceptance bindings, 3 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 348-352 on BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests, Optimization, Domain and OpticalConstructor.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; unit-tests selects BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step touching Berreman/OpticalConstructor/**):\n- 348 (BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): new BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs after AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs. MOVED into it, each born elevated: stage1Tol and dataMatrixTol with the spec 0044 §8.5/§9 band comment; the six Stage-1 constants (DarkMean 869.666; z_LP, z_CPL, θ_src as Angle; δ_an, δ_src as Retardance); the three section 7.2 matrices; the three cascade metrics (MatrixDeviation); the two largest-delta positions; the excluded point (matrix_glue.py EXCLUDED_POINTS). The Stage-1, section 7.2 and buildDesign facts read MuellerReference.<name>. Gates: build, elevation, unit-tests.\n- 349 (Optimization, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Tests): new Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs directly after FitUncertainty.fs: StagedMuellerCaptureData (the seven lab files' rows), StagedMuellerError (EmptyCaptureSetErr, AirCalibrationFitErr of Family * SolverError), StageOneCalibrationData with the stage-2 models as members (lpAnalyzer, cplAnalyzer, cplSource), private reduceAirTraces (DarkMean) and an LP-frame fit answering Result<SourceCplModel, SolverError>, and calibrateStageOne. The test loses reduceAirTraces, lpFrameCoeffs and unwrapFit and gains opticsMuellerCaptures over loadDataSet. New OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests (ADD_TEST) with two error facts. Gates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, unit-tests.\n- 350 (Domain, BerremanTests): buildDesign's projection takes the kept row's NameReading (MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity), so no projection re-reads a label; the section 7.2 prepareRow uses reading.objectPhi and loses its step-270 failure path. Same rows, same numbers.\n- 351 (Optimization, BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Tests): ObjectReconstructionErr of MatrixKind * SolverError; StagedMuellerData (stageOne, gains : GainCalibration, cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain, qz, lr, qzLr); reconstructStaged solver excluded captures: stage one, the split at the earliest bullshit check, the nine AIR blocks by the reference labels (first empty one -> EmptyCaptureSetErr naming it), the gains, the five families' projections and the Qz / Lr / QzLrProduct solves. MuellerReference gains the nine gain_summary gains. The section 7.2 fact calls reconstructStaged with MuellerReference.excludedPoints, keeps only assertions and their formatting, and gains one assertion over the nine gains. Two more StagedMuellerPathTests facts (empty AIR block, failed object solve).\n- 352 (Domain, Optimization, BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Tests): LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt extracted from createMathNetSvd (the one ‖A·x − b‖/√m; the solver reports through it); ProductRmseRatio (between, as RelativeError.between), ProductCheckData (cascade, difference, fitRmse, productRmse; rmseRatio) and productCheckOf lr qz combined combinedSystem; StagedMuellerData carries productCheck. MuellerReference gains combined_check fit_rmse / product_rmse and productCheckRmseRatio. The section 7.2 fact reads the cascade metrics and positions from the product check and gains the RMSE-ratio assertion. One StagedMuellerPathTests fact pins the product check on a two-row synthetic system.\n\nInterpretations and deviations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. loadDataSet stays in the test. 001 §Q AT-1 lists it in the hand-composed pipeline, but the brief makes the promoted path \"a pure function over the parsed capture rows\"; loadDataSet is the test's IO (KitProxy.readOnlyView + the Phone ROI CSV profile, both product since S9), so the test keeps it and binds the seven files into StagedMuellerCaptureData.\n2. The nine AIR block labels are literals of the promoted path: they are the reference procedure's gain rules (matrix_fit_linear.py assign_gain_model), which S11.1 turns into session data (001 §L \"familyGain becomes their first implementation\"). The excluded point is the caller's data (spec 0042 §0; 001 §Q AT-1 \"the excluded frame [is] applied as data\"), held by MuellerReference so §7.2 and AT-1 share it; the always-run buildDesign fact reads it too instead of a second transcription.\n3. Totality. Every failwith of the hand-composed body becomes a StagedMuellerError case (EmptyCaptureSetErr for no darkness / bullshit-check row or an empty AIR block, AirCalibrationFitErr, ObjectReconstructionErr). To avoid an unreachable Error arm when the promoted projection reads a label, step 350 makes buildDesign hand its own reading to the projection (a change_shape of buildDesign; its only consumers are MuellerReconstructionTests).\n4. One RMSE implementation. The product RMSE needs ‖A·x − b‖/√m, which createMathNetSvd computes inline; step 352 extracts it as LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt and the solver calls it, so no second formula exists (AGENTS.md \"Reuse, never copy\"). It was a separate step at first; the executability check refused a new member without a test producer in its step (CONTRACT_TESTS), so it lands with its first new consumer, the product check, whose new fact exercises it. Five steps against the 6-12 soft budget: each remaining step is one green, reviewable move, and a finer split would leave a contract without its producer or a duplicated formula.\n5. MuellerReference holds both bands, not only dataMatrixTol: the §9 comment block documents both and the Stage-1 literals move with it; AT-1's assertions (001 §Q AT-1) list the CPL retardances, the angle offset and the dial zeros, which are the Stage-1 fact's literals. Values are elevated (Angle, Retardance, DarkMean, MatrixDeviation, AirGain, ResidualRmse, ProductRmseRatio, ExcludedPoint); each degree literal was checked to survive Angle.degree / .degrees bit for bit, so every comparison is exact as before.\n6. New assertions inside the existing section 7.2 fact (no new BerremanTests fact, 001 §W): the nine AIR gains and the product-check RMSE ratio, which the promoted path now returns and AT-1 asserts (S12.1 brief), so they are proven when they land. Measured at authoring by a probe through the built assemblies over the committed data.zip (specs/0050/.artifacts/s103-probe/probe.fsx): gains worst 2.9e-11 absolute (lp_cpl.gain_air2, relative 4.5e-16), fit_rmse 2.3e-14, product_rmse 2.9e-14, ratio 5.7e-13, Stage-1 as spec 0044 recorded (0 or ≤ 1.4e-14°), design rows QZ 228 / LR 227 / QZ+LR 228 as the summary's n_rows. dataMatrixTol (1e-9) is at least 34 times the worst, per spec 0044 §9; the observed figures go into its doc.\n7. New pure module covered in OpticalConstructor.Tests (.spec-md §9): StagedMuellerPathTests' five facts reach each error case through the real SVD proxy on synthetic rows and pin the product check's arithmetic; they are error-path and arithmetic facts, not inverse physics (001 §W).\n8. Names (StagedMuellerPath, StagedMuellerCaptureData, StageOneCalibrationData, StagedMuellerError, StagedMuellerData, ProductRmseRatio, ProductCheckData, calibrateStageOne, reconstructStaged, productCheckOf, EmptyCaptureSetErr, AirCalibrationFitErr, ObjectReconstructionErr, MuellerReference) were checked unused in Berreman/, in STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and in .spec-jsonl.\n9. Gates. seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s103/seam.json) proposed the same gates and classes for 348, 349 and 351; for 350 it proposed no constructor-unit-tests and for the former separate residual step no unit-tests; both are kept per .user-md (constructor-unit-tests on steps touching its code, here Domain; unit-tests where its applies_to matches MuellerReconstruction.fs). kit-acceptance applies to Optimization and BerremanTestSupport but cannot run before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs (requires_path), as the brief says.\n\nVerification: a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step passes 'python -m ai_strategy_generator.executability ... check' (passed: true) and the step compiler's check_spec (0 findings); without the placeholder the only finding is the expected 'final step must be WIRE' (the Close section supplies it). A negative control (dropping MuellerReconstructionTests.fs from step 351's edits) fails with SCOPE_TEST. The real files equal the staged ones byte for byte; .spec-jsonl gained 5 lines and .execution-contract-json 1074, with no deletion and no CR. Scratch work: specs/0050/.artifacts/s103/ and specs/0050/.artifacts/s103-probe/.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S11.1 (Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials): appended steps 353-366 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (36 obligations S111-*, 14 acceptance bindings, 12 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 353-366 on Domain, Storage, Ui, Optimization, OpticalConstructor.Tests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests, BerremanTests and BerremanTestSupport). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). Validated on a staged copy: executability check passed (with the placeholder final WIRE step), step-compiler check_spec clean on the wired copy; the real files are byte-identical to the validated copy.\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty s36 invariants on every step):\n- 353 (Domain, BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): UniaxialParameters, TriclinicParameters and AbsorbingTriclinicParameters with their S10.1 opticalProperties builders MOVE to a new OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs compiled directly after DispersionModels.fs (before MaterialLibrary.fs); their axes stay in MuellerInverse.fs as static type-extension members after ParameterAxis; consumers open the module. New MaterialComplexityTests fact on the builders. unit-tests: LangasiteInverseTests, FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests, AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 354 (Domain, Storage, Ui, both test projects): MaterialPhysics = ComplexityPhysics of complexity (one case for now); MaterialEntry.complexity becomes physics : MaterialPhysics; shared members MaterialPhysics.anisotropy (LibraryFacets), editableComplexityOpt (MaterialComplexityEditor, an option not a bool), gyrationComponents and muKind (NkDispersionChart); every reader and fixture follows; entry files keep MaterialPayload, so every catalogue file keeps its bytes and hash. ui-tests: the six classes the census and seam-plan name.\n- 355: CrystalParameters union (UniaxialCrystal | TriclinicCrystal | AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal) with opticalProperties and toProperties (= opticalProperties.dispersive); MaterialPhysics gains CrystalParameterPhysics; facets classify anisotropy and transparency from the crystal (ladder facets do not apply); out-of-band never flags; editableComplexityOpt None so the entry opens view-only; LibraryEntryPayload gains CrystalMaterialPayload and library-material.schema.json accepts it at version 1. Eight constructor facts (both material stores) and one MaterialEditorWindowTests fact.\n- 356 (Domain, Optimization, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Tests): new OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs, compiled directly after ImportProfiles.fs (the last Domain file). StudyError, AirRepeatPair, SessionGainModel (FreeSessionGain | AnchoredSessionGain | InterpolatedSessionGain), AirAnchorGain, GainInterpolation (InterpolatedGain moved and renamed), SessionGainRule with gainAt, SessionGainModel.ruleWith. familyGain, GainCalibration, RepeatPairGain, SplitGain, CplCplGain and InterpolatedGain are deleted (moved, not copied). StagedMuellerPath names its nine AIR runs as ExperimentNames, resolves six session gain models (CPL-LP as two sessions split by time), divides each row by its rule and answers airGains; SessionGainErr added. MuellerReconstructionTests' section 7.2 fact reads the nine gains from airGains (numbers unchanged); the Stage-3 fact keeps its other pins under a new name; the familyGain checks move to the new StudySessionTests. unit-tests: MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 357: StudySession, splitAll (hand-set sessions; the rest split at DiagnosticRun into 'Session <k>' blocks) and darkRunsIn (own DarkRun runs, else every DarkRun run).\n- 358: the study's shape: StudyName, StudyNotes, ParameterScope, StudyParameterRef, ScopedParameter, ParameterLink, SessionGainSetting, FitMode, ResidualWeight, weight settings, StudyFitSettings, OpenedMaterial, Study; Study.create (CreateStudy's pure half), sessionsIn, gainModelOf. New StudyTests.\n- 359 (Domain, Storage, OpticalConstructor.Tests): StudyFile and <name>.study-json: schema/study.schema.json, validateStudyFile, int-tag converters for ParameterScope and FitMode, KitProxy.writeStudy / readStudies, KitLibraryContext.recordStudy (snapshot and pin the opened material versions, then write). New KitStudyFileTests.\n- 360: Study.withExperiments (AddExperimentsToStudy's pure half).\n- 361: ParameterAxis.parameterValueOf / writeValue, CrystalParameters.parameterAxes (the record's axes, lifted, generated never hand-written), OpenedMaterial.openFrom / withParameterState / currentCrystal, Study.openMaterial / withMaterialParameterState, Sample.openedMaterialsIn. The EXACT test: the generated axes of an opened AbsorbingTriclinicParameters material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes in names, order, field kinds and read / write on a probe. New StudyMaterialTests.\n- 362: UnknownOwner, StudyUnknown, Study.scopeOf, Study.unknownsWith (link followers left out), StudyUnknown.owners.\n- 363: Study.withParameterScope (SetParameterScope's pure half).\n- 364: Study.withLink (LinkParameters' pure half).\n- 365: ExperimentEnablement; per-session gain models, fit mode, experiment and detector weights, enablement and notes as pure updates; enabledExperiments and residualWeightOf.\n- 366: StudyContext and StudyMsg (CreateStudy | AddExperimentsToStudy | OpenMaterial | SetParameterScope | LinkParameters) with applyTo; tests over in-memory kits recorded through recordStudy. New StudyMessageTests.\n\nDecisions and departures recorded:\n- .spec-md §3.16 placed the crystal builders in MuellerInverse.fs. MaterialEntry (MaterialLibrary.fs) compiles long before MuellerInverse.fs, so a material version cannot hold the records there; step 353 moves the records with their builders to CrystalPhysics.fs, ahead of MaterialLibrary.fs. One implementation of each builder remains. The axes stay in MuellerInverse.fs (ParameterAxis is declared there and ParameterName in ItemModels.fs, both later) as static type extensions, so every caller reads them unchanged.\n- \"The editor follows\" is read as the published gyration law was in S1.2 step 10: the complexity ladder cannot carry crystal parameters, so a crystal entry opens view-only. Crystal materials reach the library through their entry file (import and drop, S3.1-S3.2) and through Promote to library (S11.5). No crystal-parameter editor is added.\n- A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec. Its eps is formula, table or constant data the ladder edits, and the brief's generated axes and exact test are the crystal records'. OpenMaterial therefore refuses a complexity-tree material with MaterialWithoutParametersErr: a material is fitted through its crystal-parameter form.\n- 001's SessionScope case is named SessionBlockScope (001 §L's own wording, \"one value per session block\"). STL declares a SessionScope union case (Apps/Trust, Trust.Adm), and AGENTS.md requires DU case names to be unique among ours, with the lower assembly keeping its name.\n- Scopes by owner: an item parameter takes ItemScope, SessionBlockScope or ExperimentScope; a material component takes MaterialScope only (001 §L \"one value for every sample of an opened material\"). The default is MaterialScope for a component, SessionBlockScope for an item parameter named gain (the intensity detector's, S7.1 step 215; 001 §I \"Gain (session-scoped)\"), and ItemScope otherwise. A linked parameter's scope cannot change, and a link joins parameters of one scope.\n- A study names its experiments by ExperimentName, because the kit stores each under its name (step 290). Sessions derive from the experiments: hand-set sessionOpt (step 294); the rest are split at each DiagnosticRun, which belongs to no session, into non-empty 'Session <k>' blocks. A session's dark comes from its own DarkRun runs, or else from every DarkRun run, because the optics-mueller kit's one darkness file serves every session. Gain settings attach to sessions by name, with FreeSessionGain by default.\n- familyGain moves as SessionGainModel.ruleWith plus SessionGainRule.gainAt. The arithmetic is unchanged: one run's gain is itself, two runs give 0.5 * (a + b), and the interpolation keeps its clamped weight expression. BerremanTests' numbers are therefore bit-identical. StagedMuellerData's gains : GainCalibration and cplCplDay1Gain become airGains : AirAnchorGain list, and MuellerReference is unchanged.\n- The messages are a Domain StudyMsg with a pure applyTo over a StudyContext, the MaterialComplexityEditor and SampleStackEditor message-DU precedent. S11.5's study view hosts them; this section adds no Elmish case and no view.\n- Gates: unit-tests runs on 353 and 356 only. 353 uses the three cheapest classes that drive each moved record. The seam plan also listed MuellerInverseTests, BiaxialInverseTests and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests, whose edits there are open lines only (the step 212 and step 345 precedent). kit-acceptance, which the seam plan proposed on 354-355, is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs (brief). ui-smoke (whole) and ui-tests (selected) run on 354-355, the steps that touch Ui code. ui-tests on 354 match the seam plan; 355 adds NkDispersionChartTests and MaterialsWindowTests because NkDispersionChart.fs changes.\n- Executability: step 353's edits also name Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs and AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs, the paths the repository census still gives the two files steps 345-346 moved. Step 354 retires MaterialEntry.complexity and creates MaterialEntry.physics, member-level as step 13 did, because the type-level census covers files no reader of the field touches. Step 355 declares LibraryEntryPayload.CrystalMaterialPayload as a create, step 217's precedent.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S11.2 (The forward model of an experiment and the study residual): appended steps 367-379 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (35 obligations S112-*, 13 acceptance bindings, 13 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 367-379 on Domain, Ui, Optimization, OpticalConstructor.Tests and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty s37 invariants on every step):\n- 367 (Domain, Ui, Tests): the drawn incidence (PlacedElement.incidenceOn, moved verbatim from the UI's private extension), BeamBranch.propagationBranch, SetupSlot.boundSourceIn (the UI's boundSource) and SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf (the UI's operatingWaveLength, 600 nm without a source) MOVE into Domain; chartForRun, boundSource and operatingWaveLength call them. ui-smoke; ui-tests over the chart classes (ElementMenu, ExperimentControls, FsxAcceptance, InverseConstructor, MainWorkbench, WorkbenchInfoAndCapture) and OutOfBandBadgeTests.\n- 368: SlotRunParam, SlotRunError, SetupSlot.runElementWith (item through its model and given values, else its library binding; no element for source / detector / mirror / lens slots), runStepOf and runEmissionOf MOVE into ItemEvaluation.fs from chartForRun (steps 252, 265) and model.runEmission (step 266). ui-smoke; ui-tests over the chart classes.\n- 369: new Domain PrefitChecks.fs (after ExperimentMatrices.fs): SlotSpecification, PrefitError (UnspecifiedSlotsErr, MissingDataErr, UnreadableDataErr, InconsistentDataErr) and Experiment.prefitCheckWith, SolverHandoffView's three checks MOVED; validateExperiment maps the Domain result onto its ExperimentHandoffStatus with every caption unchanged. New PrefitCheckTests. ui-smoke; ui-tests SolverHandoffWindowTests (unchanged).\n- 370: DataChangeFlag and MappedAttachment.changeWith (missing > changed since attach > changed since the last fit run).\n- 371: new Domain StudyForward.fs (after PrefitChecks.fs): StudyForwardError, RecordedReading, MeasuredRow, MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor (every MappedPoints kind placed on the scan by validatedFor's rules). New StudyForwardTests.\n- 372: StudyForwardContext, StudyRunUse / ExperimentRole.studyUse, Study.fittedRunsIn, StudyVectorEntry, the NumericCarrier StudyParameterVector, StudyParameterLayout and Study.parameterLayoutWith (one entry per owner of each unknown).\n- 373: ExperimentAssignment (item values, opened crystals, materialProxyOver) and StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor (owners holding the experiment, links).\n- 374: RunStep.productOf; the forward model at a scan point: Experiment.boundWith and BoundExperiment.readingAt (intensity S0 x gain + dark, polarimeter path Mueller matrix, ellipsometer Psi/Delta; settings turn, dial, tilt, retune).\n- 375: observations: MeasurementConfiguration.elementOrientation and BoundExperiment.predictedReadingOf (an ObservationRow is a BoundCutPlate of the experiment's one opened crystal through createBerremanForward at its own configuration); boundWith takes the study.\n- 376: MuellerInverse.throughputResidual (the log-throughput term MOVED out of MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor, which calls it, numbers bit-identical) and RecordedReading.residualAgainst. unit-tests: BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 377: ExperimentPrefit and Study.prefitWith (checks and change flags over the enabled runs a fit reads).\n- 378: StudyRun, SessionDark, StudyData and Study.dataWith (rows of the fitted runs; each session's dark from its Dark runs).\n- 379: Study.residualWith, the weighted study residual.\n\nInterpretations and departures, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The run rules move out of the UI. The brief places the forward model in Domain \"over S8.1's evaluator\", but the rules that bind a slot for a run, emit the source, give the drawn incidence, the bound source and the operating wavelength live today inside TableAndElementRotationView.fs (chartForRun, runEmission, incidenceOn, boundSource, operatingWaveLength). A Domain copy would be a second implementation (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'), so steps 367-368 MOVE them and the table calls them; nothing it draws or runs changes. These two steps add ui-smoke and ui-tests over the chart classes, which the brief's gate list does not name.\n2. The pre-fit checks keep the screen. SolverHandoffView keeps its ExperimentHandoffStatus as the display of the Domain result until S11.5 deletes the view, so SolverHandoffWindowTests runs unchanged; it is authorized in step 369 as validateExperiment's consumer (SCOPE_CONSUMERS) though no fact changes.\n3. \"Since the last fit run\" is an input. No fit run exists before S11.3, so MappedAttachment.changeWith compares the attachment with `fitted : DataAttachment list`, the attachments the study's last fit run read (empty before the first fit). S11.3's fit runs need to record the DataAttachment list they read so the study can pass it.\n4. The forward model's detector is the setup's first detector slot in light order (as ExperimentDataLoad.detectorKindOf reads the first detector slot), and it must hold a detector ITEM: gain, dark offset and noise are item parameters (001 §I), so a bare preset detector is StudyDetectorErr. The noise budget is not read (nothing is simulated).\n5. Gain and dark. The intensity reading is S0 x gain + dark with the gain from the assignment (the vector's value for its owner, else the item's). Deriving an anchored or interpolated session gain from its AIR runs is the staged engine's (S11.3, over S11.1's SessionGainModel.ruleWith). The dark is the mean signal of the session's Dark runs (StudySession.darkRunsIn, step 357, as a MuellerReconstruction DarkMean) and, when the study reads no Dark run for that session, the detector's darkOffset value.\n6. Roles. ScienceRun, CalibrationRun and DriftCheckRun give residual rows, DarkRun gives its session's dark, DiagnosticRun, IgnoredRun and PlannedRun are not read (StudyRunUse); disabled runs are not read at all. Owners of an unknown are counted over the enabled fitted runs only.\n7. Observations. An ObservationRow (the Mueller-matrix observation profile) is predicted as a cut plate of the experiment's one opened crystal at the observation's own configuration through MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward over CrystalParameters.opticalProperties, so it equals the spec 0044 forward exactly; settings rows go through the setup's path. A stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy through ExperimentAssignment.materialProxyOver (a copy of the MaterialProxy record whose resolveVersion answers the working copy; no new proxy type).\n8. Residual layout and weights. Element entries run after run and row after row, then every Mueller row's log-throughput entry: the layout of MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor, so a polarimeter study at unit weight IS that vector (step 379 pins it on a three-observation uniaxial study; S12.2 asserts AT-2). Every entry of a run is multiplied by residualWeightOf (experiment weight x detector weight). Psi and Delta differences are in radians, Delta wrapped by Math.IEEERemainder(., 2 pi). Sigma columns are not read. Errors are typed (StudyForwardError); no penalty is added: what an error costs is S11.3's engines' choice.\n9. The log-throughput term moves into Domain (MuellerInverse.throughputResidual) so the study and the fit share ONE formula; MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor calls it (the same log and subtraction, bit-identical). That step runs unit-tests over BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests, the cheapest class reaching throughputResidualFor, as the unit-tests applies_to (MuellerInverse.fs, Optimization) requires.\n10. File placement. Step 356 calls ImportProfiles.fs \"the last Domain file\", but steps 304, 317 and 322 compile ExperimentDataProxy.fs, ExperimentDataLoad.fs, DataSplits.fs and ExperimentMatrices.fs after it; PrefitChecks.fs and StudyForward.fs therefore go after ExperimentMatrices.fs, the true last file, because they read the data seam.\n11. Names were checked against the Berreman tree, STL (C:/GitHub/Softellect) and the authored .spec-jsonl (specs/0050/.artifacts/s112/namecheck.py, names1.log); readingOf became predictedReadingOf (DialSign.readingOf exists) and ofValues ofParameterValues (SourceEmission.ofValues exists). The retired private UI members use their census keys (OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.incidenceOn, OpticalConstructor.Ui.SolverHandoffView.unspecifiedElements).\n12. Step 374 was split in two (scan-point readings; observation rows) to keep each step reviewable; thirteen steps against the 10-18 soft budget. kit-acceptance is not selected (KitAcceptanceTests.fs arrives in S12.1).\n\nVerification: a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step passes 'python -m ai_strategy_generator.executability ... check' (passed: true) and the step compiler's check_spec (0 findings); without the placeholder the only finding is the expected 'final step must be WIRE' (the Close section supplies it). Earlier runs caught and fixed SYMBOL_CENSUS_UNKNOWN (private members' census keys), SCOPE_CONSUMERS (SolverHandoffWindowTests as validateExperiment's consumer) and CLOSING_SCOPE (Ui.Tests in the closing reach). seam-plan's proposals were compared: its constructor-unit-tests classes are covered by the whole light suite; its omission of ui-tests on 367-368 (no UI fact edited) was not adopted, because those steps rewrite chartForRun. The real files equal the staged ones byte for byte; .spec-jsonl gained 13 lines and .execution-contract-json 2534, with no deletion and no CR. Scratch work: specs/0050/.artifacts/s112/.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S11.3 (Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs): appended steps 380-393 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (36 obligations S113-*, 14 acceptance bindings, 14 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 380-393 on Domain, Storage, Optimization, Ui and OpticalConstructor.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). Validated on a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step: executability check passed; step-compiler check_spec clean on the wired copy; the real files are byte-identical to the validated copy.\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty s38 invariants on every step):\n- 380 (Optimization, Tests): the watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve. OptimizerIterationObserver (reportIteration, cancellation) and IterationWatch (UnwatchedIterations | WatchedIterations) in OptimizationInterface; AlglibAdapter maps completion code 8 to SearchCancelled, runLm under a watch sets minlmsetxrep and a report callback that tells each iteration and calls minlmrequesttermination on a cancelled token (unwatched: exactly today's calls), optimize () = optimizeWatched UnwatchedIterations; IterationWatch.levenbergMarquardtSolver holds createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt's body (ELEV013: a member, not a one-parameter function). unit-tests: FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests (numbers unchanged).\n- 381 (Optimization, Tests): ScaledSearch (start, bounds) and ScaledSearch.solveWith, the one bounded request (400 iterations, 1e-12) in MuellerFitting; SearchBox.centredSearch; fitWithResidual calls them, numbers unchanged. New StudyEngineTests. unit-tests: AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests, FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.\n- 382 (Domain, Storage, Tests): FitStartCount (>= 1) and StudyFitSettings.starts (initial 1), Study.withFitStarts, study.schema.json settings.starts.\n- 383 (Domain, Tests): new Domain FitRuns.fs after StudyForward.fs: FitStage (Joint/Calibration/Object, tags 1-3), CalibrationUse (held fixed / as prior), StudyEngineKind (linear / nonlinear), FitRunNotes, FitChiSquared, FitMemberFailure, FitMemberOutcome, FitRunMember, FitRunEntry, FitRunParameter, ObjectMatrixFit, FitRun (schema 1), StudyName.fitRunNameAt (<stem>@yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ), FitRunName.fileStem, NonlinearSolverError.failureText. New FitRunTests.\n- 384 (Domain, Storage, Tests): KitError.FitRunExistsErr; schema/fitrun.schema.json, validateFitRunFile, int-tag converters, FitRun.fileText / parseFitRun, KitProxy.writeFitRun (a listed name refused, nothing written: append-only with no new proxy verb, step 127's rule) and readFitRuns (per study, stamp order). New KitFitRunFileTests, including 'a fit run is never rewritten'.\n- 385 (Domain, Tests): FitRunError, StagedStudy and Study.stageWith: instruments are the items of the enabled Calibration runs; stage 1 fits the Calibration runs and holds every other unknown at its start; stage 2 fits Science/DriftCheck runs and refuses an item-scoped instrument unknown (publish first); joint fits every residual run; runs outside the stage's reads are disabled; CalibrationAsPrior frees each calibrated parameter within value ± 50 sigma with its prior.\n- 386 (Optimization, Tests): new Optimization StudyEngine.fs after StagedMuellerPath.fs: StudyFitError, CalibrationPolarizer (by item model form), and StagedStudy.engineWith: linear for the stage-1 calibration shape (LP/CPL AIR runs of the three reference families over capture rows, entries only the reference stage-1 constants) and the stage-2/joint black-box shape (whole sixteen-element matrices behind known instruments, intensity detectors with known gain, capture rows); nonlinear otherwise.\n- 387: the nonlinear engine: StudyFitSolution, studySearchBox (50), ScaledStudyProblem (centre = start, unit = span/100, priors as (x − c)/σ rows, the 1.0e3 penalty for a refused evaluation), fitNonlinear (settings.starts members: the parameters' starts, then UniformDeviateProvider-placed starts; cumulative iteration watch; FitCancelledErr; the converged member of least chi-squared).\n- 388 (Domain, Optimization, Tests): moves so the study can call the staged path: Family.text, MatrixKind.text, SolverError.describe, AnalyzerModel.linearAt / circularAt, LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections / concat (buildDesign and reconstructStaged call them); StageOneAirRows and calibrateFromAirRows (calibrateStageOne's body; the AIR-label filter moves to calibrateStageOne), airAnchorGainOf (fitAirGain + meanTime), projectCaptureRow (prepareRow), StagedMuellerError.describe. unit-tests: MuellerReconstructionTests (bit-identical).\n- 389: the linear engine, stage 1: calibrateLinear hands the study's Dark runs and LP-LP / LP-CPL / CPL-LP AIR runs to calibrateFromAirRows and maps lpZero, cplZero, cplAnalyzerRetardance and the source model (thetaRel − 45°, retardance) onto the instruments' dialZero / c2.retardance / c2.fastAxisOffset; Angle.parameterValue, Retardance.parameterValue.\n- 390: the linear engine, stage 2: reconstructLinear builds each run's source and analyzer models from the instruments' (calibrated) values, φ from the first object slot's drawn R1, the session dark, and the session gain rule (free: the detector's gain; anchored/interpolated: ruleWith over airAnchorGainOf of the named AIR runs), projects every capture row, solves one system per object group by reconstruct; single groups fill the item's sixteen entries, series groups are combined matrices (for S11.4's product check).\n- 391: StudyFitRequest, StudyFitParam and runFit: stage, prefit over the last fit run's dataRead, data, engine choice, engine, and a FitRun stamped by the ClockProvider holding mode, stage, use, engine, fitted runs, the data hashes read, every parameter read, the entries' starts and fitted values, members and object matrices; nothing written.\n- 392 (Tests): the staged hand-off: stage 2 refuses unpublished instruments; a stage-1 run published through Item.publishRevision fixes each instrument value in stage 2; as priors they become prior-carrying entries for the nonlinear engine.\n- 393 (Optimization, Ui, Tests): new Ui StudyFitJob.fs after KitArchiveJob.fs: StudyFitJobHost (posting over JobRunner.startBackground with a watch posting each iteration as indeterminate JobProgress; onUiThread), StudyFitJobState, StudyFitMsg (RunFit, CancelStudyFit, StudyFitProgressed, StudyFitEnded), StudyFitEnvironment.create (readFitRuns, createMathNetSvd, fixed-seed deviates, runFit) and updateWith (one fit at a time; writeFitRun on completion only). New StudyFitJobTests. ui-smoke.\n\nInterpretations and departures, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The linear engine IS S10.3's staged Mueller path, driven by the study. The brief names \"S10.3's staged path / buildDesign + reconstruct\" for linear and \"the Eigenvalue Calibration Method path over the AIR runs\" for stage 1; both are linear least squares through MuellerSolverProxy, and only the reference estimators reproduce AT-1's stage-1 constants and matrices within dataMatrixTol (an LM fit of a physical model would converge elsewhere). So stage 1 calls calibrateFromAirRows and stage 2 projectCaptureRow + reconstruct, moved public in step 388 and called back by the reference path (one implementation). The linear shapes require capture rows (the Phone ROI CSV profile) and LP / CPL instruments classified by their item model's form; everything else is nonlinear.\n2. The stage-1 hand-off mapping (lpZero → the LP analyzer's dialZero, cplZero and |δ_an| → the CPL analyzer's dialZero and c2.retardance, θrel − 45° and δ_src → the CPL prep's c2.fastAxisOffset and c2.retardance) round-trips through the item values into stage 2's models (AnalyzerModel.linearAt / circularAt, CplSource), so the staged path's numbers are what the reference computes; it follows the built-in circular polarizer's form (retarder at 45° plus its offset, step 217) and each item's own dial sign.\n3. Session gain models are applied by the linear engine (step 378's record left this to S11.3): free = the detector's gain value, anchored / interpolated = SessionGainModel.ruleWith over airAnchorGainOf of the named AIR runs, interpolated per row capture time. The nonlinear engine fits a detector's gain as its parameter (S11.2's residual), so it refuses a fitted run whose session is anchored or interpolated (SessionGainNeedsLinearEngineErr) rather than silently ignoring the model.\n4. A stage is expressed through the study's own levers, so S11.2's layout, prefit, data and residual serve every stage unchanged: runs outside the stage's reads are disabled, out-of-stage unknowns held at their start. Stage 2 refuses an item-scoped instrument unknown (stage 1 must be published first, 001 §L); session- and experiment-scoped unknowns are refitted by whichever stage reads their runs. CalibrationAsPrior frees each calibrated parameter within ± 50 σ with its prior; with the engine's scaling rule (unit = span / (2·50), the ±50 scaled box every inverse suite uses, AbsorbingBiaxialSample.searchBox, LangasiteInverseTests) its scaled unit is its σ, and a study whose bounds are start ± 50 × the harness scale reproduces the harness's request (S12.2's AT-2).\n5. Per-iteration progress and Cancel need the LM solve itself to report and stop, and it runs whole inside one ALGLIB call, so the adapter (the one file allowed to name ALGLIB) gains a watch: minlmsetxrep + a report callback + minlmrequesttermination (completion code 8 → SearchCancelled). Unwatched solves make exactly today's calls, so every BerremanTests number is unchanged (FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests and AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests, the cheapest fitting classes, run on steps 380-381). Only minlm is watched; the other routines run as before. Progress is an iteration count with no total (JobRunner's indeterminate mode, \"<k> iterations (t s)…\"), cumulative over multi-start members.\n6. Multi-start: the count is a study fit setting (FitStartCount, default 1, stored in the study file), not an app configuration knob; one start keeps the reference kits' studies as cheap as the inverse suites. Further starts are drawn by the injected UniformDeviateProvider (.spec-md §4); the job composes UniformDeviateProvider.fromSeed (NoiseSeed 1), so a study refits reproducibly, and every member's start is recorded in the fit run.\n7. Fit runs are append-only without a new proxy verb (step 123 says kinds add no verbs): writeFitRun refuses a name listKindFiles already holds (KitError.FitRunExistsErr) and writes nothing; readFitRuns reads per study in stamp order. The name is <study file stem>@yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ from the ClockProvider, read once when the fit's solution is in; the fit run is written only by the job's completion message.\n8. \"The full parameter vector used\" is every parameter of every item the fitted runs use and every opened material component, with its state as read (FitRunParameter), plus each entry's start and fitted value and every multi-start member's start and outcome, so a later revision of an item never makes an old run irreproducible (001 §I). dataRead records each read file's path at the hash the fit read (the change flag's current hash, else the attachment's), which step 377's prefitWith takes back as `fitted`.\n9. PublishCalibration's revision write is S11.5's (it needs S11.4's sigma); the hand-off facts (step 392) publish through Item.publishRevision (step 225) with a test-local sigma. The study view that sends RunFit and binds StudyFitJobState (progress row with Cancel) is S11.5's. No ui-tests class is touched: the job hosting is proven headlessly in constructor-unit-tests, as JobRunnerCancelTests and KitArchiveJobTests (step 200) do; step 393 runs ui-smoke because the Ui project changes. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1.\n10. Results (σ, correlation, rank, per-experiment RMSE, realizability, product check, profile likelihood) are S11.4's; S11.3 stores what they need: the entries, the members, the object matrices (series = M_comb) with rank and RMSE.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S11.4 (Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood): appended steps 394-404 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (33 obligations S114-*, 11 acceptance bindings, 11 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 394-404 on Domain, Storage, Optimization and OpticalConstructor.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty s39 invariants on every step):\n- 394 (Domain, Tests): ResidualJacobian.rank (singular values above 1e-6 of the largest, through the RealMatrix seam and Svd(false) conditionNumber uses) and LeastSquaresSystem.residualsAt (A·x − b), which residualRmseAt now reads with the same operations in the same order. New OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests (ADD_TEST). unit-tests: MuellerReconstructionTests, FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests (numbers unchanged).\n- 395 (Domain, Storage, Tests): FitCorrelation, SigmaFraction, SuspectThresholds (initial 0.95 / 0.1, tryCreate) as StudyFitSettings.suspect, Study.withSuspectThresholds, InvalidSuspectThresholdErr, study.schema.json settings.suspect.\n- 396 (Domain, Tests): the result shapes in FitRuns.fs before FitRun: FitEntryRef, FitCoordinate, FitProblemSubject, JacobianColumnNorms and CorrelationMatrix (NumericCarriers), FitProblemQuality, FitEntrySigma, RunResidual, MuellerRealizability / ObjectRealizability.realizability (−1e-12 · trace allowance), SeriesProductCheck, SuspectReason, ProfileOutcome, ProfilePoint, ParameterProfile, FitRunResults.\n- 397 (Optimization, Tests): new Optimization/FittedProblems.fs between StagedMuellerPath.fs and StudyEngine.fs: IterationWatch.after (moved out of fitNonlinear, which calls it), FitCoordinateIndex, FitProfileError, ProfileRun and FittedProblem (jacobian and report through FitQuality.residualJacobian / reportFrom about a frame offset by one hundred, quality, sigmaAt, entrySigmas, profileAt by held re-fits through ScaledSearch.solveWith under the fit's watch).\n- 398 (Optimization, Tests): reduceAirTraces public; AirTrace.fringeResidualAt and SourceCplModel.lpFrameResidualOn, stage one's two cosine models written in the instruments' constants. unit-tests: MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 399 (Optimization, Tests): EngineProblems and StagedStudy.nonlinearProblemsWith (the scaled study residual at the fitted vector; each run's residualWith alone).\n- 400 (Optimization, Tests): ObjectRunSystem, ObjectGroupSystem, objectSystemsWith (reconstructLinear's projection moved, numbers unchanged), ProductCheckData.storedFor, SeriesProductCheck.rmseRatio, objectProblemsWith (each object solve over its sixteen column-major elements; each run's own rows; productCheckOf for every series whose items each have a solve of their own).\n- 401 (Optimization, Tests): AirRunRows, AirFamilyRuns, airRunsWith (calibrateLinear's selection moved, numbers unchanged), calibrationProblemsWith (the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP fringes over the instruments' entries; each AIR run's own trace).\n- 402 (Optimization, Tests): engineProblemsWith, EngineProblems.sigmasFor, SuspectCoordinate and suspectsWith (undetermined σ, σ past the fraction of the entry's bounds, |ρ| past the threshold), realizabilityWith (each black-box item's Cloude eigenvalues at its fitted values, at reference orientation).\n- 403 (Optimization, Tests): StagedStudy.resultsWith gathering everything, with a profile of every suspect entry; the synthetic intensity studies: an identifiable pair (gain and dark over a full analyzer scan, ρ = −√(2/3)), an exactly confounded pair (gain and the source's intensity scale: rank 1, no σ, flat gain profile) and a nearly confounded pair (gain and dark over 0°-20°: |ρ| > 0.95, profile χ²_min · (1 + j²/7)).\n- 404 (Domain, Storage, Optimization, Tests): FitRun.results (schema version 1 kept: no fit-run file exists before S12), fitrun.schema.json sixteen fields, runFit fills results from resultsWith before reading the clock.\n\nInterpretations and departures, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Results are read off the solves each engine made, in that solve's own coordinates: the nonlinear fit's scaled study residual and priors (step 387), each linear object solve's design A·x − b (step 390), and stage one's three AIR fits (step 389). The study residual cannot serve the linear engine: it reads a detector's gain as its parameter (step 374), while the linear engine divides each row by its session's AIR-anchored or interpolated gain (step 390), and stage one fits normalised traces with a free visibility.\n2. σ for stage one's constants. S11.5 publishes every calibrated value with its σ (CalibratedParameter, step 221), so the five instrument constants need one. Stage one fits cosine coefficients (p, q) and derives the constants by closed forms (freeCosineFit, FringeVisibility.retardance, sourceCplFromLpFrame). Step 398 writes the same two models in the constants themselves (V·cos 2(α − z); and the LP-frame model at the coefficients sourceCplFromLpFrame reads back on 0° < θ < 90°), a one-to-one reparameterisation, so the minimum and the residual are unchanged and FitQuality's covariance in the constants is the propagated one, with no second covariance formula. The LP-LP visibility stays a free nuisance coordinate (FringeVisibilityCoordinate); the CPL-LP fit stays phased on the LP zero as the reference fits it (its σ is conditional on that zero).\n3. The Jacobian frame. FitQuality.residualJacobian steps √ε · max(|x|, 1e-12), a rule for metre-scale thicknesses: in a solve's own O(1) coordinates a coordinate at or near zero (a Mueller off-diagonal, a scaled entry that did not move) gets a step near 1e-20 and a garbage column. Changing that rule would move BerremanTests' numbers. FittedProblem therefore calls FitQuality's residualJacobian and reportFrom about a frame offset by one hundred (y ↦ residual(start + y − 100) at y = 100), so the step is about 1.5e-6, the order of ALGLIB's own 1e-6 differentiation step, and FitQuality is reused unchanged.\n4. Rank. ResidualJacobian had no rank. Step 394 counts singular values above 1e-6 of the largest: a forward-difference Jacobian at that step carries noise near 1e-8 of a column, so an exactly confounded pair (gain against the source's intensity scale) is rank 1, while a direction 1e4 times weaker still counts. σ, the correlation and the condition are recorded only at full rank (None otherwise), which also keeps every stored number finite (System.Text.Json refuses NaN and infinity).\n5. Suspect and its thresholds. A parameter is suspect when its σ is undetermined, when σ exceeds sigmaFraction of its bounds' span (a unit-free reading; every unknown has bounds), or when |ρ| with another entry of the same solve exceeds correlation. The thresholds are study fit settings (the brief), initially 0.95 and 0.1, stored in the study file; they are not an application setting.\n6. The profile. A suspect entry is stepped at x̂ + jσ, j = −3 … 3, points outside its bounds left out, j = 0 being the fit itself; an entry without σ is stepped at seven points evenly across its bounds. Each point re-fits the same solve with that coordinate held, through ScaledSearch.solveWith (the one bounded LM request, step 381), under the fit's watch, so Cancel stops it (ProfileCancelledErr → FitCancelledErr; the job writes nothing). The profile pass counts its own iterations from one through IterationWatch.after (moved out of fitNonlinear, step 387). Linear and calibration solves are profiled the same way: their LM re-fit converges to the exact least-squares profile.\n7. Realizability covers every black-box item the fitted runs use, under any engine, at its fitted values through the item evaluator at reference orientation (steps 247-248), with a round-off allowance of −1e-12 · trace (the trace of the coherency matrix is m00). The product check covers every series whose items each have a solve of their own: productCheckOf (step 352) is called with the cascade of the later items folded by cascadeProduct, so [QZ; LR] gives exactly M_LR · M_QZ and longer series their full light-order product; SeriesProductCheck.rmseRatio forms the ratio through ProductRmseRatio.between.\n8. No stub. The engines are not changed to carry their problems: each results member re-derives its solve from the same pure inputs (scaledProblemWith; objectSystemsWith, the projection reconstructLinear now calls; airRunsWith and calibrateFromAirRows, the selection calibrateLinear now calls), so StudyFitSolution keeps its shape and no engine answers an empty placeholder while a later step fills it. FitRun gains results only in step 404, where runFit fills them, so no fit run is ever written with empty results by product code.\n9. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1; no BerremanTests class reaches FittedProblems.fs or StudyEngine.fs, so unit-tests runs only on the steps changing MuellerInverse.fs, MuellerReconstruction.fs and StagedMuellerPath.fs (394, 398), on the cheapest classes that read them. No Ui file changes, so ui-smoke and ui-tests are not selected; the results tabs that show these shapes are S11.5's.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S11.5 (Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes): appended steps 405-419 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (37 obligations S115-*, 15 acceptance bindings, 15 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 405-419 on Domain, Storage, Ui, Controls, App, OpticalConstructor.Tests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests and AGENTS.md). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). Validated on a staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step: executability check passed; step-compiler check_spec clean on the wired copy; the real files are byte-identical to the validated copy.\n\nStep plan (steps 405-418 IMPLEMENT, 419 WIRE_UI; build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; ui-smoke whole (light) on every step touching OpticalConstructor.Ui / Ui.Tests / App; ui-tests by touched class; the twenty s40 invariants on every step):\n- 405 (Domain, Storage, Tests): EntryProvenance gains FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo = { kit : KitId; studyStem : FileStem; fitRunStem : FileStem }, UserManaged, no attribution; database provenance kind 6, no catalogue id; library-common.schema.json shape.\n- 406 (Domain, Tests): new Domain StudyPublishing.fs after FitRuns.fs: PublishError and Study.calibratedItemsWith (item-owned fitted entries -> CalibratedParameter (value, sigma from results.sigmas, run) in each item's next revision through Item.publishRevision; link followers take the leader's; session/run-owned values left out; republishing writes nothing). New StudyPublishingTests (ADD_TEST).\n- 407 (Domain, Tests): ItemId.toLibraryEntryId / toElementValueId, ItemLabel.entryName, FitRun.provenanceIn, PromotionSubject, Study.promotedMaterialWith (the opened version's entry under CrystalParameterPhysics of the crystal the run produced), FitRun.promotedBlackBoxWith (a CustomMueller ConstantMueller polarizer preset of the fitted matrix through the item evaluator), FitRun.promotionSubjectsWith.\n- 408 (Domain, Tests): KitLibraryContext.promoteMaterial / promoteBlackBox: next version (first for an unheld id) built under FitProvenance, sealed and put through the import seam with MoveLatestVersion, then snapshotReferences into the kit; read-only refused before any write. Tests over a SQLite library.\n- 409 (Domain, Tests): StudyMsg.SetOpenedMaterialParameter (study * material version * Parameter) through withMaterialParameterState.\n- 410 (Ui, Tests): OpenedKit.studies / fitRuns read at open; model kitStudies, kitFitRuns, studySurface (StudySurfaceState); studyContext, selectedStudyOpt, studyFitRuns; messages StudyCommand (applyTo + recordStudy behind the read-only guard), SelectStudy, SetNewStudyName, ToggleNewStudyExperiment. New StudyWindowModelTests (ADD_TEST); KitOpeningTests fact.\n- 411 (Ui, Tests): ParameterEditDraft keyed by StudyParameterRef; EditStudyParameter; ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView extracted and called by the Items panel (unchanged) and the unknowns table. ui-tests: ItemsPanelTests.\n- 412 (Ui, Tests): StudyFitJobHost.inert; KitWindowShell.studyFits; model studyFit and studyForwardContext; StudyFit of StudyFitMsg through updateWith; a completed run joins kitFitRuns and is chosen (completion refresh, .spec-md §10.4).\n- 413 (Ui, Tests): PublishCalibration (calibratedItemsWith + recordItem per item) and PromoteToLibrary (promoteMaterial / promoteBlackBox), kitStatus telling each outcome.\n- 414 (Controls, Ui, Tests, Ui.Tests): flow step Unknowns (Inverse only), StudyUnknownsView.fs (studyBarView, New study form, experiments, material offers, unknowns grid with owner/state/value/bounds/sigma/scope/link, the shared editor), ids, TestAppScope.studyKitIn. New StudyViewTests (ADD_TEST). ui-tests: KitWindowTests, ScrollExtentTests, StudyViewTests.\n- 415: flow step Fit, StudyFitView.fs (pre-fit list through prefitWith, Run joint = StudyRunFitButton / Run stage 1 / Run stage 2 on one row, calibration use, progress with Cancel, fit error, fit-run history), SelectFitRun, SetStudyCalibrationUse, studyPrefitsOpt.\n- 416 (Domain, Controls, Ui, Tests, Ui.Tests): SolverHandoffView.fs, SolverHandoffWindow.fs, SolverHandoffWindowKey, the hand-off ids and ExperimentCollectionStore.fs deleted; docs cut; DELETE_TEST SolverHandoffWindowTests -> StudyViewTests (eight validation facts deleted as covered by PrefitCheckTests and InverseConstructorTests, three view facts migrated); ScrollExtentTests and WireUiFinalCompositionTests facts renamed; WindowLauncherTests key list shrinks. ui-tests count falls by 8.\n- 417: flow step Results, FitResultsTab, StudyResultsView.fs (values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood from the stored FitRun.results), selectedFitRunOpt (latest by default), ownerCaption, fitEntryCaption.\n- 418: flow step Publish, StudyPublishView.fs (calibration preview through calibratedItemsWith, Publish calibration, one Promote per promotionSubjectsWith subject, the no-undo lines).\n- 419 WIRE_UI (App, Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md): ConstructorScene.mount composes StudyFitJobHost.onUiThread over the window's dispatch; AGENTS.md gotcha 'The Inverse flow ends at the study'; ui-smoke acceptance through a shown Inverse window and a real kit folder.\n\nInterpretations and departures, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The fitted provenance names the study and the fit run by the file stems the kit stores them under (StudyName.fileStem, FitRunName.fileStem): StudyName and FitRunName are declared after LibraryEntryFiles.fs (steps 221, 358), and moving them would split StudyName.tryCreate from its StudyError. Nothing is moved.\n2. A black-box object's library form is a polarizer preset whose behaviour is ConstantMueller [one component at reference orientation] and whose category is CustomMueller: the one library kind that holds a fixed Mueller matrix (an item-model form holds no values, step 215). Its entry id is the item's GUID, so the first promotion adds version 1 and each later one mints the next version.\n3. Promotion writes through the import seam (sealEntry + putEntryVersion, step 94), the one path that stores a whole entry version with its own provenance; the material store's saveMaterial writes UserProvenance only (step 69). The snapshot reuses snapshotReferences (step 139). The opened version stays pinned, so the study and its samples are unchanged; nothing is replaced, so no undo is needed.\n4. Publish calibration publishes item-owned fitted values only; a session- or run-owned value (a gain) has no single item value and stays in the fit run. Every published value needs its sigma (CalibratedParameter validates sigma > 0), so an undetermined sigma refuses the publish. A link's follower takes its leader's calibration, because stage 2 refuses an uncalibrated ItemScope instrument unknown (step 385). Publishing one run twice writes no second revision.\n5. The four study steps are the Inverse constructor's alone, as Data is (step 323); Plan (S14.2) goes between Unknowns and Fit at its 001 §O position. They are surfaces of the kit window, so no window and no keepOnScreen call is added; ScrollExtentTests gains one fact per surface.\n6. One parameter editor: ParameterEditDraft is keyed by StudyParameterRef; an opened material component is set through the new StudyMsg case SetOpenedMaterialParameter, the item parameter through S7.2's SetParameterState. No unlink verb is added (001 §P names LinkParameters alone).\n7. A fit writes its fit run, so RunFit sits behind the read-only guard (step 185); the Results step reads a read-only kit's runs.\n8. The hand-off's eight validation facts test the checks step 369 moved and PrefitCheckTests / InverseConstructorTests already prove, so they are deleted; its three view facts migrate to StudyViewTests. ExperimentCollectionStore.fs goes with the hand-off, its last user (step 152).\n9. Contract effects follow the earlier sections: a create per new field, case, id or member; retirements only where the consumer census is covered by the step's edits (CollectionName / ExperimentCollectionSnapshot list a file step 152 deletes, so their removal is carried by the how_to and its closing grep).\n10. The WIRE_UI acceptance runs the real host over a study of no experiment (NoStageRunErr), proving the worker-to-UI-thread round trip through a shown window without lab data; the fit path itself is proven by StudyFitJobTests (step 393) and StudyWindowModelTests, and end to end by S12's acceptance tests.\n11. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1; no BerremanTests class reaches the changed files, so unit-tests is not selected.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S12.1 (AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit): appended steps 420-430 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (34 obligations S121-*, 11 acceptance bindings, 11 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 420-430 on Domain, Ui, Controls, OpticalConstructor.Tests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md and data/optics-mueller). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; the twenty-one s41 invariants on every step; kit-acceptance selects OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests from step 421, which creates the file, on every later step, since each touches the import code, the study, the acceptance file or the kit):\n- 420 (Domain, Ui, Tests, Ui.Tests): KitIdProvider { mintKitId } in Kit.fs; KitIdProvider.system and openKitWith in KitOpening.fs (openKitAt = openKitWith KitIdProvider.system, signature unchanged); KitStartContext.kitIds, CreateKit opens through it; KitStartWindow composes system. Two KitStartTests facts. Gates: constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, ui-tests (KitStartWindowTests).\n- 421 (Ui.Tests): TestAppScope.inverseModelOver (studyKitIn's composition, which it now calls); new KitAcceptanceTests.fs (trait kit-acceptance, FsxAcceptanceTests pattern): buildOpticsMuellerKit copies the committed data/ tree into <output>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/optics-mueller, over freshAppContext's SQLite :memory: library, a mutable test clock at 2026-05-31T12:00:00Z, a fixed kit id and nine fixed item ids; CreateKit, the aliased lab template, the nine items (Laser = heNe633 preset, LP1/LP2 real LP, CPL1/CPL2 circular polarizer, AIR empty slot, QZ/LR black box, Phone intensity detector; LP2 dial negative, CPL2 dial positive; the five instrument constants and the 32 black-box elements unknown), the Source/Prep/Obj1/Obj2/Analyzer/Detector table, two grids (28 single-object + 12 two-object setups) and the two -90 LR setups by SetSetupName/CreateSetup. Fact: items and setups.\n- 422 (Domain, Ui, Tests): DataSplitError.SplitKeyUnknownErr / SplitKeyReadableErr; DataSplit.withGroupOver (an unreadable group offered over a named setup, its experiment named by its key); TableAndElementRotationMsg.OfferSplitGroupOver (ticks the offer, writes nothing); MatchByTemplate unchanged.\n- 423 (Ui, Ui.Tests): ConstructorUiId.dataSplitGroupSetupChoice; the split panel's unmatched row gains a 'Record over:' ComboBox of the kit's setups. ui-tests: DataStepTests.\n- 424 (Ui.Tests): the build attaches the seven final lab files in place (SplitByColumn + ToggleSplitOffer + OfferSplitGroupOver + MatchByTemplate), sets roles (nine AIR runs Calibration, six darkness Dark, two BullshitCheck Diagnostic), the six hand-set gain sessions, the two day-1 LR#90 corrections with their audit note and the excluded frame (capture 17 of LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2). Fact: 53 experiments with data, roles, sessions, correction, exclusion; no lab file touched.\n- 425 (Domain, Tests): StudyMsg.SetSessionGainModel and SetFitMode (applyTo through withSessionGainModel / withFitMode); StudySession.gainModelOffers (free; anchored to the session's Calibration runs; interpolated between its first and last).\n- 426 (Controls, Ui, Ui.Tests): studySessionGrid, studySessionGainChoice, studyFitModeChoice, SessionGainModel.caption; the Unknowns step's 'Sessions and gains' grid and the Fit step's mode choice, withheld read-only. ui-tests: StudyViewTests, ScrollExtentTests, KitWindowTests.\n- 427 (Ui.Tests): the build creates QZ-LR (53 experiments), sets it staged and its six reference gain models, runs stage 1 at 12:01:00Z, publishes, runs stage 2 at 12:02:00Z through the shell's posting host. assertReferenceInstruments / assertReferenceObjects compare with BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference at dataMatrixTol.\n- 428 (Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md, data/optics-mueller): the equality fact; the committed kit created once by running it and copying its built folder (data/ and .oc/ excepted); AGENTS.md gotcha 'The reference kits are AT-1's and AT-2's output, never hand-edited'.\n- 429 (Ui.Tests): TestAppScope.emptyLibraryAppContext; the committed kit opened read-only (OpenKitReadOnly) against an empty library, snapshots resolving every item model, attachments at their hashes, StudyFitParam.runFit of stage 2 reproducing the reference, the folder unchanged. ui-smoke (TestAppScope).\n- 430 (Ui.Tests): SendKit through KitArchiveProxy.create and KitArchiveJobHost.immediate, OpenKitZip into a fresh folder: files equal, the study's residual vector at its start point equal.\n\nInterpretations and departures, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Three product gaps block a message-only, file-identical build, and nothing is deferred, so this section closes them first: (a) a new kit's id was minted by Guid.NewGuid inside openKitAt with no seam (step 150), so two builds could never be file-identical; KitIdProvider mirrors ItemIdProvider (step 230). (b) A lab group the template cannot read (Darkness, LP-(Darkness)-CPL2, BullshitCheck-2 ..., step 269) had no message path into an experiment: AttachDataFile attaches every row and no message names an experiment (steps 286, 290, 310, 320); the user now names the setup and the experiment takes the key's name, through step 320's offer path. (c) No message set a session's gain model or the fit mode (steps 365, 366, 410-419), so the reference's anchored and interpolated gains (step 356) were out of the app's reach; StudyMsg gains both, and the study view gains their controls. Each has its product tests; the kit-acceptance gate runs from step 421 on.\n2. The lab template is NamingTemplate.standard with aliases ({source:LP1=LP,CPL1=CPL} ... {analyzer:LP2=LP,CPL2=CPL}): item labels are unique (001 §I), while the lab's names say LP and CPL on both sides (step 268's aliases).\n3. The LR correction: the optics-mueller caveat (its AGENTS.md 'Current Known Caveats' and notes/images_final_export_task.md 'LR Rotation Caveat') concerns the day-1 CPL-CPL dataset; its LR#45 runs were re-measured at +45 on day 2 (CPL-(LR#45)-CPL-2, CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2). So the final data's only mislabelled runs are CPL-(LR#90)-CPL and CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL, re-pointed to -90 setups with an audit note; no +45 run is re-pointed. The reference used +90; a Mueller rotation has period 180°, so -90 and +90 give the same rotation (to ~1e-16), and the reference values stay reproducible within dataMatrixTol. The φ of the corrected two-sample setup is QZ's (step 390), unchanged.\n4. Roles: all nine AIR runs (the -2R and -BR repeats included) are CalibrationRun: stage 1 calibrates on the LP-LP/LP-CPL/CPL-LP ones (step 389) and every session's gain anchors to them (step 385 reads them); DriftCheckRun would make stage 2 fit an AIR run as an object run, breaking the black-box shape (step 386). Darkness captures are DarkRun over their family's AIR setup and hold no session, so every session's dark is all six (step 357), as the reference's 869.666. BullshitChecks are DiagnosticRun; the CPL-LP gain split is the two hand-set sessions, read from the earliest BullshitCheck time.\n5. Determinism of the built kit: a test clock (12:00:00Z for every kit write, 12:01:00Z and 12:02:00Z for the two fit runs, so append-only names never collide), a fixed kit id and fixed item ids. Nothing else stored is time- or machine-dependent (steps 225, 313, 383: no time field outside the kit file and fit runs; the lock is under the ignored .oc/).\n6. The read path runs stage 2 through StudyFitParam.runFit directly: under a read-only kit the window's RunFit is refused because it writes the fit run (steps 185, 413). Stage-1 values are checked as the committed items' published calibrations, since a re-run of stage 1 over calibrated instruments fits nothing.\n7. Step 428's edits list every root kit file by name and the folder data/optics-mueller/library: the snapshots are named library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json by the built-in GUIDs, and the source and polarizer preset GUIDs are minted by S1.3's implementer (step 20), so their file names are not known at authoring time. No step before has listed a folder.\n8. Gates: kit-acceptance cannot run before step 421 creates its file, so step 420 runs without it. ui-smoke runs where Ui, App or TestAppScope change; ui-tests selects the classes whose facts change. unit-tests is not selected: no step touches BerremanTestSupport, MuellerReference or the solver.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite (its suites are unit-tests, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, ui-tests), so every step that creates or selects a kit-acceptance test fails 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN (temporal.py replay: 'suite discovery is missing or unknown'; checker.py: 'selector needs a suite with known test discovery'). The installed adapters cannot fill it before KitAcceptanceTests.fs exists: test-census refuses a listing with no test (dotnet_capture.py:344, '--list-tests listed no test'), and test-capture's TRX merge refuses a partial discovery (trx_inventory.py:88). The inventory is outside the spec author's write scope. Remedy: seed an explicit empty suite, \"kit-acceptance\": {\"tests\": [], ...} with the Ui.Tests project, in .repository-inventory-json (the format accepts an empty tests list, inventory.py:85-89), or teach the adapter a forward-pointing gate (kit-acceptance.gates declares expected_by \"0050\"). S12.2 (AT-2) meets the same gap. Validation: with that one suite seeded into a staged COPY of the inventory, and a placeholder final WIRE step, 'executability check' passed, and the step compiler's check_spec reports 0 findings on that wired copy (on the unwired copy only the expected 'final step must be WIRE', which the Close section supplies); without the seed the only findings are the DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN ones above. The real files are byte-identical to the validated staged copy.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S12.2 (AT-2 and the absorbing-biaxial-noisy reference kit): appended steps 431-440 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (33 obligations S122-*, 10 acceptance bindings, 10 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 431-440 on BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md and data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned).\n\nStep plan (every step IMPLEMENT; build and elevation on every step; the twenty-one s42 invariants on every step; kit-acceptance selects OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests on every step):\n- 431 (BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): CommittedKit gains AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit (data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy); ensembleSeeds MOVES from InverseFitHarness to BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample (MuellerInverseTests and BiaxialInverseTests name it qualified); AbsorbingBiaxialSample gains noisySeeds (the noisy suite's five), absorbingReportedQuantities (its nineteen quantities), RecoveryBandBreach and absorbingBandBreaches (the band table, total); AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests asserts its bands through it. unit-tests: AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests, BiaxialInverseTests, MuellerInverseTests, MuellerReconstructionTests.\n- 432 (Ui.Tests): AT-1's clock and start screen factored into testClockAt / kitStartOver; buildAbsorbingKit: the absorbing crystal material (CrystalParameterPhysics of AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbing) and its 100 um plate sample written as user entry files and dropped on the Library window, applied through the import dialog; kit with fixed id, template {obj1}; items Laser (heNe633 = referenceWaveLength), Polarimeter T and R (Mueller polarimeter, decentLab defaults), five plates; table with a second detector on the plate's reflected ray. absorbingBuild: one lazily shared build for every AT-2 fact but the ensemble.\n- 433 (Ui.Tests): three grids over three drafts (A1+A2 OpticAxisCut, A1 OtherOpticAxisCut, A3 ZCut/XCut/YCut) record five setups and one experiment per plate; configurationsOf reads each scan as 0044 configurations; joined in kit order they equal a1 first four @ a2 @ a1 last four @ a3.\n- 434 (Ui.Tests): noisyObservationsOf (product noisyObserveAbsoluteWith over absorbing, decentLab, fullConfigurations), observationFileOf (KeyedObservation.observationFileText keyed by plate); five data/noisy-observations-seed-<n>.csv; seed 1 attached in place by SplitByColumn (Mueller-matrix observations, key sample) + MatchByTemplate.\n- 435 (Ui.Tests): study AbsorbingTriclinic, OpenMaterial, fifteen SetOpenedMaterialParameter (start perturbedStart, bounds start +- searchBox.halfWidth x the harness scale); studyResidualAtStart / studyDataOf factored out of AT-1's Send fact; facts: MaterialScope, generated axes = AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes, data identity, residual = throughputResidualFor within 1e-12 relative.\n- 436 (Ui.Tests): runStudyFitThroughShell factored out of AT-1; the build ends with RunFit (JointStage) at 12:01:00Z, one nonlinear fit run; assertAbsorbingRecovery (promotedMaterialWith + absorbingBandBreaches of each quantity's relative error).\n- 437 (Ui.Tests): the xUnit v3 Explicit five-seed ensemble on its own build: seeds 2-5 re-attached through the split messages, fitted, statisticsFor + absorbingBandBreaches over the scatters.\n- 438 (Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md, data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy): assertSameKitFiles factored out of AT-1; the equality fact; the committed kit created once from the built folder (.oc/ excepted, data/ included); AGENTS.md's reference-kit gotcha names the AT-2 kit.\n- 439 (Ui.Tests): openCommittedReadOnly / assertCommittedUnchanged factored out of AT-1; the committed kit read-only against an empty library: observation files regenerated byte-identical, snapshots resolve, data and model identity, StudyFitParam.runFit within the bands, folder unchanged.\n- 440 (Ui.Tests): sendAndReopen factored out of AT-1; SendKit + OpenKitZip: files equal, residual at start equal.\n\nInterpretations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. One experiment per plate, as 001 says; the five seeds are five measurements of the same plates. The committed kit attaches seed 1's file (the study fits it, assertion 3); the other four files sit in data/ and are compared byte for byte; the Explicit ensemble re-attaches them in turn through SplitByColumn + MatchByTemplate (step 318 (b): a group matches the experiment its key names) on its own build.\n2. A scan reading T and R in one experiment needs a detector on each branch (BeamLayout.effectiveCapture, TableAndElementRotationView.fs:draftCapture/availableCaptures), so the kit holds the one Mueller-polarimeter model as two items, Polarimeter T and Polarimeter R; their noise parameters default to NoiseParam.decentLab (step 217).\n3. The plates are five items of ONE sample entry (a 100 um plate of the one material version). The cut is carried by each observation row (S9.2 step 301; the forward model reads it, step 375), so the items differ by label and the test maps label to cut.\n4. A crystal material enters the library through its entry file (step 355), so the material and its sample are written as user entry files and dropped on the Library window (steps 104, 107, 111): message-only, with fixed GUIDs so the build is file-identical.\n5. The kit template is {obj1}: setups and experiments are named by the plate; the observation file keys its rows by plate label, so the split matches each group by name.\n6. The box: the nonlinear engine's scaled unit is the bounds' span over 2 x 50 (step 387), so bounds of start +- searchBox.halfWidth x absorbingScalingAround's scale reproduce the harness's search.\n7. The seeds: AT-2 needs the noisy suite's five seeds without transcription, so ensembleSeeds moves to BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample and noisySeeds (= first five) to AbsorbingBiaxialSample. The executability check requires every consumer of the retired harness name to be edited, so BiaxialInverseTests (1000 s) is selected in step 431 with the other touched classes.\n8. The shared builders AT-1 composes inline (clock, start screen, fit hosting, residual at start, file comparison, read-only open, send round trip) are factored once and called by both tests (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'); AT-1's facts keep their assertions.\n9. absorbingBuild is a module-level Lazy so the ~3-minute fit runs once per test run; facts never write into the built folder. The fit deadline is 1800 s.\n10. Gates: seam-plan proposes ui-smoke and ui-tests (all_discovered) for steps editing KitAcceptanceTests.fs because the inventory has no kit-acceptance suite; ui-tests excludes the kit-acceptance trait and ui-smoke selects only its own trait, so (as S12.1 did) those steps run build, elevation and kit-acceptance. Step 431 adopts seam-plan's unit-tests classes plus BiaxialInverseTests (edited) and MuellerReconstructionTests (reads the changed locator), and kit-acceptance (AT-1 reads the locator; applies_to BerremanTestSupport/**). Step 437's Explicit fact is discovered and skipped, so the kit-acceptance count does not rise there.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (same as S12.1, needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite, so every step creating or selecting a kit-acceptance test fails 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN only (36 findings, steps 421-441 of the wired copy). Remedy as S12.1 recorded: seed an explicit empty kit-acceptance suite for the Ui.Tests project in the inventory, or teach the adapter the forward-pointing gate. Validation: with that suite seeded into a staged COPY of the inventory and a placeholder final WIRE step, 'executability check' passed and the step compiler's check_spec reports 0 findings on the wired copy (on the unwired copy only the expected 'final step must be WIRE', which the Close section supplies). The real files are byte-identical to the validated staged copy.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S13.1 (MaterialSourceProxy and refractiveindex.info): appended steps 441-452 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (35 obligations S131-*, 12 acceptance bindings, 12 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 441-452 on Domain, Storage, Ui, Controls, App, OpticalConstructor.Tests and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). One new contract, <SVC:MaterialSourceProxy> (proxy, fsharp, OpticalConstructor.Domain): ADD_CONTRACT 443, IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT 447; the cycle mints it.\n\nStep plan (build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty-one s43 invariants on every step):\n- 441 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Tests): SourcePullInfo gains recordHash : ContentHash (the SHA-256 of the record's text at pull time, ContentHash.ofBytes); library-common.schema.json requires it in the pulled provenance shape; every SourcePullInfo literal (BuiltinCatalogue.licensedMaterialContent, LibraryEntryFilesTests, EntryFileJsonTests) sets it; EntryFileJsonTests +1.\n- 442 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Tests): PulledRecord; CatalogueImportProxy.pulledRecordsOf (by record, entry, version) over the in-memory double and createInDatabase; LibraryEntryEnvelope.pulledSourceRows derived from SourcePullProvenance, kept exactly by stageVersion (step 60's PulledSource table, no model change); contract fact over both stores + LibraryDatabaseTests fact.\n- 443 ADD_CONTRACT (Domain, Tests): new MaterialSources.fs before CatalogueImport.fs: MaterialSourceError (7 Err cases), MaterialSourceHit, MaterialSourceQuery.filter (the one search rule), SourceMaterialRecord, SourceSnapshotFileCount/Progress/Observer/Info/Outcome, MaterialSourceProxy { sourceName; snapshotVersion; searchRecords; fetchRecord; updateSnapshot }, InMemorySourceRecord, InMemoryMaterialSource + MaterialSourceProxy.createInMemory. New MaterialSourceProxyTests (7).\n- 444 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Tests): CatalogueImportContext.materialSources (create sets []); new MaterialSourcePulls.fs after CatalogueImport.fs: MaterialSourcePullError, SourcePullChange (PullAddedEntry, PullMintedVersion, PullFoundUnchanged, PullRecordAbsent), SourcePullResult, SourceRefreshInfo, SourceRefresh; pullRecord, refreshPulls, updateSourceSnapshot through sealEntry + putEntryVersion. New MaterialSourcePullTests (8).\n- 445 IMPLEMENT (Storage, Tests): MaterialImport gains ImportError.describe, RefractiveIndexInfoCatalogText.hits (line-based SHELF/BOOK/PAGE reader of catalog-nk.yml answering MaterialSourceHit) and RefractiveIndexInfoText.referencesOpt; fixtures/catalog-nk.yml; MaterialImportTests +3.\n- 446 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Ui, App, Tests, Ui.Tests): DataLocations.materialSourcesFolder (default %LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Sources), DataLocationKind.MaterialSourcesLocation last (caption 'Online source snapshots'), DataLocations.rows arm, ConfigKey.materialSourcesFolder = MaterialSourcesFolder, test appsettings TestRun/Sources, TestAppScope; five location facts widened. ui-tests: AppConfigTests, AppContextTests, DataLocationsWindowTests.\n- 447 IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT (Storage, Domain, Tests): new MaterialSourceStore.fs after KitArchiveStore.fs: SourceSnapshotStamp (.snapshot-json, schema/material-source-snapshot.schema.json, validateSourceSnapshot, parseVersionedText) and SourceSnapshotText, SourceArchiveUrl, SourceArchiveDownloader with the one marked HTTP seam http, MaterialSourceProxy.createRefractiveIndexInfo (snapshot <sources>/refractiveindex.info, CC0-1.0, citation 'refractiveindex.info, <record>: <REFERENCES>', update via KitArchiveProxy.create's listZipEntries/extractKitZip, whole-folder replace). New MaterialSourceFixture + MaterialSourceStoreTests (8) over fixture snapshots built from fixtures/Si.yml, formula2.yml and catalog-nk.yml and test-written GitHub-style archives; no test calls http.\n- 448 IMPLEMENT (Tests): new MaterialSourcePullSqliteTests (4): over freshLibraryDatabase + createInDatabase + the real adapter: a pull is a user material at version 1 with provenance, pulled-source row and CC0 attribution; an unchanged update mints nothing; a changed page mints version 2 and keeps version 1; a second pull writes nothing.\n- 449 IMPLEMENT (Ui, Ui.Tests): AppContext compose sets catalogueImports.materialSources = [ createRefractiveIndexInfo locations.materialSourcesFolder SourceArchiveDownloader.http ClockProvider.system ]; AppContextTests +1. ui-tests: AppContextTests.\n- 450 IMPLEMENT (Ui, Controls, Tests): new MaterialSourcesView.fs after MaterialsWindowView.fs: SourceSnapshotJobHost/Handle (posting, onUiThread, immediate, inert, as KitArchiveJobHost), MaterialSourcesContext { imports; jobs; pullsApplied }, model, eight messages, init/update/view; captions and derived ids in ConstructorUiIdOfDomain; nine fixed UiIds. New MaterialSourcesModelTests (6). ui-smoke whole.\n- 451 IMPLEMENT (Ui, Controls, Ui.Tests): MaterialSourcesWindow (Online sources, 720 x 640, keepOnScreen, cancels on Closed), WindowKey.MaterialSourcesWindowKey, materialSourcesWindow id, WireUiFinalCompositionTests.rootWindowFactory arm; ScrollExtentTests +1; new MaterialSourcesWindowTests (3 ui-tests, 2 ui-smoke). ui-tests: ScrollExtentTests, MaterialSourcesWindowTests.\n- 452 WIRE_UI (Ui, Controls, Ui.Tests): MaterialsWindowContext.openOnlineSources, MaterialsWindowMsg.OpenOnlineSources, the Browse verbs row's 'Online sources…' while the import seam carries a source, MaterialsWindow bakes the single-instance window whose pullsApplied dispatches MaterialsImportApplied; materialsOnlineSourcesButton; MaterialsWindowTests +3 ui-tests, +1 ui-smoke acceptance over AppContext.create (fileLocations) that never presses Update snapshot. ui-tests: MaterialsWindowTests.\nCounts: constructor-unit-tests +40, ui-tests +8, ui-smoke +3; no test removed.\n\nInterpretations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. The record hash rides in the provenance (SourcePullInfo.recordHash), not in a new PulledSource column. An entry's content hash always changes with the snapshot version, so 'only where a record's hash changed' needs the record's own hash; in the provenance it travels with the entry file, the database payload and every kit snapshot, and the EF model and LibrarySchemaVersion (1) stay as S2.1 left them. The entry schemas keep version 1 (no pulled file was released; step 405's precedent).\n2. The pulled-source row (S2.1) is derived from a version's SourcePullProvenance inside stageVersion, as facet rows are, so every storing path (pull, kit snapshot, re-import of an export) keeps it; a fork is the user's and has none.\n3. One MaterialSourceProxy is one adapter (S13.2's PTB and Henke are further creates in the same list); sourceName is a data field. The search rule is shared (MaterialSourceQuery.filter: every word, case-insensitive, in name or record), and MaterialImport's catalog reader answers the same MaterialSourceHit, so no second hit shape exists.\n4. The sources live on CatalogueImportContext.materialSources, the library-exchange seam every library window already carries (S3.3's exportFolderOpt precedent), so no Materials window construction is re-threaded.\n5. A refresh mints the entry's next version from its latest (id, name, category and description kept) with the record's new physics and pull; nothing mutates, a user's edit stays as an older version. A record the snapshot no longer lists answers PullRecordAbsent and writes nothing (an update is never blocked by one removed page). A retired pulled material is left out of a refresh and a pull of its record is refused, so nothing revives what the user retired. pullRecord of a held record refreshes it, so pulling twice writes once.\n6. The snapshot version is the clock's UTC date (yyyy-MM-dd): 001 §D allows 'snapshot date or commit'; the date is deterministic under ClockProvider and needs no second HTTP call.\n7. The refractiveindex.info layout was verified on 2026-11-04 against github.com/polyanskiy/refractiveindex.info-database: default branch main; database/catalog-nk.yml (SHELF / BOOK / PAGE with name and data); pages at database/data/<data> (e.g. main/Ag/nk/Johnson.yml) with REFERENCES, COMMENTS and DATA; CC0 1.0 Universal. The archive URL is GitHub's branch archive (https://github.com/polyanskiy/refractiveindex.info-database/archive/refs/heads/main.zip); the adapter relies on its one top folder, not on that folder's name.\n8. The extraction REUSES S6's archive seam (KitArchiveProxy.create: listZipEntries reads names through KitTreeEntry.tryOfZipEntryName, extractKitZip reports and cancels per file and removes what it wrote), so no second zip extractor exists; the KitFolder target type is accepted for that reuse.\n9. The snapshot stamp is .snapshot-json (001 §A: once per folder, named by its extension), canonical JSON validated by its own schema, a version mismatch a typed error (.spec-md §4 'Stored formats').\n10. The sources folder defaults beside library.db under %LOCALAPPDATA% (slow data shared by every kit, 001 §G), is the last DataLocations field and DataLocationKind, and is listed by the Data locations window.\n11. SourceSnapshotJobHost follows KitArchiveJobHost (step 200) and StudyFitJobHost (step 393), the precedent of one host per job type; it lives in MaterialSourcesView.fs because only that surface runs it.\n12. The Online sources surface is a single-instance window opened from the Materials window (the brief's keepOnScreen and ScrollExtentTests need a window); completion refresh goes through pullsApplied -> MaterialsImportApplied, the S3.2 import dialog's path.\n13. MaterialImport's page reading (importMaterial) is unchanged: a page it cannot read is SourceRecordUnreadableErr. No YAML package is added; the catalog reader is line-based like the page reader.\n14. Contract effects follow steps 190, 194 and 405: a new member or case is a create of that symbol. SourcePullInfo's change_shape was replaced after SYMBOL_CENSUS_UNKNOWN (the type is step 24's, absent from today's inventory); AppContext's and MaterialsWindow's change_behavior were dropped after SCOPE_CONSUMERS (signatures unchanged; S8.3/S8.4 precedent); WireUiFinalCompositionTests left step 451's ui-tests arm after SELECTOR_EMPTY_ARM (all its facts are ui-smoke), while its rootWindowFactory still gains the MaterialSourcesWindowKey arm (step 190's precedent) so the match stays exhaustive.\n15. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates', the brief and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s131/seam.json, seam-wired.json). Not adopted from seam-plan: kit-acceptance on 446, 449, 451 and 452 (proposed only because they edit OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests; they touch neither the study, the run law, the data-import code nor the acceptance files); its whole-suite ui-tests for 446 and its project-wide class lists for 451 (its Ui.Tests.fsproj / UiIds.fs edits reach every class); and constructor-unit-tests by class (the suite is light and runs whole).\n\nValidation (ASG tools from C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator; scripts and logs in specs/0050/.artifacts/s131/):\n- executability check on the staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step reports only the two unminted '<SVC:MaterialSourceProxy>' placeholders (steps 443, 447; §9.6), which the cycle's minting step resolves; step_compiler check_spec reports the same.\n- Because §9.6 stops both tools before their deeper checks, a probe copy turned the two contract steps into plain IMPLEMENT steps and seeded the kit-acceptance suite into a copied inventory (the S12.1/S12.2 gap): executability check passes with no findings once the placeholder WIRE step's gates are bound, and check_spec reports nothing on it; on the unwired probe only the mid-campaign 'final step' SELECTION_REQUIRED note for step 452 (kit-acceptance, unit-tests), which the next section's steps make non-final.\n- Negative probe: MaterialSourceStoreTests.fs removed from step 447's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its eight facts.\n- The real .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json are byte-identical to the validated staged copy; pre-existing lines unchanged; LF only.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (unchanged from S12.1 and S12.2, needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite, so steps 421-440 fail 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN; this section adds no kit-acceptance step.\n\nNote for the S13.2 mapper: PTB OCDB and the Henke calculator are further MaterialSourceProxy creates appended to AppContext compose's materialSources list (step 449); pullRecord, refreshPulls, updateSourceSnapshot, the Online sources window and its choice row serve them unchanged. Their records' extra data (sigma arrays, f1/f2) arrives through SourceMaterialRecord.material's physics.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S13.2 (PTB OCDB, the Henke compound calculator and glass catalogues): appended steps 453-464 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (35 obligations S132-*: 12 step obligations, S132-BUILD, S132-ELEVATION and the twenty-one S132-INV-* invariants; 12 acceptance bindings, 12 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 453-464 on Berreman/Berreman, BerremanTests, Domain, Storage, Ui, Controls, OpticalConstructor.Tests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests and data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). No new registered contract: PTB and Henke are further creates of S13.1's MaterialSourceProxy (SVC_BigBoy_0002), so every step is IMPLEMENT and 464 is WIRE_UI.\n\nStep plan (build and elevation on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step; the twenty-one s44 invariants on every step):\n- 453 IMPLEMENT (Berreman core, Storage, BerremanTests, Tests): Dispersion.fs TabulatedNkUncertainty (NumericCarrier sigmaN/sigmaK), TabulatedNkTable.uncertaintyOpt (tryCreate sets None, no number moves), withUncertainty (SampleCountMismatchErr / new InvalidUncertaintyErr); MaterialImport maps the new case to NoDataErr; entry-file round trip. unit-tests: BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests (+1); constructor +1.\n- 454 IMPLEMENT (Storage, Tests): ImportError.MalformedSourceFileErr; the tabulated entry assembly MOVES into TabulatedNkTable.isotropicEntry (entryFromTabulated calls it); PtbOcdbText.importMaterial / headlineOpt (n = 1-delta, k = beta, nm, sigma = (HB - LB) / (2 x level)); fixture fixtures/ptb-Co.txt (PTB's Co.txt header + three rows, CC BY 4.0); MaterialImportTests +2, error-render fact widened.\n- 455 IMPLEMENT (Storage, Domain doc, Tests): the refractiveindex.info snapshot body MOVES into private SourceSnapshotLayout / SourceArchiveSpec members (snapshotVersion, heldVersion, installFrom, updateFromArchive) that createRefractiveIndexInfo calls (S13.1 facts unchanged); MaterialSourceProxy.createPtbOcdb (PTB OCDB, <sources>/ptb-ocdb, CC-BY-4.0, github.com/PTB-SR/ocdb master archive, ocdb/db/COPYING required, it and ocdb/db/data/*.txt kept; hits '<stem> (PTB OCDB)'; citation 'PTB Optical Constants Database (OCDB), ocdb/db/data/<record>: <headline>'); MaterialSourceFixture PTB writers; MaterialSourceStoreTests +4.\n- 456 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Tests): new HenkeCompounds.fs before MaterialSources.fs: HenkeCompoundError (8 Err cases), the 92 ChemicalElements (IUPAC 2021 abridged weights; bracketed mass numbers for Tc, Pm, Po, At, Rn, Fr, Ra, Ac), ChemicalFormula.tryParse, CompoundDensity, CompoundSpec (recordId '<formula>@<density>', entryName, tryOfRecord, tryOfQuery), AtomicScatteringFactors (NumericCarrier), CompoundSpec.indexTableWith (n = 1 - delta, k = beta, CXRO's relation, union grid over the common energy range, lambda via toMeters ElectronVolt). New HenkeCompoundsTests (6).\n- 457 IMPLEMENT (Storage, Domain doc, Tests): HenkeScatteringText.factors (.nff reader, f1 = -9999 rows left out); MaterialSourceProxy.createHenkeCompounds (CXRO Henke, <sources>/cxro-henke, LicenseRef-CXRO; update downloads sf/<symbol>.nff for the 92 elements in Z order through the one HTTP seam's downloader, per-file progress and Cancel, installed through the shared layout; search answers the compound its query writes; fetch computes indexTableWith, recordHash over the record text + element files, Henke et al. 1993 citation); fixtures si.nff, o.nff (test-local values, CXRO format); MaterialImportTests +1, MaterialSourceStoreTests +5.\n- 458 IMPLEMENT (Tests): MaterialSourcePullSqliteTests +3: a pulled PTB record keeps its uncertainties in the SQLite library and its attribution cites PTB under CC-BY-4.0; changed bounds mint version 2 and keep version 1; a pulled Henke compound is a user material v1 under CXRO's provenance, its licence named.\n- 459 IMPLEMENT (Ui, Ui.Tests): AppContext compose offers [refractiveindex.info; PTB OCDB; CXRO Henke] over locations.materialSourcesFolder; AppContextTests' step-449 fact widened. ui-tests: AppContextTests.\n- 460 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Tests, Ui.Tests, data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy): Studies.fs OpenedMaterialPhysics (OpenedCrystalPhysics | OpenedTablePhysics) replaces OpenedMaterial.crystal; a single isotropic TabulatedNK segment opens with Known components row<i>.n / row<i>.k (ParameterName.tableRowIndex / tableRowExtinction); a freed component of an uncertain table takes prior { centre = opened value; sigma = source sigma } unless a prior is given; currentPhysics replaces currentCrystal; StudyForward's ExperimentAssignment.physics / physicsOf, materialProxyOver substitutes materialPhysics, observedCrystalOpt reads crystalOpt; promotedMaterialWith drops a fitted table's source uncertainty; crystal paths keep their numbers; AT-2's committed AbsorbingTriclinic.study-json rewritten to the new key. Tests +5. ui-tests: StudyViewTests; kit-acceptance: KitAcceptanceTests.\n- 461 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Tests): EntryProvenance.FileImportProvenance of EntryFileImportInfo { file : FileName; fileHash : ContentHash } (UserManaged, no attribution), database provenance kind 7, library-common.schema.json shape; three provenance facts widened.\n- 462 IMPLEMENT (Storage, Tests): AgfFormulaNumber.riiFormOf (AGF formulas 1-13 rewritten term for term as refractiveindex.info formulas 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 7), GlassCatalogueText.ofBytes (UTF-16 LE/BE, UTF-8) and importGlasses through the unchanged lowerFormulaAxis + entryOfAxis (Glass); fixture fixtures/test-glasses.agf (test-local values); MaterialImportTests +3.\n- 463 IMPLEMENT (Domain, Storage, Tests): GlassCatalogueRead, CatalogueImportContext.readGlassCatalogue (Storage create reads, hashes, imports); decideDroppedFiles reads a .agf file's glasses as sealed version-1 envelopes under FileImportProvenance and minted ids, decided under DroppedFileOrigin, writing nothing; contract facts over both stores (+6).\n- 464 WIRE_UI (Ui, Controls, Ui.Tests): Materials window Browse verb 'Import glass catalogue…' (materialsImportGlassCatalogueButton, pickGlassCatalogueFile *.agf), ImportGlassCatalogue answered as DropMaterialEntryFiles [ file ] through one helper, MaterialsWindow.ImportGlassCatalogue seam; MaterialsWindowTests +3 ui-tests, +1 ui-smoke acceptance over AppContext.create. ui-tests: MaterialsWindowTests.\nCounts: constructor-unit-tests +36, unit-tests +1, ui-tests +3, ui-smoke +1; no test removed.\n\nInterpretations, recorded because the mapper cannot edit .spec-md:\n1. Sigma lives in S1.1's TabulatedNkTable as an optional NumericCarrier of per-sample one-sigma arrays (the brief's 'optional per-sample sigma-n / sigma-k arrays'); tryCreate sets None, so every existing table, number and hash is unchanged, and no committed entry is tabulated (the built-ins' dispersive axes are step 8's published laws). The physics inside a payload is bound by the serializer (step 30), so no schema changes.\n2. PTB's file format was verified on 2026-11-04 at github.com/PTB-SR/ocdb (branch master; ocdb/db/data/<name>.txt; '# n = (1-delta) - (i*beta)'; 3-sigma lower and upper bounds as absolute values; ocdb/db/COPYING: the data files are CC BY 4.0). n = 1 - delta and k = beta (the engine's n + ik with k >= 0); one sigma = (HB - LB) / (2 x level), the level read from the file's '<k>-sigma' comment. Asymmetric bounds are reduced to that half-width, the brief asking for sigma arrays.\n3. The PTB snapshot is the repository archive (master.zip) restricted to ocdb/db/COPYING and ocdb/db/data/*.txt; there is no index file, so the catalog is the record files in ordinal order, hit '<stem> (PTB OCDB)'. Attribution comes for free from S3.3's CC-BY rule with citation 'PTB Optical Constants Database (OCDB), ocdb/db/data/<record>: <the record's first comment line>'.\n4. The snapshot body of S13.1's refractiveindex.info adapter MOVES into private SourceSnapshotLayout / SourceArchiveSpec members that all three adapters call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'); S13.1's facts keep their assertions.\n5. Henke: CXRO's per-element files (henke.lbl.gov/optical_constants/sf/<symbol>.nff, H to U, verified 2026-11-04) are the snapshot, fetched one file per element through S13.1's one HTTP seam (no tar.gz reader is added; per-file progress and Cancel per element). CXRO's relation n = 1 - r0 lambda^2 sum N_q (f1 + i f2) / 2 pi gives n = 1 - delta, k = beta; r0 (CODATA 2018) and N_A (exact) are written once; lambda goes through the Units seam's eV relation, so no photon-energy constant is re-transcribed. The element table (92 symbols with IUPAC 2021 abridged standard atomic weights, bracketed mass numbers for the eight without one) is physical-constant code, not a library seed. Formulas are element symbols with optional counts; parentheses, isotopes and charges are refused.\n6. The Henke source has no catalog: its search parses the query as '<formula> <density in g/cm3>' and answers the one compound, its record '<formula>@<density>'; a query that names none is SourceRecordUnreadableErr whose reason says 'write a chemical formula and a density in g/cm³, for example SiO2 2.2', which the Online sources window shows as its error (no view change). recordHash = SHA-256 of the record text followed by the element files, so an update that changes an element's factors mints a new version through step 444's rule. CXRO states no licence: the licence is the SPDX-form 'LicenseRef-CXRO' (shown by name, S3.3 cites only CC-BY) and the citation names Henke, Gullikson and Davis 1993 and CXRO.\n7. Pulled PTB and Henke tables are filed under CategoryIds.semiconductor, the category the tabulated refractiveindex.info import files (MaterialImport.fs:502); the user re-files them.\n8. 'A study that opens such a material (S11.1) takes sigma as its components' prior' required opening tabulated materials, which step 361 had excluded ('A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec'). Following 001 §N ('a material complexity ... publishes its ParameterAxis list') and 001 §D, a single isotropic tabulated segment now opens; every other complexity is still refused. The working copy keeps ONE list (OpenedMaterial with physics : OpenedMaterialPhysics) so every reader of opened materials and their parameters (libraryReferences, unknownsWith, the layout, SetOpenedMaterialParameter, EditStudyParameter, the unknowns table, fit-run parameters, promotion subjects) reads table components unchanged, and the S11.3 residual's prior rows weigh them. Components are row<i>.n and row<i>.k, opened Known as S11.1 opens crystal components; a component freed without a prior takes { centre = the opened value; sigma = its source sigma } (sigma > 0), an explicit prior is kept. A promoted fitted table drops the source uncertainty (its uncertainty is the fit run's). The forward model solves a stack of an opened table with the working table at every wavelength; an observation of a table plate is ObservationPlateErr as before. This departs from .spec-md §7's 'the committed kits are created in S12 after the shapes settle': OpenedMaterial's serialized key changes from crystal to physics, so step 460 rewrites data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/AbsorbingTriclinic.study-json (AT-1's QZ-LR opens no material and keeps its bytes) and runs kit-acceptance; no migration is needed because nothing is released.\n9. The Planner (S14) reads PTB sigma from the opened copies' priors and the tables' uncertaintyOpt; no planner-specific member is added here (S14's work).\n10. AGF formulas follow OpticSim.jl's evaluation (src/GlassCat/utilities.jl, verified 2026-11-04) and are rewritten term for term as refractiveindex.info formulas (1 Schott -> 3; 2/6/11 Sellmeier 1/3/5 -> 2; 3 Herzberger -> 7; 4 Sellmeier 2 -> 1; 5 Conrady -> 5; 7/8 Handbook of Optics -> 4; 9 Sellmeier 4 -> 2; 10/12/13 Extended -> 3), then lowered by the unchanged lowerFormulaAxis, so no second formula engine exists. Conrady's lambda^-3.5 is refused by the lowering itself (no finite term sum). A catalogue holding a glass that does not lower is refused whole, naming every such glass, so nothing imports silently in part; the decision table and dialog have no channel for skipped rows.\n11. AGF files are decoded by byte-order mark (UTF-16 LE/BE, UTF-8), else UTF-16 LE when one of the first two bytes is zero, else UTF-8; AGF prevalence of UTF-16 was not verified, so both are read.\n12. 'Imported-from-file provenance' is a new EntryProvenance case, FileImportProvenance { file (leaf name); fileHash }, step 405's precedent (no existing case fits); database kind 7; no attribution.\n13. A glass catalogue imports through the one import path (decideDroppedFiles + the import dialog, identify -> confirm), each glass a version-1 entry under a minted id and DroppedFileOrigin; a second drop of the same file collides by name (side by side by default) rather than deduplicating, because identity is GUID + version + hash, never the name. The Materials window gains 'Import glass catalogue…' (open dialog, *.agf) whose message is answered as a drop of the file; dropping a .agf on the Materials or Library window works through the same decideDroppedFiles.\n14. Contract effects follow S13.1's practice: new symbols and cases are creates; no change_shape / retire is declared on symbols of earlier steps absent from today's inventory (S13.1 note 14). OpenedMaterial.crystal, currentCrystal, crystalOf and ExperimentAssignment.crystals are replaced in step 460, their consumers named in its how_to.\n15. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates', the brief and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s132/seam.json, seam.csv). Departures: unit-tests on 453 (Dispersion.fs is in its applies_to; the brief's gate list omits it); kit-acceptance on 460 (it touches the study code, KitAcceptanceTests.fs and data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy); not adopted from seam-plan: kit-acceptance on 459 (it edits OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests only for AppContextTests), whole-suite ui-tests on 460 (only StudyViewTests is touched outside the kit-acceptance file), and constructor-unit-tests by class (the suite is light and runs whole).\n\nValidation (ASG tools from C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator; scripts and logs in specs/0050/.artifacts/s132/):\n- executability check on the staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step and the kit-acceptance suite seeded into a copied inventory: passed with no findings after the placeholder's gates were bound; step_compiler check_spec reports nothing on the wired copy and, on the unwired copy, only the mid-campaign 'final step' SELECTION_REQUIRED note for step 464 (kit-acceptance, unit-tests), which the next sections make non-final.\n- Unseeded: only DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN for kit-acceptance (steps 421-440 as before, and 460).\n- Negative probe: MaterialSourceStoreTests.fs removed from step 457's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its five facts.\n- The real .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json are byte-identical to the validated staged copy; pre-existing lines unchanged; LF only.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (unchanged from S12.1, S12.2 and S13.1, needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite, so steps 421-440 and now 460 fail 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN.\n\nNote for the S14 mappers: PTB sigma reaches the Planner as (a) TabulatedNkTable.uncertaintyOpt on a tabulated material (step 453) and (b) the ParameterPrior of an opened table component freed in a study (step 460); opened copies are OpenedMaterial.physics (OpenedCrystalPhysics c | OpenedTablePhysics t), crystalOpt reads the crystal.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S14.1 (The Measurement Planner: kit inputs and the structural layer): appended steps 465-475 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (34 obligations S141-*: 11 step obligations, S141-BUILD, S141-ELEVATION and the twenty-one S141-INV-* invariants; 11 acceptance bindings, 11 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 465-475 on OpticalConstructor.Domain, OpticalConstructor.Tests, BerremanTestSupport and BerremanTests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). No registered contract: layer 1 is pure Domain logic with no proxy or IO, so every step is IMPLEMENT.\n\nStep plan (build and elevation on every step; the twenty-one s45 invariants on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on 465-472; unit-tests by class on 473-475):\n- 465 (Domain, Tests): new PlannerSymmetry.fs (last in Domain): ComponentCount; Anisotropy.independentIndexCount (REUSES MaterialComplexityEditor.Anisotropy as the optical class); Centrosymmetry; Gyrotropy; the 32-case PointGroup (crystal-class names, Hermann-Mauguin symbol, anisotropy, centrosymmetry, gyrotropy, orientationAngleCount, all); CrystalSymmetry; CrystalParameters.symmetry (uniaxial record: 3, 32, 4, 422, 6, 622 per its own doc; triclinic and absorbing: 1). New PlannerSymmetryTests (+3).\n- 466 (Domain, Tests): CrystalAxis (diag(1, 4, 9) marker; normalOf reads an oriented marker's eps), CrystalAxisPair, TensorComponent, CrystalComponent, CrystalParameters.components (parameterAxes names paired positionally with each record's components), SampleCut.normalAxisOpt through orientForCut, CrystalOrientation.normalAxisOpt through the layer rotation (Propagation ResolvedLayer.getLayer's rule). +3.\n- 467 (Domain, Tests): new MeasurementPlanner.fs: DetectorReach, LookTilt, AxisAspect, PlannerLook, MeasurementConfiguration.plannerLookWith, LookSight and PlannerLook.sightOf (the layer-1 rules). New PlannerReportTests (+5).\n- 468 (Domain, Tests): UnseenReason (+ text), TargetSight, CrystalParameters.targetSightOf, CrystalParameters.snellCap (internalAngle of the smallest principal index at IncidenceAngle.maxValue). +3.\n- 469 (Domain, Tests): SampleCut.plateText, PlannerRemedy, TargetFinding, OffAxisCutNeed, PlannerFinding (text), RecoverabilityReport, PlannerError.UnknownPlannerTargetErr, CrystalParameters.structuralReport. +4.\n- 470 (Domain, Tests): PlannerSource, OpticRole, PlannerOptic, DetectorRecording, PlannerDetector (with its NoiseParam), LabProfile.ofItems / reachOf / reaches, PlannerError.UnresolvedPlannerItemErr. New PlannerInputsTests (+3).\n- 471 (Domain, Tests): PlannerPlate, PlannerPrior, PlannerInputs, Study.plannerInputsWith (StudyContext, choiceOf, material version), PlannerError.UnopenedPlannerMaterialErr / NonCrystalPlannerMaterialErr. +3.\n- 472 (Domain, Tests): PlannerInputs.looks and PlannerInputs.structuralReport. +3.\n- 473 (BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): MOVE MuellerInverseTests' quartz ground truth and its C1-C4 design (waveLength .. fullConfigurations, with both banners) into new BerremanTestSupport/QuartzSample.fs. unit-tests: BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests, numbers unchanged.\n- 474 (BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): MOVE BiaxialInverseTests' design (plate, configuration, principalCuts, b1-b3, fullConfigurations, and the ablation fact's local normalOn as normalIncidenceOn) into new BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialDesign.fs; b1 = principalCuts |> List.collect normalIncidenceOn (same twelve configurations, the azimuth list written once). unit-tests: BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests (about 997 s), numbers unchanged.\n- 475 (BerremanTests): new class BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests (+4): C1 blind to g33 with n_o, n_e, g33 unrecoverable and the x-cut proposed (with an off-axis-cut finding); c1 @ c3 and the full C1-C4 set leave nothing; the normal z-cut biaxial design flags n3, g33, g23, g13, g12 with oblique incidence AND further cuts (x, y) as the remedy; z+x and every-cut-normal (b1) flag exactly g23, g13, g12 with the tilt alone; the full biaxial set leaves nothing. No forward solve, no fit: designs are read through plannerLookWith FullMuellerReach.\n\nInterpretations and decisions recorded (the brief is binding; these resolve what it leaves open):\n1. Convention. The layer-1 rules speak the parameterization the study engine fits, the engine's bi-anisotropic rho (MuellerInverse.fs module header: along z the TRANSVERSE gyration acts, g33 does not). 001 §M's 'a c-cut at normal incidence sees n_o only (and g33)' is the crystallographic reading; the acceptance fact the Planner must reproduce is 'C1 is completely blind to g33', so the engine convention governs. Consequently MuellerInverse.gyrationProjection (the crystallographic G(theta), which its own doc says is deliberately not used to predict this engine) is NOT called; the brief's other two reuses are kept: internalAngle gives the Snell cap (468) and orientForCut gives the axis a cut puts on the plate normal (466).\n2. The rules are first order (what a look's normalized reading depends on linearly): the transverse rule for indices, gyration diagonals and absorption; an index at normal incidence needs two distinct transverse indices (linear retardance) under a non-intensity reach, otherwise an oblique look; gyration needs FullMuellerReach; an off-diagonal gyration component needs an oblique look on a principal cut (BiaxialInverseTests measured this); an absorption off-diagonal needs both axes transverse. So C1's n_o is unrecoverable by layer 1 although MuellerInverseTests measures a ~700x weaker second-order multiple-reflection sensitivity: '3 of 4 unrecoverable' is the fact's own wording, and the weak channel is layer 2's to quantify.\n3. Point groups: the 18 gyrotropic classes are those of 001's source (specs/0046/.manual/018 cites arXiv 2003.10872): 1, 2, m, 222, mm2, 4, -4, 422, 4mm, -42m, 3, 32, 3m, 6, 622, 6mm, 23, 432; -6, -6m2 and -43m are the non-gyrotropic acentric classes. Orientation angles: triclinic 3, monoclinic 1. Nothing stores a point group: 001's prior is 'material class or point group', and the kit's material class is its crystal record, whose point groups the report states (uniaxial record 3/32/4/422/6/622 from its doc; triclinic records class 1).\n4. A plate's cut is its substrate layer's CrystalOrientation (the kit's one statement of how the crystal sits in the plate): PrimaryAxes is a z-cut; an EulerRotation is classified by rotating the marker exactly as the system builder rotates a layer; a plate with no principal axis on its normal has every axis transverse, so layer 1 never calls a component unseen through it (layer 2 measures it). AT-2's committed kit keeps one PrimaryAxes sample and carries each cut on its observation rows, so read as a kit its plates are z-cuts; the S14.2 acceptance over AT-2 is design-level.\n5. The lab's angle range is the table's (normal incidence to IncidenceAngle.maxValue, 89 degrees): no item model publishes an angle limit (step 215). So a real kit's z-cut-only inventory yields the off-axis-cut finding (a tilt reaches the axis at most snellCap off the normal: 40.4 degrees for quartz), and 'never' findings come from reach (no full-Mueller reach for gyration) or from having no plate.\n6. Reach: polarimeter -> FullMuellerReach; ellipsometer -> EllipsometricReach; an intensity detector -> FullMuellerReach (the HAUP class, a polarizer and an analyzer) when the kit holds two or more polarizing optics (polarizer presets, real polarizers, compounds containing one), else IntensityOnlyReach.\n7. Targets are the study's unknown components of the opened crystal (Study.unknownsWith, so link followers drop out); known and calibrated components are prior. Item unknowns (retardances, gains) are not crystal components and are layer 2's. A tabulated opened material is NonCrystalPlannerMaterialErr (001 §M targets gyrotropic crystals).\n8. Inputs take StudyContext + choiceOf (the two fields of StudyForwardContext layer 1 needs), so layer 1 needs no data proxy or solver; S14.2 can pass context.kit and context.choiceOf.\n9. Designs move whole (C1-C4 is one table; B1-B3 likewise) into BerremanTestSupport as QuartzSample and BiaxialDesign; the Planner facts name each by module because configuration, fullConfigurations and the plates share names.\n10. Remedies: a missing principal cut that would see the target at normal incidence (uniaxial candidates z and x only, a y-cut duplicating the x-cut per MuellerInverse.SampleCut's doc); a tilt (with the cap); a full-Mueller reach. Off-diagonal gyration gets the tilt alone ('cutting more plates does not substitute for tilting them'). Finding texts format angles with one decimal under InvariantCulture.\n11. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates', the brief and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s141/seam.json, seam.csv). Departures from seam-plan: constructor-unit-tests runs whole (light, 13 s) rather than by class on 465/467/470; unit-tests on 475 selects only BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests (seam-plan lists every class because the step edits BerremanTests.fsproj; adding one compile line changes no other class; the brief names the new class). seam-plan proposes no kit-acceptance for 473/474 and none is added (KitAcceptanceTests reads neither new module).\n\nValidation (ASG tools from C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator; scripts and logs in specs/0050/.artifacts/s141/):\n- executability check on the staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step: no finding on steps 465-475; unseeded, the only findings are the pre-existing DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN for kit-acceptance (steps 421-440, 460 and the placeholder).\n- Seeded (an empty kit-acceptance suite injected into a COPIED inventory, staging only): 'executability check' passed with no findings after the placeholder's gates were bound; step_compiler check_spec reports nothing on the wired copy and, on the unwired copy, only the mid-campaign 'final step must WIRE' note for step 475, which the Close section supplies.\n- Negative probe: PlannerInputsTests.fs removed from step 472's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its three facts.\n- The real .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json are byte-identical to the validated staged copy; pre-existing lines unchanged; LF only.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (unchanged from S12.1-S13.2, needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite, so steps 421-440 and 460 fail 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN.\n\nNote for the S14.2 mapper: layer 2 builds on PlannerInputs (lab with each detector's NoiseParam, sources with lambda and tunable limits, plates, prior = the opened copy with its priors and PTB sigma, targets), PlannerLook / MeasurementConfiguration.plannerLookWith, RecoverabilityReport and PlannerError (extend it); the facts class is BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests; QuartzSample holds C1-C4 and fullConfigurations (perturbedStart, scalingAround and the noisy-ensemble helpers are still MuellerInverseTests class bindings, to move if a layer-2 fact needs them); BiaxialDesign holds B1-B3 and normalIncidenceOn.\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper S14.2 (The Planner's numerical layer, the plan, the cache and the Plan view): appended steps 476-492 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (40 obligations S142-*: 17 step obligations, S142-BUILD, S142-ELEVATION and the twenty-one S142-INV-* invariants; 17 acceptance bindings, 17 behavior seams, 1 closing scope over steps 476-492 on Domain, Optimization, Storage, Ui, Controls, App, OpticalConstructor.Tests, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests, BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests and AGENTS.md). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). No registered contract: the Planner adds fields to the existing KitProxy (STORE_BigBoy_0004) and no new proxy, so steps 476-491 are IMPLEMENT and 492 is WIRE_UI.\n\nStep plan (build and elevation on every step; the twenty-one s46 invariants on every step; constructor-unit-tests whole (light) on every step touching OpticalConstructor code; ui-smoke whole (light) on every step touching Ui / Ui.Tests / App; ui-tests and unit-tests by class):\n- 476 (Optimization + FitResultsTests, StudyEngineTests): reuse seams, each a MOVE with numbers unchanged: FitQuality.covarianceMatrix -> public covarianceOf (reportFrom calls it); FittedProblem's offset frame -> ScaledVector.offsetResidualOf / offsetOrigin / offsetJacobianOf (jacobian and report call them); disturb's angle shift -> MeasurementConfiguration.misalignedBy (draw order kept); scaledProblemWith's unit -> ParameterInterval.searchUnit. +2 constructor facts. unit-tests: MuellerInverseTests; kit-acceptance: KitAcceptanceTests.\n- 477 (Domain, Optimization, Tests): NoiseVariance, CandidateRows, PlannerError.NoiselessPlannerCandidateErr / PlannerShapeErr; new PlannerInformation.fs (last in Optimization): SingularValue, SingularSpectrum (NumericCarrier; ofRows marked InteropBoundary over MathNet Svd(true)), SingularDirection (text), InformationLogDeterminant, CovarianceTrace, TargetBound, PlannerInformation (over: rows scaled to the first candidate's noise; rank via ResidualJacobian.rank; confounded / weakest directions; conditionOpt; scaledSigmasOpt = sqrt diag FitQuality.covarianceOf at the reference noise; logDeterminant; traceOpt; boundsOver a scaling), ReducedChiSquared.noiseVariance. New PlannerInformationTests (+4).\n- 478 (Optimization, Tests): PlanCriterion (D / target-restricted A), PlanOption, RankedOption, PlannerInformation.rankWith (greedy: rank, then log det or trace at full rank; ties keep order). +3.\n- 479 (Optimization, Tests): NoiseParam.noiseVarianceOver (mean over the throughput residual's entries of element^2/3 or throughput^2/3 plus rotation^2/3 times the entry's squared sensitivity to the configuration's incidence and azimuth, through misalignedBy and the offset frame) and candidateRowsOver (offset-frame Jacobian of throughputResidualFor over noiseless observations at the nominal point, with that noise). +2.\n- 480 (BerremanTestSupport, BerremanTests): MOVE MuellerInverseTests' solverParameters, forward, scalingAround (as quartzScalingAround), blindStart, wideBox, noisyObserve (as noisyQuartzObservations) and recoverFromNoisy (as recoverQuartzFromNoisy, Result) into QuartzSample, and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests' forward / recoverFromNoisy into AbsorbingBiaxialSample (absorbingForward, recoverAbsorbingFromNoisy). unit-tests: MuellerInverseTests, AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests, numbers unchanged.\n- 481 (BerremanTests): MeasurementPlannerTests +3: full C1-C4 rank 4 with every constant bounded and C1 alone rank 2 with exactly n_e and g33 confounded; for one noisy quartz fit and one noisy AT-2 fit, the planner's bounds over the fit's own Jacobian at its reduced chi-squared equal predictedRelativeErrors within 1e-12 relative. unit-tests: MeasurementPlannerTests.\n- 482 (Domain, Tests): PlanCandidate (source x principal-cut plate x emitted observable; incidenceRange 0-60 deg / 4, azimuthRange 0-67.5 deg / 4; capture; caption), PlanCoverage + coverageIn, PlannerInputs.polarimeterOpt / unplacedPlates / candidates. PlannerInputsTests +2.\n- 483 (Domain, Tests): InstrumentChoice, InstrumentFinding, PlannerInputs.instrumentFindingsWith (polarizer x compensator through the item evaluator; four 15-degree grid angles of least 4x4 generator condition; 16x16 designRow instrument matrix conditionNumber; CompensatorMissingFinding; compounds unpaired), PlannerError.InstrumentEvaluationErr. +3.\n- 484 (Domain, Storage, Tests): KitRelativePath.plannerCacheFolder; KitProxy.readPlannerCacheFile / writePlannerCacheFile (FileName directly under .oc/planner; read-only view refuses the write); in-memory and folder. KitProxyTests +2, KitProxyFolderTests +2.\n- 485 (Domain, Storage, Tests): PlannerCacheKey (source, plate, detector items, observable, opened material, targets), PlannerCacheEntry, PlannerInputs.cacheKeyWith, PlannerError.PlannerCacheErr; new Storage PlannerCacheStore.fs (after KitContentFiles.fs): cacheFileName = contentHashOf(nodeOf key).candidate-json, fileText / parsePlannerCacheEntry (no schema, the lock's rule), KitContext.cachedPlannerRows (hit without computing; miss computed and written under ReadWriteKitAccess only). New PlannerCacheTests (+5).\n- 486 (Domain, Optimization, Tests): new PlannerRuns.fs: PlanCandidateCount, PlanProgress, PlanObserver, PlanCandidate.configurations, PlannerInputs.scalingWith / forwardWith / candidateRowsWith / priorRows, PlanStanding, RankedPlanStep, PlanReport, PlannerInputs.planWith (structural report, instrument findings, coverage, per-candidate progress and Cancel, baseline = priors + in-kit candidates, rankWith); PlannerError.PlanCancelledErr / PlannerForwardErr. New PlanRunTests (+5, one proving a new plate computes only its own candidates through the cache).\n- 487 (Domain, Ui, Tests): new Ui PlanJob.fs (after StudyFitJob.fs): PlanJobHandle, PlanJobHost (posting / onUiThread / inert; JobProgress with a known total per candidate), PlanJobState, PlanRequest, PlanMsg (RunPlan, CancelPlan, PlanProgressed, PlanEnded), PlanEnvironment.create (plannerInputsWith, planWith, rows through cachedPlannerRows), PlanMsg.updateWith; PlannerError.PlanRaisedErr / UnknownPlannerStudyErr. New PlanJobTests (+5).\n- 488 (Ui, Tests): KitWindowShell.planRuns, PlanSurfaceState, model planJob / planSurface / planMaterials / planMaterialOpt / planReportOpt, messages StudyPlan of PlanMsg (not refused read-only: it writes no kit file and no cache read-only), SetPlanMaterial, SetPlanCriterion. New PlanWindowModelTests (+3).\n- 489 (Ui, Tests): GenerateSetupGrid's body becomes a private function taking the grid, the collection and the role; AddPlannedExperiment (read-only guarded) records the candidate's plate in the table's Object 1 slot as a setup and a PlannedRun experiment whose one block sweeps R2 then R1 (draft built by chooseElement / setRange / addScanAxis / chooseMeasurement), refusing an in-kit candidate, an uncaptured branch or a table with no sample slot. PlanWindowModelTests +3.\n- 490 (Controls, Ui, Tests, Ui.Tests): ConstructorFlowStep.PlanFlowStep between Unknowns and Fit (Inverse only); fourteen ConstructorUiIds (PlanRunButton among them) and planMaterialChoice; new PlanView.fs (after StudyUnknownsView.fs): materials, criteria, Run plan / Cancel on one row with a determinate per-candidate progress bar, error, and the report's findings, rank text, confounded combinations, bounds grid and instrument lines; KitWindowView; TestAppScope.planKitOver / planKitIn. New PlanViewTests (ui-tests +2, ui-smoke +1); ScrollExtentTests +1; KitWindowTests and KitWindowModelTests flow-strip facts changed. ui-tests: KitWindowTests, PlanViewTests, ScrollExtentTests.\n- 491 (Controls, Ui, Ui.Tests): planCandidateList, planCandidateRow, addPlanCandidateButton; the ranked candidates with rank, log det or trace and bounds, Add to kit while writes are offered and the candidate is not in the kit, else 'In the kit as <name>'. PlanViewTests ui-tests +1, ui-smoke +1. ui-tests: KitWindowTests, PlanViewTests, ScrollExtentTests.\n- 492 WIRE_UI (App, Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md): Program.fs ConstructorScene.mount composes planRuns = PlanJobHost.onUiThread; AGENTS.md's gotcha 'The Inverse flow ends at the study' lists Unknowns -> Plan -> Fit and names the Planner's files, its .oc/planner/ cache and Add to kit's PlannedRun experiments; KitWindowTests ui-smoke acceptance runs a plan in a shown Inverse window over a real kit folder (two candidate files cached). ui-tests: KitWindowTests.\n\nInterpretations and decisions recorded (the brief is binding; these resolve what it leaves open):\n1. CRB = covariance account. The information is F = sum J_i^T J_i / sigma_i^2; rows are kept scaled to one reference noise (the first candidate's), so the bound is FitQuality.covarianceOf of those rows at that noise as its reduced chi-squared: by construction the covariance a fit of those candidates reports at that residual level. The brief's 'bounds equal predictedRelativeErrors' is therefore asserted exactly (1e-12) by running the planner over a noisy fit's own Jacobian at its solution with the fit's reduced chi-squared as the noise; the noise-model path is proven in constructor tests (stub forward). No new inverse-physics claim (001 §W): the planner-before-measuring agreement with the ensemble is not asserted as a new band.\n2. Noise. The bench model is uniform max errors (variance u^2/3); a candidate's homoscedastic noise is the linearised expected mean square of its throughput-residual entries: element / throughput reading variances plus the rotation budget turned through each entry's sensitivity to its configuration's incidence and azimuth (the misalignment disturb draws). Deterministic: no simulation seed.\n3. Jacobians use step 397's offset frame (moved to ScaledVector members) so a component at zero is differentiable; the acceptance equality uses the fit's own raw-rule Jacobian so it is bit-exact.\n4. Candidates are AT-2-shaped experiments: one plate (Object 1), one Mueller polarimeter's budget (the lab's first), one branch the plate emits, one source line, R2 over 0/20/40/60 deg x R1 over 0/22.5/45/67.5 deg (the spec 0044 designs' A2 incidences with normal incidence and A1 azimuths), constants not settings. Only Mueller polarimeters read candidates (the bench model defines Mueller readings; layer 1 shows gyration needs a full Mueller reach); intensity (HAUP) labs get the instrument-matrix findings instead.\n5. A plate whose orientation puts no principal axis on its normal has no candidate (the observation forward places plates by SampleCut, step 375) and is named in the report; this departs from step 467's note that layer 2 measures such a plate.\n6. Layer-2 coordinates are the study's targets (the opened crystal's unknown components, step 471); item unknowns are not coordinates of these candidates (their observation rows depend on the crystal alone). Baseline = the targets' priors plus every candidate a kit experiment already holds (coverageIn), so the ranking proposes the next experiment; CRBs are reported only at full rank, otherwise the rank and the confounded combinations say what is missing.\n7. Cache: one entry per (sample, experiment) candidate, keyed by its own items with their parameter states, its branch, the opened material (nominal point and bounds) and the targets; file .oc/planner/<sha256>.candidate-json; the entry keeps its key so a stale or colliding file is a miss; no schema (cache, the lock's rule); written only under ReadWriteKitAccess; never sent (step 196/198 already exclude .oc/).\n8. Instrument matrix: polarizer x compensator pairs evaluated by the item evaluator; four compensator angles from a 15-degree grid minimising the 4x4 generator condition; the 16x16 designRow stack's conditionNumber reported; compounds (a CPL turning as one piece) are not paired.\n9. RunPlan writes no kit file, so it is not read-only guarded; Add to kit is. Add to kit reuses GenerateSetupGrid's recording body and the draft's own functions; an added planned experiment is removed through the Experiments bay (no separate undo). The window message is StudyPlan of PlanMsg (two-word case, as StudyFit).\n10. Gates follow .user-md 'Choosing a step's gates', the brief and executability seam-plan (specs/0050/.artifacts/s142/seam.json, seam.csv). Departures from seam-plan: 476 keeps unit-tests (MuellerInverseTests) and kit-acceptance (KitAcceptanceTests) because it refactors code the study fits, AT-2's data and the noisy ensemble run (seam-plan proposed only build and elevation, no test file being edited); constructor-unit-tests runs whole (light, 13 s) where seam-plan listed classes; 490 / 491 do not run kit-acceptance (seam-plan proposed it because TestAppScope / the Ui.Tests project change; nothing KitAcceptanceTests reads changes) and select ui-tests KitWindowTests, PlanViewTests and ScrollExtentTests rather than every class using TestAppScope; 480 runs no kit-acceptance (it adds declarations to AbsorbingBiaxialSample, which a build catches; no behaviour changes); 492 is not the spec's final step, so it does not take seam-plan's final-step whole-suite set.\n\nValidation (ASG tools from C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator; scripts and logs in specs/0050/.artifacts/s142/):\n- executability check on the staged copy with a placeholder final WIRE step: on steps 476-492 the only unseeded finding is DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN for kit-acceptance on step 476 (the known gap, as for 421-440 and 460).\n- Seeded (an empty kit-acceptance suite injected into a COPIED inventory, staging only): 'executability check' passed with no findings; step_compiler check_spec reports nothing on the wired copy; on the unwired copy its only note is the mid-campaign final-step rule (step 492 would need explicit unit-tests / kit-acceptance selections as the spec's last step), which the Close section's final step supplies.\n- Negative probe: PlannerInformationTests.fs removed from step 477's edits gives SCOPE_TEST on its facts.\n- Pointer audit: every `file:symbol` pointer to existing code resolves in the tree; symbols that only later steps create are cited by step number.\n- The real .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json are byte-identical to the validated staged copy; pre-existing lines unchanged; LF only; numbers contiguous to 492.\n\nUNRESOLVED EVIDENCE GAP (unchanged from S12.1-S14.1, needs the supervisor or operator): .repository-inventory-json has no 'kit-acceptance' suite, so steps 421-440, 460 and now 476 fail 'executability check' with DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN.\n\nNote for the Close mapper: the planner adds Optimization PlannerInformation.fs / PlannerRuns.fs, Storage PlannerCacheStore.fs, Ui PlanJob.fs / PlanView.fs and the test classes PlannerInformationTests, PlannerCacheTests, PlanRunTests, PlanJobTests, PlanWindowModelTests (constructor), PlanViewTests (Ui.Tests) and three MeasurementPlannerTests facts (BerremanTests, about 4 minutes for the two noisy fits).\n"}
{"at": "2026-11-03T15:18:31Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "decision", "content": "Mapper Close (the composition root and the whole-tree proof): appended steps 493-494 to specs/0050/.spec-jsonl and extended specs/0050/.execution-contract-json (28 obligations CLOSE-*: CLOSE-READONLY-FIXTURE, CLOSE-WIRE, CLOSE-REMOVALS, CLOSE-WHOLE-TREE, CLOSE-BUILD, CLOSE-ELEVATION, CLOSE-ELEVATION-FULL and the twenty-one CLOSE-INV-* invariants; 2 acceptance bindings, 1 behavior seam (close-wire on 494), 1 closing scope over steps 493-494 on AGENTS.md, OpticalConstructor.App, OpticalConstructor.Ui and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests). .spec-md is not edited (planner-owned). No registered contract: the closing work composes nothing new, so 493 is IMPLEMENT and 494 is the final WIRE_UI on OpticalConstructor.App.\n\nStep plan (the twenty-one s47 invariants on both steps):\n- 493 IMPLEMENT (Ui.Tests): openCommittedReadOnly and assertCommittedUnchanged (step 439) MOVE from KitAcceptanceTests into TestAppScope, public, bodies unchanged but for an owner : FolderName parameter (every TestAppScope helper takes the calling class's folder), with the recording's type and every helper only they call; a helper the AT builds also call moves with them. KitAcceptanceTests' facts of steps 429 and 439 call them from TestAppScope, assertions kept. Gates: build, elevation, kit-acceptance (selected KitAcceptanceTests), ui-smoke (all_discovered, light).\n- 494 WIRE_UI (App, Ui, Ui.Tests, AGENTS.md): the root's stale docs (Program.fs file doc first paragraph, Startup.workbenchSettings / Startup.context, AppContext.fs file doc) state the composition; AGENTS.md (Build & test test locations; Project layout notes and four lines: BerremanTestSupport, Catalogue/Builtin, OpticalConstructor.Database, data/; three gotchas after 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE': the library is data in the SQLite database, everything else lives in a kit folder, Main and Inverse open the kit start screen; the flow-strip sentence in 'Main ribbon'); WireUiFinalCompositionTests gains three ui-smoke facts: the app composed as Startup composes it over TestAppScope.fileLocations goes Launcher -> start screen -> a kit under the test output, shows every flow-strip step of the Inverse and the Main window, releases the kit on Close kit and opens Data locations; and each committed kit (OpticsMuellerKit, AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit) opens read-only from the start screen through the moved fixture, shows every Inverse step and leaves data/ unchanged. The acceptance greps the 001 §R removals (ocproj case-insensitively, and SceneProxy, ExperimentCollectionProxy, recent.json, seedAll, TestDbContext, SolverHandoffView, MuellerDataSet, MuellerDataProxy, Data/MuellerMatrix, experimentRegex, measuredElementOf). Gates: build, elevation, elevation-full, and constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, ui-tests, unit-tests and kit-acceptance all whole (all_discovered).\n\nInterpretations and decisions recorded (the brief is binding; these resolve what it leaves open):\n1. Two steps, inside the brief's 2-5. AGENTS.md rides the final WIRE_UI (as steps 419 and 492 carried theirs): a separate AGENTS.md-only step would edit no compiled file, run no gate but the invariants, and leave its obligation without an executable check, which profile 1 refuses.\n2. The final step changes no code in Program.fs or AppContext.fs. Every composition the brief lists is wired by the step that introduced it (steps 83, 88, 89, 100, 180, 189, 191, 195, 210, 239, 323, 414-419, 490-492); the WIRE_UI rewrites the two files' stale spec-0038 docs (verified today at Program.fs:1-6, :37-47, :50-58 and AppContext.fs:1-9) and proves the composition headless.\n3. Opening the committed kits 'from the start screen READ-ONLY': the real KitStartWindow offers Open read-only only after a KitLockedErr, which would need a lock written into data/. The facts therefore send OpenKitReadOnly through the start screen's update, as AT-1 / AT-2 do (step 429, .spec-md §3.12), through the fixture step 493 moves into TestAppScope (KitAcceptanceTests.fs compiles after WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:233; reuse is a move, never a copy), and mount the Inverse model in kitWindowView as step 312's facts do.\n4. The 'Experiments-bay note': step 328 already moved Attach data file... out of the bay in the 'Main ribbon' gotcha; this step adds the one fact still missing there, the flow strip (Experiments is the bay; Data and the study's steps are the Inverse window's alone, ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf).\n5. The final step also runs the scoped elevation gate: its applies_to covers the edited .fs files, so the gate plan includes it beside elevation-full; it is declared and bound (CLOSE-ELEVATION) rather than left implicit.\n6. ui-tests is not run at 493: the seam plan proposes it with no class, because 493 only adds public fixture functions to TestAppScope and edits KitAcceptanceTests, whose trait ui-tests excludes; no ui-tests fact changes.\n7. The removal grep uses ocproj case-insensitively over Berreman/ (the s47-t4-no-ocproj form, widened from OpticalConstructor/ to Berreman/, which holds no ocproj outside OpticalConstructor today) so .ocproj and the ProjectFile aggregate's names are both covered.\n\nValidation: python -m ai_strategy_generator.executability check and step_compiler check_spec report no finding for steps 493-494 except DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN [kit-acceptance] ('selector needs a suite with known test discovery'). That finding is pre-existing on steps 421-440, 460 and 476: specs/0050/.repository-inventory-json holds no kit-acceptance suite (only unit-tests, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests), because the gate's requires_path, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs, is created by step 421 and does not exist in the tree yet. Resolving it needs a test census of that suite once the file exists, and the inventory is outside the spec author's write scope; it is an unresolved evidence gap, not a spec defect, and no gate, test or oracle was weakened for it.\n"}
