{"at": "2026-11-04T20:50:22Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "input", "content": "[auto-loop 1/10]\n\nThe claim-check report flagged 45 item(s) that MUST be fixed before handoff. Apply the following edits to .spec-md:\n\n1. §0.1, .spec-md line 17 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs` — `DispersionModel.toEpsAxis` | The transcendental models lower to the new data case. Their evaluation kernels move into the core. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs does not exist. The actual file is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:686 (DispersionModel.toEpsAxis); :766-769 lowers TaucLorentz, GaussianOscillator, ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann through EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate. The symbols and four-model baseline exist at that different path.\n2. §0.1, .spec-md line 18 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs` — `MaterialEntry`, `builtInEntries`, `standardCategories`, `tryFindCategory` | `complexity` becomes mandatory and `properties` is derived from it. The seed values are deleted. Category names resolve through the category store. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs declares standardCategories at :146, tryFindCategory at :158, MaterialEntry at :260 and builtInEntries at :497; :266-267 has properties and optional complexity. The existing declarations resolve only after adding the omitted directory prefix.\n3. §0.1, .spec-md line 19 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs` — module `Library` | Presets carry frozen GUID ids. `SeedSamples`, `SeedSources`, `seedEntries`, `seedTrees` and the self-seeding `createInMemory` are deleted. The grouping tree is derived from the entries. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs declares module Library at :19, SeedSamples at :651, SeedSources at :812, seedEntries at :884, seedTrees at :904 and createInMemory at :970-972, which closes over seedEntries and seedTrees.\n4. §0.1, .spec-md line 20 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs` — `VersionsInUse`, `decideVersioning` | `VersionsInUse` is replaced by a one-way per-version pin. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs does not exist. The actual declarations are Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs:52 (VersionsInUse) and :120 (decideVersioning). A future pin replacement is not evidence of an existing pin.\n5. §0.1, .spec-md line 21 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs`, `SampleStore.fs` | The in-memory stores keep their shapes, read the pin and stop self-seeding. They remain the test doubles. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Neither OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs nor SampleStore.fs resolves from the repository root. Their actual files are under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/: MaterialStore.fs:191-195 seeds builtInEntries and SampleStore.fs:186-187 seeds SeedSamples.allSeedSamples; both accept VersionsInUse. These substantiate the in-memory, self-seeding baseline at corrected paths, not the proposed pin implementation.\n6. §0.1, .spec-md line 22 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Seeding/` | Deleted. `SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` move to Domain as `CatalogueImport`. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Seeding/ directory does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding/ contains OpticalConstructor.Seeding.fsproj and Seeding.fs; the latter declares SeedingProxy at :46 and its seedAll member at :59-67. CatalogueImport is a declared future replacement.\n7. §0.1, .spec-md line 23 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Database/` (C#) | The `Test` entity, `TestDbContext` and the initial migration are replaced by the library model, created by `EnsureCreated` and stamped with a schema version. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Database/ directory does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/ contains Test.cs:8 (class Test), TestDbContext.cs:14-29 (the context and its Test entity mapping), and Migrations/20260711000000_Initial.cs:19 (CreateTable). EnsureCreated and the schema stamp are proposed changes.\n8. §0.1, .spec-md line 24 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs`, `ProjectFile.fs`, `SchemaValidation.fs`, `RecentFiles.fs`, `Domain/Project.fs` | The shared serializer options move to a canonical-JSON module and validation becomes per kind. The `.ocproj` aggregate, `recent.json` and `Autosave` are deleted. `RecentFiles.bump` moves into the kit history. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The paths as written do not resolve from the repository root. Under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/, ProjectJson.fs:131 defines options, ProjectFile.fs:19-42 defines .ocproj save/open, SchemaValidation.fs:64 defines validate, and RecentFiles.fs:36, :41 and :77 defines recent.json, bump and Autosave. The aggregate is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Project.fs:26 (OpticalConstructorProject), not Domain/Project.fs.\n9. §0.1, .spec-md line 25 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` | Tabulated imports produce the tabulated case. The importer is reused as the refractiveindex.info record parser. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:158 defines buildTabulatedClosure and :183-194 defines entryFromTabulated with complexity = None; :502 and :544 call it for refractiveindex.info and CSV imports. The proposed table data case is future behavior.\n10. §0.1, .spec-md line 26 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs` | `DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv` stays as the \"Phone ROI CSV\" import profile. The archive store is deleted. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs:106 declares DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv, and :151-199 contains the archive dataset resolution/read path that invokes this parser. The retained parser exists at the corrected path.\n11. §0.1, .spec-md line 27 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs` | `MuellerDataSet`, `MuellerArchivePath`, `MuellerDataProxy`, `experimentRegex`, `objectRegex` and `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` are deleted. `familyGain` becomes the first gain-model implementation. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs declares MuellerDataSet at :360, MuellerArchivePath at :371, MuellerDataProxy at :400, experimentRegex at :504, objectRegex at :508, MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed at :516 and familyGain at :859.\n12. §0.1, .spec-md line 28 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs` | Receives the parameter-record builders promoted from `BerremanTests` (§3.16). |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs does not exist. The real module is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs:62. Builder sources do exist in Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs:98 (buildTriclinic) and AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:73 (buildAbsorbing); their promotion is future work.\n13. §0.1, .spec-md line 29 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs` | The run law folds any number of objects through each item's Mueller matrix. The source is a real Stokes state. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs:24-44 declares RunStep and detectorStokes. The current fold applies every SampleStep matrix and starts from unpolarizedStokes, with special handling of the first preparatory polarizer. The proposed item/source model is future work.\n14. §0.1, .spec-md line 30 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs` | Experiments v2: setup reference, scan, role, session and data attachment. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs:225-236 declares Experiment with setup, varied, measurement, range, dataFileOpt and sourceWaveLengthOpt. The v2 fields are proposed changes, not missing current artifacts.\n15. §0.1, .spec-md line 31 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`, `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs` | The in-memory seams are deleted; `KitProxy` replaces them. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Neither OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs nor ExperimentCollectionStore.fs resolves from the repository root. The actual files under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ declare SceneProxy/createInMemory at Scene.fs:107,129 and ExperimentCollectionProxy/createInMemory at ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:73,96; both stores start as empty maps. KitProxy is a future replacement.\n16. §0.1, .spec-md line 32 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/` | Receives the bench noise model, the fit wrappers and the recovery statistics from `BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs`, the staged Mueller pipeline, the study engine and the Planner's numerical layer. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Neither OpticalConstructor.Optimization/ nor BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs resolves from the repository root. The actual project is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/, whose fsproj compiles InverseFit.fs and MuellerInverseSolver.fs. The donor is Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs:171 (NoiseParam), :230/:253 (RecoveredQuantity/RecoveryStatistics), :493/:503 (fit wrappers), :553 onward (noise functions), and :645 (statisticsFor).\n17. §0.1, .spec-md line 33 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs` — `AppContext.create` | Composes the SQLite library proxies over the configured locations and imports the catalogues on start. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs:78 declares AppContext.create; :88-108 composes in-memory library, scene and collection stores. SQLite composition and catalogue import are proposed future wiring.\n18. §0.1, .spec-md line 34 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs` | Hosts a `KitContext` in place of the scene and collection seams. `measuredElementOf` is deleted. New surfaces are hosted through messages. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1445 declares measuredElementOf; :1471-1478 uses it for captureDetectors. AppContext.fs:104,108 supplies the collection and scene proxies that the future KitContext replaces.\n19. §0.1, .spec-md line 35 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindow.fs` | Deleted. Their three checks become the study's pre-fit validation. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Neither OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs nor SolverHandoffWindow.fs resolves from the repository root. Under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/, SolverHandoffView.fs:100-116 implements the three ordered validation branches: unspecified elements, missing attachment, and load/schema/range validation. SolverHandoffWindow.fs:19,30-37 hosts that view. The existing checks are real at corrected paths.\n20. §0.1, .spec-md line 36 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `AppConfig.fs`, `appsettings.json` | Main and Inverse open the kit start screen, and the footer gains a Data locations link. New settings keys are added; the MSSQL keys are removed. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The named paths do not resolve from the repository root. Under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/, Program.fs:96,114 initializes Main/Inverse and :178 reads BuildInfo.version for the footer; AppConfig.fs:48,53,58 declares DatabaseProvider, OpticalConstructorMssql and OpticalConstructorSqlite keys. appsettings.json:1-4 exists but currently has empty appSettings and connectionStrings objects. The new start screen and settings are future changes.\n21. §0.1, .spec-md line 37 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs` — `ConstructorUiId` | One static member per new control. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The cited repo-root-relative OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs does not exist. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs:27 declares ConstructorUiId and its fixed IDs are static members (for example :275-279). The new members are prospective additions.\n22. §1, .spec-md line 59 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (Today nothing persists. Every store is in memory and is re-seeded at each start (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs:AppContext.create`).) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape claim from Today and the current composition assertion. The cited root-relative file is absent; the actual AppContext.create is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs:78. Its library stores are in memory, but not every store is seeded: SourceProxy begins empty at Domain/ElementId.fs:1101-1102, and scene/collection maps begin empty at Domain/Scene.fs:129-130 and Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:96-97 (all under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/). The literal nothing-persists statement also overreaches: AppContext.fs:109-113 composes ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder, Storage/ExperimentExportFile.fs:50-62 writes exports, and Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1350 invokes exportRun. This supports nonpersistent library/session stores, not absence of all disk output.\n23. §1, .spec-md line 59 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (No window saves or opens an `.ocproj` file (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs`).) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred current-wiring claim. OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs does not resolve from the repository root. At the corrected path Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs:24,35, FileName.saveProject/openProject exist. Searches of OpticalConstructor.Ui, OpticalConstructor.App and OpticalConstructor.TestWindows under Berreman/OpticalConstructor/ found no calls to either member, so the behavioral assertion is supported but the supplied pointer is invalid.\n24. §1, .spec-md line 59 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (The EF Core project holds one unreferenced `Test` table.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred current-artifact and numeric-count claim. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/TestDbContext.cs:21,29 contains one DbSet<Test> and maps it to Test; Migrations/20260711000000_Initial.cs:19 creates it. The unreferenced qualifier is false without a production-only restriction: Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs:77-94 constructs the context, inserts Test and queries context.Tests, and OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj:303 references the database project. No app consumer was found, but test consumers do exist.\n25. §1, .spec-md line 61 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (On the inverse side, an `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) is a frozen snapshot with one varied element, one capture and one machine-specific data path.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred current-shape claim. Experiments.fs does not exist at the repository root. The actual type is Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs:225-236: setup is a captured descriptor list, measurement is one MeasurementMode, varied is VariedElement option, and dataFileOpt is DataFilePath option. Thus the varied element and data attachment are optional, not universally present. Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3402 supplies file.Path.LocalPath to DataFilePath, supporting the machine-specific-path concern.\n26. §1, .spec-md line 61 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (The run law takes the first bound sample (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:measuredElementOf`).) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred current-behavior claim. The cited file does not exist at the repository root. In Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1445-1454, measuredElementOf does select the first bound sample, but its caller at :1471-1478 selects capture branches. Actual execution at :2751-2786 builds a SampleStep for each bound sample on the detector path, and Domain/ExperimentRun.fs:36-44 folds every SampleStep matrix. The first-sample limitation concerns capture selection, not limiting matrix propagation to one sample. Independently, .execution-contract-json obligation S81-CAPTURE-HOST and .spec-jsonl steps 253-254 describe the future per-object capture change; those declarations do not establish the stronger baseline assertion.\n27. §1, .spec-md line 61 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (The Inverse flow ends at a stub (`SolverHandoffView.fs`).) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred existing-wiring claim. SolverHandoffView.fs is absent at the repository root. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs:29-30 contains the no-solving message and :100-116 performs validation; SolverHandoffWindow.fs:19,37 hosts it. However, a search of non-test F# product sources found no construction of SolverHandoffWindow or use of SolverHandoffWindowKey beyond its declaration. The existence of the stub and its descriptive comments does not mechanically establish that the current Inverse flow reaches it.\n28. §1, .spec-md line 61 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (The working inverse code lives outside the constructor: `MuellerReconstruction`, `MuellerInverse`, and the noise and fit harness in the TEST project (`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs`).) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred current-placement/wiring claim. BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs does not resolve from the repository root; the actual test-only harness is Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs:303, with NoiseParam at :171 and fit wrappers at :493/:503. MuellerReconstruction and MuellerInverse are product modules at Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs:15 and MuellerInverse.fs:62. Their being outside the constructor can only mean outside its active inverse UI flow, not outside the constructor projects. Ui/SynthesisFitPage.fs:24 even imports MuellerInverse, so broad claims that none of its code is referenced by the UI would require qualification.\n29. §3.7, line 109 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (7. **Start-up import applies only what overwrites nothing.** Add, Reuse, Add-version and Mark-inactive rows apply automatically and are logged. Divergence and name-collision rows wait in the one import dialog, with their default action pre-selected, and nothing in them applies unconfirmed. A dropped file and a kit's snapshot always open the dialog.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile 1 unsupported semantic interpretation and behavior-seam mismatch. Operator source specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md:189-200 defines one per-entry table and says the decisions show as one dialog with a row per entry; it does not exempt nonconflicting startup rows. .execution-contract-json S31-STARTUP-IMPORT and .spec-jsonl step 98 instead apply unasked rows before any dialog, while S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING/step 112 opens a dialog only for rows awaiting choices. The final sentence also conflicts with the candidate: steps 150 and 156 filter SameContentHash out of pendingDecisions and skip the dialog when none remain; step 174 preserves that bypass. Operator source 001:271 says one dialog shows all kit-snapshot rows. The cited source does not contain the claimed automatic-startup exception, and repeating it in the contract does not establish source coverage.\n30. §3.14, line 117 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (- An item instantiates a model. The rows 001 §I marks as existing — the source preset (λ), the ideal LP/CP presets and the stack `Sample` — are models themselves, and an item references them.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile 1 semantic interpretation. The existing physics is real: Domain/ElementId.fs:203-214 defines Sample/structure, :262-269 defines SourcePreset wavelength/tuning, :338-344 defines PolarizerPreset, and :889-891 instantiates ideal LP/CP. Operator source 001:337-342 marks that physics as existing. However, :326-334 separately requires an item to instantiate an ItemModel, a library entry with extension .item-model-json; the existing markers do not state an exception to that model contract. .execution-contract-json S71-ADD-ITEM and .spec-jsonl step 223 instead let ItemModelChoice refer directly to a source preset, polarizer preset or sample version. The cited source does not support the claim that these existing entries are themselves the required ItemModel entries; the contract repeats the interpretation rather than independently establishing it.\n31. §3.16, line 121 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (16. **The crystal builders are product physics.** `buildTriclinic` (`BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs`), `buildAbsorbing` (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`) and the uniaxial builder used by `MuellerInverseTests` are what the study engine evaluates. They are promoted into `MuellerInverse.fs` as members of their parameter records, so ONE implementation exists. The constants, cuts, designs, `perturbedStart` and `searchBox` move to `BerremanTestSupport`, as 001 §Q says.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The existing artifacts resolve: Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs:98 declares buildTriclinic, AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:73 declares buildAbsorbing, and MuellerInverseTests.fs:110 declares buildUniaxialGyrotropic, passed to createBerremanForward at :131. Domain/MuellerInverse.fs:851-858 evaluates the caller-supplied builder. The claimed destination is an unsupported source interpretation: operator source specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md:603 expressly includes buildAbsorbing among the ground truth/design artifacts to move into BerremanTestSupport. .spec-jsonl step 334 and the S101 absorbing-builder obligation instead move it into product MuellerInverse.fs. The following spec bullet acknowledges the departure, but §2.1 makes 001 authoritative and no operator source pointer authorizes overriding that explicit destination. Current builder existence is confirmed; source coverage of the proposed relocation is refuted.\n32. .spec-md:215 (§7 Preset string ids) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (| Preset string ids → GUIDs | Compatibility break accepted: nothing persisted holds a preset id. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape: the migration relies on an absence of persisted preset ids. This row names neither a persisted format/file nor a unique type/member whose storage contract establishes that absence. AppContext.fs:91, :104 and :108 currently constructs in-memory source, collection and scene stores, but Domain/Project.fs:41 includes placements and Domain/Placement.fs:349 includes valueId : ElementValueId option, so the existence of those in-memory stores alone does not establish the unqualified claim about all persisted data. Under Phase 2 the row has no qualifying pointer.\n33. .spec-md:217 (§7 Test EF table + migration) -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `Test` EF table + migration → library model | Compatibility break accepted: nothing references it. The database is created from the model (`EnsureCreated`) and stamped. A mismatch is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`; the remedy is to recreate it from the catalogues, after \"Export my library\" if needed. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape from 'nothing references it'. The existing table and migration resolve, but the claimed absence of references is contradicted by Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs:83-94: migrate constructs TestDbContext and calls Database.Migrate, insertRow calls context.Tests.Add(Test(Name = name)), and readSingle reads context.Tests. Its fact at :125 executes that round trip. OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj:303 also references the Database project. No product consumer was found; the sentence does not qualify its claim that way. This is a nonexistent no-reference relationship, not a shifted line pointer.\n34. .spec-md:225 (§7 Migration intent) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (There is no release, so no stored data predates this spec except what the repository commits.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape claim: this asserts the absence of pre-existing persisted data. The sentence supplies no file, symbol or inventory pointer for that assertion. AGENTS.md states that there is no release, but that alone does not mechanically establish that no uncommitted user data exists.\n35. .spec-md:230 (§7 Migration intent, preset identities) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (| Preset string ids → GUIDs | Compatibility break accepted: nothing persisted holds a preset id. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape claim: the absence of persisted references justifies the proposed break. The row names neither a concrete preset-id type nor the persistence consumer/inventory that establishes the absence. Current serialization can carry ElementPlacement.valueId (OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs:349) through OpticalConstructorProject.placements (Project.fs:41); absence of existing saved instances needs a separately anchored claim.\n36. .spec-md:232 (§7 Migration intent, EF proof) -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `Test` EF table + migration → library model | Compatibility break accepted: nothing references it. The database is created from the model (`EnsureCreated`) and stamped. A mismatch is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`; the remedy is to recreate it from the catalogues, after \"Export my library\" if needed. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape claim, refuted specifically at 'nothing references it'. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/TestDbContext.cs:21,29 exposes DbSet<Test> and maps the Test table. OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs:83-95 migrates that context, inserts Test(Name = name), and reads it; :127 onward asserts the migration and round trip. OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj:303 references the Database project. The profile-1 contract S21-RETIRE-EF-PROOF and .spec-jsonl step 59 correctly acknowledge this consumer and declare DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.TestDbMigrationTests, matching the live module at TestDbMigrationTests.fs:20. No product consumer was found, but the unqualified assertion has no matching current state. EnsureCreated and schema stamping are future effects.\n37. .spec-md:256 (§8 Seams and extensibility) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (new abstraction layers over the existing proxies;) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Matched 'existing'. Neither this bullet nor its paragraph names a proxy type, defining file or member. The repository contains multiple distinct proxy contracts, so 'the existing proxies' is unanchored under Phase 2; discovering some proxies does not identify the set this sentence means.\n38. .spec-md:314 (§S1.0 Problem statement) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (S1.1 turns the two closure routes into axis data, and S1.2 makes `complexity` mandatory.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred numeric/existing-route assumption. The sentence does not name either route or a file/type that defines the counted set; complexity is a field name, not a unique route identifier. Searches find buildTabulatedClosure in OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:158 and EpsAxisEvaluated in Berreman/Dispersion.fs:369, with multiple producers in DispersionModels.fs and MaterialLibrary.fs. Treating those as exactly two conceptual routes requires the missing definition of the counted set, so this unanchored claim cannot receive a mechanically re-derived count.\n39. .spec-md:327 (§S2.0 Problem statement) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Every library proxy keeps its shape and gains a SQLite `create`, proved by contract suites run against both stores.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred 'unchanged shape' assumption. This sentence names no library proxy type, member signature or defining file; create is not a unique identifier. The adjacent VersionsInUse name identifies the usage provider, not the set of library proxy records whose shapes are promised to stay the same. The operator source §C enumerates MaterialProxy, CategoryProxy, SampleProxy, SourceProxy and LibraryProxy, but the audited paragraph itself does not anchor that set.\n40. .spec-md:341 (§S4.0 Problem statement) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Today's experiments and scenes persist into the kit. The in-memory scene and collection seams and the `.ocproj` aggregate are deleted.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred existing-seam assumption. The paragraph supplies descriptions and a file extension, but no defining path or unique type/member for the current scene store, collection store or aggregate. Repository searches locate SceneProxy (Scene.fs:107), ExperimentCollectionProxy (ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:73), and OpticalConstructorProject (Project.fs:26), but under Phase 2 the audited paragraph must name its intended anchors rather than require this inferred mapping. Kit persistence and deletion are future effects.\n41. .spec-md:365 (§S8.0 Problem statement) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The run law walks every object in light order, and the source is a real Stokes state whose default reproduces today's charts.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred 'same as today' assumption. No chart, current run-law symbol, test or baseline is named in this sentence. ExperimentRun.fs:36-44 contains the present detectorStokes fold, beginning with unpolarizedStokes and special-casing the first preparing polarizer, but the audited sentence does not identify that mechanism or which chart comparisons define parity. Future preservation cannot be anchored by the generic word 'charts'.\n42. .spec-md:365 (§S8.0 Problem statement) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Quick swap, the grid generator and the naming template follow; the template replaces the label regex.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption that an existing label parser is being replaced. The sentence names no file, parser type or regex member. A search locates experimentRegex at Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs:504 and its consumer MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed at :511-517, also named explicitly by operator source §R. The audited paragraph omits those anchors, so 'the label regex' remains unanchored under Phase 2.\n43. S11.0 Problem statement, line 372 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (It fits staged or jointly on the existing engines, chosen automatically.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The sentence and its paragraph name no file, symbol, or uniquely identifiable engine type. 'the existing engines' is an unanchored reuse claim; the automatic choice is proposed behavior, not evidence of an existing artifact.\n44. S11.0 Problem statement, line 372 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The study view replaces the hand-off stub.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption phrase: replacing 'the hand-off stub' presupposes an existing artifact. No file or class name identifies it in this paragraph. Repository search finds a candidate at Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs:14, whose opening documentation describes a validation-only terminal screen, but the spec does not anchor its claim to that module.\n45. S12.0 Problem statement, line 378 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Every expected value comes from where it already lives.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: No source file, symbol, or fixture identifies where the expected values already live. AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests is declared at Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs:60 and is named earlier in the paragraph as AT-2, but that does not identify the sources for every expected value across both acceptance tests.\n\nThe report also has 2 NOT-CHECKED claim(s) the auditor could not mechanically verify. These do not block handoff, but review each and either add a resolvable <file>:<symbol> pointer in .spec-md so a re-run can verify it, or confirm it is correct as written:\n\n1. .spec-md:236 (§7 Migration intent, harness and samples) -- NOT-CHECKED. The claim (| Harness and samples (test → product / test support) | Migration provided: a move. `BerremanTests`' numbers are unchanged. |) could not be verified: Matched 'unchanged'. Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs exists, including InverseFitHarness at :303 and assertMuellerEqual at :530. The sentence declares numerical parity after a future move; it names no before/after numerical baseline that this current-tree pointer audit can compare. Existence of the harness is verified, but the future parity result is not.\n2. .spec-md:276 (§9 Done when) -- NOT-CHECKED. The claim (`BerremanTests`' numbers are unchanged.) could not be verified: Matched 'unchanged'. This is explicitly a future completion condition. Berreman/BerremanTests and its numerical assertions exist, but the sentence gives no completed implementation or concrete before/after result to compare in this audit. Numerical preservation is not established by the existence of the test project.\n\nMake NO other edits to .spec-md beyond the items above; every remaining claim in the report was CONFIRMED."}
{"at": "2026-11-04T20:50:22Z", "commit_ref": "b6585d0", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Repaired the 45 findings and reviewed both NOT-CHECKED parity claims from the 2026-11-04 auto-loop 1/10 report. Changes are limited to .spec-md, .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json plus this safe-writer history append. The narrative changes only the reported passages: repository-root paths now resolve to inspected declarations; persistence, optional experiment fields, first-sample capture selection, propagation, handoff reachability and inverse-module ownership describe the code accurately; migration policy no longer assumes saved data or test consumers are absent; numerical parity is a future verification obligation with source assertions, not a measured pre-implementation claim.\n\nThe operator source remains authoritative. Under 001 sections B/E, changed catalogue and kit-snapshot decisions include every row, including Reuse, and no library/import-log change precedes confirmation; the unchanged catalogue manifest skip remains. Updated the affected planning, startup, dialog, registration, snapshot and test-fixture consumers, including the stale all-Reuse bypass tests. Under 001 section I, every item carries an exact ItemModel version; source, ideal-polarizer and stack forms use typed physics bindings, and snapshots include the model and its dependencies. Added the three required built-in model entries to the future export's exact edit reach and updated downstream consumers. Under 001 section Q, buildTriclinic and buildAbsorbing retain their named test-support contracts and move with their modules; their tensor expressions are shared product members called by the retained test builders, without duplicated kernels or a product dependency on test support.\n\nValidation: installed ASG executability check passed with no findings; gate-bindings resolved successfully; all 494 ordered steps retain valid effects and matching acceptance hashes, and the final wiring anchor remains. The validator caught two empty ui-tests selector arms during repair; the installed inventory places those composition classes in ui-smoke, whose all_discovered selection already covers them, so only the empty arms were removed. Edited spec files are LF. The pre-existing mixed history line endings and all prior history bytes are preserved. No product source, tests, gates, inventory, acceptance oracle, section plan or contract registry was edited. Product builds/tests were not run for this spec-authoring cycle."}
