{"at": "2026-11-04T21:29:58Z", "commit_ref": "93279f6", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "input", "content": "[auto-loop 2/10]\n\nThe claim-check report flagged 7 item(s) that MUST be fixed before handoff. Apply the following edits to .spec-md:\n\n1. §4 Order and greenness; .spec-md:132 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (- **Order and greenness.** Sections land in plan order, and each step leaves every gate it runs green. Superseded code is deleted in the change that replaces it. A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile-1 executable-binding audit, rather than a claim that future gates have run: compared AGENTS.md Build & test and specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md §U with .spec-jsonl, .execution-contract-json and the live .gates catalog through the read-only effective_plan/explicit_selections helpers. Step 2 effectively runs ui-smoke, ui-tests and kit-acceptance, but gate_selection declares only unit-tests and constructor-unit-tests, and no execution-contract obligation binds those additional (step, gate) pairs. The same omission occurs at other steps. Inventory/effect replay has no kit-acceptance tests at step 2; their first declared creation is step 421. Thus executable test/fixture and acceptance pointers needed for the stated green progression are missing. Existing declared command hashes match their descriptors; that does not cover the omitted effective gates. No oracle was created or modified.\n2. .spec-md:242 (section 7, project-file history) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (| `.ocproj`, `recent.json`, autosave files | Compatibility break accepted: no window ever saved or opened `.ocproj`. The kit history starts empty. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption from the migration rationale. The row names only the .ocproj format, recent.json and autosave files, not a concrete file:symbol/file:line or a uniquely named UI type establishing the absence of callers. A current-tree search finds saveProject/openProject in OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs:24/:35 and test callers, and no UI/App callers. That supports a narrower present-tree observation but cannot establish the unanchored historical wording \"no window ever saved or opened\". Phase 2 therefore requires REFUTED-NO-POINTER.\n3. S9.0, line 358 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The optics-mueller lab files move into their kit folder.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred existing-source claim from the move instruction. This sentence and its paragraph identify neither a source file/directory nor a unique code identifier for the lab files. Independent discovery finds Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip and the reference scripts/summaries, and operator source 001:564 specifies their destination, but these pointers are absent from the audited paragraph. Under Phase 2 the source claim is un-anchored.\n4. S10.0, line 364 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The study engine and the Planner need what `BerremanTests` holds today, so it moves into product code. The ground truth and designs move to `BerremanTestSupport`, and the §7.2 pipeline and its expected values are promoted. `BerremanTests`' numbers are unchanged.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The current-artifact premise is not anchored: BerremanTests names a project/namespace containing many test classes, not the particular harness, ground-truth declarations or the class containing the §7.2 fact. No concrete file or unique source type is named in this paragraph. Independent inspection finds InverseFitHarness.fs, BiaxialSample.fs, AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs and MuellerReconstructionTests.fs in Berreman/BerremanTests, all compiled by BerremanTests.fsproj, but supplying those omitted anchors would repair the spec rather than verify its pointer. The move and unchanged numerical outcomes are future obligations, not measured post-change facts.\n5. S11.0, line 372 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The study MUST choose staged or joint fitting automatically, reusing `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign` / `reconstruct` and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs:createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt` through `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile-1 semantic interpretation audit: the reuse pointers resolve at MuellerReconstruction.fs:928/:959, MuellerInverseSolver.fs:36 and MuellerInverse.fs:850. However, operator source 001:421-428 lists joint/staged fit modes and makes the LINEAR/NONLINEAR engine choice automatic. It does not require automatic staged/joint mode selection. Independently read .execution-contract-json S113-FIT-STAGE, S113-ENGINE-CHOICE and S113-FIT-RUN against .spec-jsonl steps 385, 386 and 391: the request supplies a stage, stageWith applies it, and engineWith selects LinearStudyEngine or NonlinearStudyEngine. There is no source requirement, obligation or behavior seam implementing the automatic staged/joint choice asserted here. The defect is the unsupported future interpretation, not missing numerical solver functions.\n6. S12.0, line 378 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (AT-1 MUST reuse the literals in `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:1003` and the stage-1 and product-check assertions in that file's §7.2 fact.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Read MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:1003 -> expectedQz, followed by expectedLr and expectedComb at :1010/:1017. The §7.2 fact begins at :802; its stage-1 block at :847-859 calculates calibration constants but contains no assertion against expected stage-1 values. Its actual assertions at :1025-1068 cover matrix ranks, matrix errors and cascade/product metrics. The stage-1 expected literals and assertion are in a DIFFERENT fact, 'Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values', at :593 and :629-639. Thus the literal and product pointers are real, but the claimed stage-1 assertions do not exist in the named §7.2 fact; this is not a nearby line-number drift.\n7. C.0, line 396 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The whole suites, `elevation-full` and `kit-acceptance` are green together.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile-1 audit of the declared future completion result, not a claim that unimplemented code is already green. Read .spec-jsonl step 494: it does explicitly select all_discovered for the solver, constructor, UI and kit suites. However, independently resolving effective_plan and explicit_selections against the actual gate descriptors finds unbound required consumers earlier in this chunk. For example, step 493 resolves ui-tests but declares no ui-tests selection and no .execution-contract-json obligation binds (493, ui-tests); steps 386, 387, 389-391 and 393 similarly omit required unit-tests selections/obligations; steps 422, 424, 427, 428 and 430 omit required ui-smoke selections/obligations. These are SELECTION_REQUIRED / missing acceptance bindings, not runtime pass evidence. The read-only inventory freshness, acceptance-text binding, declared test/contract-consumer replay, package-generation, behavior-seam and closing-scope checks found no additional issue, and command hashes matched for checks that were declared. Matching those declared checks cannot establish coverage for the omitted gates. No build or test was run and no frozen oracle was edited.\n\nMake NO other edits to .spec-md beyond the items above; every remaining claim in the report was CONFIRMED."}
{"at": "2026-11-04T21:29:58Z", "commit_ref": "93279f6", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Spec-author auto-loop 2/10: scoped repair of the seven claim-check findings. Changed only specs/0050/.spec-md, .spec-jsonl and .execution-contract-json, then appended this row through history_cli. The seven .spec-md replacements are confined to the flagged paragraphs: present-tree ProjectFile caller evidence replaces the historical claim; the lab-data move names its source and destinations; harness/sample/pipeline moves name verified source declarations; the requested joint/staged mode is distinguished from automatic linear/nonlinear engine choice; AT-1 names the separate stage-1 fact and its literals; greenness and closing coverage are explicit future obligations, including producer ordering.\n\nExecutable repairs: 90 missing effective gate selections/check bindings repaired across 67 steps: ui-tests 48, ui-smoke 17, unit-tests 17, kit-acceptance 8 (after the producer). Added narrow class selections, measured-light whole ui-smoke selections, and 67 consumer-regression obligations bound into the corresponding acceptance_bindings. Command identities come from the installed executability gate-bindings CLI. Each new selected class was checked separately against inventory plus chronological effect replay at its step. The effective gate roster is identical before and after this repair. All 1249 prior obligations, behavior seams, temporal checks, closing scopes, test/contract/package effects, acceptance texts/hashes, red pairs, 494 step numbers and the final whole-suite selections are preserved.\n\nRemaining authority conflict: handoff is NOT clear. With specs/0050/.spec-bundle lacking gates_required_only, ASG effective_plan automatically selects kit-acceptance at steps 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 212, 335, 336, 337, 338, 339, 340, 341, 342, 343, 344, 345, 346, 348, 349, 351, 352, 353, 356, 376, 380, 381, 386, 387, 388, 389, 390, 391, 393, 397, 398, 399, 400, 401, 402, 403 and 404. The inventory has no kit-acceptance suite, and its first producing effect is step 421, consistent with operator source 001 section U and .spec-md section 9. Binding those 44 selections to future tests would invent discovery. Their SELECTION_REQUIRED and missing gate-obligation findings remain intentionally unresolved. The bundle/gate owner needs to make the authored per-step required_gates authoritative (gates_required_only: true in .spec-bundle), or supply an equivalent producer-aware gate policy. A read-only explicit-required-gates comparison has no missing selections or bindings; the final whole-suite requirements survive. .spec-bundle, .gates, override files, inventory and oracle are outside this round's write scope and were not edited. No test was removed or invented to evade the conflict.\n\nValidation: read_inventory freshness; validate_effects; chronological replay_effects; check_coverage (acceptance and closing reach); check_package_generations; temporal predicate checks; every declared selector arm; build prerequisites and producer coverage; every command binding; and git diff --check passed in the read-only component audit. Only the 44 premature kit gate pairs remain unbound in the current effective plan. The installed CLI gate-bindings ran successfully. An attempted read-only CLI check --matrix over an in-memory Windows named pipe returned Invalid argument; no file was created. The ordinary compiler-preview command was not used because it creates temporary bundles outside the four-file scope and a provisional oracle; no full compiler-validation success is claimed. No build or product test ran. There is no frozen acceptance oracle in this bundle, and none was created. Edited spec files have LF endings. The pre-existing .history bytes are preserved; its existing CRLF is not rewritten, and this append uses the mandated safe writer.\n"}
