{"at": "2026-11-04T22:02:12Z", "commit_ref": "971e47d", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "input", "content": "[auto-loop 3/10]\n\nThe claim-check report flagged 6 item(s) that MUST be fixed before handoff. Apply the following edits to .spec-md:\n\n1. §0.2 New artifacts, line 52; profile-1 test-consumer validity audit -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (| `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs` (AT-1, AT-2) | The `kit-acceptance` gate. |) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The file is correctly declared as future, but the execution binding has an unsupported validity interval. Operator requirement specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md:690 says kit-acceptance is forward-pointing until section 12 creates the file. The live .gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates requires Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs. .spec-jsonl step 421 is the first ADD_TEST/effect creating that file/class, and S121-AT1-ITEMS-SETUPS binds its gate there. Independently computing effective_plan and replay_effects with the ASG executability modules shows kit-acceptance is already scheduled at steps 2 and 335, while the required class is absent in both post-states (and remains absent at 420); those steps declare no kit-acceptance selection, and .execution-contract-json has no kit-acceptance check at either step. explicit_selections reports SELECTION_REQUIRED. Thus the gate-to-test pointer cannot resolve at its earlier consumers; this refutation concerns the execution binding, not the mere absence of a deliberately future file. Acceptance hashes, command identities, effect/coverage validation, test-lifetime replay and package-generation checks were checked separately without modifying or freezing the candidate/oracle.\n2. §3.23 (.spec-md:128) -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (- S10.1 moves the noise FUNCTIONS (`disturb`, `misread`, `misreadAbsolute`, `noisyObserveWith`, `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith`, `NoiseSeed`, `UniformDeviateProvider`) and the rest of 001 §Q's promoted list into Optimization, which opens the Domain types. One implementation exists throughout.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile 1 execution-binding failure, not a hallucinated source symbol: InverseFitHarness.fs:114/:208/:553/:567/:589/:604/:626 contains NoiseSeed, UniformDeviateProvider and the five named functions. Operator 001:595-602 supports their product move, and S101-NOISE-MOVE/S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE bind its unit-test consumers. However, independently computing the effective plan with ASG effective_plan/explicit_selections selects kit-acceptance at S10.1 steps 335-343, including the noise moves 339-340. None of those steps declares a kit-acceptance gate_selection or has a matching execution-contract acceptance/check binding. Replaying inventory plus declared effects gives no kit-acceptance tests at those steps; KitAcceptanceTests is first created by ADD_TEST in step 421. The .gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates command filters Category=kit-acceptance and requires that future file. Thus this move has missing executable proof and an invalid fixture-consumer interval; citing the move requirement again does not establish coverage. No candidate, gate or oracle was edited.\n3. §4 Order and greenness; .spec-md:132 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (- **Order and greenness.** Sections MUST land in plan order; each step MUST leave every effective gate green except its declared, captured ADD_RED failures. Before handoff, every effective gate and prerequisite MUST have an obligation/check binding in `.execution-contract-json`, and every filtered gate MUST have an explicit `.spec-jsonl` `gate_selection` whose classes exist after that step's effects. `kit-acceptance` MUST run only from its first test-producing step (421) onward; §9 names the verification before that producer. Superseded code MUST be deleted in the change that replaces it. A reuse MUST be a move or a call: the new home and deletion of the old body MUST land together.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile-1 binding audit against operator .manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md §S (green sections), §U (kit-acceptance is forward-pointing until section 12) and AGENTS.md gates. The read-only effective_plan helper computes kit-acceptance in step 2's effective roster. Step 2 has gate_selection entries for unit-tests, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests, but none for kit-acceptance; no .execution-contract-json obligation/check binds (2, kit-acceptance). Replaying the measured inventory and declared test effects places the first kit-acceptance test at step 421, whose effects create KitAcceptanceTests. The same premature unbound gate occurs in other steps. The candidate therefore lacks executable pointers needed for its stated before-producer exclusion and complete binding requirement. Checked command hashes match current descriptors, present selections resolve to post-effect classes, declared prerequisites are present, behavior-seam/acceptance coverage and package-effect replay report no findings. Those checks do not supply the missing gate obligation or test producer; future pass results were not measured.\n4. §8, persistence and import negative scope; .spec-md line 231 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (- an editor for the database outside the existing Library and Materials windows.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The phrase explicitly says existing but the bullet supplies neither a file/symbol pointer nor a declared type name. Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs:34 and MaterialsWindow.fs:29 are discoverable likely targets, but the paragraph does not name LibraryWindow or MaterialsWindow or link those files. Under the required unanchored-claim rule, finding plausible windows independently does not supply the missing specification anchor.\n5. §9, acceptance gates and pre-S12 coverage; .spec-md line 253 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (- **Acceptance.** `kit-acceptance` (AT-1, AT-2: trait `kit-acceptance`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs`) runs from the step that creates that file onward, on every step touching the study, the run law, the import code, the acceptance files or the two kits. Before S12 the run-law and import steps are proved by `constructor-unit-tests` and the `FsxAcceptanceTests` classes under `ui-tests`.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: The kit-acceptance gate itself resolves to .gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates, and step 421 creates OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with ADD_TEST and the acceptance gate. Post-creation edits to the named acceptance/run-law/Optimization/test-support/kit paths carry that gate. However, the same paragraph claims pre-S12 run-law and import steps are proved by FsxAcceptanceTests under ui-tests: .spec-jsonl step 246 edits ExperimentRun.fs and step 374 edits ExperimentRun.fs/StudyForward.fs, but both select only constructor-unit-tests alongside build/elevation. Import steps 301-303 and 307 likewise omit ui-tests. Their .execution-contract-json bindings S81-SOURCE-EMISSION, S112-FORWARD-MODEL and S92 import obligations provide no missing Fsx ui-tests check. FsxAcceptanceTests exists at OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:51, but the claimed execution binding is absent. This is unsupported coverage under profile 1, not a missing test-class declaration.\n6. .spec-md line 396 -- REFUTED-POINTER-HALLUCINATED. The claim (Handoff MUST also require every earlier effective gate to have a valid post-effect selection and an acceptance/check binding in `.execution-contract-json`; the final whole-suite checks MUST NOT substitute for that per-step coverage or for the producer ordering in §4.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Profile-1 audit of the referenced per-step coverage found absent bindings, not just an unrun future check. Using the read-only ASG effective_plan and explicit_selections helpers, then independently comparing every effective (step, gate) pair with .execution-contract-json obligations and replaying .spec-jsonl test effects, kit-acceptance is effective at steps including 335, 356, 380 and 404, but each lacks gate_selection[kit-acceptance] and any obligation check binding for that pair. The post-effect suite is empty at those steps; step 421 first declares its KitAcceptanceTests producer. The helpers report SELECTION_REQUIRED and the independent comparison reports GATE_JUSTIFICATION. Operator source 001:690 explicitly makes this gate forward-pointing until section 12 creates the test file. Thus the referenced contract does not provide the claimed earlier effective-gate selections/bindings or consumer ordering; step 494 cannot supply them retroactively. The not-yet-frozen oracle is not treated as a defect in this in-authoring cycle.\n\nMake NO other edits to .spec-md beyond the items above; every remaining claim in the report was CONFIRMED."}
